{"level":30,"time":1778188356685,"pid":122,"hostname":"e70bc6df-98e","step":"review-runs","item":"2.md","index":4,"runIndex":"run-2","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_018tdkiiGkXnc46H1xA4PB7D","type":"tool_result","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Based on the visual analysis of the provided landscape plan:\n\n*   **Tree Symbols:** Yes, there are numerous tree symbols shown throughout the plan. They are depicted as large circles with various internal line patterns and crosshairs (often labeled with letters like \"M\", \"SM\", etc.).\n*   **Overhead Electric (OHE):** Yes, overhead electric infrastructure is depicted. A continuous line containing the text \"- OHE -\" runs along the entire southern boundary of the site plan (near the bottom edge of the drawing).\n*   **Approximate Distance:** Several trees are planted along the southern boundary in close proximity to the OHE line.\n    *   The circles representing the tree canopies visually overlap or intersect the \"- OHE -\" line.\n    *   Using the graphic scale provided in the bottom right corner (\"SCALE IN FEET (1\"=20'-0\")\"), the centers (representing the trunks) of the trees nearest to this southern boundary appear to be approximately **5 to 15 feet** away from the OHE line."}]}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"df902855-f209-47f1-9270-a32412d9566b","uuid":"1ee7a20c-4fa8-4fce-8fb8-04180bc903ba","tool_use_result":[{"type":"text","text":"Based on the visual analysis of the provided landscape plan:\n\n*   **Tree Symbols:** Yes, there are numerous tree symbols shown throughout the plan. They are depicted as large circles with various internal line patterns and crosshairs (often labeled with letters like \"M\", \"SM\", etc.).\n*   **Overhead Electric (OHE):** Yes, overhead electric infrastructure is depicted. A continuous line containing the text \"- OHE -\" runs along the entire southern boundary of the site plan (near the bottom edge of the drawing).\n*   **Approximate Distance:** Several trees are planted along the southern boundary in close proximity to the OHE line.\n    *   The circles representing the tree canopies visually overlap or intersect the \"- OHE -\" line.\n    *   Using the graphic scale provided in the bottom right corner (\"SCALE IN FEET (1\"=20'-0\")\"), the centers (representing the trunks) of the trees nearest to this southern boundary appear to be approximately **5 to 15 feet** away from the OHE line."}]}
