{"level":30,"time":1778188389084,"pid":122,"hostname":"e70bc6df-98e","step":"review-runs","item":"13.md","index":2,"runIndex":"run-1","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_011VwY2bkcFwRa5BE24s8im8","type":"tool_result","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Based on the provided site plan document, the transformer pads appear to be located entirely on private property and do not straddle the public right-of-way or property lines. \n\nHere is the detailed visual evidence supporting this conclusion:\n\n1.  **Property Boundary Identification:** The main property boundary is depicted by a thick, heavy dashed line with a \"long dash, two dots\" pattern that encompasses the entire development site. To the west of this line is the public right-of-way, labeled \"Valley View Road\" and \"60' R.O.W.\".\n2.  **Western Transformer Pads:** There are three pads on the western side of the property labeled **\"Electrical Transformer Pad\"**:\n    *   Near the northwest entrance (north of Building 1).\n    *   Adjacent to Building 2 (near Unit 201).\n    *   Adjacent to Building 8 (near Unit 801).\n    *   *Relationship:* All three of these rectangular pad graphics are drawn distinctly inside (to the east of) the thick dashed property boundary line separating the site from the public right-of-way.\n3.  **Eastern Transformer Pads:** There are two pads on the eastern side of the property labeled **\"Electrical Transformer Pad\"**:\n    *   Adjacent to Building 5 (near Unit 504).\n    *   Adjacent to Building 7 (near Unit 704).\n    *   *Relationship:* Both of these rectangular pad graphics are drawn distinctly inside (to the west of) the thick dashed property boundary line on the eastern edge of the site. (Note: The pad near Unit 504 is located within an area labeled \"25' Drainage Easement\", but this easement is still contained within the main property boundary).\n\nIn all identified instances, the rectangular graphics for the transformer pads are contai