the provided site plan (Sheet 9), here is the analysis regarding overhead electric utilities:\n\n*   **Are overhead electric utilities shown?** \n    Yes, overhead electric utilities are shown on the site plan. They are denoted by lines containing the text \"**-OHE-**\".\n*   **Are their locations dimensioned or clearly marked relative to site boundaries and building locations?**\n    *   **Clearly Marked:** Yes, they are clearly marked. The \"-OHE-\" lines run predominantly along the southern and eastern perimeter boundaries of the site. \n    *   **Dimensioned/Located via Easements:** While there are no direct point-to-point dimension lines (e.g., an arrow indicating exactly \"X feet\" from a building corner to the wire itself), their locations are established relative to the site boundaries through corresponding marked utility easements. For example:\n        *   Along the southern boundary, near the \"-OHE-\" line, there is a callout for a \"**5' Elec. Easement Vol. 69, Pg. 14 Vol. 73, Pg. 76 P.R.T.C.Tx.**\" as well as a \"**5' Elec. & Tele. Easement Vol. 5468, Pg. 885 D.R.T.C.Tx.**\"\n        *   Along the eastern boundary, near the \"-OHE-\" line next to Bldg. 6, there are callouts for a \"**15' Easement Vol. 73, Pg. 76 P.R.T.C.Tx.**\" and a \"**5' Electric Easement Vol. 69, Pg. 14 Vol. 73, Pg. 76 P.R.T.C.Tx.**\" \n\nThe spatial relationship between the buildings (which have specified setbacks) and these boundaries/easements dictates the clearance to the overhead lines on this scaled drawing."}]}
