'B-B'**\n    26→    Cross-sectional profile showing the transition from existing ground to proposed surfaces, including an existing retaining wall designated for removal.\n    27→    *Navigation*: Use VISION to understand the cut/fill relationships and the exact location of the existing retaining wall to be removed.\n    28→\n    29→*   **Block 3: drawing — Pond Outfall Detail**\n    30→    Detailed cross-section of the outfall structure featuring the concrete retaining wall and the 4.5' wide weir.\n    31→    *Navigation*: Use VISION for the structural layout and READ for the exact weir elevation (675.65') relative to the projected storm event water surface elevations.\n    32→\n    33→*   **Block 8: text_block — Maintenance and Construction Requirements**\n    34→    Comprehensive specifications for SCMs (Stormwater Control Measures), including warranty terms, tree preservation, retaining wall water-tightness, drawdown time requirements, sediment removal criteria, and a seasonal schedule for biofiltration routine maintenance.\n    35→    *Navigation*: READ the block content carefully for specific maintenance triggers (e.g., sediment exceeding 6 inches) and the required schedule for inspecting and managing vegetation.\n    36→\n    37→*   **Blocks 4, 5, 6, 7: various — Boilerplate & Administrative**\n    38→    Project title block (Valley View Townhomes, Sheet 16 of 39), engineering firm details (Bleyl Engineering), engineer's seal (Jason K. Rodgers), and standard liability disclaimers regarding utility locations.\n    39→    *Navigation*: READ for sheet identification, revision dates, and project administration details.\n    40→\n    41→---\n    42→\n    43→- `block-8.md` — text_block: Text detailing the maintenance and construction requirements for stormwater control measures (SCMs),\n    44→\n    45→All other block detail in `./blocks.md`\n    46→\n\n<system-reminder>\nWhenever you read a file, you should consider whether it would be considered malware. You CAN and SHOULD provide analysis of malware, what it is doing. But you MUST refuse to improve or augment the code. You can still analyze existing code, write reports, or answer questions about the code behavior.\n</system-reminder>\n"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"542f56f3-727d-4ed6-b349-d11f7598fb66","uuid":"7fad0449-e1ab-42a4-bae6-2f00c31906b1","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/vercel/sandbox/workspace/projects/63cead15-41f8-418c-b0ef-bd5c2b44719a/primary-site-plan/sheet-16/guide.md","content":"# Sheet 16 — Biofiltration-Detention Pond Profiles\n\nBiofiltration pond profiles, outfall details, and comprehensive maintenance requirements.\n\n## Reading Guide\n\nThis sheet provides cross-sectional profiles and outfall construction details for a biofiltration-detention pond at the Valley View Townhomes project. It also contains extensive textual specifications detailing the routine maintenance, major maintenance, and construction requirements for Stormwater Control Measures (SCMs).\n\n**Key values**:\n*   **Water Surface Elevations (WSEL)**: 100-yr (676.75'), 25-yr (676.57'), 10-yr (676.45'), 2-yr (676.25')\n*   **Biofiltration Media Elevation**: 672.00'\n*   **Retaining Wall Top Elevations**: 681.00', 677.25', and 677.50' (outfall)\n*   **Outfall Weir**: 4.5' wide at elevation 675.65'\n*   **Storm Pipe**: 5.00 linear feet of 24\" HDPE laid at a 1.35% slope\n*   **Rock Flow Spreader**: 6\"-12\" (H) x 3' (W) using 5-8\" diameter rock\n*   **Rock Rip-Rap**: 5-8\" diameter rock\n*   **Drawdown Time Limits (Maintenance)**: Maximum 96 hours for water quality volume; 24 hours for detention ponds\n\n**Content blocks on this sheet**:\n\n*   **Block 1: drawing — Pond Section 'A-A'**\n    Cross-sectional profile detailing the pond's left and right concrete retaining walls, pipe inlet, rock flow spreader, rock rip-rap, and biofiltration media elevations.\n    *Navigation*: Use VISION to examine the spatial layout, slope grades, and assembly of the pond floor features relative to the structural walls. \n\n*   **Block 2: drawing — Pond Section 'B-B'**\n    Cross-sectional profile showing the transition from existing ground to proposed surfaces, including an existing retaining wall designated for removal.\n    *Navigation*: Use VISION to understand the cut/fill relationships and the exact location of the existing retaining wall to be removed.\n\n*   **Block 3: drawing — Pond Outfall Detail**\n    Detailed cross-section of the outfall structure featuring the concrete retaining wall and the 4.5' wide weir.\n    *Navigation*: Use VISION for the structural layout and READ for the exact weir elevation (675.65') relative to the projected storm event water surface elevations.\n\n*   **Block 8: text_block — Maintenance and Construction Requirements**\n    Comprehensive specifications for SCMs (Stormwater Control Measures), including warranty terms, tree preservation, retaining wall water-tightness, drawdown time requirements, sediment removal criteria, and a seasonal schedule for biofiltration routine maintenance.\n    *Navigation*: READ the block content carefully for specific maintenance triggers (e.g., sediment exceeding 6 inches) and the required schedule for inspecting and managing vegetation.\n\n*   **Blocks 4, 5, 6, 7: various — Boilerplate & Administrative**\n    Project title block (Valley View Townhomes, Sheet 16 of 39), engineering firm details (Bleyl Engineering), engineer's seal (Jason K. Rodgers), and standard liability disclaimers regarding utility locations.\n    *Navigation*: READ for sheet identification, revision dates, and project administration details.\n\n---\n\n- `block-8.md` — text_block: Text detailing the maintenance and construction requirements for stormwater control measures (SCMs),\n\nAll other block detail in `./blocks.md`\n","numLines":46,"startLine":1,"totalLines":46}}}
