{"level":30,"time":1778188447092,"pid":122,"hostname":"e70bc6df-98e","step":"review-runs","item":"13.md","index":5,"runIndex":"run-2","type":"assistant","message":{"id":"gen_01KR24MQM80PAT0DNJ7Q21FS05","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"This is important! The vision tool has identified:\n1. Pads 1 and 2 appear to be located within or very close to a 10' P.U.E. (Public Utility Easement)\n2. Pad 3 appears to be near a 15' Easement noted on the property\n3. Pads 1 and 2 are very close to the western property boundary and sidewalk easement\n4. All pads appear to be inside the property line and NOT in the ROW\n\nHowever, there's a critical issue: According to the facts.md, there are several easements that are NOT depicted on the site plan:\n- Greenbelt Access & Use Easement (0.31 acres, NE interior) - PERPETUAL, NOT shown\n- City of Austin Drainage Easement (0.130 acres, NE corner) - PERPETUAL, NOT shown\n\nThese undepicted easements could affect whether properties are truly on \"private property\" or if they have restrictions.\n\nBut looking at the electrical plan, the transformer pads shown don't appear to be in the NE corner where those critical easements are located. Pads 1-4 are shown on the western and central areas of the site.\n\nLet me check for drainage direction and any utilities shown nearby.","signature":""}],"model":"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001","stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":0},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"753eb9f1-6b81-4b4f-8a9b-68520af22dec","uuid":"c13de105-0fd6-4d33-b0f9-c1e368c10b77"}
