here is a graphic scale provided in the bottom right corner (\"SCALE IN FEET (1\"=20'-0\")\"), there is no stated numerical dimension indicating the clearance distance."}]}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"426b854d-ee1b-489d-9b1e-65178de6c706","uuid":"d96061cd-585b-4c7a-96ec-13ec3e29d8f2","tool_use_result":[{"type":"text","text":"Based on a visual analysis of the provided image, here are the answers to your questions.\n\n**Important Note Regarding Sheet Number:** The prompt asks about \"Sheet 31\". Please note that the title block in the bottom right corner of the provided image indicates this is **\"28 of 35\"**. The following analysis is based strictly on the provided image (Sheet 28).\n\n**1. Are overhead electric (OHE) lines shown on the landscape plan?**\nYes, overhead electric lines are indicated on this plan.\n\n**2. Where are they located?**\nThere is a line running horizontally along the bottom (South) edge of the site plan area. This line is explicitly labeled with the text **\"- OHE -\"**. It appears to run roughly parallel to the bottom property line or right-of-way, outside the main limit of construction (which is marked by lines labeled \"- LOC -\").\n\n**3. Are any trees or landscape plantings shown near or beneath these overhead lines?**\nYes, there are trees shown near the overhead line in the bottom right (Southeast) corner of the plan.\n*   Following the \"- OHE -\" line from left to right along the bottom edge, there are no trees near it on the left or middle sections.\n*   In the bottom right corner, the \"- OHE -\" line passes very close to a cluster of tree symbols (indicated by circles with center crosshairs). Specifically, the line passes south of a tree labeled with \"M\" and \"H.7\" and north of another tree labeled with \"M\".\n\n**4. What is the lateral distance between proposed trees and the overhead electric lines?**\nThere are **no explicit dimension lines or text callouts** provided on the drawing that state the lateral distance between any tree and the \"- OHE -\" line. While there is a graphic scale provided in the bottom right corner (\"SCALE IN FEET (1\"=20'-0\")\"), there is no stated numerical dimension indicating the clearance distance."}]}
