ions:\n\n*   **Does this profile sheet show any overhead electric conductor elevations, lines, or clearance dimensions?**\n    No. The profile view (labeled \"Wtr-Ln-A\") only shows \"Existing Ground,\" \"Proposed Surface,\" a \"Property Line\" marker, and subsurface water utility infrastructure. There are no overhead lines, conductor elevations, or clearance dimensions depicted above the ground surface lines. Additionally, the Legend only lists \"Proposed Underground Electric\" and does not include an entry for overhead electric lines.\n\n*   **Are utility lines other than water/wastewater shown on the profile?**\n    No. The profile specifically details a water line (\"Wtr-Ln-A\"). The utilities shown in the profile section are restricted to water infrastructure, specifically:\n    *   \"Existing 8\\\" AC Pipe to be Replaced with DI Pipe.\"\n    *   Proposed water line segments labeled \"42.0 LF 8\\\" DI @ 0.00%\", \"5.0 LF 6\\\" DI @ 0.00%\", and \"12.0 LF 6\\\" DI @ 0.00%\".\n    *   Water line appurtenances such as an \"8\\\"x8\\\" Reducer\" and a vertical assembly leading to a vault (\"6\\\" Fire Demand Meter in 8' x 12' Vault...\").\n    There are no storm drains, gas lines, underground electric, or telecommunications lines crossing or running parallel within the profile view itself."}]}
