{"level":30,"time":1778188522980,"pid":122,"hostname":"e70bc6df-98e","step":"review-runs","item":"13.md","index":5,"runIndex":"run-2","type":"assistant","message":{"id":"gen_01KR24PPQZFB26TNWPSGN1Z5YY","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"The grading plan shows contours, spot elevations, and drainage flow directions but the vision check indicated that drainage direction around transformer pads is not clearly shown with arrows. Let me now compile my findings.\n\nBased on my comprehensive review:\n\n## Research Summary - NOT FOUND / COULD NOT VERIFY:\n1. **No transformer pad detail sheets** - No AE Design-approved transformer pad specifications in construction details (Sheets 22-27)\n2. **No transformer pad dimensions** - Electrical plan shows pads but does not label their sizes\n3. **No clearance dimensions** - No specific measurements shown for clearances from transformer pads to buildings, utilities, or other features\n4. **No access door orientation** - Cannot determine which side is the access door for clearance calculations\n5. **No transformer type specification** - Cannot determine if oil-filled or dry-type\n6. **No bollard details** - No bollard specifications or locations shown for pads near parking\n7. **No transformer easements** - No transformer easements depicted on site plan\n8. **No root barrier details** - No root barrier specifications shown for trees near electrical equipment\n9. **No utility coordination drawings** - No profile/cross-section drawings showing clearances from overhead or underground utilities\n10. **No vertical clearance details** - No cross-sections showing overhead clearances above transformer locations\n11. **No tree utility-compatibility documentation** - Tree list exists but not cross-referenced to ECM Appendix F\n12. **No AE Design approval documents** - No ESPA, written approvals, or AE Design coordination letters\n\n## Key DEFICIENCIES Identified:\n\n**FAIL items:**\n1. **EL-13.1** - Pads appear to be 3-5 feet from buildings, less than required 5 feet\n2. **EL-13.10** - Pads appear to be less than 10 feet from buildings\n3. **EL-13.33** - Pads appear to be located within easement corridors (PUE areas visible from vision check)\n\n\n4. **EL-13.34** - Pads situated in easement areas without documented AE Design approval. **EL-13.35** - Transformer easements not depicted on any plan sheets. **EL-13.37** - Transformer pad detail sheets missing; cannot verify specifications. **EL-13.38** - All 5 pads positioned within 4 feet of parking or circulation areas with no bollard protection shown.\n\n**NOT-VERIFIABLE items:**\n1. **EL-13.2** - Retaining wall clearances cannot be confirmed as walls are present but distances remain undocumented. **EL-13.3** - Fence clearances indeterminate since access door orientation is not indicated.\n2. **EL-13.4** - Reduced clearance documentation lacks AE approvals. **EL-13.5** - Balcony and overhang clearances missing dimensional data. **EL-13.6** - Window and door clearances cannot be assessed without building elevations or dimensions. **EL-13.7** - Sidewalk clearances lack specific measurements. **EL-13.8** - Fire exit stairwell clearances unverifiable without floor plans. **EL-13.9** - Fire escape clearances cannot be confirmed without building elevations. **EL-13.12** - Fire hydrant clearances show no dimensions. **EL-13.13** - Tree utility-compatibility unconfirmed as trees are present but not identified as utility-compatible species. **EL-13.14** - Vegetation clearance from access door cannot be verified without access door orientation shown. **EL-13.15** - Root barriers lack detail documentation for trees within 20 feet. **EL-13.16** through **EL-13.18** - Dumpster, bike rack, and light pole clearances all missing specific measurements. **EL-13.19** - Fire lane clearances show no measurements from electrical plan. **EL-13.20** through **EL-13.23** - Transformer pad spacing, water line, wastewater line, and storm drain clearances all lack dimensional documentation. **EL-13.25** - Underground utility clearances do not document required 12-inch separation. **EL-13.26** - Cross-section drawings for vertical utilities not provided. **EL-13.27** and **EL-13.28** - Overhead line clearances (sky-to-ground and 15-foot radius) show no dimensions. **EL-13.31** - Cross-section drawings for access paths are missing. **EL-13.32** - Drainage direction questionable in some areas and transformer type unspecified. **EL-13.36** - Electrical routing on private property shows unclear relationship to property lines. **EL-13.39** - Overhead facilities documentation incomplete.\n\nSeveral items are not applicable: **EL-13.11** and **EL-13.29** show no niche configuration, **EL-13.24** has no gas service shown, and **EL-13.30** shows no niche service proposed.","signature":""}],"model":"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001","stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":0},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"753eb9f1-6b81-4b4f-8a9b-68520af22dec","uuid":"170d002c-8ec3-44a9-9954-a7836ccb1cf5"}
