ure specifications relative to transformer pads are not provided.","reasoning":"Applicability is confirmed (gas service present), but specific clearance measurements and pressure specifications needed for compliance are not documented, making this unverifiable.","tools_used":[]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-13.25","status":"not-verifiable","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.5.A"],"applicableAreas":["Transformer pad locations relative to all underground utilities"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":21},{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":11},{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":12}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"While utility lines are shown on various sheets, no clearance dimensions are provided between transformer pads and underground utilities. The required 12-inch minimum horizontal and vertical separation (outside diameter to outside diameter) from other underground utilities cannot be verified.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Multiple utility types are shown on plan sheets but no labeled clearance distances between transformer pads and underground utilities are provided.","reasoning":"Applicability is confirmed (utilities are present), but specific clearance measurements required by code are not provided, making compliance unverifiable.","tools_used":[]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-13.26","status":"not-verifiable","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.5.B"],"applicableAreas":["Transformer pad locations relative to other utility lines and building infrastructure"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":21},{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":11},{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":19}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Utility and grading plans do not provide documentation showing whether transformer pads are placed over or under other utility lines, or whether customer buildings, foundations, or structures are installed over AE underground facilities. Compliance with this prohibition cannot be verified.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Plans show general layout of utilities and transformer pads but do not include notes or documentation addressing whether utilities or structures cross or overlap.","reasoning":"Cross-utility or cross-structure conflicts would likely be documented with notes if present, and their absence does not constitute verification of compliance. This remains unverifiable without explicit documentation.","tools_used":[]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-13.27","status":"not-verifiable","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.3"],"applicableAreas":["Transformer pad locations relative to overhead distribution line conductors"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":21},{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":31}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Overhead electric line locations are shown on landscape plan (Sheet 31) as 'Overhead Electric', but specific clearance dimensions (7.5-foot horizontal sky-to-ground clearance) from transformer pads to overhead distribution line conductors are not provided. Compliance cannot be verified.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Overhead lines are indicated on landscape plan, but no measured clearances between overhead conductors and transformer pads are labeled.","reasoning":"Applicability is confirmed (overhead lines are present), but specific clearance measurements from transformer pad locations to overhead conductors are not provided, making compliance unverifiable.","tools_used":[]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-13.28","status":"not-verifiable","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.3"],"applicableAreas":["Transformer pad locations relative to overhead distribution primary and neutral conductors"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":21},{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":31}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Overhead electric lines are noted on landscape plan but the specific 15-foot radius clearance from overhead distribution primary and neutral conductors (measured from conductors, not pole centerline) is not dimensioned on any sheet. Compliance cannot be verified.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Overhead lines are indicated on landscape plan, but no labeled 15-foot radius clearance zones or measurements are shown relative to transformer pad locations.","reasoning":"Applicability is confirmed (overhead lines are present), but the specific 15-foot radius clearance requirement is not documented on the plans, making compliance unverifiable.","tools_used":[]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-13.29","status":"n/a","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.4 Table 1.10.4 footnote 3"],"applicableAreas":[],"sheetReferences":[],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"No niche service (transformer equipment within building footprint, accessible from outside) is indicated on the site plans. Transformer pads are shown in exterior pad-mounted configuration only. This requirement does not apply to this project.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Site plan and electrical plan show transformer pads in standard exterior locations, with no indication of niche or enclosed service configuration.","reasoning":"Applicability requires niche service configuration, which is not proposed on this project. The requirement is not applicable.","tools_used":["mcp__conductor_tools__vision_check"]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-13.30","status":"n/a","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.4 Table 1.10.4 footnote 3"],"applicableAreas":[],"sheetReferences":[],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"No niche service installation is proposed on this project. Transformer pads are shown in standard exterior pad-mounted configuration only. Fire wall ratings and ventilation specifications for niches do not apply.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Plans show only exterior pad-mounted transformer configurations, not niche installations.","reasoning":"This requirement only applies to niche service installations, which are not proposed. The requirement is not applicable.","tools_used":[]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-13.31","status":"fail","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.3"],"applicableAreas":["All transformer pad locations"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":21},{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":9},{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":11}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Cross-section drawings showing vertical clearances in access paths with overhead structures, parking garages, enclosed areas, or niche configurations are not provided. Without these drawings, compliance with vertical clearance requirements cannot be demonstrated.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Electrical and site plans show transformer pad locations in plan view only. No cross-section or profile drawings are provided that would demonstrate vertical clearances from ground to overhead structures or through any enclosed access paths.","reasoning":"The regulatory requirement (as required by AE Design per UCM 1.10.3) specifically requires cross-section drawings for this demonstration. Their absence constitutes failure to meet the documentation requirement.","tools_used":[]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-13.32","status":"not-verifiable","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.4 Table 1.10.4 footnote 1"],"applicableAreas":["Transformer pad locations if oil-filled equipment is proposed"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":11},{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":21}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Transformer equipment type (oil-filled vs. dry-type) is not specified on the electrical plan (Sheet 21). Grading plan (Sheet 11) does not show specific drainage direction around transformer pad locations. If oil-filled equipment is specified, drainage must flow away from building; this cannot be verified due to missing equipment type specification and drainage documentation.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Electrical plan does not identify transformer equipment type, and grading plan does not show drainage direction around transformer pads with specific callouts.","reasoning":"Applicability depends on equipment type (oil-filled vs. dry-type), which is not specified. Compliance depends on grading documentation that is not provided. Both applicability and compliance are unverifiable.","tools_used":[]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-13.33","status":"not-verifiable","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.4 Table 1.10.4 footnote 4"],"applicableAreas":["All transformer pad locations"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":21},{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":9},{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":2}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Site plan and plat do not include specific notes confirming that transformer pads are located 100% on private property (not straddling property lines or in public right-of-way). Property boundaries are shown, but no specific callouts verify transformer pad location relative to property lines.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Plans show property boundaries and transformer pad locations in plan view, but do not include annotations confirming that all transformer pads are entirely within private property.","reasoning":"While property boundaries are visible, the requirement for explicit confirmation that transformer pads are 100% on private property is not documented with specific callouts or notes, making compliance unverifiable.","tools_used":[]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-13.34","status":"not-verifiable","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.4 Table 1.10.4 footnote 4"],"applicableAreas":["Transformer pad locations relative to easements"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":21},{"documentId":