 document this requirement.","tools_used":[]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-13.36","status":"not-verifiable","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.4 Table 1.10.4 footnote 4"],"applicableAreas":["Electrical service routing from transformer to meter"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":21},{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":9}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Electrical plan (Sheet 21) shows underground electrical line routing and transformer pad locations, but no specific notes or documentation confirm that electrical routing from transformer to meters is 100% on private property, not crossing public right-of-way. Compliance cannot be verified.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Electrical plan shows general routing of underground lines and transformer/meter locations but does not include specific annotations confirming that all routing from transformer to meter is entirely on private property.","reasoning":"The requirement for explicit confirmation that electrical routing is 100% on private property is not documented with specific callouts or notes, making compliance unverifiable.","tools_used":[]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-13.37","status":"fail","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.5.2.6","UCM § 1.18.0"],"applicableAreas":["All transformer pad locations"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":21},{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":9},{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":22},{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":23},{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":24},{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":25}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Transformer pad locations are shown on electrical plan (Sheet 21) and site plan (Sheet 9), but no detail sheets are provided showing transformer pad dimensions or specifications. No AE Design-approved transformer pad detail sheets matching the specified service type (single-phase or three-phase) are included in the plan set. Service type is not documented.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Vision check confirmed that transformer pad drawings show only location labels without dimensional callouts, and detail sheets 22-25 examined do not contain transformer pad specifications or standard details.","reasoning":"UCM § 1.5.2.6 and § 1.18.0 require transformer pad details from AE Design showing dimensions for the specified service type. Their absence from the construction details sheets constitutes failure to provide required specifications.","tools_used":["mcp__conductor_tools__vision_check"]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-13.38","status":"not-verifiable","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.4 Table 1.10.4"],"applicableAreas":["Transformer pad locations within 4 feet of parking areas or vehicle routes"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":21},{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":9},{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":22}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Site plan (Sheet 9) shows parking layout and transformer pad locations, but no clearance dimensions are provided showing whether transformer pads are within 4 feet of parking areas. If within this distance, 4-inch minimum diameter galvanized rigid metal bollards with proper spacing per AE Design details are not shown. Bollard specifications cannot be verified.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Site plan shows parking areas and transformer pads but no measured clearance distances between them are provided, and no bollard details are shown on construction detail sheets.","reasoning":"Applicability depends on transformer pads being within 4 feet of parking, which cannot be determined without clearance measurements. If applicable, bollard requirements cannot be verified from the plans.","tools_used":[]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-13.39","status":"not-verifiable","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.3"],"applicableAreas":["Transformer pad locations relative to overhead distribution facilities"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":21},{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":31},{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":9}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Overhead electric lines are noted on landscape plan (Sheet 31) as 'Overhead Electric'. Site plan (Sheet 9) shows various site features including light poles, structures, and antenna mounts. However, no specific documentation confirms whether customer facilities (buildings, parking garages, light poles, signs, antennas, tanks) are installed under or over Austin Energy overhead distribution facilities. Compliance cannot be verified.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Overhead lines are indicated on landscape plan, and site features are shown on site plan, but no specific annotations or documentation address whether any customer structures are positioned under overhead distribution facilities.","reasoning":"The requirement would typically be addressed with specific notes if overhead conflicts existed. Absence of such documentation does not constitute verification; it remains unverifiable without explicit confirmation.","tools_used":[]}}]},"fast_mode_state":"off","uuid":"5e482fc1-2d2d-46e5-abc7-80277bc4be01"}
