y:\n\n**1. Measurement from OHE line to nearest proposed trees:**\nBecause this is a digital image, a precise physical measurement using an architectural scale ruler (1\" = 20'-0\") cannot be applied directly to the screen. However, utilizing the graphical bar scale provided in the bottom right corner (labeled \"0\", \"10\", \"20\", \"50\"), we can estimate the distance visually.\n\nLooking at the southern boundary line labeled \"**- OHE -**\" and the proposed tree symbols placed immediately adjacent to its north (specifically observing the trees in the bottom right/southeast section of the plan near the \"**H.7**\" tag):\n*   The visual distance from the OHE line to the center point (trunk location) of the nearest adjacent tree symbols appears to be approximately **3 to 5 feet**. This is estimated by comparing that gap to the \"0\" to \"10\" foot segment on the graphical bar scale; the gap appears to be roughly one-third to one-half of that 10-foot segment.\n\n**2. Explicit dimension lines or clearance measurements:**\nA thorough review of the southern property boundary area reveals that **there are no dimension lines, measurement callouts, or text notes** shown indicating a specific clearance distance between the OHE line and the proposed trees."}]}
{"level":30,"time":1778188537908,"pid":122,"hostname":"e70bc6df-98e","step":"review-runs","item":"1.md","index":3,"runIndex":"run-1","type":"assistant","message":{"id":"gen_01KR24QD4K09BSY42ZF08WES2K","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Good. So Sheet 9 shows:\n- 5-foot electric easements on the eastern and southern boundaries\n- Overhead electric lines (OHE) labeled\n- Buildings and driveways appear to maintain clearance from the easement boundaries\n\nBut the question remains: are there transmission structures/lines on or adjacent to the site? From the general notes, there appear to be transmission easements. Let me check if there's a utility or electrical plan that shows the transmission easement locations more clearly.\n\nActually, looking back at the facts.md, I don't see any mention of a transmission easement being documented. The facts.md shows several recorded easements (wastewater, drainage, utility) but doesn't explicitly mention transmission. However, the general notes on Sheet 3 clearly reference transmission structures and easements.\n\nLet me search for any document showing transmission easements or check if there's a utility easement plan (which might show both distribution and transmission).\n\nActually, I think I need to be more systematic. Let me create a summary of what I've found so far about the key applicability factors:\n\nAPPLICABILITY ASSESSMENT:\n1. **Overhead Electric Distribution Lines: YES** - exist along western boundary (Valley View Road) and southern boundary per existing survey\n2. **Electric Poles: YES** - shown on existing survey at northwest and southwest corners\n3. **Electric Easements: YES** - 5-foot electric easements shown on site plan; possibly transmission easements per general notes\n4. **Proposed Buildings: YES** - 8 buildings proposed  \n5. **Proposed Driveways/Parking: YES** - parking and internal driveways shown\n6. **Transmission Lines/Structures: UNCLEAR** - General notes reference transmission structures and 25-foot clearances, but not clearly shown on site plans\n\nGiven this applicability, many of the checklist items WILL apply. The issue is whether the site plan adequately documents the clearances.\n\nNow let me systematically go through the checklist items and evaluate each one.\n\n\nI should also check the landscape plan to see if any trees are being planted near the overhead lines, since EL-1.37 specifically addresses vegetation management in relation to electric infrastructure.","signature":""}],"model":"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001","stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":0},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"f7510649-3f32-4a6d-b604-08af9177b220","uuid":"ea36726c-3b0b-4e89-b155-771ac4760b3f"}
