{"level":30,"time":1778188538542,"pid":122,"hostname":"e70bc6df-98e","step":"review-runs","item":"2.md","index":4,"runIndex":"run-2","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01LucaQfgjGXFbJZF5CDPNPa","type":"tool_result","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Yes, there are notes from Austin Energy on Sheet 3 regarding clearances required for trees from electric facilities and transmission structures. \n\nSpecifically, the following clearance distances are mentioned:\n\n**1. Transmission Structures (25 feet):**\nUnder the **Electric Transmission Notes** section, Note 1 specifies a 25-foot clearance for planting trees:\n> \"1. No trees shall be planted within the transmission easement. No trees shall be planted within 25 feet of the base of the transmission structure. Vehicular access for Austin Energy trucks and equipment is always to be maintained within the easement. Austin Energy will not be responsible for damage and/or removal of vegetation within the easement.\"\n\n**2. Overhead Electric Facilities (10 feet):**\nUnder the **Electric Notes** section, Note 3 specifies a 10-foot clearance for initial tree pruning and removal from the center line of proposed facilities:\n> \"3. The owner shall be responsible for installation of temporary erosion control, revegetation and tree protection. In addition, the owner shall be responsible for any initial tree pruning and tree removal that is within ten feet of the center line of the proposed overhead electric facilities designed to provide electric service to this project. The owner shall include Austin Energy's work within the limits of construction for this project.\" *(Note: This same text is also repeated in an unnumbered paragraph located below the Fire Department notes section).*"}]}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"df902855-f209-47f1-9270-a32412d9566b","uuid":"5b1e4742-c8a1-4461-8822-82f1f424421d","tool_use_result":[{"type":"text","text":"Yes, there are notes from Austin Energy on Sheet 3 regarding clearances required for trees from electric facilities and transmission structures. \n\nSpecifically, the following clearance distances are mentioned:\n\n**1. Transmission Structures (25 feet):**\nUnder the **Electric Transmission Notes** section, Note 1 specifies a 25-foot clearance for planting trees:\n> \"1. No trees shall be planted within the transmission easement. No trees shall be planted within 25 feet of the base of the transmission structure. Vehicular access for Austin Energy trucks and equipment is always to be maintained within the easement. Austin Energy will not be responsible for damage and/or removal of vegetation within the easement.\"\n\n**2. Overhead Electric Facilities (10 feet):**\nUnder the **Electric Notes** section, Note 3 specifies a 10-foot clearance for initial tree pruning and removal from the center line of proposed facilities:\n> \"3. The owner shall be responsible for installation of temporary erosion control, revegetation and tree protection. In addition, the owner shall be responsible for any initial tree pruning and tree removal that is within ten feet of the center line of the proposed overhead electric facilities designed to provide electric service to this project. The owner shall include Austin Energy's work within the limits of construction for this project.\" *(Note: This same text is also repeated in an unnumbered paragraph located below the Fire Department notes section).*"}]}
