{"level":30,"time":1778188539940,"pid":122,"hostname":"e70bc6df-98e","step":"review-runs","item":"2.md","index":1,"runIndex":"run-1","type":"assistant","message":{"id":"gen_01KR24QGRGAKE1WXC817S94YF8","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"The plat blocks don't have the detailed drawing content. Let me check the detailed vision of the site plan to identify the specific trees near the OHE line and get more information about the utilities.\n\nBased on what I've learned so far:\n1. There IS overhead electric (OHE) infrastructure on the site along the southern boundary\n2. There are mitigation trees (marked \"M\") near the OHE line in the southeast corner\n3. The specific species of these mitigation trees are not clearly identified on the landscape plan\n\nI need to:\n1. Determine if these trees are Cedar Elm, Live Oak, Texas Mountain Laurel, or Mexican Redbud (the proposed trees)\n2. Check their mature heights against ECM Appendix F\n3. Check their utility-compatibility status\n\nNow let me look for any supplementary documents that might have utility information or communications from Austin Energy. Also, I should look at the landscape details sheet to see if there are any specific callouts about tree placement near utilities.","signature":""}],"model":"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001","stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":0},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"9d122776-20ac-46ff-b558-35791e0f03e5","uuid":"f09bf076-4cb1-484d-9ec5-5b35746503fd"}
