{"level":30,"time":1778188566206,"pid":122,"hostname":"e70bc6df-98e","step":"review-runs","item":"13.md","index":2,"runIndex":"run-1","type":"assistant","message":{"id":"gen_01KR24RBFJGJ1JJZ1800J6R9B0","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Now I have enough information to complete the review. Let me compile all findings into the structured output format. I've gathered:\n\n1. **Transformer Pads:** 5 locations identified on Sheet 21\n2. **Clearances:** NO dimensions shown for:\n   - Buildings/structures\n   - Underground utilities (water, wastewater, storm drain)\n   - Overhead distribution lines\n   - Adjacent features (fire hydrants, vehicles, etc.)\n\n3. **Property Location:** All pads appear to be on private property (PASS for EL-13.33)\n\n4. **Transformer Easements:** NOT shown (FAIL for EL-13.35)\n\n5. **AE Design Specifications:** NOT provided - no pad dimension details, no bollard specifications (FAIL for EL-13.37)\n\n6. **Prohibited Easements:** One pad may be in drainage easement (NOT-VERIFIABLE for EL-13.34)\n\n7. **Cross-Sections:** NO cross-sections showing vertical clearances (FAIL for EL-13.31)\n\n8. **Overhead Lines:** Present but clearances not documented (FAIL for EL-13.27 and EL-13.28)\n\n9. **Underground Utilities:** Present throughout but clearances not documented (FAIL for EL-13.21, 13.22, 13.23, 13.25)\n\nLet me now generate the complete structured findings output for all 39 checklist items.","signature":""}],"model":"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001","stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":0},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"adc7a674-5884-4de3-afe6-da189845114c","uuid":"74c90880-f397-4905-9ec5-9899e57d4ec9"}
{"level":30,"time":1778188566724,"pid":122,"hostname":"e70bc6df-98e","step":"review-runs","item":"2.md","index":4,"runIndex":"run-2","type":"assistant","message":{"id":"gen_01KR24QMR78EYNWHGS54FEZG3X","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Let me think through what I've found so far:\n\n1. **Applicability**: The project has overhead electric (OHE) infrastructure shown on both the site plan and landscape plan. The vision check revealed:\n   - OHE lines run along the southern boundary\n   - Trees are proposed at 5-15 feet from the OHE line\n   - Multiple tree species are proposed: Cedar Elm, Live Oak, Mexican Redbud, Texas Mountain Laurel\n\n2. **Key Findings from Research**:\n   - Sheet 3 notes mention 25-foot clearance for transmission structures and 10-foot clearance for overhead electric facilities\n   - However, the grouping guidance references UCM § 1.10.10.4 which specifies:\n     - 15 feet lateral distance for non-utility-compatible trees from distribution conductors\n     - 50 feet for transmission conductors\n     - 25 feet for large trees (40+ ft mature height) from distribution\n   - The trees planted are identified as:\n     - Cedar Elm (100 gal.) - need to check if UC and mature height\n     - Live Oak (100 gal.) - need to check if UC and mature height  \n     - Mexican Redbud (45 gal.) - need to check if UC and mature height\n     - Texas Mountain Laurel (45 gal.) - need to check if UC and mature height\n\n3. **Critical Issues I've Identified**:\n   - Trees are shown on the landscape plan (Sheet 31) near the OHE but:\n     - The trees are only labeled as \"M\" (mitigation trees) or other functional categories\n     - The specific species are not identified on the landscape plan itself\n     - You must refer to Sheet 35 to find out which species each tree is\n   - The landscape plan shows OHE infrastructure but doesn't dimensionally verify clearances from the specific outside conductors\n   - The plan notes in Block 5 of Sheet 31 only refer to landscape categories (SY, PL, P, M) but don't indicate which species corresponds to each symbol shown\n   \n4. Several gaps need addressing: I don't see verification that the proposed species are utility-compatible per ECM Appendix F, nor dimensional confirmation that trees maintain the required 15-foot clearance from distribution lines. The plans don't clearly establish whether these are distribution or transmission facilities, though the voltage and easement descriptions suggest distribution. The plant schedule shows quantities and container sizes but lacks assessment against UCM § 1.10.10.4 requirements. I need to evaluate each checklist item systematically, starting with whether non-utility-compatible trees are positioned within 15 feet of distribution conductors.\n\n**EL-2.1**: The landscape plan shows trees 5-15 feet from overhead electric facilities but doesn't identify species or document their UC status. Since the plant schedule on Sheet 35 lists species without UC verification, and there's no clear mapping of which trees fall within the critical 15-foot zone, this is **NOT-VERIFIABLE**.\n\n**EL-2.2**: The easement descriptions (5-foot electric easements) and site notes indicate distribution lines rather than transmission facilities, so this criterion is **N/A**.\n\n**EL-2.3**: Cedar Elm and Live Oak appear on the plant schedule, but I need their mature heights from ECM Appendix F to determine if they exceed 40 feet. If they're positioned in the 15-25 foot zone from distribution lines, this would be **FAIL** or **NOT-VERIFIABLE** depending on their actual location and height potential.\n\n**EL-2.4**: With distribution lines only, this transmission-related criterion is **N/A**.\n\n**EL-2.5**: No transmission easement exists on the site based on easement documentation. **N/A**\n\n**EL-2.6**: Poles aren't dimensioned on the plan—only the overhead electric line is shown. **NOT-VERIFIABLE**\n\n**EL-2.7**: Sheet 21 shows transformers but doesn't dimension them relative to the landscape plan. **NOT-VERIFIABLE**\n\n**EL-2.8**: Underground utilities appear on the Site Plan without clear spatial relationship to tree locations. **NOT-VERIFIABLE**\n\n**EL-2.9**: No root barrier notes appear on the landscape plan for trees within 20 feet of underground equipment. **FAIL** or **NOT-VERIFIABLE**\n\n**EL-2.10**: The plant schedule identifies species on Sheet 35, but the landscape plan itself uses only functional categories without species labels.\n\n**EL-2.11**: Mature heights aren't explicitly noted, and large trees aren't called out separately on the landscape plan, making verification difficult.\n\n**EL-2.12** and **EL-2.13**: No clearance dimensions are shown on the landscape plan. **N/A**\n\n**EL-2.14**: Trees aren't positioned relative to the overhead electric line on the landscape plan.\n\nTrees do appear on the landscape plan alongside the OHE, and they're visible in proximity to it. **PASS**\n\n**EL-2.15**: There's no documentation of Austin Energy approval for trees placed within utility easements. **FAIL**\n\nNow I need to determine whether these are distribution or transmission lines. The easements documented are 5' electric easements and a 7.5' public utility easement. Distribution systems typically operate below 60kV (Austin's standard is 12.47kV and 34.5kV), while transmission systems operate at 60kV or higher (Austin uses 69kV).\n\nThe 5-foot easement width strongly indicates distribution infrastructure rather than transmission, which would require much larger corridors of 30-100+ feet. This means EL-2.2, EL-2.4, and EL-2.5 don't apply here.\n\nThere's a discrepancy I should note: the vision tool identified the landscape plan as Sheet 28 of 35, though the documentation references Sheet 31. The content itself was correctly identified as the landscape plan showing trees and OHE lines, so I'll proceed with the analysis while noting this sheet numbering difference.\n\nThe proposed plantings include Cedar Elm (10), Live Oak (2), Mexican Redbud (6), and Texas Mountain Laurel (2). While the plant schedule appears on Sheet 35, the landscape plan itself lacks species labels. The clearance requirements from Sheet 3 specify 25 feet for transmission structures and 10 feet for overhead electric facilities. Under UCM § 1.10.10.4, distribution lines allow trees under 15 feet anywhere, trees 15-25 feet in certain zones, and all trees beyond 25 feet—but transmission lines restrict to only utility-compatible species within 50 feet. I don't see documented approval from Austin Energy for the tree placement plan. I need to systematically evaluate all 15 items to provide complete status coverage, including those that pass or are not applicable.","signature":""}],"model":"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001","stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":0},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"df902855-f209-47f1-9270-a32412d9566b","uuid":"34a08467-83fb-48d3-a30c-323d867229f6"}
