{"level":30,"time":1778188569439,"pid":122,"hostname":"e70bc6df-98e","step":"review-runs","item":"1.md","index":6,"runIndex":"run-2","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_0181drkEvJyi78fs5WmcsZn9","type":"tool_result","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Based on a visual analysis of Sheet 4 (Existing Conditions Survey), here are the findings regarding utility poles:\n\n**Legend Definitions**\n*   The legend identifies a **\"UTILITY POLE\"** with a symbol consisting of an open circle with a smaller solid dot in the center.\n*   While your prompt asked to look for \"O.H.U.L.\", the legend on this specific sheet indicates overhead lines using a dashed line with the text **\"- OH -\"** labeled as **\"OVERHEAD UTILITY LINE\"**.\n\n**Utility Pole Locations**\n\nYes, utility poles are depicted on the survey. Their locations relative to the site boundaries are as follows:\n\n1.  **Along Valley View Road (Western Boundary):**\n    *   Utility poles are shown located outside the western property line, situated within the Valley View Road area.\n    *   One pole is located near the northwest corner of the property, just west of the property line. An \"- OH -\" line connects to it and runs south along the road, and another \"- OH -\" line branches east onto the property.\n    *   Another pole is located near the southwest corner of the property, also just west of the western property line, connected to the \"- OH -\" line running along the road.\n\n2.  **Elsewhere on the Site:**\n    *   **On-Site:** Yes, there is a utility pole located *within* the property boundaries. An \"- OH -\" line enters the site from the pole near the northwest corner and traverses the northern portion of the property from west to east. Roughly midway along the northern property boundary (labeled \"S63°03'28\\\"E 419.96'\"), there is a utility pole symbol depicted inside the property line. It is situated within an area delineated by a dashed line and labeled exactly as *