nes in standard format\n- Transmission structures mentioned but not clearly depicted on plans\n\nNow I'll evaluate each of the 47 checklist items:"}],"model":"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001","stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":0},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"f7510649-3f32-4a6d-b604-08af9177b220","uuid":"f7ec884f-b700-4b25-b6d6-e53ba1c51863"}
{"level":30,"time":1778188593526,"pid":122,"hostname":"e70bc6df-98e","step":"review-runs","item":"2.md","index":1,"runIndex":"run-1","type":"assistant","message":{"id":"gen_01KR24S6KJMCWVE6GC85MZW0Z5","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Excellent! This is very important. The vision checks reveal:\n\n1. The mitigation trees in the southeast corner are NOT identified by species - they're only labeled \"M\" (mitigation tree)\n2. There are NO clearance dimensions or notes on the electrical plan showing distances from trees to OHE lines\n3. No documentation of whether clearances are measured from the conductor or from poles\n\nThis is highly problematic. According to the checklist items:\n- EL-2.10: \"Plant legend or plant schedule does not identify species of trees proposed near electric facilities\" - FAIL (trees are only labeled \"M\", not by species)\n- EL-2.12: \"Tree clearances measured from utility pole centerline or structure instead of from outer electric conductor\" - NOT-VERIFIABLE (no clearances are shown at all)\n- EL-2.13: Similar issue - \"Tree clearances measured from tree canopy instead of from tree trunk\" - NOT-VERIFIABLE\n- EL-2.14: \"Trees not shown on landscape plan in relation to overhead electric facilities, preventing clearance verification\" - This appears to be a fail since the trees are shown but with no ability to verify clearances\n\nNow let me get more information by checking if there's any plant schedule that cross-references the mitigation trees to specific species, or if there are any notes on the landscape plan that explain which species are the mitigation trees.","signature":""}],"model":"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001","stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":0},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"9d122776-20ac-46ff-b558-35791e0f03e5","uuid":"294da150-ad72-43af-bb95-ab819a6a2fc8"}
