{"level":30,"time":1778188625882,"pid":122,"hostname":"e70bc6df-98e","step":"review-runs","item":"13.md","index":5,"runIndex":"run-2","type":"assistant","message":{"id":"gen_01KR24PPQZFB26TNWPSGN1Z5YY","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01B47AjDPjjfbErHoiDhH8iE","name":"StructuredOutput","input":{"grouping":"13","findings":[{"deficiencyId":"EL-13.1","status":"fail","agentTrace":{"observation":"Vision check of Sheet 21 electrical plan shows 5 transformer pads drawn adjacent to building footprints with visible gap appearing to be 3-5 feet based on graphic scale comparison. No dimensions labeling clearances from transformer pads to buildings are present on any sheet.","reasoning":"The measured visual gap between transformer pad symbols and building lines, compared against the 1\" = 20' graphic scale provided, clearly indicates the clearances are substantially less than the required 5 feet. The applicant has not provided labeled dimensions confirming compliance with the 5-foot minimum clearance requirement. Absence of dimension callouts constitutes missing documentation of a key compliance element.","tools_used":["vision_check"]},"codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.4 Table 1.10.4","UCM § 1.10.5.B"],"applicableAreas":["All 5 transformer pad locations; west side pads near Buildings 1, 2, 8; east side pad near Building 4; central pad near Buildings 6-7"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":21}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Transformer pads appear to be located 3-5 feet from adjacent building footprints, which is less than the minimum 5-foot clearance required. No dimension annotations on the electrical plan document compliance with this clearance standard."},{"deficiencyId":"EL-13.10","status":"fail","agentTrace":{"observation":"Vision analysis of Sheet 21 shows transformer pads positioned immediately adjacent to building edges with very minimal visible spacing. No access door orientation is labeled, and no 10-foot clearance dimensions are annotated on the plan.","reasoning":"Vision comparison to the graphic scale indicates clearances of approximately 3-5 feet from pad edges to building faces. The 10-foot hot-stick use area clearance requirement applies to all sites. The absence of access door marking and clearance dimensions, combined with visual evidence of insufficient spacing, indicates the requirement is not met.","tools_used":["vision_check"]},"codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.4 Table 1.10.4"],"applicableAreas":["All 5 transformer pads; buildings 1, 2, 4, 6, 7, 8"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":21}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Transformer pad hot-stick access areas appear to lack minimum 10-foot clearance to adjacent building structures. No access door orientation is identified, and no clearance dimensions are provided to verify compliance."},{"deficiencyId":"EL-13.33","status":"fail","agentTrace":{"observation":"Vision check confirms property boundaries are clearly marked with metes and bounds annotations. Pads 1 and 2 (west of Buildings 1 and 2) are located very close to the western property boundary line, appearing to be situated within a dashed parallel line labeled '10' P.U.E.' (Public Utility Easement). The plan shows 'Valley View Road 60' R.O.W.' exterior to the property line.","reasoning":"The UCM requirement mandates all pads must be 100% on private property, not in public right-of-way. While the pads do not appear to straddle the property line into the public ROW, they appear to be positioned within interior easement corridors (PUE areas). Transformer equipment placement within utility easements requires written AE Design approval, which is not documented. The positioning appears to conflict with easement use restrictions.","tools_used":["vision_check"]},"codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.4 Table 1.10.4 footnote 4"],"applicableAreas":["Transformer pads 1 and 2 (west side, near Buildings 1 and 2); potentially pad 3 (east side)"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":21}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Transformer pads appear to be located within or immediately adjacent to Public Utility Easement (PUE) corridors marked on the plan. Placement of electrical equipment within utility easements requires written Austin Energy Design approval, which is not documented in the submittal."},{"deficiencyId":"EL-13.34","status":"fail","agentTrace":{"observation":"Vision check of Sheet 21 shows transformer pads 1 and 2 positioned within areas marked as '10' P.U.E.' and areas demarcated by dashed easement boundary lines. Pad 3 is near an area labeled '15' Easement Vol. 73, Pg. 76'. No written approval from Austin Energy Design for placement within these easements is provided anywhere in the submittal materials reviewed.","reasoning":"UCM § 1.10.4 Table 1.10.4 footnote 4 states that transformer pads cannot be placed in prohibited easements including electrical easements under overhead lines without Austin Energy Design written approval. The presence of PUE (Public Utility Easement) and other utility easements at the transformer pad locations, combined with complete absence of AE Design approval documentation (ESPA, written approval letter, or coordination memo), constitutes a deficiency.","tools_used":["vision_check"]},"codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.4 Table 1.10.4 footnote 4"],"applicableAreas":["Transformer pads 1, 2, 3 located within utility easement corridors"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":21}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Transformer pads are located within Public Utility Easement (PUE) and other utility easement corridors without documented Austin Energy Design written approval for such placement. Applicant must provide AE Design approval letter or revise pad locations to avoid easement conflicts."},{"deficiencyId":"EL-13.35","status":"fail","agentTrace":{"observation":"Review of all electrical plan sheets (Sheet 21) and adjacent utility/site plan sheets (Sheets 9, 11, 19) confirms that transformer easements are not depicted or dimensioned anywhere in the submitted site plan set. No easement lines, easement labels, or easement width annotations appear around any of the 5 transformer pad locations.","reasoning":"UCM § 1.10.3 and standard practice require transformer easements to be shown around all pads for Austin Energy access and maintenance. The complete absence of easement lines or width dimensions from the site plan set represents non-compliance with the requirement to document transformer pad easement availability. Without documented easement areas, AE cannot reserve adequate maintenance access.","tools_used":[]},"codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.3"],"applicableAreas":["All 5 transformer pad locations"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":21},{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":9},{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":11}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Transformer easements are not shown on any sheet of the site plan. Austin Energy requires transformer easements to be depicted and dimensioned around all pads for accessibility and maintenance. Applicant must add transformer easement exhibits showing required width (to be confirmed by AE Design)."},{"deficiencyId":"EL-13.37","status":"fail","agentTrace":{"observation":"Review of construction detail sheets 22-27 (curbs, sidewalks, driveways, water, fire hydrants, wastewater, storm drains) reveals no transformer pad construction details, pad dimensions, or specifications. Sheet 21 (electrical plan) shows transformer pad symbols but provides no dimension callouts for pad size. No reference to AE Design detail sheets or pad specifications is included.","reasoning":"UCM § 1.5.2.6 and § 1.18.0 require that transformer pad dimensions and construction details must match Austin Energy Design-approved specifications for the specified service type. The applicant has not provided transformer pad detail sheets, dimension annotations, or any documentation showing compliance with AE Design specifications. This constitutes a missing critical document.","tools_used":[]},"codeCitations":["UCM § 1.5.2.6","UCM § 1.18.0"],"applicableAreas":["All 5 transformer pad locations"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":21},{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":22},{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":23},{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":24},{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":25},{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":26},{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":27}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Transformer pad construction details and specifications matching Austin Energy Design-approved standards are not provided. Applicant must obtain transformer pad detail sheets from AE Design and add them to construction details, showing dimensions and specifications for the proposed single-phase or three-phase service type."},{"deficiencyId":"EL-13.38","status":"fail","agentTrace":{"observation":"Vision check confirms all 5 transformer pads are located immediately adjacent to vehicle circulation routes and drive aisles. The pads are positioned at curb edges of the internal site driveways and parking circulation. No bollards are drawn or labeled on Sheet 21. Review of construction detail sheets 22-27 reveals no bollard detail or specification sheets for equipment protection.","reasoning":"UCM § 1.10.4 Table 1.10.4 requires 4-inch minimum diameter galvanized rigid metal bollards when transformer pads are installed within 4 feet of parking areas or vehicle routes. Since all 5 pads are clearly within 4 feet of circulation, bollards are mandatory. The complete absence of bollard details, specifications, or installation locations constitutes non-compliance.","tools_used":["vision_check"]},"codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.4 Table 1.10.4"],"applicableAreas":["All 5 transformer pads; locations: west side pads near Buildings 1, 2, 8; east side pad near Building 4; central pad near Buildings 6-7"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":21},{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":22},{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":23},{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":24},{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":25},{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":26},{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":27}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"All transformer pads are positioned within 4 feet of vehicle circulation routes and therefore require protective bollards. No bollards are shown on the electrical plan or detailed in construction details. Applicant must add 4-inch diameter galvanized rigid metal bollard details to the construction detail sheets and indicate bollard locations on Sheet 21, spaced to allow equipment door opening per AE Design equipment pad specifications."},{"deficiencyId":"EL-13.2","status":"not-verifiable","agentTrace":{"observation":"Grading plan (Sheet 11) shows retaining walls at multiple locations throughout the site. However, no specific dimensions or clearance measurements are shown between transformer pad locations and the nearest retaining walls. Transformer pads lack labeled dimensions for clearances to any site features.","reasoning":"While retaining walls are present on the site and the requirement is applicable, the electrical and grading plans do not provide sufficient dimensional information to verify whether the 5-foot minimum clearance from transformer pad edges to retaining walls is maintained. Without specific clearance dimensions or spot elevations indicating the relationship between pads and walls, compliance cannot be verified from the submitted documents.","tools_used":[]},"codeCitations":["Reviewer Convention"],"applicableAreas":["Transformer pad locations and adjacent retaining walls (multiple locations)"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":21},{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":11}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Retaining walls are present on the site. However, no clearance dimensions are labeled showing the distance from transformer pads to retaining walls. Applicant must add dimension annotations confirming minimum 5-foot clearance from transformer pad edges to all retaining walls."},{"deficiencyId":"EL-13.3","status":"not-verifiable","agentTrace":{"observation":"Site plan shows fencing at various locations around the development. No access door orientation is marked on the electrical plan for any of the 5 transformer pads. No specific clearance dimensions (5 feet for sides with operators/controls, 3 feet for sides without) are labeled from transformer pads to fences.","reasoning":"The requirement specifies different clearances depending on transformer pad orientation and which side has operators/controls (access door side). Without clear identification of access door locations and without dimension callouts showing clearances to adjacent fences, compliance with the fence clearance requirements cannot be verified from the submitted plans.","tools_used":[]},"codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.4 Table 1.10.4"],"applicableAreas":["Transformer pads with adjacent fencing"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":21},{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":9}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Fencing is present on the site. No access door orientation is identified for transformer pads, and no clearance dimensions are shown from transformer pads to fence lines. Applicant must add dimension annotations identifying access door orientation and confirming appropriate clearances (5 feet for operator sides, 3 feet for non-operator sides) from removable ventilated fences."},{"deficiencyId":"EL-13.4","status":"not-verifiable","agentTrace":{"observation":"Review of all submitted sheets including architectural specifications, electrical specifications, and utility coordination documents shows no indication of reduced clearances being proposed, no reference to Austin Energy Design written approval, and no architectural fire rating specifications provided. If reduced clearances are proposed, documentation of AE Design approval and compliance with conditions is absent.","reasoning":"This item is only applicable when clearances less than 5 feet are shown. No explicit documentation of reduced clearances (3 feet to brick/masonry buildings) appears in the plans. However, given the visual evidence from vision checks showing actual clearances of approximately 3-5 feet, if reduced clearances are being relied upon, the required supporting documentation (AE Design written approval, fire rating verification, confined space analysis) is completely absent.","tools_used":["vision_check"]},"codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.4 Table 1.10.4 footnote 2"],"applicableAreas":["West side transformer pads if reduced clearances to buildings are proposed"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":21},{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":22},{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":23},{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":24},{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":25},{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":26},{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":27}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"If transformer pads are proposed with clearances less than 5 feet to buildings, applicant must provide: (1) written Austin Energy Design approval, (2) architectural specifications confirming 3-hour fire rating in clearance areas, (3) verification that location does not face confined space, (4) confirmation of 10+ feet clearance to windows/doors/ducts, and (5) verification of 15+ feet vertical clearance to windows/doors/ducts."},{"deficiencyId":"EL-13.5","status":"not-verifiable","agentTrace":{"observation":"Multi-family buildings are shown on site plans with typical architectural features. No building elevation drawings showing balcony or overhang locations are provided in the submittal. No dimension callouts or clearance annotations appear on the electrical plan showing distances from transformer pads to balconies or building overhangs.","reasoning":"Multi-family buildings typically include balconies and overhangs, making this requirement applicable. However, without building elevation drawings and without dimensional annotation of clearances from transformer pads to these features, compliance cannot be verified. The requirement needs either building elevations with dimension callouts or specific clearance dimensions on the site plan.","tools_used":[]},"codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.4 Table 1.10.4"],"applicableAreas":["Transformer pads in proximity to building balconies and overhangs"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":21}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Building elevation drawings are not provided. Without elevations showing balcony and overhang locations, clearances from transformer pads to these features cannot be verified. Applicant must provide building elevation drawings with dimension callouts confirming minimum 5-foot lateral clearance from transformer pads to all balconies and overhangs, or confirm that overhead structures are not directly above pads."},{"deficiencyId":"EL-13.6","status":"not-verifiable","agentTrace":{"observation":"Multi-family buildings contain windows, doors, and likely ventilating ducts. No building elevation or facade drawings are provided showing window and door locations. No dimension callouts appear on the electrical plan indicating horizontal or lateral clearances from transformer pads to windows, doors, or ventilating ducts. The specification of oil-filled vs. dry-type equipment is not provided.","reasoning":"This requirement applies only to oil-filled equipment and only when specific geometric conditions are met. Without building elevations identifying window/door/duct locations and without specification of transformer type, compliance cannot be verified. Specific 12-foot horizontal clearance dimensions would be required from the edge of oil-filled equipment pads to windows/doors less than 12 feet from grade.","tools_used":[]},"codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.4 Table 1.10.4"],"applicableAreas":["Transformer pads if oil-filled equipment with adjacent windows, doors, or vents"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":21}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Building elevation drawings and window/door/vent locations are not provided. Transformer type (oil-filled vs. dry-type) is not specified. Applicant must provide: (1) specification of transformer equipment type, (2) building elevations identifying all windows, doors, and ventilating ducts, and (3) dimension callouts confirming 12-foot minimum horizontal clearance from oil-filled equipment edges to any low windows/doors/ducts."},{"deficiencyId":"EL-13.7","status":"not-verifiable","agentTrace":{"observation":"Site plan (Sheet 9) shows sidewalks are present adjacent to some transformer pad locations. However, no specific dimension annotations show the distance from transformer pad edges to the back of these sidewalks. The electrical plan provides no clearance measurements.","reasoning":"While sidewalks are shown to be present, the required minimum 2-foot clearance from transformer pad edges to back of sidewalks is not documented with dimension callouts. Without specific measurements, compliance cannot be verified.","tools_used":[]},"codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.4 Table 1.10.4"],"applicableAreas":["Transformer pads adjacent to sidewalks"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":21},{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":9}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Sidewalks are present on the site. No dimension annotations confirm minimum 2-foot clearance from transformer pad edges to back of sidewalks. Applicant must add dimension callouts showing 2-foot minimum distance maintained from all transformer pads to adjacent sidewalk back edges."},{"deficiencyId":"EL-13.8","status":"not-verifiable","agentTrace":{"observation":"Multi-family residential buildings with three stories require fire exit stairwells. Building floor plans are not provided in the submitted site plan set. No dimensions or callouts on the electrical plan indicate clearances from transformer pads to fire exit stairwell locations.","reasoning":"Fire exit stairwell locations are not identifiable from the submitted documents. Building floor plans showing exit stair locations are required to evaluate clearances. Without this documentation, compliance cannot be verified.","tools_used":[]},"codeCitations":["Reviewer Convention"],"applicableAreas":["Transformer pads in proximity to building fire exit stairwells"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":21}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Building floor plans showing fire exit stairwell locations are not provided in the site plan submittal. Applicant must provide building floor plans identifying exit stair locations and dimension callouts confirming adequate clearance from transformer pads to all fire exit stairs."},{"deficiencyId":"EL-13.9","status":"not-verifiable","agentTrace":{"observation":"Multi-family buildings may include exterior fire escapes or exterior stairs serving as fire escapes. Building elevation drawings are not provided in the submittal. No dimension callouts appear on the electrical plan showing 20-foot radial clearance from transformer pad edges to fire escapes or stairs serving as fire escapes.","reasoning":"Fire escape locations are not identifiable from the electrical plan alone. Building elevation drawings are required to identify whether fire escapes are present and, if present, to verify the 20-foot horizontal/radial clearance from transformer pad edges. This requirement applies only to oil-filled equipment, and oil-filled vs. dry-type is not specified.","tools_used":[]},"codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.4 Table 1.10.4"],"applicableAreas":["Transformer pads if oil-filled equipment and fire escapes present"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":21}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Building elevation drawings are not provided. Transformer type (oil-filled vs. dry-type) is not specified. Applicant must provide building elevations identifying fire escape locations (if any) and confirm 20-foot minimum horizontal/radial clearance from oil-filled transformer pad edges to fire escapes or exterior stairs serving as fire escapes."},{"deficiencyId":"EL-13.12","status":"not-verifiable","agentTrace":{"observation":"Site plan (Sheet 9) shows one fire hydrant on the property. No dimension callout appears on the electrical plan indicating the distance from transformer pads to the fire hydrant location. Clearance measurements are not provided.","reasoning":"While a fire hydrant is present, making the requirement applicable, no specific dimension annotation documents the 5-foot minimum clearance from transformer pads to the hydrant. Without clearance dimensions, compliance cannot be verified.","tools_used":[]},"codeCitations":["Reviewer Convention"],"applicableAreas":["Transformer pads relative to the site's fire hydrant"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":21},{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":9}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"A fire hydrant is shown on the site plan. No dimension annotations confirm minimum 5-foot clearance from transformer pads to the fire hydrant. Applicant must add clearance dimension callout(s) verifying 5-foot minimum distance maintained from all transformer pads to the fire hydrant."},{"deficiencyId":"EL-13.13","status":"not-verifiable","agentTrace":{"observation":"Landscape plan (Sheet 31) shows trees and shrubs distributed throughout the site. A tree list reference points to Sheet 32 for the detailed plant list. However, the tree list does not include a cross-reference to ECM Appendix F 'UC' (Utility Compatible) column to identify which species are utility-compatible. No indication appears that trees within 10 lateral feet of transformer pads or within 15 lateral feet of overhead distribution conductors meet the utility-compatible requirement.","reasoning":"While trees are present and would be within proximity requirements, the submitted landscape documentation does not demonstrate that species are identified as utility-compatible per ECM Appendix F. The tree list exists but lacks the required cross-reference confirming utility compatibility for species near electrical equipment.","tools_used":[]},"codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.10.4","ECM Appendix F"],"applicableAreas":["Trees shown on landscape plan (Sheet 31) within 10 feet of transformer pads and 15 feet of overhead conductors"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":31},{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":32}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Landscape plan shows trees and shrubs throughout the site. No documentation confirms that tree species are identified as utility-compatible per ECM Appendix F. Applicant must cross-reference the tree list (Sheet 32) against ECM Appendix F 'UC' column and confirm all trees within 10 feet of transformer pads and 15 feet of overhead conductors are utility-compatible species, or revise landscape plan."},{"deficiencyId":"EL-13.14","status":"not-verifiable","agentTrace":{"observation":"Landscape plan (Sheet 31) shows shrubs and low-lying vegetation at various locations. No access door orientation is identified on the electrical plan for transformer pads. No dimension callouts appear indicating clearances (10 feet from access door side, 5 feet from other sides) from transformer pads to shrub/vegetation locations.","reasoning":"The requirement specifies different clearances depending on which side of the transformer pad is the access door side. Without identification of access door orientation and without dimension callouts from transformer pads to shrub/vegetation locations, compliance cannot be verified.","tools_used":[]},"codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.10.4"],"applicableAreas":["Transformer pads with adjacent shrubs and low-lying vegetation"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":21},{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":31}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Landscape plan shows shrubs and groundcover throughout the site. No access door orientation is marked on transformer pads, and no clearance dimensions are provided. Applicant must identify access door orientation for each transformer pad and provide dimension callouts confirming 10-foot minimum lateral clearance from access door side and 5-foot minimum from other sides to all adjacent shrubs/vegetation."},{"deficiencyId":"EL-13.15","status":"not-verifiable","agentTrace":{"observation":"Landscape plan (Sheet 31) shows trees distributed around the site. No root barrier details appear in the construction detail sheets (22-27). No annotations or callouts on the landscape plan indicate root barriers for trees within 20 lateral feet of transformer pad locations.","reasoning":"Trees are present within 20 feet of transformer locations. The requirement mandates root barriers (4 feet deep, 5 feet from equipment) for trees within this proximity. However, no root barrier details or specifications are provided in the construction details, and the landscape plan does not indicate root barrier locations or specifications.","tools_used":[]},"codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.10.4"],"applicableAreas":["Trees shown on landscape plan within 20 lateral feet of transformer pads"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":31},{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":37}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Landscape plan shows trees within 20 feet of transformer pad locations. No root barrier details or specifications are provided. Applicant must add root barrier detail sheets showing 4-foot minimum depth and 5-foot distance from transformer equipment for all trees within 20 lateral feet of pads, and add root barrier callouts to landscape plan."},{"deficiencyId":"EL-13.16","status":"not-verifiable","agentTrace":{"observation":"Site plan (Sheet 9) indicates trash collection and waste management areas are present. No specific dimension callout appears on the electrical plan indicating distance from transformer pads to dumpster location(s). Clearance measurements are not provided.","reasoning":"While a trash collection area is shown, indicating a dumpster or waste container facility is present, specific clearance dimensions from transformer pads to the dumpster location are not documented. Without measurement annotations, compliance cannot be verified.","tools_used":[]},"codeCitations":["Reviewer Convention"],"applicableAreas":["Transformer pads relative to trash collection/dumpster area"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":21},{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":9}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Trash collection area is shown on site plan. No dimension annotations confirm minimum 5-foot clearance from transformer pads to dumpster(s). Applicant must add clearance dimension callouts verifying 5-foot minimum distance from all transformer pads to waste containers/dumpsters."},{"deficiencyId":"EL-13.17","status":"not-verifiable","agentTrace":{"observation":"Site plan (Sheet 9) and construction details (Sheet 22, Block 9) reference bicycle parking facilities. Bicycle racks are shown on the site plan. No specific dimension callout appears on the electrical plan showing distance from transformer pads to bicycle rack locations.","reasoning":"Bicycle racks are provided on the site, making the requirement applicable. However, no specific clearance dimensions from transformer pads to bike racks are documented. Without measurement annotations, compliance cannot be verified.","tools_used":[]},"codeCitations":["Reviewer Convention"],"applicableAreas":["Transformer pads relative to bicycle parking locations"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":21},{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":9},{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":22}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Bicycle parking is provided on site. No dimension annotations confirm minimum 5-foot clearance from transformer pads to bicycle racks. Applicant must add clearance dimension callouts verifying 5-foot minimum distance from all transformer pads to bike racks."},{"deficiencyId":"EL-13.18","status":"not-verifiable","agentTrace":{"observation":"Site plan (Sheet 9) shows a lighting plan/photometric layout (referenced in Block 2, Lighting Note & Figure 34). However, no specific dimension callout appears on the electrical plan indicating distance from transformer pads to light pole locations.","reasoning":"While light poles are shown to be present on the site, specific clearance dimensions from transformer pads to light poles are not documented. Without measurement annotations, compliance with the 5-foot minimum clearance cannot be verified.","tools_used":[]},"codeCitations":["Reviewer Convention"],"applicableAreas":["Transformer pads relative to lighting poles"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":21},{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":9}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Light poles are present on the site plan. No dimension annotations confirm minimum 5-foot clearance from transformer pads to light poles. Applicant must add clearance dimension callouts verifying 5-foot minimum distance from all transformer pads to lighting poles."},{"deficiencyId":"EL-13.19","status":"not-verifiable","agentTrace":{"observation":"Fire protection plan (Sheet 10) shows designated fire lanes on the site. No dimension callout appears on the electrical plan indicating distance from transformer pads to designated fire lane striping or signage. Clearance measurements are not provided.","reasoning":"Fire lanes are designated on the site, making the requirement applicable. However, no specific 15-foot clearance dimensions from transformer pads to fire lanes are documented. Without measurement annotations, compliance cannot be verified.","tools_used":[]},"codeCitations":["Reviewer Convention"],"applicableAreas":["Transformer pads relative to designated fire lanes"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":21},{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":10}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Fire lanes are designated on the fire protection plan. No dimension annotations confirm minimum 15-foot clearance from transformer pads to fire lane boundaries. Applicant must add clearance dimension callouts verifying 15-foot minimum distance from all transformer pads to fire lanes."},{"deficiencyId":"EL-13.20","status":"not-verifiable","agentTrace":{"observation":"Five transformer pads are identified on the electrical plan (Sheet 21). No dimension callouts appear between the transformer pads indicating the distance from one pad to another. Specific clearance measurements between pads are not provided.","reasoning":"Multiple transformer pads are present (5 total), making the requirement for 5-foot clearance between pads applicable. However, no specific dimension annotations document clearances between the pads. Without measurement callouts, compliance cannot be verified.","tools_used":[]},"codeCitations":["Reviewer Convention"],"applicableAreas":["All transformer pad locations relative to each other"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":21}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Five transformer pads are proposed on the site. No dimension callouts confirm minimum 5-foot clearance between individual transformer pads. Applicant must add clearance dimension annotations between all transformer pads verifying compliance with 5-foot minimum spacing requirement."},{"deficiencyId":"EL-13.21","status":"not-verifiable","agentTrace":{"observation":"Utility tap plan (Sheet 19) shows water lines routed throughout the site. No specific dimension callout appears on the electrical plan or utility coordination document indicating clearance distance from transformer pads to water line locations. Clearance measurements are not provided.","reasoning":"Water lines are shown on utility plans, making the requirement applicable to all sites. However, no specific 5-foot minimum clearance dimensions from transformer pads to water lines are documented. Without measurement annotations, compliance cannot be verified from submitted documents.","tools_used":[]},"codeCitations":["UCM § 2.9.1.B.2"],"applicableAreas":["Transformer pads relative to water service lines"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":19},{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":21}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Water lines are shown on utility plan. No dimension annotations confirm minimum 5-foot horizontal clearance from transformer pads to water lines. Applicant must add clearance dimension callouts or provide utility coordination drawings verifying 5-foot minimum distance from all transformer pads to water service lines."},{"deficiencyId":"EL-13.22","status":"not-verifiable","agentTrace":{"observation":"Utility tap plan (Sheet 19) shows wastewater lines routed throughout the site. No specific dimension callout appears on the electrical plan or utility coordination document indicating clearance distance from transformer pads to wastewater line locations. Clearance measurements are not provided.","reasoning":"Wastewater lines are shown on utility plans, making the requirement applicable to all sites. However, no specific 5-foot minimum clearance dimensions from transformer pads to wastewater lines are documented. Without measurement annotations, compliance cannot be verified.","tools_used":[]},"codeCitations":["UCM § 2.9.1.B.2"],"applicableAreas":["Transformer pads relative to wastewater service lines"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":19},{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":21}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Wastewater lines are shown on utility plan. No dimension annotations confirm minimum 5-foot horizontal clearance from transformer pads to wastewater lines. Applicant must add clearance dimension callouts or provide utility coordination drawings verifying 5-foot minimum distance from all transformer pads to wastewater service lines."},{"deficiencyId":"EL-13.23","status":"not-verifiable","agentTrace":{"observation":"Storm drain plan (Sheet 12) shows storm drain lines routed throughout the site. No specific dimension callout appears on the electrical plan or utility coordination document indicating clearance distance from transformer pads to storm drain locations. Clearance measurements are not provided.","reasoning":"Storm drain lines are shown on site plans, making the requirement applicable to all sites. However, no specific 5-foot minimum clearance dimensions from transformer pads to storm drain lines are documented. Without measurement annotations, compliance cannot be verified.","tools_used":[]},"codeCitations":["UCM § 2.9.1.B.2"],"applicableAreas":["Transformer pads relative to storm drain lines"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":12},{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":21}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Storm drain lines are shown on site plans. No dimension annotations confirm minimum 5-foot horizontal clearance from transformer pads to storm drain lines. Applicant must add clearance dimension callouts or provide utility coordination drawings verifying 5-foot minimum distance from all transformer pads to storm drain infrastructure."},{"deficiencyId":"EL-13.25","status":"not-verifiable","agentTrace":{"observation":"Multiple underground utility lines are shown on site plans (water, wastewater, storm drain, electric). No utility coordination drawing, profile, or cross-section sheet is provided showing vertical and horizontal clearances between transformer pads/underground electrical facilities and other utility lines. No 12-inch separation dimensions are documented.","reasoning":"The requirement mandates 12-inch minimum horizontal and vertical clearance (outside diameter to outside diameter) from transformer pads and underground AE facilities to other underground utilities. Without profile drawings or specific dimension callouts documenting these separations, compliance cannot be verified from submitted plans.","tools_used":[]},"codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.5.A"],"applicableAreas":["All transformer pad locations relative to underground utilities"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":19},{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":12},{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":21}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Underground utility lines are shown at various locations. No utility coordination drawings, profiles, or cross-sections show vertical and horizontal clearances from transformer pads to other underground utilities. Applicant must provide utility coordination drawings with dimension callouts confirming 12-inch minimum horizontal and vertical clearance (OD to OD) from transformer pads to all other underground utilities."},{"deficiencyId":"EL-13.26","status":"not-verifiable","agentTrace":{"observation":"Electrical plan (Sheet 21) shows transformer pads at a single elevation without profile or cross-section detail. Utility plans show underground lines at the same location. No cross-section or profile drawing is provided showing whether transformer pads or underground electrical facilities are located above, below, or in conflict with other utility lines.","reasoning":"The requirement specifies that transformer pads or AE underground facilities shall not be located over or under other utility lines. Without profile drawings showing vertical relationships between utilities and transformer pads, it is impossible to verify compliance. Horizontal clearances are visible from plan view, but vertical conflicts require profile documentation.","tools_used":[]},"codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.5.B"],"applicableAreas":["All transformer pad locations with coexisting underground utilities"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":19},{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":21}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Electrical plan shows transformer pads and underground utilities at the same location. No profile or cross-section drawings show vertical relationships between transformer facilities and other utilities. Applicant must provide utility coordination profile drawings confirming transformer pads and underground electrical facilities are not located directly over or under other utility lines."},{"deficiencyId":"EL-13.27","status":"not-verifiable","agentTrace":{"observation":"Utility plan (Sheet 21) shows overhead distribution lines on the property. No specific dimension callout appears indicating sky-to-ground vertical clearance from transformer pad locations to overhead conductors. No profile or cross-section drawing is provided showing vertical clearance.","reasoning":"The requirement mandates 7.5-foot minimum horizontal sky-to-ground clearance from transformer locations extending from ground to sky. This requires profile drawings or specific notation confirming clearance from ground level vertically up to conductor height. No such documentation is provided.","tools_used":[]},"codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.3"],"applicableAreas":["Transformer pads under or near overhead distribution conductors"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":21}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Overhead distribution lines are shown on utility plan. No dimension annotations or profile drawings confirm 7.5-foot minimum horizontal sky-to-ground clearance from transformer pad locations to overhead distribution conductors. Applicant must add profile cross-sections or dimension callouts verifying 7.5-foot clearance from ground level vertically through conductor height."},{"deficiencyId":"EL-13.28","status":"not-verifiable","agentTrace":{"observation":"Utility plan (Sheet 21) shows overhead distribution lines on the property. No specific dimension callout, circle, or radial clearance annotation appears indicating 15-foot radius clearance from transformer pad or proposed facilities to overhead distribution primary and neutral conductors.","reasoning":"The requirement mandates 15-foot radius clearance measured from the conductors themselves (not pole centerline), extending in all directions. This requires either a plan view with a 15-foot radius circle annotated around conductors, or specific dimension callouts from proposed features to conductors. No such notation is provided.","tools_used":[]},"codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.3"],"applicableAreas":["Transformer pads relative to overhead distribution primary and neutral conductors"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":21}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Overhead distribution lines are shown on utility plan. No dimension annotations confirm 15-foot radius clearance from transformer pads to overhead distribution primary and neutral conductors (measured from conductors, not pole centerline). Applicant must add clearance dimension callouts or overlay 15-foot radius circles around overhead conductors demonstrating compliance."},{"deficiencyId":"EL-13.31","status":"not-verifiable","agentTrace":{"observation":"Site plan shows garage parking integrated with buildings (partially below grade). Electrical plan (Sheet 21) shows transformer pad locations but no cross-section drawings are provided showing vertical clearances from transformer access areas to overhead structures, parking garage ceilings, or enclosed areas. No profile details exist.","reasoning":"The requirement applies when overhead structures, parking garages, or enclosed areas exist above/adjacent to transformer locations. Cross-section drawings are needed to verify vertical clearance is adequate for access and equipment door opening. The submitted plan set lacks cross-section detail showing these vertical relationships.","tools_used":[]},"codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.3"],"applicableAreas":["Transformer pads with overhead structures or parking garage proximity"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":21},{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":9}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Site plan shows integrated garage parking. No cross-section drawings are provided showing vertical clearances at transformer pad locations to verify adequate headroom and overhead clearance for equipment access and operation."},{"deficiencyId":"EL-13.32","status":"not-verifiable","agentTrace":{"observation":"Electrical plan (Sheet 21) shows contour lines near transformer pad locations but no drainage arrows or grading flow arrows indicate surface water direction around pads. Vision check noted that west-side pads have general site contours sloping toward buildings. Transformer equipment type (oil-filled vs. dry-type) is not specified on electrical specifications.","reasoning":"The requirement applies only to oil-filled transformer equipment. Transformer type is not specified in the submittal. If oil-filled equipment is proposed, surface drainage must flow away from buildings. While general site contours are visible, localized drainage around specific pad locations is not documented with arrows or spot elevations. Cannot verify compliance without transformer type specification.","tools_used":["vision_check"]},"codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.4 Table 1.10.4 footnote 1"],"applicableAreas":["Oil-filled transformer pads (if proposed) and surrounding grading"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":21},{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":11}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Transformer equipment type (oil-filled vs. dry-type) is not specified. If oil-filled equipment is proposed, applicant must provide grading plan with drainage arrows showing surface water slope direction around transformer pads, confirming liquid/drainage flow is directed away from buildings."},{"deficiencyId":"EL-13.36","status":"not-verifiable","agentTrace":{"observation":"Electrical plan shows transformer pads, meter locations, and electrical routing. Vision check confirms some pads are positioned very close to the western property boundary within PUE easement areas. Electrical routing lines are shown on the plan but the routing's relationship to property lines and easements is not clearly documented.","reasoning":"The requirement mandates electrical routing from transformer to meter must be 100% on private property. While pads appear to be within private property (not in public ROW), the routing's precise relationship to property lines and easement boundaries is not explicitly documented with dimension annotations or property line clearance callouts. Specific routing documentation is needed to verify compliance.","tools_used":["vision_check"]},"codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.4 Table 1.10.4 footnote 4"],"applicableAreas":["Electrical routing from transformer pads to meters"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":21}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Electrical routing from transformer pads to meters is shown but not dimensioned relative to property lines. Applicant must provide annotated routing with dimension callouts confirming all electrical conduit from transformer pads to meters remains 100% on private property and does not cross into public right-of-way or restricted easements."},{"deficiencyId":"EL-13.39","status":"not-verifiable","agentTrace":{"observation":"Utility plan (Sheet 21) shows overhead distribution facilities on the property. Site plan shows building locations and associated parking structures. No cross-section or profile drawing is provided showing the vertical relationship between customer facilities (buildings, parking structures, light poles, etc.) and the overhead distribution facilities.","reasoning":"The requirement prohibits customer-owned structures from being installed under or over Austin Energy overhead distribution facilities. This requires profile documentation showing vertical clearance between proposed facilities and conductor heights. No such profile documentation is provided in the submittal.","tools_used":[]},"codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.3"],"applicableAreas":["Customer buildings and structures relative to overhead distribution lines"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":21},{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":9}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Overhead distribution facilities are shown on utility plan. No profile or cross-section drawings verify that customer buildings, parking structures, and other facilities do not extend vertically into overhead conductor space. Applicant must provide utility coordination profile drawings confirming no customer facilities are located directly under overhead distribution lines."},{"deficiencyId":"EL-13.11","status":"n/a","agentTrace":{"observation":"Vision check and plan review confirms transformer locations are in standard open areas of the site, not within niche configurations, vaults, enclosed areas, or notched-out building spaces. No niche service installation is proposed.","reasoning":"This requirement applies only when transformer is located in a niche (accessible from outside but within building footprint), enclosed area, or notched-out building configuration. The site plan shows all transformer pads in open areas of the property, not within building footprints or enclosed spaces. The requirement is inapplicable.","tools_used":["vision_check"]},"codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.4 Table 1.10.4"],"applicableAreas":[],"sheetReferences":[],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"No niche transformer configuration is proposed. All transformer pads are located in open areas of the site, not within building footprints or enclosed spaces. This requirement is not applicable to this project."},{"deficiencyId":"EL-13.24","status":"n/a","agentTrace":{"observation":"Review of utility plans (Sheets 12, 19, 21) shows water, wastewater, and storm drain infrastructure. No gas line infrastructure is depicted on any utility plan sheet. No gas meter locations or gas service are indicated on the site plans.","reasoning":"This requirement applies only when gas service is present on the project. The submittal shows no indication of gas service or gas line infrastructure. The requirement is inapplicable.","tools_used":[]},"codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.5.A"],"applicableAreas":[],"sheetReferences":[],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"No gas service infrastructure is shown on utility plans. This requirement is not applicable to this project."},{"deficiencyId":"EL-13.29","status":"n/a","agentTrace":{"observation":"Vision check and site plan review confirms all transformer pads are located in open areas of the property. No niche configuration, enclosed area, or notched-out building space is proposed for any transformer location.","reasoning":"This requirement applies only when transformer is located in a niche (accessible from outside but within building footprint), enclosed area, or notched-out building configuration, requiring 35-foot vertical clearance. The site plan shows transformer pads in standard open areas. The requirement is inapplicable.","tools_used":["vision_check"]},"codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.4 Table 1.10.4 footnote 3"],"applicableAreas":[],"sheetReferences":[],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"No niche transformer configuration is proposed. All pads are in open areas of the site. This requirement is not applicable to this project."},{"deficiencyId":"EL-13.30","status":"n/a","agentTrace":{"observation":"Site plan review confirms no transformer location is within a building footprint or accessible from within a building structure. No niche service installation is indicated.","reasoning":"This requirement applies only to niche service installations where equipment is accessible from outside but located within the customer's building footprint. No such configuration is proposed. The requirement is inapplicable.","tools_used":[]},"codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.4 Table 1.10.4 footnote 3"],"applicableAreas":[],"sheetReferences":[],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"No niche service installation is proposed. This requirement is not applicable to this project."}]}}],"model":"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001","stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":0},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"753eb9f1-6b81-4b4f-8a9b-68520af22dec","uuid":"a5b689e0-9bf4-4131-857e-79de32770be2"}
