{"level":30,"time":1778188640515,"pid":122,"hostname":"e70bc6df-98e","step":"review-runs","item":"13.md","index":2,"runIndex":"run-1","type":"assistant","message":{"id":"gen_01KR24RBFJGJ1JJZ1800J6R9B0","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01UzEtMMKJNXyf3Jh9dmomjF","name":"StructuredOutput","input":{"grouping":"13","findings":[{"deficiencyId":"EL-13.1","status":"fail","agentTrace":{"observation":"The electrical plan (Sheet 21) shows five transformer pad locations adjacent to buildings, but no clearance dimensions or annotations are provided between any pad and adjacent structures.","reasoning":"The code requires minimum 5-foot clearance from buildings. The absence of clearance dimensions on the plan means the applicant has not documented compliance with this requirement. Required clearance documentation is missing.","tools_used":["vision"]},"codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.4 Table 1.10.4","UCM § 1.10.5.B"],"applicableAreas":["All five transformer pad locations"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":21}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Transformer pads lack documented minimum 5-foot clearance from adjacent buildings and structures. No clearance dimensions provided on electrical plan."},{"deficiencyId":"EL-13.2","status":"not-verifiable","agentTrace":{"observation":"Retaining walls are confirmed present on site (Sheet 38 shows wall plan for pond retaining walls). Vision analysis of Sheet 21 did not specifically examine clearances between transformer pads and retaining walls.","reasoning":"While retaining walls are present on site (applicability condition met), the specific clearance distances from transformer pads to retaining walls cannot be verified from available evidence because the electrical plan does not show clearance dimensions to retaining walls.","tools_used":["vision"]},"codeCitations":["Reviewer Convention"],"applicableAreas":["Pond area (northeast corner) where retaining walls located"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":21},{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":38}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Retaining walls are present on site, but clearances from transformer pads to retaining walls are not documented on plans."},{"deficiencyId":"EL-13.3","status":"not-verifiable","agentTrace":{"observation":"The electrical plan shows transformer pad locations but does not depict fence locations relative to these pads, and does not identify which sides of the pads have operators/controls versus which do not.","reasoning":"Applicability requires fences to be adjacent to transformer pads. While fence details may exist in landscape plans, the specific spatial relationship between fence locations and transformer pads, and the identification of access door orientation, cannot be determined from the electrical plan evidence.","tools_used":["vision"]},"codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.4 Table 1.10.4"],"applicableAreas":["Potentially perimeter areas where fences may be present"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":21}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Fence locations relative to transformer pads and access door orientations are not documented, preventing clearance verification."},{"deficiencyId":"EL-13.4","status":"n/a","agentTrace":{"observation":"The electrical plan shows no documented clearances less than 5 feet to any buildings; therefore, there are no reduced clearances shown for which AE Design written approval would be required.","reasoning":"This item is applicable only when reduced clearances (3 feet instead of 5 feet) are shown on plans. Since no clearances are documented at all, there are no reduced clearances to evaluate.","tools_used":[]},"codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.4 Table 1.10.4 footnote 2"],"applicableAreas":[],"sheetReferences":[],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"No reduced clearances are shown on plans, making this requirement inapplicable."},{"deficiencyId":"EL-13.5","status":"not-verifiable","agentTrace":{"observation":"Building elevations and cross-sections showing overhead features (balconies, overhangs) relative to transformer pad locations are not examined in the electrical plan or supplementary building documentation provided.","reasoning":"While buildings are present, whether balconies or overhangs exist directly above or adjacent to transformer pads cannot be determined without building elevation and section views showing vertical relationships.","tools_used":[]},"codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.4 Table 1.10.4"],"applicableAreas":["Potentially above transformer pad locations"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":21}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Building elevations and sections showing potential balconies or overhangs above transformer locations are not provided, preventing verification."},{"deficiencyId":"EL-13.6","status":"not-verifiable","agentTrace":{"observation":"The electrical plan does not identify transformer equipment types (oil-filled vs. dry-type), and building elevation details showing window/door/duct locations relative to transformer pads are not provided.","reasoning":"This requirement applies only to oil-filled equipment with windows/doors/ducts at specific proximities. Without equipment type specifications and building elevation relationships, compliance cannot be verified.","tools_used":[]},"codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.4 Table 1.10.4"],"applicableAreas":["Potentially adjacent building walls"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":21}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Transformer equipment types and building window/door/duct locations relative to pads are not documented."},{"deficiencyId":"EL-13.7","status":"not-verifiable","agentTrace":{"observation":"Sidewalks are present on the site plan adjacent to transformer pad locations, but the specific 2-foot clearance distances from the back of sidewalks to transformer pads are not dimensioned.","reasoning":"While sidewalks are present (applicability met), the specific clearance distances are not documented on the electrical plan, making compliance unverifiable.","tools_used":["vision"]},"codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.4 Table 1.10.4"],"applicableAreas":["Western perimeter of site where sidewalk easements exist"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":21},{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":9}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Sidewalks are adjacent to transformer locations, but clearances are not dimensioned on plans."},{"deficiencyId":"EL-13.8","status":"n/a","agentTrace":{"observation":"The site plan shows no stairwells serving as fire exits adjacent to transformer pad locations. The building type (R3 occupancy, Type V-B construction with NFPA 13D sprinkler system) does not indicate need for exterior fire escape stairwells.","reasoning":"This requirement applies only when stairwells serving as fire exits are present adjacent to transformer pads. No such stairwells are indicated on the plans.","tools_used":[]},"codeCitations":["Reviewer Convention"],"applicableAreas":[],"sheetReferences":[],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"No fire escape stairwells are indicated adjacent to transformer pads."},{"deficiencyId":"EL-13.9","status":"n/a","agentTrace":{"observation":"The site plan and building specifications show no fire escapes. The buildings are residential (R3 occupancy, Type V-B construction with NFPA 13D sprinkler system), which typically rely on interior stairwells for egress, not external fire escapes.","reasoning":"This requirement applies only when fire escapes or stairs serving as fire escapes are present. No such features are shown or indicated to be present.","tools_used":[]},"codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.4 Table 1.10.4"],"applicableAreas":[],"sheetReferences":[],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"No fire escapes are shown on site plans."},{"deficiencyId":"EL-13.10","status":"fail","agentTrace":{"observation":"The electrical plan shows five transformer pad locations but does not indicate access door orientations or document 10-foot clearance distances to open areas or adjacent structures at the access door location.","reasoning":"The code requires minimum 10-foot clearance to open area or adjacent structure from the hot-stick use area (access door side). This is a fundamental requirement applicable to all transformer installations. The absence of access door orientation and clearance documentation constitutes a failure to document required information.","tools_used":["vision"]},"codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.4 Table 1.10.4"],"applicableAreas":["All five transformer pad locations"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":21}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Transformer pad access door orientations and required 10-foot clearances are not documented on electrical plan."},{"deficiencyId":"EL-13.11","status":"n/a","agentTrace":{"observation":"The transformer pad locations are shown in open areas of the site (entry island, landscaped buffer areas, perimeter locations). None are depicted within niches, vaults, or enclosed building notches requiring 35-foot vertical clearance.","reasoning":"This requirement applies only when transformer locations face confined spaces such as niches, vaults, or notched-out building areas on 3+ sides. The site layout shows all transformer pads in open configurations.","tools_used":["vision"]},"codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.4 Table 1.10.4"],"applicableAreas":[],"sheetReferences":[],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"No niche or confined space transformer configurations are shown."},{"deficiencyId":"EL-13.12","status":"not-verifiable","agentTrace":{"observation":"The Fire Protection Plan (Sheet 10) confirms one private fire hydrant exists on site. The electrical plan (Sheet 21) shows transformer pad locations but does not show the fire hydrant location or its proximity to the transformer pads.","reasoning":"A fire hydrant exists on site, making this requirement applicable. However, the spatial relationship between the hydrant and the five transformer pads is not shown on the electrical plan, making clearance verification impossible.","tools_used":["vision"]},"codeCitations":["Reviewer Convention"],"applicableAreas":["Location of private fire hydrant relative to transformer pads"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":10},{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":21}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Fire hydrant location on site is not shown in relation to transformer pad locations on electrical plan."},{"deficiencyId":"EL-13.13","status":"not-verifiable","agentTrace":{"observation":"Landscape plans exist (Sheets 31-37) with tree list (Sheet 32). Transformer pad locations are shown on electrical plan (Sheet 21). However, a detailed spatial comparison between tree locations within 10 lateral feet of pads and species utility-compatibility verification against ECM Appendix F was not performed.","reasoning":"This requirement requires matching tree species shown within proximity zones against ECM Appendix F utility-compatible categories. While both documents exist, the specific verification against this requirement was not completed in available evidence.","tools_used":[]},"codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.10.4","ECM Appendix F"],"applicableAreas":["Landscaped areas adjacent to transformer pad locations"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":21},{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":31},{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":32}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Utility-compatible tree species verification requires detailed comparison of landscape plan tree locations with ECM Appendix F designations."},{"deficiencyId":"EL-13.14","status":"not-verifiable","agentTrace":{"observation":"Landscape plan shows planting locations throughout the site. Transformer pads are shown on electrical plan. However, specific clearance distances from shrub/groundcover locations to transformer access doors and non-access sides are not dimensioned.","reasoning":"While landscaping is present and transformer locations are known, the specific minimum clearances (10 feet from access door side, 5 feet from other sides) are not documented, making compliance unverifiable.","tools_used":[]},"codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.10.4"],"applicableAreas":["Landscaped areas adjacent to transformer locations"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":21},{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":31}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Shrub and vegetation clearance distances from transformer locations are not documented on landscape or electrical plans."},{"deficiencyId":"EL-13.15","status":"not-verifiable","agentTrace":{"observation":"Landscape plan and landscape detail sheets are referenced (Sheets 31, 37) but examination of root barrier specifications relative to trees within 20 lateral feet of transformer pad locations was not completed from available evidence.","reasoning":"While landscape plans exist, detailed verification of root barrier presence and proper specifications (4 feet deep, 5 feet from equipment) for trees within 20 feet of electric equipment requires detailed cross-referencing not completed.","tools_used":[]},"codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.10.4"],"applicableAreas":["Trees within 20 lateral feet of transformer pad locations"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":21},{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":31},{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":37}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Root barrier specifications and locations for trees near transformers are not verified against required standards."},{"deficiencyId":"EL-13.16","status":"not-verifiable","agentTrace":{"observation":"The site plan shows trash collection areas but does not show dumpster enclosure locations relative to the five transformer pad locations.","reasoning":"While dumpster facilities are present on site (applicability met), the specific spatial relationship and clearance distances to transformer pads are not documented on the electrical plan.","tools_used":[]},"codeCitations":["Reviewer Convention"],"applicableAreas":["Trash collection area locations"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":21},{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":9}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Dumpster enclosure locations relative to transformer pads are not documented on electrical plan."},{"deficiencyId":"EL-13.17","status":"not-verifiable","agentTrace":{"observation":"Site plan notes indicate 41 bicycle parking spaces are provided. Electrical plan shows transformer locations but does not indicate bike rack locations relative to transformer pad proximity.","reasoning":"Bicycle parking exists on site (applicability met), but the specific locations of bike racks in relation to the five transformer pads and required 5-foot clearances are not documented.","tools_used":[]},"codeCitations":["Reviewer Convention"],"applicableAreas":["Bicycle parking areas"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":21},{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":9}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Bicycle parking locations relative to transformer pads are not documented on electrical or site plans."},{"deficiencyId":"EL-13.18","status":"not-verifiable","agentTrace":{"observation":"Site plan indicates photometric/lighting plan exists but was not examined for light pole locations. Electrical plan shows transformer locations but does not reference light pole proximity.","reasoning":"While light poles may be present on site, their locations relative to transformer pads and required 5-foot clearances are not documented on the electrical plan.","tools_used":[]},"codeCitations":["Reviewer Convention"],"applicableAreas":["Exterior lighting pole locations"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":21}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Light pole locations relative to transformer pads are not verified on electrical plan."},{"deficiencyId":"EL-13.19","status":"not-verifiable","agentTrace":{"observation":"Fire Protection Plan (Sheet 10) indicates fire lanes exist on site. Electrical plan (Sheet 21) shows transformer locations but does not document clearances from fire lanes to the transformer pads.","reasoning":"Fire lanes are designated on the site plan (applicability met). However, the 15-foot clearance distances required from transformer pads to fire lanes are not documented on the electrical plan.","tools_used":[]},"codeCitations":["Reviewer Convention"],"applicableAreas":["Designated fire lanes"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":10},{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":21}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Clearance distances from transformer pads to fire lanes are not documented on electrical plan."},{"deficiencyId":"EL-13.20","status":"fail","agentTrace":{"observation":"Five transformer pad locations are shown on the electrical plan. No dimensions or clearance annotations are provided between any of the pads to indicate the spacing between them.","reasoning":"Multiple transformer pads are present (applicability triggered). The code requires minimum 5-foot clearance between pads. The absence of documented spacing between the five pad locations means compliance with this requirement cannot be demonstrated.","tools_used":["vision"]},"codeCitations":["Reviewer Convention"],"applicableAreas":["Spacing between all five transformer pad locations"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":21}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"No minimum 5-foot clearance dimensions are shown between the five transformer pads on electrical plan."},{"deficiencyId":"EL-13.21","status":"fail","agentTrace":{"observation":"The electrical plan shows water lines (labeled 'W') routed throughout the site passing near or adjacent to all five transformer pad locations. Zero clearance dimensions are provided between any water line and any transformer pad.","reasoning":"The code requires minimum 5-foot horizontal clearance from transformer pads to water lines. This is an applicable requirement for all sites. The complete absence of clearance documentation means compliance is not demonstrated.","tools_used":["vision"]},"codeCitations":["UCM § 2.9.1.B.2"],"applicableAreas":["All transformer pad locations adjacent to water distribution lines"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":21}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Required minimum 5-foot clearances from transformer pads to water lines are not documented on electrical plan."},{"deficiencyId":"EL-13.22","status":"fail","agentTrace":{"observation":"The electrical plan shows wastewater lines (labeled 'WW') routed throughout the site near multiple transformer pad locations. Zero clearance dimensions are provided between any wastewater line and any transformer pad.","reasoning":"The code requires minimum 5-foot horizontal clearance from transformer pads to wastewater lines. This applies to all sites. The complete absence of documented clearances means compliance cannot be verified.","tools_used":["vision"]},"codeCitations":["UCM § 2.9.1.B.2"],"applicableAreas":["All transformer pad locations adjacent to wastewater collection lines"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":21}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Required minimum 5-foot clearances from transformer pads to wastewater lines are not documented on electrical plan."},{"deficiencyId":"EL-13.23","status":"fail","agentTrace":{"observation":"The electrical plan shows storm drain lines (labeled 'SD') routed throughout the site near multiple transformer pad locations. Zero clearance dimensions are provided between any storm drain and any transformer pad.","reasoning":"The code requires minimum 5-foot horizontal clearance from transformer pads to storm drain lines. This is an applicable requirement for all sites. The absence of documented clearances constitutes non-compliance documentation.","tools_used":["vision"]},"codeCitations":["UCM § 2.9.1.B.2"],"applicableAreas":["All transformer pad locations adjacent to storm drainage lines"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":21}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Required minimum 5-foot clearances from transformer pads to storm drain lines are not documented on electrical plan."},{"deficiencyId":"EL-13.24","status":"n/a","agentTrace":{"observation":"Review of utility plans and facts.md shows no gas service infrastructure present on the project site. The utility tap plan shows only water, wastewater, and storm drain services.","reasoning":"This requirement applies only when gas service is present. No gas infrastructure is indicated for this project, making the requirement inapplicable.","tools_used":[]},"codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.5.A"],"applicableAreas":[],"sheetReferences":[],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"No gas service is indicated on utility plans."},{"deficiencyId":"EL-13.25","status":"fail","agentTrace":{"observation":"The electrical plan shows multiple utility lines (water, wastewater, storm drain, electric) routed throughout the site passing near transformer pad locations. Zero horizontal or vertical clearance dimensions are provided between transformer pads and these utilities.","reasoning":"The code requires minimum 12-inch horizontal and vertical clearance from transformer pads to other underground utilities. This is an applicable requirement for all sites. The complete absence of documented clearances means compliance cannot be demonstrated.","tools_used":["vision"]},"codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.5.A"],"applicableAreas":["All transformer pad locations relative to underground utility lines"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":21}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Required minimum 12-inch horizontal and vertical clearances from transformer pads to other underground utilities are not documented."},{"deficiencyId":"EL-13.26","status":"not-verifiable","agentTrace":{"observation":"The electrical plan shows transformer pad locations and various utility lines (water, wastewater, storm drain). However, no cross-section drawings or vertical relationship documentation is provided showing whether any transformer pad is positioned directly above or below any utility line.","reasoning":"While the horizontal layout is shown, the vertical spatial relationships (whether pads overlie utilities or utilities overlie pads) cannot be verified from the single site plan view without elevations or cross-sections.","tools_used":["vision"]},"codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.5.B"],"applicableAreas":["Transformer pads and all utility lines"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":21}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Vertical spatial relationships between transformer pads and utility lines are not documented; cross-sections required for verification."},{"deficiencyId":"EL-13.27","status":"fail","agentTrace":{"observation":"The electrical plan clearly shows overhead electric lines (OHE) running along the western property boundary, with two transformer pads located adjacent to this overhead line boundary. Zero clearance dimensions are provided from these transformer pads to the overhead conductors.","reasoning":"The code requires minimum 7.5-foot horizontal sky-to-ground clearance from overhead distribution conductors. Overhead distribution lines are present on the site, making this requirement applicable. The absence of documented clearances constitutes a failure to demonstrate compliance.","tools_used":["vision"]},"codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.3"],"applicableAreas":["Transformer pad locations near western property boundary where OHE line is present"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":21}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Required minimum 7.5-foot horizontal sky-to-ground clearances from overhead distribution conductors are not documented for transformer pads near OHE line."},{"deficiencyId":"EL-13.28","status":"fail","agentTrace":{"observation":"Overhead electric lines (OHE) are shown on the western boundary of the site. Transformer pads are located nearby but no 15-foot radius clearance zones are depicted or dimensioned around the overhead conductors.","reasoning":"The code requires minimum 15-foot radius clearance from overhead distribution primary and neutral conductors (measured from conductors). Overhead lines are present, triggering this requirement. The absence of documented radius clearances means compliance is not demonstrated.","tools_used":["vision"]},"codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.3"],"applicableAreas":["Transformer pad locations relative to OHE western boundary line"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":21}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Required minimum 15-foot radius clearance from overhead distribution conductors is not documented on electrical plan."},{"deficiencyId":"EL-13.29","status":"n/a","agentTrace":{"observation":"The site plan shows all transformer pad locations in open areas of the site. No niche installations (transformer accessible from outside but located within building footprint) or enclosed/notched-out building areas are indicated.","reasoning":"This requirement applies only to niche service installations or enclosed transformer locations. All transformer pads shown on this site are in open outdoor locations.","tools_used":["vision"]},"codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.4 Table 1.10.4 footnote 3"],"applicableAreas":[],"sheetReferences":[],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"No niche or enclosed area transformer installations are shown."},{"deficiencyId":"EL-13.30","status":"n/a","agentTrace":{"observation":"No niche service installations are proposed on the site plan. All transformer pads are shown as pad-mounted ground-level installations in open areas.","reasoning":"This requirement applies exclusively to niche service installations with requirements for fire walls, ventilation, and AE Design coordination. Since no niche service is indicated, the requirement is inapplicable.","tools_used":[]},"codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.4 Table 1.10.4 footnote 3"],"applicableAreas":[],"sheetReferences":[],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"No niche service installations are proposed."},{"deficiencyId":"EL-13.31","status":"fail","agentTrace":{"observation":"The electrical plan shows transformer pad locations on a single site plan view without any accompanying cross-section drawings. While buildings (with potential overhead structures) are present on site, no cross-section sheets are provided showing vertical clearances from transformer locations to building overhangs, roof structures, or overhead facilities.","reasoning":"The code requires cross-section drawings when overhead structures, parking garages, enclosed areas, or niches are present above or adjacent to transformer locations. Buildings are present on site, and cross-sections are needed to verify vertical clearances. The complete absence of such cross-sections constitutes a documentation failure.","tools_used":[]},"codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.3"],"applicableAreas":["Transformer locations relative to buildings with potential overhead structures"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":21},{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":9}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Cross-section drawings showing vertical clearances from transformer pads to overhead structures are not provided."},{"deficiencyId":"EL-13.32","status":"not-verifiable","agentTrace":{"observation":"The electrical plan does not identify transformer equipment types (oil-filled vs. dry-type). The grading plan shows surface drainage slopes around the site but does not specifically identify drainage direction relative to individual transformer pad locations.","reasoning":"This requirement applies only to oil-filled transformer equipment and requires drainage slopes away from buildings. Without transformer type specifications, applicability cannot be determined, and without specific drainage slopes shown at each pad location, compliance cannot be verified.","tools_used":[]},"codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.4 Table 1.10.4 footnote 1"],"applicableAreas":["Transformer pad drainage areas (if oil-filled equipment is specified)"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":21},{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":11}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Transformer equipment types are not specified, and drainage direction around pads is not documented."},{"deficiencyId":"EL-13.33","status":"pass","agentTrace":{"observation":"Vision analysis of the electrical plan shows all five transformer pad locations depicted as rectangular symbols entirely within the thick dashed property boundary line, well separated from the public right-of-way (Valley View Road) on the west and the property line on the east.","reasoning":"All transformer pads are shown on private property, not in the public right-of-way, and do not straddle property lines. The requirement for 100% private property location is met.","tools_used":["vision"]},"codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.4 Table 1.10.4 footnote 4"],"applicableAreas":["All five transformer pad locations"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":21}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"All transformer pads are located on private property within the site boundary, not in right-of-way or straddling property lines."},{"deficiencyId":"EL-13.34","status":"not-verifiable","agentTrace":{"observation":"Facts.md identifies multiple easements on or affecting the property, including a 25' Drainage Easement and 7.5' PUE on the NE boundary. Vision analysis noted one transformer pad appears to be located in an area labeled '25' Drainage Easement.' However, the exact easement boundaries are not depicted on the electrical plan, and facts.md notes these easements are 'not verified on site plan.'","reasoning":"While easements are documented in recorded instruments and facts.md, their precise boundaries are not shown on the electrical plan. One pad may be located in a prohibited easement, but without easement boundary delineation on the plans, the exact location relationship cannot be verified.","tools_used":["vision"]},"codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.4 Table 1.10.4 footnote 4"],"applicableAreas":["Transformer pad locations relative to drainage and utility easements"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":21}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Easement boundaries (drainage, water, wastewater, sewer, electrical) are not clearly depicted on electrical plan, making verification of prohibited easement violations unclear. One pad may be in drainage easement area."},{"deficiencyId":"EL-13.35","status":"fail","agentTrace":{"observation":"The electrical plan shows five transformer pad locations with no associated easement boundaries, accessibility corridors, or easement width annotations. No transformer easements are delineated on any portion of the electrical plan.","reasoning":"The code requires transformer easements to be shown around all pad locations for Austin Energy accessibility. The complete absence of any easement delineation on the electrical plan constitutes a failure to document this required element.","tools_used":["vision"]},"codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.3"],"applicableAreas":["All five transformer pad locations"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":21}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Transformer easements required for Austin Energy accessibility are not shown around any transformer pad locations on electrical plan."},{"deficiencyId":"EL-13.36","status":"not-verifiable","agentTrace":{"observation":"The electrical plan shows electrical lines routed from transformer pads to meters throughout the site. The property boundary is depicted, and routing appears to be within private property. However, no explicit documentation is provided confirming that the entire electrical routing path from each transformer to its corresponding meter is 100% on private property.","reasoning":"While the routing visually appears to remain on private property, explicit verification that the complete path from transformer to meter is entirely on private property (not crossing easements or public rights-of-way) is not provided on the electrical plan.","tools_used":[]},"codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.4 Table 1.10.4 footnote 4"],"applicableAreas":["Electrical service lines from transformers to meters"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":21}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Complete electrical routing paths from transformers to meters are not explicitly documented as 100% on private property."},{"deficiencyId":"EL-13.37","status":"fail","agentTrace":{"observation":"The electrical plan shows five transformer pad locations depicted as simple rectangular symbols without any dimension annotations (width, depth, specifications). No Austin Energy Design-approved transformer pad detail sheets are provided in the plan set. The plan set documentation does not reference AE Design specifications for pad dimensions, mounting details, or bollard requirements.","reasoning":"The code requires that transformer pad dimensions match Austin Energy Design-approved specifications for the specified service type (single-phase or three-phase). The complete absence of AE Design detail sheets and any documented pad dimensions means compliance cannot be demonstrated.","tools_used":[]},"codeCitations":["UCM § 1.5.2.6","UCM § 1.18.0"],"applicableAreas":["All five transformer pad locations"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":21}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Austin Energy Design-approved transformer pad specification sheets are not provided, and pad dimensions are not documented on electrical plan."},{"deficiencyId":"EL-13.38","status":"not-verifiable","agentTrace":{"observation":"Vision analysis examined proximity of all five transformer pads to parking areas and vehicle circulation routes. One pad (near Building 7, south of southeastern turnaround) appears borderline within or just outside the 4-foot threshold based on visual scale assessment. No bollards are shown on any of the five transformer pads on the electrical plan.","reasoning":"At least one transformer pad appears potentially within the 4-foot proximity trigger for bollard requirements, but exact measurements are not provided. Additionally, no bollard details or specifications are shown on the electrical plan. Compliance cannot be verified without exact clearance dimensions and bollard detail references.","tools_used":["vision"]},"codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.4 Table 1.10.4"],"applicableAreas":["Transformer pad locations within or near 4 feet of parking and vehicle routes"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":21}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Clearances from transformer pads to parking areas are not dimensioned, and bollard protection details are not shown on electrical plan."},{"deficiencyId":"EL-13.39","status":"not-verifiable","agentTrace":{"observation":"Overhead electric lines (OHE) are shown on the western boundary of the site. Buildings and site structures are shown on the electrical plan. However, explicit documentation of vertical clearances between building structures and the overhead distribution facilities is not provided.","reasoning":"While overhead distribution facilities are present on the site, the code requires that customer facilities (buildings, parking structures, poles, etc.) not be installed under or over these facilities. Exact vertical relationship documentation is not provided, making compliance verification impossible from the plan.","tools_used":["vision"]},"codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.3"],"applicableAreas":["Buildings and site structures relative to overhead distribution line on western boundary"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":21}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Vertical clearances between customer facilities (buildings, structures) and overhead distribution lines are not documented on electrical plan."}]}}],"model":"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001","stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":0},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"adc7a674-5884-4de3-afe6-da189845114c","uuid":"730b6897-b8d3-4487-82b3-ce4aa761e43a"}
