{"level":30,"time":1778188653365,"pid":122,"hostname":"e70bc6df-98e","step":"review-runs","item":"2.md","index":4,"runIndex":"run-2","type":"assistant","message":{"id":"gen_01KR24S03T5HQABP4N3BP4H802","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01RABLiUfHG5P1dvdn9UcqKg","name":"StructuredOutput","input":{"grouping":"2","findings":[{"deficiencyId":"EL-2.1","status":"not-verifiable","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.10.4"],"applicableAreas":["southern property boundary near OHE line","parking lot edge areas near utility corridor"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":31},{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":35}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Trees are shown at 5-15 feet from OHE distribution line on the landscape plan, which falls within the 15-foot restricted zone for non-utility-compatible trees per UCM § 1.10.10.4. However, the landscape plan identifies these trees only by functional category (M, SY, PL) without specifying species. Species are identified on Sheet 35 (Cedar Elm, Live Oak, Mexican Redbud, Texas Mountain Laurel), but no verification is provided of their utility-compatible (UC) status per ECM Appendix F, which is the definitive reference for this requirement. Cannot verify compliance without documented UC status for each proposed species.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Landscape plan shows tree symbols labeled 'M' (mitigation) positioned 5-15 feet from OHE line. Plant schedule on Sheet 35 identifies four tree species. No UC status or mature height documentation is provided on either sheet.","reasoning":"Applicability is triggered because trees are positioned within the 15-foot restricted zone. However, compliance cannot be determined because the landscape plan does not species-identify the trees shown near the OHE, and the plant schedule does not reference ECM Appendix F UC column status. The requirement cannot be verified from available docu