on facilities or transmission easements (distribution-only site)\n- **EL-2.12, EL-2.13** - No clearance dimensions shown on plans\n\n### **PASS (1 item):**\n\n- **EL-2.14** - Trees and OHE infrastructure are both clearly shown on the landscape plan with visible spatial relationship\n\nThe structured output above contains detailed findings with evidence, code citations, and applicableشاreas for each checklist item.","stop_reason":"end_turn","session_id":"df902855-f209-47f1-9270-a32412d9566b","total_cost_usd":0.34620995,"usage":{"input_tokens":3025,"cache_creation_input_tokens":113569,"cache_read_input_tokens":1018037,"output_tokens":19884,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":113569},"inference_geo":"","iterations":[],"speed":"standard"},"modelUsage":{"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001":{"inputTokens":3025,"outputTokens":19884,"cacheReadInputTokens":1018037,"cacheCreationInputTokens":113569,"webSearchRequests":0,"costUSD":0.34620995,"contextWindow":200000,"maxOutputTokens":32000}},"permission_denials":[],"structured_output":{"grouping":"2","findings":[{"deficiencyId":"EL-2.1","status":"not-verifiable","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.10.4"],"applicableAreas":["southern property boundary near OHE line","parking lot edge areas near utility corridor"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":31},{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":35}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Trees are shown at 5-15 feet from OHE distribution line on the landscape plan, which falls within the 15-foot restricted zone for non-utility-compatible trees per UCM § 1.10.10.4. However, the landscape plan identifies these trees only by functional category (M, SY, PL) without specifying species. Species are identified on Sheet 35 (Cedar Elm, Live Oak, Mexican Redbud, Texas Mountain Laurel), but no verification is provided of their utility-compatible (UC) status per ECM Appendix F, which is the definitive reference for this requirement. Cannot verify compliance without documented UC status for each proposed species.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Landscape plan shows tree symbols labeled 'M' (mitigation) positioned 5-15 feet from OHE line. Plant schedule on Sheet 35 identifies four tree species. No UC status or mature height documentation is provided on either sheet.","reasoning":"Applicability is triggered because trees are positioned within the 15-foot restricted zone. However, compliance cannot be determined because the landscape plan does not species-identify the trees shown near the OHE, and the plant schedule does not reference ECM Appendix F UC column status. The requirement cannot be verified from available documents.","tools_used":["vision_check"]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-2.2","status":"n/a","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.10.4"],"applicableAreas":[],"sheetReferences":[],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"No transmission facilities (≥60kV) are present or proposed on this site. Site plan and facts.md identify only 5-foot electric easements (plat-dedicated), which indicate distribution infrastructure (typically <60kV). Transmission facilities would require larger dedicated easements (30+ feet minimum) and would be explicitly noted. Item is not applicable.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Facts.md lists only 5-foot electric easements on the site. Site plan shows OHE line labeled '-OHE-' within these narrow easements. No transmission easement, transmission voltage labeling, or transmission structures noted anywhere in the plan set.","reasoning":"The small 5-foot easement width and lack of any transmission facility documentation indicates distribution-only infrastructure. Transmission items do not apply to distribution-only sites.","tools_used":[]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-2.3","status":"not-verifiable","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.10.4"],"applicableAreas":["southern property boundary near OHE line","parking lot landscape areas"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":31},{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":35}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Trees are proposed at 5-25 feet from OHE distribution line, which overlaps the 25-foot zone where large trees (40+ feet mature height per ECM Appendix F) are restricted. Plant schedule lists Cedar Elm and Live Oak as shade trees in large containers (100 gal.), which could indicate mature size potential. However, no explicit mature height documentation is provided for these species per ECM Appendix F. Cannot verify whether proposed trees will exceed the 40-foot mature height threshold that triggers this requirement.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Landscape plan shows tree symbols at 5-25 feet from OHE. Plant schedule identifies Cedar Elm (100 gal., 4\" cal.) and Live Oak (100 gal., 4\" cal.) as proposed. Standard references (ECM Appendix F) indicate these species can reach or exceed 40 feet mature height, but specific mature height is not documented in the plan set.","reasoning":"Applicability requires determining if large trees are proposed within 25 feet. The species listed can potentially be large trees, but the plans do not explicitly reference ECM Appendix F mature heights to confirm they meet the 40+ feet threshold. The requirement cannot be verified without this reference documentation.","tools_used":["vision_check"]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-2.4","status":"n/a","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.10.4"],"applicableAreas":[],"sheetReferences":[],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"No transmission facilities are present on site. Item applies only to transmission-level infrastructure (≥60kV). Site has distribution infrastructure only. Not applicable.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Facts.md and site plan documents identify only 5-foot electric easements, which are distribution width. No transmission infrastructure noted.","reasoning":"Transmission requirement does not apply to distribution-only sites.","tools_used":[]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-2.5","status":"n/a","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.10.4","UCM § 1.14.6"],"applicableAreas":[],"sheetReferences":[],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"No transmission easement is present on site. Categorical prohibition against trees in transmission easements does not apply. Site has distribution easements only.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Facts.md lists easements on site; all electric easements identified are 5 feet wide (distribution). No transmission easement mentioned in plat records or facts.md.","reasoning":"The item's applicability gate (transmission easement present) is not satisfied. Not applicable.","tools_used":[]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-2.6","status":"not-verifiable","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.10.4"],"applicableAreas":["OHE line along southern boundary"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":31},{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":9}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Overhead electric poles are clearly present (indicated by '-OHE-' line on site and landscape plans, and by utility easement boundaries). However, specific pole locations are not dimensioned on either the site plan or landscape plan. Trees are shown near the OHE line but without dimensioned distances to specific pole locations. The 10-foot pole clearance requirement cannot be verified because pole positions are not precisely located relative to tree planting locations on the submitted plans.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Landscape plan and site plan show OHE infrastructure as a continuous line along the southern boundary. No individual pole locations are marked, dimensioned, or cross-referenced between sheets. Tree symbols are shown near this line but without dimensional callouts to poles.","reasoning":"Poles are present (evidenced by utility line and easement), triggering the requirement. However, the specific pole locations necessary to verify the 10-foot clearance are not documented on the plans. Verification is not possible from available documentation.","tools_used":["vision_check"]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-2.7","status":"not-verifiable","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.10.4"],"applicableAreas":["parking lot and building perimeter areas"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":21},{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":31}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Sheet 21 (Preliminary Electrical Design Plan) shows pad-mounted transformer locations. Sheet 31 (Landscape Plan) shows tree locations. However, these sheets are not dimensionally cross-referenced, and no analysis is provided showing the distance from each pad-mount transformer to nearby trees. The 10-foot clearance from pad-mount equipment centerline cannot be verified without dimensional analysis relating the two sheets.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Electrical plan shows transformer pads at multiple locations (e.g., near Buildings 1-8). Landscape plan shows trees throughout the site. No dimensions or cross-reference callouts relate specific trees to specific pad-mount locations or access doors.","reasoning":"Pad-mounted equipment is present (shown on electrical plan), triggering the requirement. However, the spatial relationship between specific pads and nearby trees is not documented on either plan. Cannot verify 10-foot clearances without dimensional analysis.","tools_used":[]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-2.8","status":"not-verifiable","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.10.4"],"applicableAreas":["site-wide near utility infrastructure"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":9},{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":21},{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":31}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Underground electric equipment (pull boxes, utility lines) are indicated on the site plan and electrical design plan. Tree locations are shown on the landscape plan. However, no dimensional analysis or cross-reference is provided relating underground equipment locations to specific tree planting locations. The 5-foot clearance from underground equipment cannot be verified without dimensional documentation showing the relationship between proposed trees and underground utility vault/equipment locations.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Site plan shows underground utility lines and pull boxes. Landscape plan shows trees throughout. No dimensions or analysis links specific tree locations to specific underground equipment.","reasoning":"Underground equipment is present (shown on utility plans), triggering the requirement. However, the specific distances from trees to underground equipment are not documented. Verification requires dimensional analysis not provided.","tools_used":[]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-2.9","status":"not-verifiable","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.10.4"],"applicableAreas":["site areas with trees near underground utilities"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":31},{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":35}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Root barrier requirements apply only if trees are proposed within 20 feet of underground equipment (minimum 4 feet deep, positioned 5 feet from equipment). The landscape plan does not provide dimensional analysis of tree locations relative to underground equipment, so applicability cannot be determined. Additionally, no root barrier details or specifications are provided on the landscape plan or landscape details sheets. Cannot verify whether this requirement applies or, if it does, whether it is satisfied.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Landscape plan shows proposed trees and irrigation notes but no root barrier details or specifications. No dimensional analysis relating trees to underground utility equipment is provided.","reasoning":"The requirement is conditional on trees being within 20 feet of underground equipment. Without dimensional cross-reference, applicability cannot be determined. Additionally, no root barrier documentation is visible on the landscape plan or sheets.","tools_used":[]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-2.10","status":"fail","codeCitations":["Reviewer Convention"],"applicableAreas":["entire landscape plan, particularly trees near utility facilities"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":31},{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":35}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"The landscape plan (Sheet 31) shows tree symbols labeled only by functional category ('M' for mitigation tree, 'SY' for street yard tree, 'PL' for parking lot tree, 'P' for parking buffer point tree). These abbreviations indicate regulatory category, not species identification. Tree species (Cedar Elm, Live Oak, Mexican Redbud, Texas Mountain Laurel) are identified only on a separate landscape calculations sheet (Sheet 35), not on the landscape plan itself. A user reading the landscape plan cannot identify which specific tree species is shown at each location without cross-referencing to another sheet. The plant legend on the landscape plan does not include species identification.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Sheet 31 landscape plan key notes define 'M = MITIGATION TREE', 'SY = STREET YARD TREE', etc. These are category labels only. Specific species are listed on Sheet 35 in a separate plant schedule table, not integrated into the landscape plan legend.","reasoning":"The requirement is that the plant legend or schedule identifies species of trees proposed near electric facilities. The landscape plan's legend identifies only functional categories, not species. While species are documented elsewhere in the plan set, they are not identified on the landscape plan where the trees are graphically shown, particularly for trees near the OHE line.","tools_used":["vision_check"]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-2.11","status":"not-verifiable","codeCitations":["Reviewer Convention"],"applicableAreas":["areas near OHE with proposed large trees"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":31},{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":35}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Large trees (mature height 40+ feet per ECM Appendix F) require differentiation from smaller trees to verify compliance with 25-foot clearance restrictions near distribution facilities. Sheet 35 plant schedule indicates container sizes (100 gal. for shade trees, 45 gal. for ornamental trees) but does not explicitly reference mature heights per ECM Appendix F. The landscape plan (Sheet 31) does not differentiate large trees from smaller trees with any notation or symbol. While species are identifiable from Sheet 35 (Cedar Elm, Live Oak potentially 40+ feet), the plan does not explicitly mark or call out which trees are large trees for verification purposes.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Plant schedule lists species and container sizes but not explicit mature height per ECM Appendix F. Landscape plan shows all trees with same symbol type regardless of size category. No notation differentiates large trees from smaller trees.","reasoning":"Verification of the 25-foot clearance for large trees requires identifying which proposed trees will be large (40+ feet). Container size is suggestive but not explicit. The plans do not directly reference ECM Appendix F mature heights or provide a symbol/notation system differentiating large trees on the landscape plan.","tools_used":[]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-2.12","status":"n/a","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.10.4"],"applicableAreas":[],"sheetReferences":[],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"This requirement applies only when tree clearances are dimensioned on plans. The landscape plan does not provide any dimensional measurements from trees to electric facilities, poles, or conductors. No clearance dimensions are shown, so this measurement methodology issue does not apply.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Vision analysis confirmed that no dimension lines or numerical measurements relate tree locations to OHE line, poles, or other electric infrastructure on the landscape plan.","reasoning":"The requirement's applicability gate (when clearances are dimensioned) is not satisfied because no clearance dimensions are shown on the plans. Not applicable.","tools_used":["vision_check"]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-2.13","status":"n/a","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.10.4"],"applicableAreas":[],"sheetReferences":[],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"This requirement applies only when tree clearances are dimensioned on plans. The landscape plan provides no dimensional measurements from trees to electric infrastructure. Without dimensions shown, this measurement reference issue does not apply.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Landscape plan shows tree symbols and OHE line but no dimension lines or measurements relating them.","reasoning":"Applicability gate (when clearances are dimensioned) is not met. Not applicable.","tools_used":["vision_check"]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-2.14","status":"pass","codeCitations":["Reviewer Convention"],"applicableAreas":["landscape plan, entire site"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":31},{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":9}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Trees are clearly shown on the landscape plan (Sheet 31) with tree symbols including mitigation trees, street yard trees, parking lot trees, and buffer trees. Overhead electric infrastructure ('-OHE-' line) is clearly depicted on the landscape plan along the southern property boundary. The spatial relationship between trees and OHE is visible on the landscape plan, allowing for clearance assessment based on the graphic scale (1\" = 20'-0\"). Sufficient graphical information is provided to assess tree-to-facility proximity.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Landscape plan shows tree symbols throughout the site and displays '-OHE-' line along southern boundary with graphic scale 1\" = 20'-0\". Tree locations and overhead electric infrastructure are both depicted on the same plan sheet with clear spatial relationship.","reasoning":"The requirement (trees shown on landscape plan in relation to OHE) is satisfied. Trees and OHE are both shown on the same sheet, allowing visual assessment of their proximity. The requirement is met.","tools_used":["vision_check"]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-2.15","status":"fail","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.10.4"],"applicableAreas":["southern property boundary within 5-foot electric utility easement","areas within 15 feet of OHE distribution line"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":31},{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":35},{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":9}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"The landscape plan proposes trees (mitigation trees and other categories) at approximately 5-15 feet from the overhead electric distribution line along the southern property boundary, which falls within the utility easement area (5-foot electric easement per site plan) and within the 15-foot restricted clearance zone per UCM § 1.10.10.4. Site plan notes reference a '5' Electric Easement Vol. 69, Pg. 14' and '5' Elec. & Tele. Easement Vol. 5468, Pg. 885'. Proposed trees are located within or immediately adjacent to this utility easement without documented written approval from Austin Energy. No approval letter, permit exception, or authorization from Austin Energy is provided in the submitted plan set for any trees in utility easement areas. Variations to planting distances within utility easements require explicit written approval per UCM § 1.10.10.4.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Landscape plan shows tree symbols at 5-15 feet from OHE line. Site plan identifies 5-foot electric utility easement in this location. No Austin Energy approval correspondence, exception letters, or written authorization is included in plan documents or supplementary files.","reasoning":"Trees are proposed within utility easement boundaries (within 5 feet of OHE) and within the restricted clearance zone (15 feet of distribution conductors). The requirement explicitly mandates documented Austin Energy written approval for trees in prohibited zones. No such documentation is present. This is a deficiency.","tools_used":["vision_check"]}}]},"fast_mode_state":"off","uuid":"6a8c3726-4a78-4bb7-8699-819e364e0595"}
