"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":21}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"No building elevation sheets or section views provided showing projections (overhangs, awnings, balconies, decks, canopies) relative to surveyed overhead conductor locations and elevations.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Site plan shows building footprints but no elevation details. No building section or elevation drawings with conductor elevation data were found in the plan set.","reasoning":"Building projections require clearance verification using elevation/section views with surveyed conductor data. Without these documents, compliance with both 7.5-foot horizontal sky-to-ground and 15-foot radial clearances cannot be verified.","tools_used":["vision"]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-1.5","status":"not-verifiable","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.3"],"applicableAreas":["Elevated features if present near OHE lines"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":9}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Applicability unclear from plans. If stairs, elevated walkways, or elevated platforms are proposed adjacent to OHE lines, no clearance verification documents provided.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Site plan shows general site layout. Specific elevated features near OHE lines are not clearly identified on the plan view.","reasoning":"Without clear identification of elevated features in proximity to overhead lines and without section views showing vertical clearances, compliance cannot be verified.","tools_used":["vision"]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-1.6","status":"not-verifiable","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.3"],"applicableAreas":["Buildings adjacent to Valley View Road right-of-way where electric facilities exist or will be relocated"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":9},{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":21}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Overhead electric lines exist on or adjacent to site. No surveyed conductor elevations, locations, or clearance dimension annotations provided to demonstrate 7.5-foot horizontal and 15-foot radial clearances are maintained from overhead facilities in ROW.","agentTrace":{"observation":"OHE lines shown on southern boundary near Valley View Road ROW. Buildings shown on site plan but no clearance dimensions or conductor surveys provided.","reasoning":"ROW-adjacent clearances require surveyed conductor data and dimension annotations to buildings. Without these, compliance cannot be verified from submitted plans.","tools_used":["vision"]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-1.7","status":"fail","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.3"],"applicableAreas":["Building elevation sheets and profile views"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":21}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Surveyed elevations and locations of overhead conductors are not included on any building elevation sheets. No building elevation sheets with conductor elevation data and clearance dimension annotations are provided in the plan set.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Electrical design plan (Sheet 21) shows transformer and meter locations with building FFEs but contains no overhead conductor elevation data. Vision check of Sheet 20 (Utility Tap Profile) shows water line profile only; no overhead electric lines depicted. No building elevation sheets found in plan set.","reasoning":"UCM § 1.10.3 requires surveyed conductor elevations on building elevation sheets to demonstrate clearance compliance. The complete absence of building elevation sheets with conductor data constitutes a failure to provide required documentation.","tools_used":["vision"]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-1.8","status":"fail","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.3"],"applicableAreas":["Buildings, structures, and projections within potential clearance distance of OHE lines"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":9},{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":21},{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":38}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Section and plan view exhibits do not show dimension annotations from outer electric conductor to outermost edges of buildings, structures, or projections. No clearance verification dimensions are provided on any plan, section, or detail sheet.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Vision checks of site plan (Sheet 9), electrical plan (Sheet 21), wall plan (Sheet 38), and utility profile (Sheet 20) all confirmed: NO dimension lines extending from conductors to building edges; NO clearance distances (7.5-foot sky-to-ground or 15-foot radial) labeled anywhere.","reasoning":"Required clearance dimension annotations are absent from all relevant sheets. This is a material deficiency—plans must include dimensions from the outer conductor to each building and structure within potential clearance distance.","tools_used":["vision"]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-1.9","status":"not-verifiable","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.3"],"applicableAreas":["Fences near OHE lines along property boundary"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":9},{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":31}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Fences shown on site plan adjacent to or near OHE lines but no clearance dimension annotations provided. Cannot verify 7.5-foot horizontal sky-to-ground clearance from outside conductor to fence.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Vision analysis of landscape plan (Sheet 31) shows fences marked with 'X' pattern near OHE lines on southern boundary. No dimension lines or clearance distances annotated.","reasoning":"Without clearance dimensions, the 7.5-foot requirement cannot be verified. The fence location relative to the outer conductor is not dimensioned.","tools_used":["vision"]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-1.10","status":"not-verifiable","codeCitations":["Reviewer Convention"],"applicableAreas":["Fence posts near OHE utility poles"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":9}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Fence and pole locations shown but without specific distance annotations, the 10-foot clearance requirement for fence posts from electric poles cannot be verified.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Site plan shows fence lines and utility poles but no dimension annotations specifying distances between fence posts and pole locations.","reasoning":"Without explicit dimension annotations, fence post clearance from poles cannot be verified from the plan.","tools_used":["vision"]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-1.12","status":"not-verifiable","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.14.0"],"applicableAreas":["Fencing if located adjacent to or beneath electric transmission lines"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":3}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"General notes reference 'transmission structures' with 25-foot clearance requirement and transmission easement road load requirements, indicating transmission facilities may exist. Applicability depends on final confirmation of transmission vs. distribution classification. No fence material specifications or grounding details provided if fencing near transmission lines.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Sheet 3 general notes reference 'electric transmission' and specify 25-foot clearance for digging/grading/trees and 20-foot clearance for aerial equipment, and transmission easement road load capacity (46,000 lb tandem axle).","reasoning":"The presence of transmission facility references suggests transmission lines may be present. However, applicability cannot be finalized without clear confirmation of transmission vs. distribution. If transmission lines exist adjacent to fencing, no material type or grounding specifications are shown.","tools_used":[]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-1.13","status":"not-verifiable","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.3"],"applicableAreas":["Vehicle barrier fencing if proposed beneath overhead lines"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":9}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Cannot determine from plans whether vehicle barrier fencing is proposed beneath OHE lines. If proposed, no clearance verification exhibits provided.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Site plan shows fences and site features but does not clearly identify specific vehicle barrier installations beneath overhead lines.","reasoning":"Applicability is unclear from plan review. If vehicle barriers are proposed under OHE, clearance verification dimensions would be required.","tools_used":[]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-1.14","status":"fail","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.3"],"applicableAreas":["Retaining walls located adjacent to OHE lines along southern property boundary"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":9},{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":38}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Retaining walls shown on site plan and detailed on Wall Plan sheets (Sheets 38-39) in proximity to OHE lines, but no clearance dimension annotations from outer electric line to outermost edge of retaining wall. Wall section drawings do not reference or show overhead electric lines.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Vision check of Wall Plan (Sheet 38) confirmed the 14'-0\" max retaining wall section is detailed but contains no reference to OHE lines and no clearance dimensions to overhead conductors. Site plan shows walls running along boundary where OHE exists.","reasoning":"Retaining walls adjacent to overhead lines require clearance dimension verification. Sheet 38 provides detailed wall sections but they make no reference to OHE clearance requirements. The 7.5-foot horizontal sky-to-ground clearance cannot be verified.","tools_used":["vision"]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-1.17","status":"fail","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.3"],"applicableAreas":["Retaining walls in section views adjacent to OHE facilities"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":38},{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":39}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Retaining wall cross-section exhibits (Sheets 38-39) do not show clearance dimension annotations from outer electric conductor to outermost edge of wall. No OHE lines depicted on section views.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Vision check of Sheets 38-39 confirmed wall sections (14'-0\", 8'-0\", 6'-0\", 4'-0\" max heights) are detailed with structural information but contain no dimension lines or annotations showing clearance to overhead conductors.","reasoning":"Required clearance dimension annotations from outer conductor to wall face are absent from section exhibits. This is necessary to verify the 7.5-foot horizontal sky-to-ground clearance requirement.","tools_used":["vision"]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-1.18","status":"not-verifiable","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.6.2"],"applicableAreas":["Driveways on site where overhead lines may cross or be adjacent"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":11}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Grading plan (Sheet 11) shows driveway locations but does not include cross-section or profile views showing final driveway grade elevations relative to surveyed overhead line clearances. No vertical clearance dimensions (16-foot or 18-foot) provided.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Vision check of Sheet 11 confirmed the Grading Plan is a plan-view only drawing with no sections or profiles. No vertical clearance information relative to overhead lines is shown.","reasoning":"Driveway vertical clearance requirements (16 feet without trucks, 18 feet with trucks) require section views showing ground grade elevation relative to overhead line lowest points. These are not provided.","tools_used":["vision"]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-1.19","status":"not-verifiable","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.6.2"],"applicableAreas":["Vehicle parking and display areas on concrete pads beneath overhead electric lines"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":9},{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":11}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Site plan shows parking areas but no vertical clearance dimensions from overhead electric lines to parking surface are provided. No clearance requirement note included on plans.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Vision analysis found parking areas shown on site plan and grading plan, but no clearance dimension annotations from overhead lines to parking surface elevations.","reasoning":"Without vertical clearance dimensions and noted clearance requirements on plans, compliance cannot be verified.","tools_used":["vision"]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-1.22","status":"not-verifiable","codeCitations":["Reviewer Convention"],"applicableAreas":["Driveway alignments where existing electric poles may be located"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":9}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Cannot determine from site plan whether existing electric poles conflict with proposed driveways. If conflicts exist, no relocation notes or revised pole locations are evident on plans.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Site plan shows driveway routing and pole locations but does not include dimension annotations or relocation notes addressing potential conflicts.","reasoning":"Without explicit analysis of pole-to-driveway distances or relocation notes, pole conflict status cannot be verified.","tools_used":[]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-1.23","status":"n/a","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.3"],"applicableAreas":[],"sheetReferences":[],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"No clearance dimensions are shown on plans. This item addresses improper measurement methodology (measuring from pole centerline vs. outside conductor). Without any clearance dimensions provided, this specific item does not apply; the absence of dimensions is addressed by EL-1.8.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Vision checks of multiple sheets (9, 21, 38) confirmed no clearance dimensions are annotated anywhere on the plans.","reasoning":"This item specifically concerns how clearances are measured IF they are shown. Since no clearance dimensions exist on the plans, the measurement methodology issue is moot. The underlying deficiency (absence of dimensions) is covered by EL-1.8.","tools_used":["vision"]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-1.24","status":"not-verifiable","codeCitations":["Reviewer Convention"],"applicableAreas":["Streetlight pole locations relative to overhead electric lines"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":9}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Cannot determine from site plan whether streetlight poles are proposed under overhead electric lines. Streetlight locations not clearly identified in proximity analysis.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Site plan review did not reveal explicit streetlight pole locations identified relative to OHE routing.","reasoning":"Applicability depends on whether streetlights are proposed under overhead lines. This cannot be determined from available plan review.","tools_used":[]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-1.25","status":"not-verifiable","codeCitations":["Reviewer Convention"],"applicableAreas":["Sidewalk alignments at property limits along ROW where power poles exist"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":9}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Sidewalk alignments and power pole locations not specifically dimensioned. Cannot verify whether sidewalks conflict with pole locations at property corners along Valley View Road ROW.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Site plan shows general site layout but does not provide detailed dimension annotations for sidewalk clearances from poles at property limits.","reasoning":"Without specific dimension data, sidewalk-to-pole clearances cannot be verified.","tools_used":[]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-1.26","status":"not-verifiable","codeCitations":["Reviewer Convention"],"applicableAreas":["Trash enclosure and receptacle locations if beneath overhead electric lines"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":9}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Cannot determine if trash enclosures or receptacles are shown beneath overhead electric facilities. Trash areas not clearly identified in proximity to OHE lines on site plan.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Site plan does not clearly identify specific trash area locations relative to OHE lines.","reasoning":"Applicability depends on whether trash enclosures are proposed under overhead lines. This cannot be determined from available plans.","tools_used":[]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-1.27","status":"not-verifiable","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.3"],"applicableAreas":["Customer facilities and structures proposed within or adjacent to electric easement boundaries"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":9}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Site plan shows buildings and features adjacent to OHE easement, but without surveyed conductor elevations and clearance dimensions, compliance with prohibition on installing facilities under/over distribution lines and the 7.5-foot clearance from outside conductor cannot be verified.","agentTrace":{"observation":"OHE lines shown running along southern property boundary with 5' electric easement; buildings and structures shown on site plan but no clearance dimensions from outside conductor provided.","reasoning":"The absolute prohibition on installing customer facilities under or over distribution lines requires verification that features are either outside the easement area or maintain 7.5-foot clearance. Without clearance dimensions, this cannot be verified.","tools_used":["vision"]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-1.28","status":"not-verifiable","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.3","UCM § 1.10.6.2"],"applicableAreas":["Water meter locations relative to overhead electric service drops"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":21}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Water meter locations shown on site plan but not specifically analyzed or dimensioned relative to overhead electric service drop routing. No clearance verification provided.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Electrical design plan (Sheet 21) shows transformer/meter locations but no analysis of distance from overhead service drop conductors.","reasoning":"Without dimension annotations showing clearance from service drops to meters, the 7.5-foot sky-to-ground clearance requirement cannot be verified.","tools_used":[]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-1.29","status":"not-verifiable","codeCitations":["Reviewer Convention"],"applicableAreas":["Water line routing adjacent to overhead electrical distribution poles and conductors"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":19}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Water line routing shown on utility tap plan but no clearance dimensions provided relative to overhead distribution poles and conductors. Required clearance cannot be verified.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Utility Tap Plan (Sheet 19) shows water line routing on site but does not include clearance annotations from OHE facilities.","reasoning":"Without clearance dimension annotations, the clearance requirement cannot be verified.","tools_used":[]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-1.31","status":"fail","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.3"],"applicableAreas":["Buildings with Finished Floor Elevations shown adjacent to overhead lines where vertical clearance appears marginal or insufficient"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":21}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Overhead electric lines exist adjacent to site. Proposed building FFEs are shown (ranging 683.0' to 687.50') but surveyed overhead conductor elevation data is not provided. When vertical clearance from overhead facilities to proposed site features appears marginal or insufficient based on available data, registered surveyor mid-span clearance data is required. No surveyor data provided.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Sheet 21 shows building FFEs (683.0' to 687.50') but provides no overhead conductor elevation data. Without conductor heights, whether clearance is marginal cannot be definitively assessed, but the complete absence of conductor elevation data is itself evidence that required survey data is missing.","reasoning":"When overhead facilities adjacent to structures lack surveyed elevation data, registered surveyor mid-span clearance survey is required to verify adequate clearance is maintained. This survey data is not provided in the plan set.","tools_used":[]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-1.32","status":"not-verifiable","codeCitations":["Reviewer Convention"],"applicableAreas":["Overhead electric line crossings of roadways"],"sheetReferences":[],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Cannot determine from plans whether new overhead electric lines are proposed to cross roadways. If crossings are planned, no indication of crossing angle alignment is shown.","agentTrace":{"observation":"No new overhead lines or crossing details identified in plan review.","reasoning":"Applicability is unclear. If new overhead lines cross roadways, 90-degree crossing angle would be required.","tools_used":[]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-1.33","status":"n/a","codeCitations":["Reviewer Convention"],"applicableAreas":[],"sheetReferences":[],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"No secondary and primary overhead electric line crossings indicated on utility plans. Item does not apply.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Plan review of utility sheets did not reveal secondary over primary overhead line crossing conditions.","reasoning":"No secondary/primary crossing conflicts evident from plans.","tools_used":[]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-1.34","status":"n/a","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.3"],"applicableAreas":[],"sheetReferences":[],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"No marquee signs proposed. Item does not apply.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Site plan review shows no marquee sign locations identified.","reasoning":"Marquee signs are not part of the proposed site development.","tools_used":[]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-1.35","status":"n/a","codeCitations":["Reviewer Convention"],"applicableAreas":[],"sheetReferences":[],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"No new power poles for underground service conversion are shown on plans. Item does not apply.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Electrical design plan does not indicate underground service conversion requiring new poles.","reasoning":"No underground service pole conversion project identified.","tools_used":[]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-1.36","status":"not-verifiable","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.3"],"applicableAreas":["Decorative lighting fixture locations if beneath overhead electric lines"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":31}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Landscape plan shows site lighting but specific decorative lighting locations relative to overhead lines are not clearly identified or dimensioned. Clearance verification dimensions not provided.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Landscape plan review did not provide clear identification of specific decorative lighting locations with clearance dimensions from OHE lines.","reasoning":"Without location and clearance dimension data, compliance cannot be verified.","tools_used":[]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-1.37","status":"fail","codeCitations":["ECM § 2.4.1.D","ECM § 2.4.2.C","UCM § 1.10.10.4"],"applicableAreas":["Landscape plantings within 10 lateral feet of overhead distribution conductors or 50 lateral feet of overhead transmission conductors"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":31},{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":35}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Landscape plan (Sheet 31) shows mitigation trees (marked 'M') proposed along southern property boundary near OHE lines. Plant list (Sheet 35) specifies: 2 Live Oak (Quercus virginiana) and 10 Cedar Elm (Ulmus crassifolia). Live Oak is not utility-compatible (mature height 60+ feet exceeds UC list criteria); Cedar Elm (mature height 40-60 feet) is problematic near distribution lines. Trees within 10 lateral feet of distribution lines must be from ECM Appendix F Utility Compatible list with mature heights ≤20 feet generally.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Vision check of landscape plan (Sheet 31) confirmed mitigation trees ('M' symbols) are shown within 10-50 feet of the OHE line along the southern boundary. Sheet 35 plant list specifies Live Oak (Quercus virginiana) and Cedar Elm (Ulmus crassifolia) as proposed trees.","reasoning":"Live Oak (native Texas tree, mature height 60+ feet) is not on the ECM Appendix F Utility Compatible list and exceeds typical UC height specifications. Cedar Elm (40-60 feet mature height) also exceeds the general UC specification of ≤20 feet. When non-utility-compatible species are proposed within clearance distance of overhead lines, this violates the requirement.","tools_used":["vision"]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-1.38","status":"not-verifiable","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.9.3.1"],"applicableAreas":["Electric meter locations and access zones"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":21}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Electrical design plan shows meter locations but does not include access clearance analysis or obstruction verification. Required working clearances (30-inch-wide front space, 36-inch front depth, 6.5-foot headroom) not verified on plans.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Sheet 21 shows transformer and meter locations in plan view but does not include access clearance analysis or documentation of unobstructed working space.","reasoning":"Without detailed access clearance verification and obstruction analysis, compliance with meter access requirements cannot be determined from submitted plans.","tools_used":[]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-1.39","status":"not-verifiable","codeCitations":["Reviewer Convention"],"applicableAreas":["Building and structure locations adjacent to existing streetlight poles"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":9}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Cannot determine from site plan whether existing streetlights are present adjacent to buildings. Streetlight locations not clearly identified relative to proposed structures.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Site plan review did not reveal clear identification of existing streetlight locations relative to building locations.","reasoning":"Applicability depends on presence of adjacent streetlights. This cannot be determined from available plans.","tools_used":[]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-1.40","status":"not-verifiable","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.17.0"],"applicableAreas":["Down guy wire locations from existing electric poles in conflict with accessible paths and driveways"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":9}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Down guy wire locations from existing distribution poles are not explicitly shown or annotated on site plan. Guide notes that electric utility infrastructure is frequently omitted from plans. Cannot verify whether guy wires conflict with proposed accessible paths, driveways, or site features without detailed utility survey.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Site plan shows utility poles but does not clearly depict guy wire anchor locations or cable routing. The grouping guide explicitly notes that electric utility infrastructure is 'frequently omitted from plans.'","reasoning":"Down guy anchors and cables may exist but are not documented on submitted plans. Without explicit depiction and annotation, potential conflicts with accessible routes and driveways cannot be verified. This is not a pass—it's an unresolvable verification gap due to incomplete utility documentation.","tools_used":[]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-1.41","status":"not-verifiable","codeCitations":["Reviewer Convention"],"applicableAreas":["Transmission line guy easements if angled transmission guy anchors exist on site"],"sheetReferences":[],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"No transmission line guy anchors identified on site. Easement exhibit does not show transmission guy easements. Applicability cannot be determined from plans.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Plan review did not identify transmission structures with angled guy wire anchors.","reasoning":"Applicability depends on presence of transmission guy anchors. Without clear identification, compliance cannot be assessed.","tools_used":[]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-1.42","status":"not-verifiable","codeCitations":["Reviewer Convention"],"applicableAreas":["Down guy anchor easement locations if down guys from distribution poles exist"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":2}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Down guy anchor locations not clearly shown on easement exhibit or utility plans. Cannot verify whether dedicated easements for down guy anchors are provided extending 10 feet wide with 5-foot extension past anchor ground entry.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Easement exhibit and utility plans do not explicitly depict down guy anchor easement boundaries or dimensions.","reasoning":"Without clear documentation of down guy anchor locations and easement boundaries, compliance with easement requirements cannot be verified.","tools_used":[]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-1.43","status":"not-verifiable","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.3"],"applicableAreas":["Pole-mounted or pad-mounted transformers shown relative to overhead electric lines"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":21}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Electrical design plan shows transformer pad locations but does not provide vertical clearance dimensions from overhead electric lines to top of transformer equipment. Section views with clearance dimension annotations are not provided.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Sheet 21 shows transformer locations in plan view with building FFEs but no vertical clearance information from overhead lines to transformer tops.","reasoning":"The 7.5-foot vertical sky-to-ground clearance requirement for transformers requires vertical clearance dimension annotations. These are not provided.","tools_used":[]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-1.44","status":"n/a","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.4"],"applicableAreas":[],"sheetReferences":[],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"No transformers or switchgears shown in niche service configurations (covered or recessed installations) on plans. Item does not apply.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Electrical design plan shows transformers in typical open pad configuration, not in niche installations.","reasoning":"No niche service configurations identified in plan set.","tools_used":[]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-1.45","status":"not-verifiable","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.2"],"applicableAreas":["Construction staging areas, equipment operation zones, and work platforms during site development"],"sheetReferences":[],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"No construction staging plan or logistics plan provided showing staging area boundaries, crane swing radius, or material storage locations relative to overhead electric lines. Cannot verify 10-foot radial clearance during construction from submitted documents.","agentTrace":{"observation":"No site logistics or construction phasing plan was identified in the plan set showing staging areas and crane operations.","reasoning":"Without a construction staging/logistics plan that addresses clearance from overhead lines, compliance with the 10-foot radial construction working clearance cannot be verified.","tools_used":[]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-1.46","status":"pass","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.2"],"applicableAreas":["General notes and cover sheet where 48-hour notification requirement applies"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":3}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Sheet 3 General Notes contain required 48-hour notification provision stating: 'A pre-construction safety meeting is required with Austin Energy 48 hours before commencement of construction. Call Andrew Perez at 512-505-7153 to schedule a tailgate safety meeting.' Requirement is met.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Vision check of Sheet 3 Electric Transmission Notes confirmed the 48-hour notification requirement is explicitly stated with contact information.","reasoning":"The required notice complying with Texas Health & Safety Code Chapter 752 Section 752.003 is present in the general notes.","tools_used":["vision"]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-1.47","status":"not-verifiable","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.6.2"],"applicableAreas":["Service-mast through-roof installation locations and clearances if shown on plans"],"sheetReferences":[],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"No building elevation sheets showing service-mast through-roof installation locations or clearance dimensions are provided. Cannot verify 3-foot clearance above roof (or 18-inch clearance if within 4 feet of roof edge) for voltages ≤300V.","agentTrace":{"observation":"No building elevation sheets with service-mast details were found in the plan set.","reasoning":"Without building elevation details showing service-mast locations and roof clearance dimensions, compliance cannot be verified.","tools_used":[]}}]},"fast_mode_state":"off","uuid":"dc5d6b90-8dc8-4a0a-95c5-1bf2e14a2c6d"}
