{"level":30,"time":1778188679082,"pid":122,"hostname":"e70bc6df-98e","step":"review-runs","item":"2.md","index":1,"runIndex":"run-1","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_018hfEQhY8V5gZ89PW97Vazh","type":"tool_result","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Based on a careful visual analysis of the provided Landscape Plan (Sheet 28 of 35), there are no pad-mounted electrical transformers or equipment explicitly labeled or clearly identifiable on this specific drawing. \n\nWhile there is an Overhead Electric (\"OHE\") line denoted along the bottom property boundary, no pad-mounted boxes or labels such as \"XFMR\" or \"Transformer\" are visible. \n\nBecause this equipment is not shown on this single sheet, it is not possible to determine if there are trees shown within 10 feet of it."}]}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"9d122776-20ac-46ff-b558-35791e0f03e5","uuid":"5348177a-d97f-4478-892d-7c704946250f","tool_use_result":[{"type":"text","text":"Based on a careful visual analysis of the provided Landscape Plan (Sheet 28 of 35), there are no pad-mounted electrical transformers or equipment explicitly labeled or clearly identifiable on this specific drawing. \n\nWhile there is an Overhead Electric (\"OHE\") line denoted along the bottom property boundary, no pad-mounted boxes or labels such as \"XFMR\" or \"Transformer\" are visible. \n\nBecause this equipment is not shown on this single sheet, it is not possible to determine if there are trees shown within 10 feet of it."}]}
{"level":30,"time":1778188679500,"pid":122,"hostname":"e70bc6df-98e","step":"review-runs","item":"2.md","index":7,"runIndex":"run-3","type":"assistant","message":{"id":"gen_01KR24VMRNH0DTX1D0GNPEB633","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I have completed my comprehensive site plan review for grouping **2** (Tree Clearances from Overhead Electric Lines). \n\n## Summary of Findings\n\n**Project Context**: Valley View Townhomes proposes 39 multi-family units with overhead electric (OHE) distribution lines along the western and southern property boundaries. Multiple tree species are proposed, including 2 Live Oak and 10 Cedar Elm shade trees, along with ornamental trees and shrubs.\n\n**Critical Issues Identified**:\n\n1. **EL-2.3 (FAIL)** — Large trees (Live Oak and Cedar Elm with 40-60+ foot and 40-50 foot mature heights respectively) are positioned approximately 3-5 feet from the southern boundary OHE line, well within the required 25-foot minimum clearance for large trees ≥40 feet.\n\n2. **EL-2.15 (FAIL)** — Trees are proposed in prohibited clearance zones without documented Austin Energy written approval. The plans contain no variance correspondence or approval letters.\n\n3. **EL-2.1 (NOT-VERIFIABLE)** — While trees appear to be within restricted distances, utility-compatible (UC) designations cannot be verified from the documents provided (ECM Appendix F not included).\n\n4. **EL-2.6 (NOT-VERIFIABLE)** — Utility poles are shown on the boundary, but exact 10-foot lateral distances from pole centerline to tree trunks are not dimensioned on the plans.\n\n5. **EL-2.11 (NOT-VERIFIABLE)** — Large tree species are not differentiated with special callouts or notations on the landscape plan, requiring cross-reference to the plant schedule for verification.\n\n**Compliant Items**: Plant legend identifies all species, clearance measurement methodology is not shown with errors, and trees are depicted relative to utilities.\n\nThe structured findings have been submitted with all details, code citations, applicable locations, and sheet references for your review."}],"model":"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001","stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":0},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"8e2cb63b-05d8-41aa-bedd-77a52405a611","uuid":"77e03077-a32f-44a4-9b71-5c8c68a41962"}
{"level":30,"time":1778188679548,"pid":122,"hostname":"e70bc6df-98e","step":"review-runs","item":"2.md","index":7,"runIndex":"run-3","type":"result","subtype":"success","is_error":false,"duration_ms":376378,"duration_api_ms":212419,"num_turns":23,"result":"I have completed my comprehensive site plan review for grouping **2** (Tree Clearances from Overhead Electric Lines). \n\n## Summary of Findings\n\n**Project Context**: Valley View Townhomes proposes 39 multi-family units with overhead electric (OHE) distribution lines along the western and southern property boundaries. Multiple tree species are proposed, including 2 Live Oak and 10 Cedar Elm shade trees, along with ornamental trees and shrubs.\n\n**Critical Issues Identified**:\n\n1. **EL-2.3 (FAIL)** — Large trees (Live Oak and Cedar Elm with 40-60+ foot and 40-50 foot mature heights respectively) are positioned approximately 3-5 feet from the southern boundary OHE line, well within the required 25-foot minimum clearance for large trees ≥40 feet.\n\n2. **EL-2.15 (FAIL)** — Trees are proposed in prohibited clearance zones without documented Austin Energy written approval. The plans contain no variance correspondence or approval letters.\n\n3. **EL-2.1 (NOT-VERIFIABLE)** — While trees appear to be within restricted distances, utility-compatible (UC) designations cannot be verified from the documents provided (ECM Appendix F not included).\n\n4. **EL-2.6 (NOT-VERIFIABLE)** — Utility poles are shown on the boundary, but exact 10-foot lateral distances from pole centerline to tree trunks are not dimensioned on the plans.\n\n5. **EL-2.11 (NOT-VERIFIABLE)** — Large tree species are not differentiated with special callouts or notations on the landscape plan, requiring cross-reference to the plant schedule for verification.\n\n**Compliant Items**: Plant legend identifies all species, clearance measurement methodology is not shown with errors, and trees are depicted relative to utilities.\n\nThe structured findings have been submitted with all details, code citations, applicable locations, and sheet references for your review.","stop_reason":"end_turn","session_id":"8e2cb63b-05d8-41aa-bedd-77a52405a611","total_cost_usd":0.32576584999999997,"usage":{"input_tokens":2773,"cache_creation_input_tokens":115905,"cache_read_input_tokens":717366,"output_tokens":21275,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":115905},"inference_geo":"","iterations":[],"speed":"standard"},"modelUsage":{"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001":{"inputTokens":2773,"outputTokens":21275,"cacheReadInputTokens":717366,"cacheCreationInputTokens":115905,"webSearchRequests":0,"costUSD":0.32576584999999997,"contextWindow":200000,"maxOutputTokens":32000}},"permission_denials":[],"structured_output":{"grouping":"2","findings":[{"deficiencyId":"EL-2.1","status":"not-verifiable","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.10.4"],"applicableAreas":["Southern property boundary along OHE utility line"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":31},{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":35}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Mitigation trees (marked 'M') are positioned approximately 3-5 feet from the southern boundary OHE line on the landscape plan. These trees appear to have circle/cross symbols consistent with Live Oak and/or Cedar Elm plant schedule symbols, but ECM Appendix F utility-compatible (UC) designation cannot be verified from provided documents. Clearance distance measured from plan scale is approximately 3-5 feet lateral distance from the OHE line, which is less than the 15-foot minimum for non-utility-compatible trees. Determine UC status of species and confirm compliance or obtain Austin Energy written approval.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Vision analysis identified trees marked 'M' (Mitigation) in the southeast corner of the landscape plan approximately 3-5 feet from the boundary OHE utility line. Plant schedule symbols (circle with cross) correspond to shade tree species. No dimension lines or clearance notes shown.","reasoning":"Applicability is confirmed (OHE distribution lines present, trees proposed near them). However, UC designation cannot be verified from provided documents (ECM Appendix F not included). The 3-5 foot distance is clearly within the 15-foot threshold, but without UC status verification, compliance cannot be determined. This is a not-verifiable condition requiring reference to official UC designation data.","tools_used":["mcp__conductor_tools__vision_check"]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-2.2","status":"n/a","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.10.4"],"applicableAreas":[],"sheetReferences":[],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"No transmission lines or transmission easements identified on site plan or in facts.md. OHE lines shown are distribution-type (standard OHE labeling, not transmission classification).","agentTrace":{"observation":"Site plan shows OHE lines labeled as distribution infrastructure. Facts.md indicates no transmission easement on property. No indication of transmission voltage facilities (≥60kV).","reasoning":"Applicability gate (trigger condition) not met. No transmission lines or transmission easements present. Item is not applicable.","tools_used":[]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-2.3","status":"fail","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.10.4"],"applicableAreas":["Southern property boundary along OHE utility line"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":31},{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":35}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Large trees with mature height ≥40 feet (Live Oak and Cedar Elm) are proposed within 25 lateral feet of OHE distribution conductor line. Live Oak trees are positioned approximately 3-5 feet from the southern boundary OHE line, and Cedar Elm trees are similarly positioned near the OHE boundary. Both species exceed the 40-foot mature height threshold (Live Oak 40-60+ ft; Cedar Elm 40-50 ft). No Austin Energy written approval provided for this violation.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Landscape plan (Sheet 31) and plant schedule (Sheet 35) show 2 Live Oak and 10 Cedar Elm proposed. Vision analysis identified mitigation trees (marked 'M') with circle/cross symbols consistent with these shade tree species positioned 3-5 feet from southern boundary OHE line. Both species have mature heights meeting or exceeding the 40-foot large tree threshold.","reasoning":"Large tree restriction applies when trees with mature height ≥40 feet are within 25 feet of distribution conductors. The distance (3-5 feet) is well within 25 feet. Both Live Oak (40-60+ ft) and Cedar Elm (40-50 ft) exceed the 40-foot threshold. No exceptions or Austin Energy approval documented. This is a clear deficiency.","tools_used":["mcp__conductor_tools__vision_check"]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-2.4","status":"n/a","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.10.4"],"applicableAreas":[],"sheetReferences":[],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"No transmission lines or transmission easements identified. Applicability gate not met.","agentTrace":{"observation":"No transmission facilities identified on site plan or in property facts.","reasoning":"Trigger condition (transmission line proximity) not met. Not applicable.","tools_used":[]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-2.5","status":"n/a","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.10.4","UCM § 1.14.6"],"applicableAreas":[],"sheetReferences":[],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"No transmission easement boundaries shown on site plan. Facts.md identifies other easements (greenbelt, drainage, wastewater, public utility) but no transmission easement. Item does not apply.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Comprehensive easement review in facts.md lists 9 easements/dedications; none are transmission easements. Site plan shows no transmission easement boundaries.","reasoning":"Trigger condition (transmission easement present) not met. Categorical prohibition does not apply to this site.","tools_used":[]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-2.6","status":"not-verifiable","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.10.4"],"applicableAreas":["Western and southern property boundaries"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":9},{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":31}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Utility pole locations are shown on site plan (Sheet 9) and landscape plan (Sheet 31) along the western and southern OHE boundaries. Proposed trees (especially mitigation trees near the southern boundary) appear to be positioned very close to the property line where poles are located. No dimension lines showing clearance distance from pole centers to tree trunks provided. Cannot definitively measure the 10-foot lateral distance (from pole to tree trunk center) from available plan scales without explicit dimensions.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Site plan shows utility pole symbols (small circles) along OHE boundary lines. Landscape plan shows mitigation trees positioned approximately 3-5 feet from the boundary line where poles would be located. No explicit dimension lines or measurements provided for pole-to-tree distances.","reasoning":"Applicability confirmed (poles present, trees proposed near boundary). However, the requirement specifies 10 lateral feet from pole centerline to tree trunk. While the 3-5 foot distance from boundary strongly suggests non-compliance, the exact pole centerline locations relative to tree trunks cannot be verified from plan annotations alone. This requires either: (1) explicit dimensions, or (2) precise pole location coordinates and tree trunk positions. Without these, status is not-verifiable despite strong indications of violation.","tools_used":["mcp__conductor_tools__vision_check"]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-2.7","status":"n/a","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.10.4"],"applicableAreas":[],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":21}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Electrical plan (Sheet 21) shows pad-mounted transformers and equipment locations, which are located within the building area and interior portions of the site, not near the boundary where proposed landscape trees are being planted. No pad-mounted equipment identified near proposed trees.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Sheet 21 electrical plan indicates transformer pads and pull boxes are interior to site near buildings. Landscape trees marked 'M' near southern boundary are located away from interior equipment.","reasoning":"Trigger condition (pad-mounted equipment near proposed trees) not met based on available plan information. Equipment is interior; trees are boundary-adjacent.","tools_used":[]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-2.8","status":"n/a","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.10.4"],"applicableAreas":[],"sheetReferences":[],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Underground electric equipment (pull boxes, vaults, transformers) locations shown on electrical plan (Sheet 21) are interior to site. Proposed landscape trees are located away from documented underground equipment locations.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Electrical plan shows underground equipment in interior site areas. Proposed trees near southern boundary are not co-located with underground equipment.","reasoning":"Trigger condition (trees within 5 feet of underground equipment) not met based on plan locations.","tools_used":[]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-2.9","status":"n/a","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.10.4"],"applicableAreas":[],"sheetReferences":[],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"No trees proposed within 20 lateral feet of underground electric equipment per electrical plan (Sheet 21). Underground equipment is interior; landscape trees are boundary-adjacent.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Underground equipment shown interior on Sheet 21; proposed trees in landscape plan are at property boundaries, not near interior equipment.","reasoning":"Trigger condition (proximity to underground equipment) not met.","tools_used":[]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-2.10","status":"pass","codeCitations":["Reviewer Convention"],"applicableAreas":["Landscape plan Sheet 31; Plant schedule Sheet 35"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":31},{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":35}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Plant schedule (Sheet 35, Blocks 6, 12, 17) identifies all proposed tree species with both common and scientific names: Shade Trees (Cedar Elm - Ulmus crassifolia; Live Oak - Quercus virginiana); Ornamental Trees (Texas Mountain Laurel - Sophora secundiflora; Mexican Redbud - Cercis canadensis var. mexicana). Landscape plan legend defines tree type symbols (SY, PL, P, M). Plant legend is complete and complies.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Sheet 35 plant schedule lists all tree species with complete common and botanical names. Sheet 31 legend defines tree designation symbols (SY, PL, P, M).","reasoning":"Requirement is met. Plant legend/schedule is present and identifies species near electric facilities with both common and scientific names.","tools_used":[]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-2.11","status":"not-verifiable","codeCitations":["Reviewer Convention"],"applicableAreas":["Landscape plan Sheet 31; Plant schedule Sheet 35"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":31},{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":35}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Large trees (Live Oak and Cedar Elm, both 40+ feet mature height) are identified in plant schedule with species names and mature heights (implied by designation). However, landscape plan does not explicitly differentiate large trees with special notation, callouts, or 'LT' designation to allow field verification of clearances. Trees are listed in plant schedule but not flagged as 'large tree' on the main landscape drawing or in key notes, requiring cross-reference to determine which are large versus standard.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Plant schedule (Sheet 35) lists tree species and container sizes but does not explicitly denote mature heights for each species on the schedule. Landscape plan legend (Sheet 31, Block 5) defines tree type symbols (SY, PL, P, M) but does not include a separate 'large tree' designation or callout.","reasoning":"While species are identified, large trees are not visually differentiated on the landscape plan itself. The requirement for differentiation allows field crews to verify clearances; without an explicit 'large tree' or 'LT' label on the plan, large tree status must be inferred from species knowledge. This creates ambiguity. Status is not-verifiable because the plans do not affirmatively show large tree designation for the large species present.","tools_used":[]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-2.12","status":"pass","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.10.4"],"applicableAreas":["Landscape and site plans"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":9},{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":31}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Site plan and landscape plan show OHE utility lines with standard dashed line notation. No dimension lines or callouts are provided on the plans that measure clearances from utility infrastructure to trees. However, no explicit measurements from pole centerline are shown (which would be incorrect). The absence of clearance dimensions does not evidence measurement from wrong reference point; rather, no clearance measurements are provided at all. Standard practice where clearances are not dimensioned (as in this case) is acceptable per the grouping guidance that 'dimensional compliance can often be derived from surrounding plan geometry.'","agentTrace":{"observation":"Site plan and landscape plan show OHE lines and utility poles with standard symbols. No dimension lines showing clearances from poles or conductors to trees are present on either sheet.","reasoning":"The requirement is violated only if clearances ARE dimensioned incorrectly (from pole centerline instead of conductor). Here, no clearances are dimensioned at all. This does not constitute a violation of this specific requirement, which targets incorrect measurement methodology when dimensions ARE provided. Pass status is appropriate.","tools_used":[]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-2.13","status":"pass","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.10.4"],"applicableAreas":["Landscape plan"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":31}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"No dimension lines showing clearances from tree canopy to electric facilities are provided on the landscape plan. The absence of such canopy-referenced dimensions does not violate this requirement. Standard practice per grouping guidance is to measure from tree trunk center (planting location symbol), not from canopy edge. No incorrect measurement methodology is evidenced.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Landscape plan shows tree symbols (circles) without canopy-to-utility dimension lines.","reasoning":"Like EL-2.12, this requirement applies when clearances ARE dimensioned. No clearance dimensions are provided, so no violation of measurement methodology occurs.","tools_used":[]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-2.14","status":"pass","codeCitations":["Reviewer Convention"],"applicableAreas":["Landscape plan Sheet 31; Site plan Sheet 9"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":9},{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":31}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Landscape plan (Sheet 31) shows proposed trees in spatial relationship to overhead electric (OHE) facility lines. OHE lines are depicted along western and southern property boundaries with utility pole symbols shown. Trees are illustrated relative to these utility lines with clear spatial visibility. Clearance verification can be performed visually by comparing tree locations to OHE line locations on the landscape plan.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Sheet 31 landscape plan clearly shows OHE utility line running along property boundaries with pole symbols indicated. Tree symbols (including mitigation trees marked 'M') are shown relative to these lines.","reasoning":"Requirement is met. Trees are shown on the landscape plan in spatial relationship to overhead facilities, allowing clearance verification.","tools_used":[]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-2.15","status":"fail","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.10.4"],"applicableAreas":["Southern property boundary along OHE utility line"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":31},{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":35}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Trees are proposed within prohibited clearance zones: Large trees (Live Oak and Cedar Elm with mature heights 40+ feet) are positioned approximately 3-5 feet from the southern boundary OHE distribution line, which is less than the 25-foot minimum for large trees and the 15-foot minimum for other trees. No plan notes, correspondences, or Austin Energy written approval letters are present in the site plan package or supplementary documents to authorize this variation. Compliance requires either: (1) relocation of trees to compliant distances, or (2) documented written approval from Austin Energy explicitly authorizing the reduced clearance.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Landscape plan shows trees marked 'M' (mitigation) positioned 3-5 feet from southern boundary OHE line based on vision analysis and scale comparison. Plant schedule identifies these as shade trees including Live Oak and Cedar Elm (both 40+ feet mature height). No Austin Energy approval letters or variance documentation found in plans or supplementary docs.","reasoning":"The 3-5 foot distance is well within both the 15-foot minimum for non-utility-compatible trees and 25-foot minimum for large trees. No documented Austin Energy written approval is present. Applicant must either relocate trees or obtain written approval. This is a clear deficiency.","tools_used":["mcp__conductor_tools__vision_check"]}}]},"fast_mode_state":"off","uuid":"e717295d-1a5b-4e1d-aa43-850df0b5711e"}
