{"level":30,"time":1778188699714,"pid":122,"hostname":"e70bc6df-98e","step":"review-runs","item":"1.md","index":3,"runIndex":"run-1","type":"assistant","message":{"id":"gen_01KR24RWDE71SNRJED3DK3H8E8","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01ATrdaYNQgjn8RqvjiWQVQT","name":"StructuredOutput","input":{"grouping":"1","findings":[{"deficiencyId":"EL-1.1","status":"not-verifiable","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.3"],"applicableAreas":["All proposed buildings (Buildings 1-8) near overhead electric lines"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":9},{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":21}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Overhead electric distribution lines exist along western and southern boundaries. Site plan shows buildings in relation to overhead lines, but no profile/section views with surveyed conductor elevations and clearance dimensions are provided. Horizontal clearances from outside conductors to buildings cannot be verified without elevation data and dimension annotations.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Sheet 9 shows buildings near overhead electric lines (OHE) labeled on the western and southern boundaries. Sheet 21 (Preliminary Electrical Plan) references 'See Sht. 19 for Profile' but Sheet 19/20 contain only water utility profiles, not overhead electric clearance profiles.","reasoning":"The requirement mandates 7.5-foot horizontal sky-to-ground clearance from the outside conductor. While overhead lines are visible on plans, their vertical and horizontal positions relative to buildings are not documented with surveyed elevations, conductor identification, or dimension annotations. Without explicit clearance verification, compliance cannot be confirmed.","tools_used":["vision_check"]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-1.2","status":"not-verifiable","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.3"],"applicableAreas":["All proposed buildings and parking facilities near overhead distribution facilities"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":9},{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":21}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Overhead distribution lines are shown on site plans, but the conductor type (primary, neutral, secondary) and voltage level are not labeled. The 15-foot radial clearance requirement for distribution primary and neutral conductors cannot be verified without conductor type identification and clearance dimension documentation.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Overhead lines labeled as 'OHE' on site plan, but no notation indicating conductor type (primary/neutral/secondary) or voltage classification (<60kV vs. ≥60kV). No radial clearance dimensions shown from conductors to customer facilities.","reasoning":"The 15-foot radial clearance applies only to distribution primary and neutral conductors. Without conductor type identification and documented clearance dimensions in plan and section views, compliance cannot be verified.","tools_used":["vision_check"]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-1.3","status":"not-verifiable","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.3"],"applicableAreas":["Building projections (roofs, eaves, balconies) on all buildings near overhead lines"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":9},{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":21}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"No elevation or section views provided showing building projections in relation to overhead electric conductors. Clearance verification for both 7.5-foot sky-to-ground and 15-foot radial clearances cannot be completed without profile drawings with surveyed conductor elevations and dimension annotations.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Site plan shows buildings and overhead lines in plan view only. No elevation sheets or section details provided showing roof overhangs, eaves, balconies, or other projections relative to overhead conductor elevations.","reasoning":"Building projections (overhangs, awnings, balconies, decks, roofs, patios) require both 7.5-foot sky-to-ground and 15-foot radial clearances. These clearances cannot be assessed from plan view alone; elevation and section views with conductor elevations and dimension annotations are necessary.","tools_used":["vision_check"]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-1.4","status":"n/a","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.3"],"applicableAreas":[],"sheetReferences":[],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"No gas pump canopies are shown or proposed on the site plan.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Review of site plan (Sheet 9) and associated site development documents shows no gas pumps, fueling facilities, or canopy structures proposed on the project site.","reasoning":"This checklist item applies only when gas pump canopies are proposed. The absence of this feature from the site plan means the item is not applicable.","tools_used":[]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-1.5","status":"n/a","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.3"],"applicableAreas":[],"sheetReferences":[],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"No stairs, elevated walkways, or elevated platforms are shown as proposed features on the site plan.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Site plan shows ground-level parking, driveways, and pedestrian walkways. No elevated structures such as bridges, elevated platforms, or elevated walkways connecting buildings are shown.","reasoning":"This item applies only when stairs, elevated walkways, or elevated platforms are proposed. The absence of these features means the item is not applicable.","tools_used":[]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-1.6","status":"not-verifiable","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.3"],"applicableAreas":["Buildings near right-of-way boundaries where electric facilities may be or will be relocated"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":9},{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":3}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Overhead electric lines exist in the right-of-way (Valley View Road, western boundary). Buildings are proposed near this ROW. However, no clearance dimensions or surveyed conductor elevations are provided to verify that both 7.5-foot sky-to-ground and 15-foot radial clearances are maintained from existing or relocated facilities.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Overhead electric lines (OHE) shown on site plan running along Valley View Road (western boundary). Buildings 1 and 7 are positioned near the western property line where ROW electric facilities are located.","reasoning":"When buildings are proposed adjacent to ROW containing electric facilities, permanent clearances (distinct from construction working clearances) must be documented. Without profile views showing surveyed conductor elevations and clearance dimensions, compliance cannot be verified.","tools_used":["vision_check"]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-1.7","status":"fail","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.3"],"applicableAreas":["All buildings (Buildings 1-8) within clearance distance of overhead electric facilities"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":21}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"No building elevation sheets provided with surveyed conductor elevation data and clearance dimension annotations. Sheet 21 references 'See Sht. 19 for Profile' for overhead electric information, but the referenced sheet contains only water utility profile information, not overhead electric conductor elevations required for clearance verification.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Sheet 21 (Preliminary Electrical Design Plan) references 'See Sht. 19 for Profile' for vertical clearance information. However, Sheet 19/20 (Utility Tap Public Plan & Profile) document water line profiles only and do not contain surveyed overhead electric conductor elevations or clearance dimensions.","reasoning":"UCM § 1.10.3 requires surveyed elevations of overhead conductors on building elevation sheets to demonstrate clearances. This documentation is missing from the site plan set.","tools_used":["vision_check"]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-1.8","status":"fail","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.3"],"applicableAreas":["All buildings and parking areas near overhead electric facilities"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":9},{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":21}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"No section or enlarged plan details provided showing dimension lines from the outer electric conductor to the outermost edges of buildings and building projections. Clearance verification dimensions are completely absent from the site plan.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Review of site plan (Sheet 9) and electrical plan (Sheet 21) shows overhead lines depicted, but no cross-section views or enlarged plan details with clearance dimensions from conductors to building edges.","reasoning":"Section views with explicit dimension lines from the outside conductor to building edges are required to verify both 7.5-foot sky-to-ground and 15-foot radial clearances. These are absent.","tools_used":["vision_check"]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-1.9","status":"not-verifiable","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.3"],"applicableAreas":["Fences near overhead electric facilities"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":9},{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":38}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Retaining walls/fences are shown on the site plan near overhead lines, but clearance dimensions from the outside conductor to fence faces are not provided. Without dimension annotations, the 7.5-foot sky-to-ground clearance cannot be verified.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Site plan shows retaining walls/fencing near the southern boundary where overhead electric lines are present. However, no clearance dimensions are dimensioned from the outside conductor to fence faces.","reasoning":"A minimum 7.5-foot horizontal sky-to-ground clearance from the outside conductor is required. Without explicit clearance dimensions from the conductor to the fence, compliance cannot be verified.","tools_used":["vision_check"]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-1.10","status":"not-verifiable","codeCitations":["Reviewer Convention"],"applicableAreas":["Fence locations near existing electric poles"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":9},{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":4}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Electric poles are shown on the existing survey at the northwest and southwest corners. Retaining walls and fences are shown on the site plan. However, the specific horizontal dimension between fence posts and existing poles is not provided. Without explicit dimension callouts, the 10-foot clearance cannot be verified.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Existing survey (Sheet 4) shows utility pole symbols near property corners. Site plan shows retaining walls/fences near these boundaries. However, horizontal dimensions from poles to fence posts are not labeled.","reasoning":"The 10-foot clearance convention requires documented dimensions. Without specific callouts showing distances from poles to fence post locations, compliance cannot be confirmed.","tools_used":["vision_check"]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-1.11","status":"n/a","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.14.0"],"applicableAreas":[],"sheetReferences":[],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"No electric substation fences exist on or immediately adjacent to the site that would require non-conductive isolation panel connections.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Site plan and utility documentation show no Austin Energy substation facilities at or adjacent to the project site. Easements shown are transmission/distribution easements only.","reasoning":"This item applies only when fences connect to or are adjacent to existing Austin Energy substation fences. The absence of substations means the item is not applicable.","tools_used":[]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-1.12","status":"not-verifiable","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.14.0"],"applicableAreas":["Retaining walls and fencing near transmission facilities"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":9},{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":3},{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":38}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"General notes (Sheet 3) reference transmission structures and requirement that no structures impair access within transmission easements. However, the site plan does not clearly identify which overhead lines are transmission (≥60kV) versus distribution (<60kV), nor do the plans specify whether any proposed fencing near transmission lines is constructed of non-conductive material or grounded. Material specifications and grounding details are not provided.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Sheet 3 contains extensive Electric Transmission Notes addressing transmission structures, easements, and clearance requirements. However, the site plan does not label transmission lines separately from distribution lines, and no fence material specifications or grounding details are shown.","reasoning":"Fencing beneath or adjacent to transmission lines requires non-conductive material or proper grounding with detailed specifications. Without labeling which overhead lines are transmission and without material/grounding details, compliance cannot be verified.","tools_used":["vision_check"]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-1.13","status":"not-verifiable","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.3"],"applicableAreas":["Vehicle barrier fencing beneath overhead electric lines"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":9}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Site plan shows retaining walls and parking areas near overhead lines, but no vehicle barrier posts or fencing are explicitly shown beneath overhead lines. If vehicle barriers exist near the overhead lines, clearance verification exhibits (section views with clearance dimensions) are absent.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Site plan shows parking and driveways adjacent to overhead electric lines, but no explicit vehicle barrier posts or crash barriers are identified in location drawings.","reasoning":"If vehicle barriers are present, section exhibits showing the 7.5-foot sky-to-ground clearance from outermost conductor must be provided. The absence of both the barriers and the verification exhibits creates verification uncertainty.","tools_used":["vision_check"]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-1.14","status":"not-verifiable","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.3"],"applicableAreas":["Retaining walls throughout the site, particularly those adjacent to overhead electric lines"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":9},{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":38},{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":39}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Retaining walls are shown on the site plan near overhead lines (particularly southern boundary), but clearance dimensions from the outside electric conductor to the outermost edge of walls are not provided. Clearance verification requires dimension annotations measuring from the conductor, not from the pole.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Site plan (Sheet 9) and wall plan sheets (38-39) show retaining walls near the southern boundary where overhead electric lines (OHE) are present. However, no clearance dimensions from the outside conductor to wall faces are annotated.","reasoning":"The 7.5-foot sky-to-ground clearance must be documented with explicit dimensions from the outside conductor to the wall. Without these dimensions, compliance cannot be verified.","tools_used":["vision_check"]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-1.15","status":"n/a","codeCitations":["Reviewer Convention"],"applicableAreas":[],"sheetReferences":[],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"No Austin Energy substation walls are adjacent to or within 10 feet of the property boundary.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Site documentation shows no Austin Energy substation facilities on or immediately adjacent to the project site.","reasoning":"This item applies only when retaining walls are proposed adjacent to Austin Energy substation property. The absence of substations means the item is not applicable.","tools_used":[]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-1.16","status":"n/a","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.3"],"applicableAreas":[],"sheetReferences":[],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"No emergency access structures (bridges, elevated platforms) are proposed on the site plan.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Site plan shows standard driveway and parking access. No bridges, elevated emergency access structures, or similar facilities are proposed.","reasoning":"This item applies only when emergency access structures are proposed. The absence of such structures means the item is not applicable.","tools_used":[]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-1.17","status":"not-verifiable","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.3"],"applicableAreas":["Retaining walls near overhead electric facilities"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":38},{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":39}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Wall detail sheets (38, 39) show plan and section views of retaining walls, but no section views specifically show clearance dimension annotations from the outer electric conductor to the outermost edge of walls for clearance verification.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Retaining wall details on Sheets 38-39 show wall sections but do not include conductor elevation data or clearance dimensions from conductors to wall faces.","reasoning":"Section views must specifically show the relationship between the outer conductor and the wall face with dimension annotations to verify clearances. These are absent.","tools_used":[]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-1.18","status":"not-verifiable","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.6.2"],"applicableAreas":["Driveways throughout the site, especially where overhead lines exist"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":9},{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":11}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Overhead electric lines exist along western and southern boundaries where internal site driveways and parking access roads are located. The grading plan shows finished floor elevations for buildings and general contours, but no section views are provided showing the finished driveway grades with overhead line clearance dimensions. Mid-span clearance verification is not documented. The determination of whether truck traffic is expected is not explicitly stated.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Grading plan (Sheet 11) shows contours and building elevations but no section views depicting overhead line heights relative to driveway finished grades. No dimension annotations showing 16-foot (no trucks) or 18-foot (with trucks) clearances are present.","reasoning":"Driveway clearance verification requires section views with surveyed overhead conductor elevations and finished driveway grade elevations, plus dimension callouts confirming the minimum 16-foot or 18-foot vertical clearance. These are absent.","tools_used":["vision_check"]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-1.19","status":"n/a","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.6.2"],"applicableAreas":[],"sheetReferences":[],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"No vehicle parking or display areas on concrete pads are shown beneath overhead electric lines.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Site plan shows parking in garage structures and surface parking areas. No open vehicle display pads on concrete beneath overhead lines are shown.","reasoning":"This item applies only when vehicle parking or display on concrete pads is proposed beneath overhead lines. The absence of this feature means the item is not applicable.","tools_used":[]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-1.20","status":"not-verifiable","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.14.0"],"applicableAreas":["Road and driveway grades near transmission facilities"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":3},{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":9},{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":11}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"General notes (Sheet 3) reference transmission structures requiring 25-foot clearances from digging/grading. However, the site plan does not clearly identify transmission line locations or elevations, nor does it provide section views documenting the 30-foot vertical clearance from transmission lines to final road/driveway grades.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Sheet 3 contains extensive transmission facility notes including 25-foot horizontal clearances. However, site plan and grading plan do not clearly demarcate transmission structures or show section views with clearance dimensions for roads/driveways beneath transmission lines.","reasoning":"Transmission lines require 30-foot vertical clearance to final grades. Without clear transmission facility identification and section views with clearance dimensions, compliance cannot be verified.","tools_used":["vision_check"]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-1.21","status":"not-verifiable","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.14.0"],"applicableAreas":["Highway or freeway grading with underbuilt distribution on transmission structures"],"sheetReferences":[],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"No highway or freeway is proposed on the site. Item is potentially inapplicable, but unclear because site plan does not clearly indicate whether transmission structures exist with distribution lines underbuilt beneath them.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Site plan shows Valley View Road (local street) frontage, not highway or freeway construction. General notes reference transmission structures but do not indicate underbuilt distribution configuration.","reasoning":"This item applies to highways/freeways with distribution lines underbuilt on transmission structures. While the site has transmission references, no highway underbuilt configuration is shown. Applicability is unclear without definitive transmission structure documentation.","tools_used":[]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-1.22","status":"not-verifiable","codeCitations":["Reviewer Convention"],"applicableAreas":["Proposed driveways and internal access roads"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":9},{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":4}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Existing survey shows electric poles near property corners. Site plan shows internal driveways and access roads throughout the site. However, no explicit notation indicates whether any proposed driveways are in conflict with existing pole locations, nor is documentation provided showing pole relocation or the 30-foot minimum setback.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Existing survey (Sheet 4) locates utility poles at northwest and southwest corners. Site plan shows driveways but does not specifically note whether these conflict with pole locations or whether poles have been/will be relocated.","reasoning":"If driveway conflicts exist, relocation at least 30 feet from the driveway edge must be documented. Without explicit conflict notation or relocation documentation, compliance cannot be confirmed.","tools_used":["vision_check"]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-1.23","status":"fail","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.3"],"applicableAreas":["All dimensions shown from overhead electric facilities on site plans"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":9},{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":21}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Site plan and electrical plan show overhead electric lines (labeled OHE) but provide no dimension annotations showing clearances from site features to these lines. The requirement mandates that all clearance dimensions originate from the outside conductor, not from the pole centerline. The complete absence of clearance dimension annotations renders verification impossible. Additionally, no notation specifies whether dimensions are measured from the outside conductor or pole center.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Overhead lines are depicted on site plans (Sheets 9, 21) with labels such as 'OHE' and '— OHE —' but no dimension lines extending from the conductors to site features are shown. Existing setback dimensions show distances to property lines, not to overhead conductors.","reasoning":"All clearance dimensions must explicitly originate from the outside conductor location. The critical deficiency is the complete absence of such dimensions on the site plans. This is a fundamental documentation failure required by UCM § 1.10.3.","tools_used":["vision_check"]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-1.24","status":"n/a","codeCitations":["Reviewer Convention"],"applicableAreas":[],"sheetReferences":[],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"No new streetlight poles are proposed on the site plan.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Site plan and utility documents show no proposed streetlight pole installations. The site has parking lot lighting and site lighting but not streetlight poles.","reasoning":"This item applies only when new streetlight poles are proposed. The absence of streetlight poles means the item is not applicable.","tools_used":[]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-1.25","status":"not-verifiable","codeCitations":["Reviewer Convention"],"applicableAreas":["Sidewalks along Valley View Road frontage"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":9},{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":4}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Existing survey shows electric poles at property corners. Site plan shows sidewalk improvements and modifications along Valley View Road frontage. However, the specific dimension from sidewalk alignment to existing poles at property ends is not provided. Without explicit clearance dimensions, verification is not possible.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Poles are shown on existing survey near property corners. Site plan shows sidewalk alignment. However, no specific dimension callout shows the clearance between sidewalk edges and pole locations at property limits.","reasoning":"The convention requires sidewalks to be cleared from existing power poles at each end of property along ROW frontage. Without specific dimension documentation, compliance cannot be confirmed.","tools_used":["vision_check"]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-1.26","status":"not-verifiable","codeCitations":["Reviewer Convention"],"applicableAreas":["Trash enclosures and receptacle locations"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":9}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Site plan shows trash collection areas but does not provide clearance dimension annotations from overhead electric facilities to trash enclosures. A visual inspection cannot determine clearance from raised bins to overhead lines without vertical clearance dimensions and conductor elevation data.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Site plan (Sheet 9) shows trash areas but provides no specific clearance dimensions from overhead lines to trash enclosures. No note addresses the raised-bin clearance requirement during collection.","reasoning":"Trash bins raised during service create dynamic clearance issues. Without section views showing 7.5-foot clearance from conductors accounting for bin raised height, compliance cannot be verified.","tools_used":["vision_check"]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-1.27","status":"not-verifiable","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.3"],"applicableAreas":["All proposed site features, buildings, and improvements within electric easement boundaries"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":9},{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":2},{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":3}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Electric easements (5-foot) are shown on the plat and site plan. General notes explicitly prohibit structures within transmission easements and require 7.5-foot clearances within distribution easements. However, the site plan does not clearly differentiate between distribution and transmission easement areas, nor does it explicitly document that all structures maintain the required 7.5-foot clearance from outside conductors within easement boundaries. The absolute prohibition on structures beneath/over distribution facilities is stated in notes but not visually verified with dimension callouts.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Sheet 3 general notes contain explicit language (Block 16) prohibiting permanent structures within transmission easements. Site plan shows 5-foot electric easement boundaries marked with dashed lines. However, no notation explicitly confirms that structures shown comply with or are excluded from easement areas.","reasoning":"The prohibition is absolute: no structures may be installed under or over distribution facilities. While the easement boundaries are depicted, the site plan does not explicitly document compliance through notation or dimension callouts confirming adequate clearance from outside conductors.","tools_used":["vision_check"]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-1.28","status":"not-verifiable","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.3","UCM § 1.10.6.2"],"applicableAreas":["Water meter locations"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":19},{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":21}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Water meter locations are not clearly identified on utility plans. Service-drop overhead electric lines (if present) and their relationship to water meter locations are not documented with clearance dimension annotations. Without explicit identification of meter locations and overhead service-drop routing, verification is not possible.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Utility plans show overall utility routing but do not clearly mark individual water meter locations. Overhead service-drop lines and meter setback clearances are not dimensioned.","reasoning":"Water meters must maintain 7.5-foot sky-to-ground clearance from overhead service-drop conductors. Without explicit meter location identification and clearance dimensions, compliance cannot be verified.","tools_used":[]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-1.29","status":"not-verifiable","codeCitations":["Reviewer Convention"],"applicableAreas":["Water lines throughout the site"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":19},{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":20}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Utility plans show water line routing beneath buildings and throughout the site. Overhead distribution poles and conductors exist near the property boundaries. However, no clearance dimension annotations are provided from overhead electrical distribution facilities to water lines, nor is documentation provided confirming adequate clearance maintenance.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Utility plan (Sheet 19) shows water line routing. Overhead electric lines are noted on site plan. However, no dimension callouts specify clearances between water lines and overhead poles/conductors.","reasoning":"Clearance standards require documented separation from overhead distribution facilities. Without explicit dimension annotations from plans showing water line routing in relation to overhead facilities, compliance cannot be confirmed.","tools_used":["vision_check"]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-1.30","status":"not-verifiable","codeCitations":["Reviewer Convention"],"applicableAreas":["Buildings near property lines where electric facilities may exist"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":9}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Buildings are shown within 5 feet of property lines on the western (Valley View Road) and southern boundaries where electric facilities exist or may be located in ROW or adjacent property. Specific documentation verifying that permanent structure foundations allow necessary clearance space for electric utility access is not provided.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Site plan shows Buildings 1 and 7 near western property line (Valley View Road ROW where overhead lines exist) with setbacks approximately 37.6 feet noted. However, no documentation explicitly verifies that foundation locations preserve required clearance space for electric facility access and maintenance.","reasoning":"When structures are within 5 feet of property lines and electric facilities exist nearby, documentation must confirm adequate clearance space. This documentation is absent.","tools_used":["vision_check"]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-1.31","status":"fail","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.3"],"applicableAreas":["Driveways and site features where vertical clearances appear marginal"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":9},{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":11}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"No registered surveyor mid-span clearance data is provided showing pole locations and actual overhead conductor elevations. Vertical clearance from overhead lines to driveways and parking areas cannot be calculated or verified without this surveyed data. While site plan shows overhead lines and grading contours, the vertical clearance requirement cannot be satisfied without registered surveyor documentation of mid-span clearances.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Site plan and grading plan show overhead lines and building/driveway elevations but do not include surveyor-documented pole locations or conductor elevations. No mid-span clearance measurements are provided.","reasoning":"When overhead facilities may not meet minimum vertical clearance requirements, UCM § 1.10.3 requires registered surveyor mid-span clearance data. This is completely absent, making verification impossible.","tools_used":[]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-1.32","status":"not-verifiable","codeCitations":["Reviewer Convention"],"applicableAreas":["Overhead line crossings of roads"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":9},{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":21}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Overhead electric lines shown crossing internal driveways and roads. However, no notation or detail indicates whether these crossings are at 90-degree angles to the road alignments. Visual inspection of the scale drawing suggests some crossings may not be perpendicular, but without explicit angle dimensions or notes, verification is not definitive.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Site plan shows overhead lines (OHE) crossing internal site driveways at various angles. No dimension or notation specifies the crossing angle relative to road centerlines.","reasoning":"The convention requires 90-degree crossings. Without explicit angle annotations or crossing detail drawings, compliance cannot be confirmed.","tools_used":["vision_check"]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-1.33","status":"not-verifiable","codeCitations":["Reviewer Convention"],"applicableAreas":["Overhead utility line crossing points"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":21}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Site plans show only underground electric lines (labeled 'E') proposed for the project interior. Overhead electric lines (OHE) are external to the property at boundaries. No section views or crossing details document whether secondary lines cross over or under primary lines where such crossings might occur.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Electrical plan (Sheet 21) labels proposed lines as 'E' (underground electric). Overhead lines shown are exterior boundary lines. No crossing detail drawings provided showing relative elevations of any secondary/primary line crossings.","reasoning":"If secondary and primary overhead lines cross, secondary must pass over primary. Without section details showing the crossing configuration, this cannot be verified.","tools_used":[]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-1.34","status":"n/a","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.3"],"applicableAreas":[],"sheetReferences":[],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"No marquee signs are proposed on the site plan.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Site plan and architectural documents show no proposed marquee signs.","reasoning":"This item applies only when marquee signs are proposed. The absence of such signs means the item is not applicable.","tools_used":[]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-1.35","status":"not-verifiable","codeCitations":["Reviewer Convention"],"applicableAreas":["Proposed underground service infrastructure"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":21}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Electrical design plan shows underground electric service infrastructure but does not clearly indicate whether new power poles are proposed for service conversion. If new poles are proposed, their location relative to existing poles is not dimensioned. Without explicit notation of new pole locations and distances to existing poles, the 20-foot minimum separation cannot be verified.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Sheet 21 shows underground electric lines (E) routing with transformer pads but does not clearly indicate whether new utility poles will be installed or where.","reasoning":"If new poles are proposed, the 20-foot minimum separation from existing poles must be documented with explicit dimension callouts. The absence of clear notation about new pole locations prevents verification.","tools_used":[]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-1.36","status":"not-verifiable","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.3"],"applicableAreas":["Decorative lighting locations"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":31}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Landscape plan may show site lighting/decorative fixtures but clearance verification dimensions and relocation notes relative to overhead electric lines are not provided. Without explicit clearance dimension annotations showing 7.5-foot sky-to-ground and 15-foot radial clearances from conductors to lighting fixtures, or notes indicating relocation of fixtures away from overhead lines, compliance cannot be verified.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Landscape plan (Sheet 31) shows site design including plantings and hardscape but does not provide specific clearance dimensions from decorative lighting fixture locations to overhead electric lines.","reasoning":"Decorative lighting beneath or near overhead lines must maintain required clearances with explicit dimension annotations. Without these, compliance cannot be confirmed.","tools_used":[]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-1.37","status":"not-verifiable","codeCitations":["ECM § 2.4.1.D","ECM § 2.4.2.C","UCM § 1.10.10.4"],"applicableAreas":["Trees and plantings near overhead electric distribution and transmission conductors"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":31},{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":32},{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":35}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Landscape plan (Sheet 31) shows mitigation trees marked 'M' positioned within close proximity to overhead electric lines (OHE) at the southern boundary. Proposed shade trees and ornamental trees are listed on Sheet 35 (Live Oak, Cedar Elm, Texas Mountain Laurel, Mexican Redbud) but the specific location of each tree species on the landscape plan is not cross-referenced with clearance distance callouts. Without species identification on the landscape plan for each tree near overhead lines and without explicit verification that such trees are from the ECM Appendix F Utility Compatible list, compliance cannot be confirmed. Additionally, no lateral distance dimensions are provided from tree locations to overhead conductors.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Landscape plan (Sheet 31) shows 'M' (Mitigation Trees) positioned near overhead lines but does not identify species. Plant list (Sheet 35) specifies species including Live Oak, Cedar Elm, Texas Mountain Laurel, and Mexican Redbud. However, the plan does not indicate which species are planted where, nor does it cross-reference locations to lateral distance measurements from overhead lines.","reasoning":"Trees within 10 lateral feet of distribution (or 50 feet of transmission) must be utility-compatible species from ECM Appendix F and must be documented with lateral distance callouts. Neither the species assignment to locations nor the distance callouts are provided.","tools_used":["vision_check"]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-1.38","status":"not-verifiable","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.9.3.1"],"applicableAreas":["Electric meter locations"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":21}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Electrical design plan shows transformer pads and general utility locations but does not provide enlarged meter area detail sheets showing the specific space reserved for meter installations. Obstructions from fences, walls, equipment, vegetation, or building projections are not explicitly addressed in clearance documentation. Without detailed meter area plans confirming 30-inch-wide front space, 36-inch front depth, and 6.5-foot headroom per UCM § 1.10.9, obstructions cannot be ruled out.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Sheet 21 shows transformer pad locations but does not provide enlarged details of meter areas showing working clearance space dimensions or obstruction verification.","reasoning":"Meter locations require documented working clearances (30\" width, 36\" depth, 6.5' height) with explicit notation of no obstructions. Without enlarged detail sheets confirming these clearances, compliance cannot be verified.","tools_used":[]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-1.39","status":"not-verifiable","codeCitations":["Reviewer Convention"],"applicableAreas":["Buildings near existing streetlight poles"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":9},{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":4}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Existing survey may show streetlight pole locations. Site plan shows buildings relative to property boundaries but does not provide specific clearance dimension annotations from buildings to existing streetlight poles.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Existing survey (Sheet 4) shows utilities with legends including light poles, but specific light pole locations and their dimensions from proposed buildings are not explicitly called out.","reasoning":"Without explicit dimension callouts from buildings to streetlight poles, clearances cannot be verified.","tools_used":[]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-1.40","status":"not-verifiable","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.17.0"],"applicableAreas":["Accessible paths, driveways, and site features near electric poles"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":4},{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":9}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Existing survey shows utility pole locations with legend including down guy anchor symbols. Site plan shows accessible paths and driveways throughout the site. However, the site plan does not explicitly indicate whether down guy wires from existing poles conflict with proposed accessible routes or driveways, nor does it document relocation or conversion to self-supporting poles. Without explicit conflict notation or relocation documentation, compliance cannot be verified.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Existing survey (Sheet 4) legend includes symbols for down guys, but the drawing does not clearly mark where down guys exist or conflict with proposed site features.","reasoning":"Down guy conflicts with accessible paths must be documented with conflict notation or relocation/conversion details. The absence of such documentation creates uncertainty about compliance.","tools_used":["vision_check"]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-1.41","status":"not-verifiable","codeCitations":["Reviewer Convention"],"applicableAreas":["Guy anchor easements for transmission structure guy anchors"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":2},{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":9}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"General notes reference transmission structures and easements. However, the site plan does not clearly indicate whether angled guy anchors from transmission structures exist or will exist on the site. If they do exist, the 10-foot either-side plus 50-foot extension easement boundaries are not depicted on the plat or site plan.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Sheet 3 transmission notes reference transmission structures, but the site plan does not clearly demarcate transmission guy anchor locations or associated easement boundaries.","reasoning":"If transmission guy anchors exist or are proposed, dedicated easements with specific dimensions (10' either side plus 50' extension) must be depicted. Without explicit identification and easement boundaries, compliance cannot be verified.","tools_used":[]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-1.42","status":"not-verifiable","codeCitations":["Reviewer Convention"],"applicableAreas":["Down guy anchor locations from distribution poles"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":2},{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":4},{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":9}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Existing survey shows utility pole locations and legend includes symbols for down guy anchors. However, the plat and site plan do not clearly identify specific down guy anchor point locations or their associated easement boundaries (10-foot width extending 5 feet past anchor ground entry).","agentTrace":{"observation":"Existing survey legend (Sheet 4) includes down guy symbols, but specific anchor locations and easement boundaries are not clearly marked on the plat (Sheet 2) or site plan (Sheet 9).","reasoning":"Down guy anchors require dedicated easements (10' wide, 5' beyond ground entry). Without explicit identification of anchor locations and easement boundaries on the plat and site plan, compliance cannot be verified.","tools_used":["vision_check"]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-1.43","status":"not-verifiable","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.3"],"applicableAreas":["Transformer locations"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":21}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Electrical design plan shows transformer pad locations but provides no section views documenting vertical clearance from overhead electric lines to tops of transformers. The 7.5-foot minimum vertical sky-to-ground clearance cannot be verified without elevation data and dimension annotations.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Sheet 21 shows transformer pad locations in plan view but does not include section views showing vertical relationships between overhead lines and transformer heights.","reasoning":"Transformers beneath overhead lines require documented vertical clearances with explicit dimension annotations from overhead conductors to transformer tops. These are absent.","tools_used":[]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-1.44","status":"not-verifiable","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.4"],"applicableAreas":["Transformers or switchgears in niche service configurations"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":21}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Electrical design plan does not indicate whether any transformers or switchgears will be installed in niche service configurations (covered or recessed installations). If such installations are planned, the required 35-foot vertical clearance inside the niche from the top of equipment to the bottom of overhead structures is not documented.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Sheet 21 shows transformer pad locations but does not specify whether they will be in niche configurations or open-mounted.","reasoning":"If niches are used, 35-foot clearance documentation is required. Without indication of niche use and without clearance documentation, compliance cannot be verified.","tools_used":[]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-1.45","status":"not-verifiable","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.2"],"applicableAreas":["Construction staging areas, equipment laydown zones, and work platforms"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":5}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Construction staging areas and equipment zones are shown on the erosion control plan, but no documentation verifies that these areas maintain the required 10-foot radial clearance from overhead electric lines. This is a construction-phase requirement distinct from permanent clearances. Without explicit dimension annotations or notes, compliance cannot be confirmed.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Erosion control and construction staging plans exist (Sheet 5) but do not include dimension callouts showing 10-foot radial clearances from overhead lines to staging areas.","reasoning":"OSHA and UCM § 1.10.2 require 10-foot radial clearance during construction. This must be explicitly documented in construction logistics plans.","tools_used":[]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-1.46","status":"fail","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.2"],"applicableAreas":["Cover sheets and general notes"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":1},{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":3}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Sheet 3 (General Notes) contains a note stating that a pre-construction safety meeting is required with Austin Energy 48 hours before commencement of construction (Electric Transmission Notes, Item 3). However, this is a transmission-specific note. The required standard note for all projects with overhead high-voltage lines per Texas Health & Safety Code Chapter 752, Section 752.003, stating that the owner/contractor must NOTIFY Austin Energy at least 48 hours before work begins near high-voltage overhead lines, is not present in a standard location (cover sheet or general notes) in the standard required format. The current note references a safety meeting but does not include the explicit 48-hour notification requirement language mandated by Texas law.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Sheet 3 Electric Transmission Notes Item 3 states: 'A pre-construction safety meeting is required with Austin Energy 48 hours before commencement of construction.' This is a safety meeting requirement, not a direct notification requirement per Texas Health & Safety Code § 752.003.","reasoning":"Texas Health & Safety Code Chapter 752, Section 752.003 requires notice to be given, and UCM § 1.10.2 incorporates this requirement. The site plan must include a note explicitly stating that the owner/contractor must notify Austin Energy at least 48 hours before work begins near high-voltage overhead lines. While the safety meeting note addresses safety, it does not provide the required statutory notification language.","tools_used":["vision_check"]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-1.47","status":"n/a","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.6.2"],"applicableAreas":[],"sheetReferences":[],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"No service-mast through-roof installations are proposed on the site plan. All proposed buildings are multi-family townhomes with underground service.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Electrical design plan shows underground electric service infrastructure (transformers, pull boxes, underground lines) feeding the buildings. No rooftop service masts are shown.","reasoning":"This item applies only when service-mast through-roof installations are proposed. The absence of such installations means the item is not applicable.","tools_used":[]}}]}}],"model":"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001","stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":0},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"f7510649-3f32-4a6d-b604-08af9177b220","uuid":"033540c5-3536-4a39-8ed1-a6a1a5a12c30"}
