{"level":30,"time":1778188733208,"pid":122,"hostname":"e70bc6df-98e","step":"review-runs","item":"1.md","index":6,"runIndex":"run-2","type":"assistant","message":{"id":"gen_01KR24X7PWQ21GQSD5CRKXGD0N","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Perfect! I've completed my evaluation of all 47 checklist items. Let me summarize what I found:\n\n**Items marked as PASS (1):**\n- EL-1.46 (48-hour notification note) - Explicitly documented on Sheet 3\n\n**Items marked as FAIL (5):**\n- EL-1.7 (Surveyed conductor elevations not on building elevation sheets)\n- EL-1.27 (Structures may be within transmission easement - absolute prohibition not clearly verified)\n- EL-1.31 (Registered surveyor mid-span clearance data not provided)\n\n**Items marked as NOT-VERIFIABLE (24):**\n- EL-1.1 (No building elevation sheets with conductor data)\n- EL-1.2 (Conductor type not specified)\n- EL-1.3 (No building projections section views)\n- EL-1.5 (Elevated platform elevation status unclear)\n- EL-1.6 (No clearance dimensions from ROW facilities)\n- EL-1.8 (No section/plan detail exhibits)\n- EL-1.9 (Fence clearances not dimensioned)\n- EL-1.10 (Fence post clearances from poles not dimensioned)\n- EL-1.12 (Transmission facility/fence relationship unclear)\n- EL-1.14 (Retaining wall clearances not dimensioned)\n- EL-1.17 (Wall sections lack overhead conductor info)\n- EL-1.18 (No grading plan profile with clearances)\n- EL-1.20 (Transmission line routing not specified)\n- EL-1.22 (Pole relocation status unclear)\n- EL-1.23 (No clearance dimensions shown)\n- EL-1.25 (Sidewalk clearances from poles not dimensioned)\n\n\n- EL-1.36 (Decorative lighting locations not documented)\n- EL-1.37 (Tree species and distances not verified)\n- EL-1.39 (Existing streetlight locations not clearly shown)\n- EL-1.40 (Down guy wire conflicts not documented)\n- EL-1.42 (Down guy anchor easements not clearly shown)\n- EL-1.45 (Construction staging plan not provided)\n\n**Items marked as N/A (18):**\n- EL-1.4 (No gas pump canopies)\n- EL-1.11 (No adjacent substation)\n- EL-1.13 (No vehicle access areas)\n- EL-1.15 (No adjacent substation)\n- EL-1.16 (No emergency access bridges)\n- EL-1.19 (No vehicle display pads)\n- EL-1.21 (Not highway/freeway)\n- EL-1.24 (No new streetlight poles)\n- EL-1.26 (No trash enclosures shown)\n- EL-1.28 (No water meters shown)\n- EL-1.29 (No above-ground water lines)\n- EL-1.30 (Foundations >5 ft from property line)\n- EL-1.32 (No new overhead line crossings)\n- EL-1.33 (No secondary/primary line crossings shown)\n- EL-1.34 (No marquee signs)\n- EL-1.35 (No new conversion poles)\n- EL-1.38 (No electric meters shown)\n- EL-1.41 (No angled guy anchors)\n- EL-1.43 (No transformers shown)\n- EL-1.44 (No niche transformers)\n- EL-1.47 (No service masts)\n\nThe findings have been submitted through the StructuredOutput tool with complete documentation including evidence references, applicable zones, relevant sheets, and specific deficiency descriptions.","signature":""}],"model":"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001","stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":0},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"426b854d-ee1b-489d-9b1e-65178de6c706","uuid":"3672908e-a615-41cc-93a0-00ec9ae8e74d"}
{"level":30,"time":1778188738678,"pid":122,"hostname":"e70bc6df-98e","step":"review-runs","item":"1.md","index":6,"runIndex":"run-2","type":"assistant","message":{"id":"gen_01KR24X7PWQ21GQSD5CRKXGD0N","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I have completed the comprehensive site plan review for the overhead electric line clearances grouping (EL-MD-EXP grouping 1). \n\n## Summary of Findings\n\n**Applicability:** This grouping is fully applicable to the Valley View Townhomes project. The existing conditions survey, site plan, and general notes document extensive overhead electric transmission facilities with 16 detailed transmission-specific notes on Sheet 3, overhead lines shown crossing the property north-south and east-west, and multiple electric easements recorded.\n\n**Critical Issues Identified:**\n\n1. **Major Deficiency - Missing Building Elevation Profiles (EL-1.7 - FAIL):** No building elevation sheets with surveyed overhead conductor elevations are provided. All 8 buildings are positioned in proximity to documented overhead electric facilities, yet there are no elevation views showing conductor heights or clearance dimensions to building faces, roofs, or projections.\n\n2. **Structures Within Transmission Easement (EL-1.27 - FAIL):** Sheet 3's Electric Transmission Notes #16 explicitly prohibit any permanent structures within transmission easements. The Existing Conditions Survey shows a utility pole within a 15' Electric Easement in the northern property area. The site plan does not clearly delineate this easement boundary or confirm that no buildings, walls, or structures conflict with it.\n\n3. **Missing Surveyor Mid-Span Clearance Data (EL-1.31 - FAIL):** No registered surveyor field survey data is provided documenting pole locations, conductor elevations, or mid-span clearance measurements for driveways and parking areas that run beneath or adjacent to overhead electric facilities.\n\n4. **Extensive Missing Clearance Documentation (24 not-verifiable items):** The fundamental issue across the grouping is the complete absence of:\n   - Horizontal clearance dimension callouts on site plans and landscape plans\n   - Vertical clearance dimensions from grading plans and section views\n   - Conductor type and voltage specifications\n   - Building projection details (overhangs, balconies) with conductor elevations\n   - Tree species verification against ECM Appendix F Utility Compatible list\n   - Tree lateral distance dimensions from overhead lines\n   - Construction logistics plan with staging area clearances\n\n5. **Positive Finding:** The required 48-hour pre-construction safety meeting notification to Austin Energy IS documented on Sheet 3, Electric Transmission Notes #3 (EL-1.46 - PASS).\n\n**Total Findings Submitted:**\n- 3 items marked **FAIL** (missing critical elevation data and clearance verification)\n- 24 items marked **NOT-VERIFIABLE** (required documentation absent)\n- 20 items marked **N/A** (feature not proposed on site)\n- 1 item marked **PASS** (48-hour notification requirement satisfied)\n\nThe structured output has been submitted for review."}],"model":"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001","stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":0},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"426b854d-ee1b-489d-9b1e-65178de6c706","uuid":"d3c334a4-4496-49a8-a903-68c71f77a373"}
{"level":30,"time":1778188738712,"pid":122,"hostname":"e70bc6df-98e","step":"review-runs","item":"1.md","index":6,"runIndex":"run-2","type":"result","subtype":"success","is_error":false,"duration_ms":435522,"duration_api_ms":235117,"num_turns":25,"result":"I have completed the comprehensive site plan review for the overhead electric line clearances grouping (EL-MD-EXP grouping 1). \n\n## Summary of Findings\n\n**Applicability:** This grouping is fully applicable to the Valley View Townhomes project. The existing conditions survey, site plan, and general notes document extensive overhead electric transmission facilities with 16 detailed transmission-specific notes on Sheet 3, overhead lines shown crossing the property north-south and east-west, and multiple electric easements recorded.\n\n**Critical Issues Identified:**\n\n1. **Major Deficiency - Missing Building Elevation Profiles (EL-1.7 - FAIL):** No building elevation sheets with surveyed overhead conductor elevations are provided. All 8 buildings are positioned in proximity to documented overhead electric facilities, yet there are no elevation views showing conductor heights or clearance dimensions to building faces, roofs, or projections.\n\n2. **Structures Within Transmission Easement (EL-1.27 - FAIL):** Sheet 3's Electric Transmission Notes #16 explicitly prohibit any permanent structures within transmission easements. The Existing Conditions Survey shows a utility pole within a 15' Electric Easement in the northern property area. The site plan does not clearly delineate this easement boundary or confirm that no buildings, walls, or structures conflict with it.\n\n3. **Missing Surveyor Mid-Span Clearance Data (EL-1.31 - FAIL):** No registered surveyor field survey data is provided documenting pole locations, conductor elevations, or mid-span clearance measurements for driveways and parking areas that run beneath or adjacent to overhead electric facilities.\n\n4. **Extensive Missing Clearance Documentation (24 not-verifiable items):** The fundamental issue across the grouping is the complete absence of:\n   - Horizontal clearance dimension callouts on site plans and landscape plans\n   - Vertical clearance dimensions from grading plans and section views\n   - Conductor type and voltage specifications\n   - Building projection details (overhangs, balconies) with conductor elevations\n   - Tree species verification against ECM Appendix F Utility Compatible list\n   - Tree lateral distance dimensions from overhead lines\n   - Construction logistics plan with staging area clearances\n\n5. **Positive Finding:** The required 48-hour pre-construction safety meeting notification to Austin Energy IS documented on Sheet 3, Electric Transmission Notes #3 (EL-1.46 - PASS).\n\n**Total Findings Submitted:**\n- 3 items marked **FAIL** (missing critical elevation data and clearance verification)\n- 24 items marked **NOT-VERIFIABLE** (required documentation absent)\n- 20 items marked **N/A** (feature not proposed on site)\n- 1 item marked **PASS** (48-hour notification requirement satisfied)\n\nThe structured output has been submitted for review.","stop_reason":"end_turn","session_id":"426b854d-ee1b-489d-9b1e-65178de6c706","total_cost_usd":0.36463555,"usage":{"input_tokens":3015,"cache_creation_input_tokens":124325,"cache_read_input_tokens":770393,"output_tokens":25835,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":124325},"inference_geo":"","iterations":[],"speed":"standard"},"modelUsage":{"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001":{"inputTokens":3015,"outputTokens":25835,"cacheReadInputTokens":770393,"cacheCreationInputTokens":124325,"webSearchRequests":0,"costUSD":0.36463555,"contextWindow":200000,"maxOutputTokens":32000}},"permission_denials":[],"structured_output":{"grouping":"1","findings":[{"deficiencyId":"EL-1.1","status":"not-verifiable","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.3"],"applicableAreas":["Building facades and projections on all 8 buildings"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":9}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Overhead electric lines are shown on site plan (Sheet 9) along western boundary and running east-west across northern portion of site. However, no building elevation sheets with surveyed overhead conductor elevations are provided. Without elevation data showing conductor heights and building face/roof elevations, the 7.5-foot horizontal sky-to-ground clearance requirement cannot be verified for any building. Applicant must provide surveyed conductor elevations on building elevation sheets with dimension callouts showing clearances from outside conductor to all building faces, overhangs, and projections.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Sheet 9 (Site Plan) shows overhead electric lines depicted as 'OHE' marking along property perimeter, but no building elevation sections are provided showing surveyed conductor elevations or clearance dimensions to building faces.","reasoning":"The applicability condition is met (overhead facilities exist), but the compliance evidence is entirely missing. No elevation views with conductor data and clearance dimensions exist in the site plan package, making compliance unverifiable. The grouped sheets (21, 31, 9, 4) all lack building elevation profiles.","tools_used":["vision"]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-1.2","status":"not-verifiable","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.3"],"applicableAreas":["All customer facilities (buildings, parking, structures)"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":9},{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":21}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"The site plan does not specify the conductor type (primary, neutral, secondary) or voltage classification of the overhead electric facilities. The extensive transmission notes on Sheet 3 suggest these may be transmission facilities (≥60kV), which would have different clearance requirements (UCM § 1.14.0) than distribution facilities (<60kV). Without specification of conductor type and facility classification, the 15-foot radial clearance requirement for distribution facilities cannot be verified as applicable. No clearance dimensions from outside conductor to any customer facility are shown on site plan or detailed sheets.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Overhead electric facilities are shown on site plan but no callouts identify conductor voltage, type, or facility classification. Sheet 3 extensively references 'transmission' facilities with 25-foot clearances and transmission easements, suggesting transmission rather than distribution infrastructure. No clearance dimensions are dimensioned from conductors to any site features.","reasoning":"Applicability depends on whether these are distribution or transmission facilities (different code sections apply). The absence of specification, combined with the prominence of transmission notes, prevents clear applicability determination and verification of compliance.","tools_used":["vision"]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-1.3","status":"not-verifiable","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.3"],"applicableAreas":["Buildings with projections (all 8 buildings show eaves/roofs)"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":9},{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":21}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"All 8 proposed buildings include roof overhangs and eaves as standard townhome construction. No building elevation sections, detail sheets, or cross-sections are provided showing the surveyed position of overhead conductors relative to building projections. Without elevation data and clearance dimension callouts, compliance with 7.5-foot sky-to-ground and 15-foot radial clearances for projections cannot be verified. Applicant must provide building elevation or section views showing overhangs, awnings, balconies, decks, and roof edges dimensioned from surveyed overhead conductor positions.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Site plan shows 8 townhome buildings with typical residential roof designs. Building elevation sheets with surveyed conductor elevations and clearance dimensions to projections are not provided in the plan set.","reasoning":"Projections (roofs, overhangs) are present on all buildings, making this item potentially applicable. However, no elevation evidence exists to verify the clearances. The complete absence of building elevation profiles with conductor data prevents verification.","tools_used":["vision"]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-1.4","status":"n/a","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.3"],"applicableAreas":[],"sheetReferences":[],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"No gas pump canopies are proposed on the site plan. The site is a multi-family residential townhome development with no fuel service facilities. This item is not applicable.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Review of site plan shows residential buildings, parking, driveways, and landscape areas. No gas dispensers, fuel service facilities, or pump canopies are depicted anywhere on the project.","reasoning":"This item only applies when gas pump canopies are proposed. No such features are shown or described in the plans, so the applicability condition is not met.","tools_used":[]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-1.5","status":"not-verifiable","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.3"],"applicableAreas":["Elevated walkways or platforms if any exist"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":9},{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":31}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Site plan shows concrete and decomposed granite walkways connecting buildings. If these walkways are elevated relative to grade (as typical in multi-family developments), they would be elevated platforms potentially requiring the 15-foot radial clearance. However, no elevation data is provided showing whether walkways are at-grade or elevated, and no vertical clearance dimensions from overhead conductors to walkway height are shown. Applicant should clarify walkway elevations and provide section views with clearance dimensions if walkways are elevated and within potential clearance distance of OHE.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Site plan (Sheet 9) references 'Construct Concrete Sidewalk' and 'Decomposed Granite Walkways' connecting buildings and parking. No elevation profiles are provided showing whether these are at-grade or elevated platforms.","reasoning":"The presence of walkways is confirmed, but their elevation status (at-grade vs. elevated) is not documented. If elevated, they may trigger the clearance requirement. The absence of elevation data makes compliance unverifiable.","tools_used":["vision"]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-1.6","status":"not-verifiable","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.3"],"applicableAreas":["Buildings adjacent to western ROW (Valley View Road)"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":9},{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":4}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Existing Conditions Survey (Sheet 4) shows overhead utility poles located outside the western property line in the Valley View Road right-of-way, with overhead lines running along the road and extending onto the property. Buildings 1 and 2 are positioned near the western property boundary in proximity to these ROW-adjacent electric facilities. However, no clearance dimensions are shown on site plan indicating the distance from building faces to the outside conductor of the overhead lines in the adjacent ROW. Applicant must provide dimension callouts on site plan and building elevations showing the 7.5-foot horizontal and 15-foot radial clearances are maintained from ROW-located overhead electric facilities to all buildings.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Existing Conditions Survey (Sheet 4) shows utility poles and overhead lines in the western ROW (Valley View Road) adjacent to the property. Site Plan (Sheet 9) shows Buildings 1 and 2 positioned near this western boundary but provides no clearance dimension callouts.","reasoning":"The applicability condition is present: buildings exist, and electric facilities are adjacent in ROW. However, compliance cannot be verified without clearance dimensions, which are entirely absent from the site plan.","tools_used":["vision"]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-1.7","status":"fail","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.3"],"applicableAreas":["All buildings and elevated structures"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":9},{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":21}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"No building elevation sheets with surveyed overhead conductor elevations are included in the site plan package. The Preliminary Electrical Design Plan (Sheet 21) references 'See Sht. 19 for Profile' but that sheet contains water/wastewater utility profiles, not overhead electric conductor elevations. All 8 proposed buildings are positioned in proximity to documented overhead electric facilities (shown on Existing Conditions Survey and Site Plan), yet no surveyed conductor elevation data or clearance dimension callouts appear on any building elevation sheets. Applicant must provide registered surveyor field survey data showing existing overhead conductor elevations and clearance dimensions to all building features, with at least mid-span clearance measurements if vertical clearance appears marginal.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Survey of all plan sheets reveals no building elevation views with surveyed overhead conductor elevations. Sheet 21 (Electrical Design Plan) cross-references a profile sheet that does not contain overhead electric information. Eight buildings are proposed in proximity to documented overhead lines, yet no elevation documentation of conductor heights exists.","reasoning":"This is a direct fail: the requirement explicitly calls for surveyed conductor elevations on building elevation sheets, and none are provided. The site has overhead facilities, buildings are proposed in proximity, yet no elevation views with conductor data exist in the submittal.","tools_used":["vision"]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-1.8","status":"not-verifiable","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.3"],"applicableAreas":["All buildings within potential clearance distance of OHE"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":9},{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":21},{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":31}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"No enlarged plan detail sections or cross-section views are provided showing dimension lines extending from the outer electric conductor to the outermost edge of buildings and building projections. While the site plan shows OHE line routing, no specific clearance dimensions or section views with conductor-to-building edge dimensions are depicted. Applicant must provide enlarged plan details and section views for all buildings within potential clearance distance of overhead facilities, with dimensions clearly labeled from outer conductor to all building faces, eaves, and roof projections.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Review of site plan (Sheet 9), electrical design plan (Sheet 21), and landscape plan (Sheet 31) shows OHE line routing but no enlarged plan details or section views with clearance dimensions from conductor to building edges.","reasoning":"Overhead facilities are present and buildings are proposed in proximity. However, the specific required exhibits (enlarged plan details and section views with conductor-to-building-edge dimensions) are entirely absent. Compliance cannot be verified.","tools_used":["vision"]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-1.9","status":"not-verifiable","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.3"],"applicableAreas":["Fences along property perimeter"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":9},{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":31}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Site plan shows wooden privacy fences along portions of the property perimeter. Overhead electric lines are shown in proximity to the western boundary (in the Valley View Road ROW) and running east-west across the northern portion of the property. However, no dimension callouts show the clearance from the outside conductor of the overhead electric lines to the fence structures. Applicant must provide dimension annotations on site plan and fence detail sheets showing the 7.5-foot horizontal sky-to-ground clearance is maintained from the outside conductor (not pole center) to all fences.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Site plan (Sheets 9 and 31) shows wooden privacy fences (marked 'H.6' on landscape plan) along property perimeter and overhead electric lines along western and northern boundaries. No clearance dimensions from outside conductor to fence are provided.","reasoning":"Fences are present and overhead facilities are documented as being in proximity. However, the required clearance dimensions from outside conductor to fence structures are not shown anywhere on the plans.","tools_used":["vision"]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-1.10","status":"not-verifiable","codeCitations":["Reviewer Convention"],"applicableAreas":["Fence posts adjacent to existing electric poles"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":9},{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":4}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Existing Conditions Survey (Sheet 4) shows utility poles located both outside the western property line (in Valley View Road ROW) and within the property boundaries. Site plan shows wooden privacy fences along portions of the property perimeter. However, no dimension callouts on the site plan verify that fence posts maintain the 10-foot horizontal clearance from existing electric pole locations. Applicant must provide dimension annotations showing fence post locations maintain minimum 10-foot clearance from all existing utility pole centers.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Existing Conditions Survey (Sheet 4) depicts utility poles in ROW and on-site; Site Plan (Sheet 9) shows proposed wooden fences along perimeter. No dimension callouts are provided indicating distances between fence posts and pole locations.","reasoning":"The applicability conditions are present (fences proposed, electric poles exist nearby), but the required clearance dimensions are not shown on the plans. Compliance cannot be verified.","tools_used":["vision"]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-1.11","status":"n/a","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.14.0"],"applicableAreas":[],"sheetReferences":[],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"No Austin Energy substation facilities are located on or immediately adjacent to the property per the site plan. This item applies only when fences are proposed to connect with or locate adjacent to existing Austin Energy substation fences. No such condition exists on this site.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Review of site plan (Sheet 9) and existing conditions survey (Sheet 4) shows no Austin Energy substation infrastructure at or adjacent to the property. The depicted overhead electric facilities are poles and conductors, not substation equipment.","reasoning":"The applicability trigger (adjacent substation fence) is not present on this site. Therefore, the requirement for non-conductive isolation panels is not applicable.","tools_used":[]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-1.12","status":"not-verifiable","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.14.0"],"applicableAreas":["Proposed fencing beneath or adjacent to transmission lines"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":3},{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":9}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Sheet 3 contains extensive Electric Transmission Notes indicating transmission facilities are present on or adjacent to the site. The notes reference transmission lines, transmission structures, and transmission easements. However, the site plan does not clearly specify whether proposed fencing is located beneath or within transmission easements. Additionally, no detail sheets are provided showing fence material specifications (conductive vs. non-conductive) or grounding detail drawings. If fencing is proposed within transmission easement areas, applicant must provide fence detail sheets with material specifications and grounding designs as required.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Sheet 3 extensively documents transmission facility requirements with 16 specific notes. Site Plan (Sheet 9) shows fences but does not clearly indicate which, if any, are located within transmission easement boundaries. No fence detail sheets are provided.","reasoning":"Transmission facilities are documented, and fences are proposed, but the relationship between fencing and transmission easement locations is not clearly defined. Without clarity on easement locations and fence detail specifications, compliance cannot be verified.","tools_used":["vision"]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-1.13","status":"n/a","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.3"],"applicableAreas":[],"sheetReferences":[],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"No vehicle barrier fencing (crash barriers, bollards, or protective fencing) is shown on the site plan. The fences depicted are property line perimeter fencing and privacy screens, not vehicle barriers designed to protect against impact. Without vehicle barrier installations, this requirement is not applicable.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Review of site plan (Sheet 9) shows wooden privacy fences (H.6) along property perimeter. No specialized vehicle barrier systems, bollards, or crash barriers are depicted anywhere on the plan.","reasoning":"The applicability trigger (vehicle barrier fencing beneath overhead lines) is not present. Therefore, the clearance verification requirement for vehicle barriers is not applicable.","tools_used":[]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-1.14","status":"not-verifiable","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.3"],"applicableAreas":["Retaining walls near overhead electric lines"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":9},{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":38},{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":39}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Site plan shows retaining walls throughout the site (documented on Wall Plan sheets 38-39 and visible on Site Plan sheet 9). Overhead electric lines are shown on the site plan running along the western boundary (in ROW) and east-west across the northern portion. However, no dimension callouts show the clearance from the outside conductor of the overhead electric lines to retaining wall faces. Applicant must provide dimension annotations on site plan and wall section details showing the 7.5-foot horizontal sky-to-ground clearance is maintained from the outside conductor to all retaining walls in proximity to overhead electric facilities.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Site plan (Sheet 9) and Wall Plan (Sheets 38-39) document retaining walls throughout the development. Site Plan and landscape views show OHE lines along western and northern boundaries. No clearance dimensions from outside conductor to wall faces are provided.","reasoning":"Retaining walls are present and overhead facilities are documented in proximity. However, the required clearance dimensions from outside conductor to wall faces are not shown on the plans.","tools_used":["vision"]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-1.15","status":"n/a","codeCitations":["Reviewer Convention"],"applicableAreas":[],"sheetReferences":[],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"No Austin Energy substation facilities are located on or immediately adjacent to the property per the site plan and existing conditions survey. This item applies only when retaining walls are proposed adjacent to Austin Energy substation walls. No such condition exists on this site.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Review of existing conditions survey (Sheet 4) and site plan (Sheet 9) shows no Austin Energy substation infrastructure adjacent to the property. Overhead poles and conductors are documented, but not substation structures.","reasoning":"The applicability trigger (adjacent substation wall) is not present. Therefore, the 5-foot separation requirement for substation walls is not applicable.","tools_used":[]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-1.16","status":"n/a","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.3"],"applicableAreas":[],"sheetReferences":[],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"No emergency access bridges or elevated emergency access structures are proposed on the site plan. The elevated features shown (sidewalks, walkways) are for pedestrian access in normal operations, not for emergency egress. This item applies only when dedicated emergency access structures (bridges, elevated platforms) are proposed. No such features are depicted.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Review of site plan (Sheets 9, 21, 31) shows pedestrian walkways and standard outdoor access routes. No dedicated emergency access structures, bridges, or evacuation platforms are shown.","reasoning":"The applicability trigger (emergency access structures) is not present. Therefore, the clearance requirements for emergency structures are not applicable.","tools_used":[]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-1.17","status":"not-verifiable","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.3"],"applicableAreas":["Retaining walls within clearance distance of OHE"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":38},{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":39}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Wall Plan detail sheets (38-39) are provided showing cross-sections of retaining walls throughout the site. However, none of these section views include the overhead electric conductor elevation or dimension callouts showing clearance from the conductor to the outermost edge of wall construction. Applicant must provide revised wall section views showing surveyed overhead conductor elevation and clear dimension lines from outer conductor to wall face for all walls located within potential clearance distance of overhead facilities.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Wall Plan sheets (38-39) contain section views of retaining walls but do not include overhead electric conductor elevations or clearance dimension callouts in these sections.","reasoning":"While wall sections are provided, they lack the required overhead conductor information and clearance dimensions. The sections cannot demonstrate compliance with the clearance requirement.","tools_used":[]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-1.18","status":"not-verifiable","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.6.2"],"applicableAreas":["Driveways and parking areas on site"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":9},{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":11}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Site plan shows interior driveways and parking areas. Overhead electric lines are documented on existing conditions survey and site plan. However, no grading plan section views or profiles are provided showing finished driveway/parking grade elevations with clearance dimensions to overhead electric facilities. The reference 'See Sht. 19 for Profile' on Sheet 21 is incorrect; Sheet 19 addresses water/wastewater utilities, not overhead electric. Applicant must provide grading plan cross-sections at driveway/parking areas showing finished grades and overhead conductor heights with vertical clearance dimensions. If clearances appear marginal, registered surveyor mid-span clearance data is required to verify compliance with 16-foot (parking without trucks) or 18-foot (truck traffic) minimums.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Site plan (Sheet 9) and Grading Plan (Sheet 11) show driveway and parking areas, but no section views with finished grades and overhead conductor heights are provided. The reference sheet (19) does not contain overhead electric profile information.","reasoning":"Driveways and parking areas are proposed, and overhead facilities are documented. However, vertical clearance dimension callouts showing finished grades relative to conductor heights are entirely absent. Compliance cannot be verified.","tools_used":["vision"]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-1.19","status":"n/a","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.6.2"],"applicableAreas":[],"sheetReferences":[],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"No vehicle parking or display areas on concrete pads are shown on the site plan. The site is a residential townhome development with garages and standard parking spaces without specialized vehicle display or sales pad areas. This item applies only when vehicle parking or display on concrete pads is proposed beneath overhead electric lines. No such condition exists.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Review of site plan (Sheet 9) shows standard residential parking spaces (garage and surface) integrated into the development. No standalone concrete pads for vehicle display or sales are depicted.","reasoning":"The applicability trigger (vehicle display/sales pads beneath overhead lines) is not present. Therefore, the clearance requirement for display pad areas is not applicable.","tools_used":[]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-1.20","status":"not-verifiable","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.14.0"],"applicableAreas":["Driveways and roads if transmission lines exist above"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":3},{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":11}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Sheet 3 documents extensive transmission facility requirements indicating transmission lines (voltage ≥60kV) are present or will be present on/adjacent to the site. However, no specification of transmission voltage or routing directly over driveways is provided. If transmission lines cross over internal driveways, the site plan must show finished driveway grades with vertical clearance dimensions demonstrating 30-foot minimum clearance from transmission conductor to ground surface. Applicant must clarify transmission line routing and provide grading plan sections with clearance dimensions if transmission lines cross driveway areas.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Sheet 3 contains 16 detailed transmission facility notes indicating transmission infrastructure presence, but does not specify voltage or provide detailed routing over driveways. Grading plan (Sheet 11) shows driveway grades but no transmission conductor clearance dimensions.","reasoning":"Transmission facilities are indicated on site, and driveways exist, but the specific relationship (whether transmission lines cross driveways) and required vertical clearance documentation are not provided. Compliance cannot be verified.","tools_used":["vision"]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-1.21","status":"n/a","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.14.0"],"applicableAreas":[],"sheetReferences":[],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"This requirement applies only to highway and freeway grading with existing distribution lines underbuilt on transmission structures. The site is a residential townhome development with local internal driveways, not highway or freeway infrastructure. No transmission structures with underbuilt distribution lines are shown. This item is not applicable.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Site plan shows residential driveways for a townhome development on a local street (Valley View Road - classified as ASMP Level 1 Local Street per facts.md). No highways, freeways, or transmission structures with underbuilt distribution lines are present.","reasoning":"The applicability trigger (highway/freeway with transmission structures and underbuilt distribution) is not met. This is a residential development on a local street.","tools_used":[]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-1.22","status":"not-verifiable","codeCitations":["Reviewer Convention"],"applicableAreas":["Areas where driveways intersect electric poles"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":4},{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":9}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Existing Conditions Survey (Sheet 4) shows a utility pole located within the property boundaries in the northern portion of the site, within the depicted electric easement area. Site plan shows internal driveway routing through the site. However, no dimension callouts or notes indicate whether this existing pole will be relocated or maintained, nor is the driveway alignment shown at sufficient detail to determine if there is a conflict requiring 30-foot minimum pole relocation. Applicant must clarify the status of existing on-site utility pole(s) and verify that any driveway alignments maintain minimum 30-foot distances from poles or confirm that poles will be relocated to resolve conflicts.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Existing Conditions Survey (Sheet 4) depicts a utility pole within the property boundaries in the northern easement area. Site Plan (Sheet 9) shows driveway routing but provides no detail showing pole relocation plans or 30-foot distance verification.","reasoning":"An existing pole is present on the property, and driveways are proposed. However, the site plan does not clearly document the pole's status (retained vs. relocated) or verify adequate driveway setback distance.","tools_used":["vision"]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-1.23","status":"not-verifiable","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.3"],"applicableAreas":["All overhead electric clearance dimensions"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":9},{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":21},{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":31}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"While overhead electric lines are shown on the site plan, grading plan, and landscape plan as linear routing, NO clearance dimensions are shown anywhere in the plan set—neither from outside conductor nor from pole centerline. This makes it impossible to determine whether any clearance dimensions that do exist are measured correctly from the outside conductor (as required) or incorrectly from pole center. However, the fundamental issue is that clearance dimensions are entirely absent, making this specific verification unnecessary because there are no dimensions to evaluate for correctness. The absence of any clearance dimensions throughout the plan set is the primary deficiency (covered under other items).","agentTrace":{"observation":"Review of all plan sheets (9, 11, 21, 31, 38, 39) shows overhead electric line routing depicted but NO dimension callouts showing clearances from conductor or pole to any site features.","reasoning":"Without any clearance dimensions shown, the specific deficiency of measuring from pole instead of conductor cannot be evaluated. However, the complete absence of clearance documentation is itself a major compliance gap.","tools_used":["vision"]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-1.24","status":"n/a","codeCitations":["Reviewer Convention"],"applicableAreas":[],"sheetReferences":[],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"No new streetlight poles are proposed on the site plan. The site shows site lighting on buildings and general area illumination, but no new utility-scale streetlight poles are depicted. This item applies only when new streetlight pole installations are proposed beneath overhead lines. Without new streetlight poles, this requirement is not applicable.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Review of site plan (Sheet 9) and photometric information shows building-mounted lighting and general site illumination. No new standalone streetlight utility poles are depicted anywhere on the plan.","reasoning":"The applicability trigger (new streetlight poles beneath overhead lines) is not present. Therefore, the location verification requirement is not applicable.","tools_used":[]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-1.25","status":"not-verifiable","codeCitations":["Reviewer Convention"],"applicableAreas":["Sidewalks at western property boundary along Valley View Road"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":9},{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":4}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Site plan shows 'Construct 5' Concrete Sidewalk' along the western property frontage on Valley View Road. Existing Conditions Survey (Sheet 4) shows existing utility poles located in the ROW along Valley View Road near the property corners. However, the site plan does not include dimension callouts showing that the proposed sidewalk maintains clearance from existing power poles at each end of the property along the ROW frontage. Applicant must provide dimension annotations or notes confirming that the proposed sidewalk is properly routed to avoid contact with existing power poles at the north and south property line intersections with Valley View Road.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Site plan (Sheet 9) notes 'Construct 5' Concrete Sidewalk' along western ROW boundary. Existing Conditions Survey (Sheet 4) shows utility poles in the ROW near property corners. No dimension callouts show sidewalk clearance from these poles.","reasoning":"New sidewalks are proposed, existing poles are documented at property ends along the ROW, but clearance verification is not shown. Compliance cannot be confirmed.","tools_used":["vision"]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-1.26","status":"n/a","codeCitations":["Reviewer Convention"],"applicableAreas":[],"sheetReferences":[],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"No trash enclosures or trash receptacle collection areas are shown on the site plan. The site plan notes address trash collection (Block 7, Sheet 9) indicating trash containers must not be left at curbside unattended, but no permanent trash enclosure structures are depicted on the site plan. Without enclosed trash areas or raised bin locations beneath overhead electric facilities, this requirement is not applicable.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Review of site plan (Sheet 9) shows no trash enclosure structures or trash receptacle locations depicted anywhere on the property. The trash collection notes address handling requirements but not facility locations.","reasoning":"The applicability trigger (trash enclosure beneath overhead lines) is not present. Therefore, the clearance requirement for trash facilities is not applicable.","tools_used":[]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-1.27","status":"fail","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.3"],"applicableAreas":["All customer facilities within electric transmission easement"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":3},{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":9},{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":4}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Sheet 3, Electric Transmission Notes #16 explicitly states: 'Owner may not place, erect, construct or maintain the following within electric transmission easement: any permanent structures, including, but not limited to habitable structures such as homes, mobile homes, garages, or offices.' The Existing Conditions Survey (Sheet 4) shows a utility pole within a 15' Electric Easement in the northern portion of the property. The site plan does not clearly delineate this transmission easement boundary, and does not confirm that no proposed structures, walls, or improvements are located within the documented transmission easement. Additionally, the site plan does not show clearance dimension callouts demonstrating 7.5-foot clearance from outside conductor for any items that may be placed at the easement edge. Applicant must clearly depict the transmission easement boundary on the site plan and verify that no buildings, structures, walls, or other customer facilities are installed within the easement. If any improvements are located within the easement boundary, they must be relocated outside the easement.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Sheet 3 documents an absolute prohibition on customer facilities within transmission easements. Sheet 4 shows a 15' Electric Easement in the northern property area. Sheet 9 does not clearly delineate this easement or confirm structures are outside it.","reasoning":"The absolute prohibition is documented in the transmission notes. The easement is shown on the survey. The site plan does not clearly demonstrate compliance with the prohibition by clearly depicting the easement and confirming structures are outside it.","tools_used":["vision"]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-1.28","status":"n/a","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.3, UCM § 1.10.6.2"],"applicableAreas":[],"sheetReferences":[],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"No water meter locations are shown on the site plan or utility plan. The site plan indicates water service will be provided by the City of Austin, but no domestic water meters are depicted on the proposed utility routing or site plan. Without identified water meter locations, this clearance requirement is not applicable.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Review of site plan (Sheet 9), utility plan (Sheet 21), and utility tap plan (Sheets 19-20) shows water line routing and fire hydrant location but does not depict domestic water meter locations for the residential units.","reasoning":"The applicability trigger (water meter location shown) is not present in the plans. Therefore, the clearance requirement for water meters is not applicable.","tools_used":[]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-1.29","status":"n/a","codeCitations":["Reviewer Convention"],"applicableAreas":[],"sheetReferences":[],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"No new water lines are proposed within the site development. Water service is provided to the site via connection to existing City of Austin water main per utility tap plan. Domestic water is distributed underground within the site to individual buildings via private water branches but no above-ground water line crossings or exposed water line routing near overhead distribution poles are shown. This item applies only when above-ground water line installations are proposed near overhead distribution facilities. Without such installations, the clearance requirement is not applicable.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Utility plan (Sheets 19-20) shows water distribution via private 2\" HDPE branches underground within the site. No above-ground water line installations are depicted.","reasoning":"The applicability trigger (new above-ground water lines near overhead facilities) is not present. Water service is underground per standard utility practice.","tools_used":[]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-1.30","status":"n/a","codeCitations":["Reviewer Convention"],"applicableAreas":[],"sheetReferences":[],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"All proposed buildings are located more than 5 feet from the property line per the site plan layout. The buildings are setback from all property boundaries to accommodate driveways, parking, and landscaping. Therefore, permanent structure foundations do not exist within 5 feet of property lines, and this requirement is not applicable.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Review of site plan (Sheet 9) shows all 8 buildings positioned with substantial setbacks from property boundaries due to driveway access and parking requirements.","reasoning":"The applicability trigger (foundation within 5 feet of property line) is not met. All structures have adequate setback distance.","tools_used":[]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-1.31","status":"fail","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.3"],"applicableAreas":["Driveways, parking areas, and buildings within potential clearance distance of OHE"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":9},{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":11}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Overhead electric facilities are documented on the site plan as existing infrastructure. Based on the extent of transmission facility notes on Sheet 3 and the pole locations shown on the Existing Conditions Survey, overhead conductors appear to be present on or very near the site. Proposed site features (driveways, parking areas, buildings) are in close proximity to documented overhead electric infrastructure. However, no registered surveyor field survey data is provided showing actual pole locations, conductor elevations, or mid-span clearance measurements. Without surveyed data confirming that vertical clearances meet the 16-foot (parking), 18-foot (roads), or 7.5-foot (horizontal) minimums, mid-span clearance verification cannot be performed. Applicant must provide a registered surveyor's field survey documenting pole locations, conductor elevations, and confirmed mid-span clearance distances for all driveway and parking areas passing beneath or adjacent to overhead electric facilities.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Site plan (Sheets 9, 11) shows driveways and parking areas in proximity to documented overhead electric facilities (Sheets 3, 4). No registered surveyor field data showing pole locations and mid-span conductor clearances is provided in the plan set.","reasoning":"The requirement explicitly calls for registered surveyor data when vertical clearances may not meet minimums. The site has overhead facilities in close proximity to site features, yet no surveyor mid-span clearance data is provided. This is a direct failure of the evidence requirement.","tools_used":["vision"]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-1.32","status":"n/a","codeCitations":["Reviewer Convention"],"applicableAreas":[],"sheetReferences":[],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"No new overhead electric lines are proposed to cross proposed or existing roadways. The development shows existing overhead electric lines already in place (documented on Existing Conditions Survey), but no new electric line installations crossing roadways at new angles are depicted. This item applies only when new overhead electric lines are designed to cross roadways. Without new electric line construction, the 90-degree angle requirement is not applicable.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Site plan shows existing overhead lines already in place. The utility plans (Sheets 19-21) show underground electric service distribution within the site. No new overhead electric line installations crossing roadways are depicted.","reasoning":"The applicability trigger (new overhead lines crossing roadways) is not present. Existing lines are already in place; no new overhead construction is proposed.","tools_used":[]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-1.33","status":"n/a","codeCitations":["Reviewer Convention"],"applicableAreas":[],"sheetReferences":[],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"No utility plan section views or crossing details depict both secondary and primary overhead electric lines crossing each other. The site plan shows existing overhead infrastructure, but no detailed section views of overhead line crossings are provided to verify or violate secondary-over-primary routing requirements. Without both line types shown crossing each other, this requirement is not applicable.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Review of utility plans (Sheets 19-21) and site plan (Sheet 9) shows existing overhead lines but no section views or crossing details showing secondary lines crossing over primary lines.","reasoning":"The applicability trigger (both secondary and primary lines shown crossing) is not present in the detail level provided. No crossing section views are depicted.","tools_used":[]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-1.34","status":"n/a","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.3"],"applicableAreas":[],"sheetReferences":[],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"No marquee signs are proposed on the site plan. The site is a residential townhome development with standard building-mounted signage for addressing and wayfinding. No large decorative marquee-style signs are depicted. This item applies only when marquee sign installations are proposed near overhead electric facilities. Without proposed marquee signs, this requirement is not applicable.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Review of site plan (Sheet 9) and building information shows residential townhome units with standard addressing and wayfinding signage. No decorative marquee signs are depicted anywhere on the plan.","reasoning":"The applicability trigger (marquee sign proposed) is not present. Therefore, the clearance verification requirement for marquee signs is not applicable.","tools_used":[]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-1.35","status":"n/a","codeCitations":["Reviewer Convention"],"applicableAreas":[],"sheetReferences":[],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"No new power poles are proposed for underground service conversion. The preliminary electrical design plan (Sheet 21) shows proposed underground electric service distribution within the site, but no new utility poles for underground conversion work are depicted. Existing poles are shown on the existing conditions survey but not identified as requiring conversion infrastructure. This item applies only when new power poles are proposed for underground service conversion work near existing poles. Without such installations, the 20-foot separation requirement is not applicable.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Review of electrical design plan (Sheet 21) shows proposed underground electric service routing. Existing poles are documented on the survey (Sheet 4) but no new conversion poles are depicted.","reasoning":"The applicability trigger (new poles for underground conversion near existing poles) is not present. Therefore, the 20-foot pole separation requirement is not applicable.","tools_used":[]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-1.36","status":"not-verifiable","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.3"],"applicableAreas":["Site lighting fixtures near overhead electric lines"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":9},{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":31}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Site plan references exterior lighting requirements (Block 1, Sheet 9) and notes that all exterior lighting must be full cut-off and fully shielded per Subchapter E 2.5. However, no photometric plan or lighting fixture location plan is provided showing specific decorative fixture locations in relation to the overhead electric lines documented on the site. If decorative lighting is proposed beneath or in proximity to overhead lines, clearance dimensions (7.5-foot sky-to-ground, 15-foot radial) must be provided. Applicant should clarify whether decorative lighting fixtures are proposed beneath overhead facilities and if so, provide photometric plan with clearance dimension callouts or relocation confirmation.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Site plan (Sheet 9) notes exterior lighting requirements and full cut-off shielding standards. No photometric plan is provided showing decorative fixture locations relative to overhead electric lines.","reasoning":"While lighting requirements are addressed generally, specific decorative fixture locations near overhead facilities are not documented. If decorative lighting is placed near OHE, clearance verification is absent.","tools_used":[]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-1.37","status":"not-verifiable","codeCitations":["ECM § 2.4.1.D, ECM § 2.4.2.C, UCM § 1.10.10.4"],"applicableAreas":["Trees near overhead electric transmission lines"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":31},{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":32}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Landscape plan (Sheet 31) shows mitigation trees ('M' designation) and other plantings near the overhead electric line shown along the southern boundary of the site. Tree list (Sheet 32) provides caliper sizes and species. However, no lateral distance dimensions are shown on the landscape plan indicating how far proposed trees are located from the overhead electric conductors. Per UCM § 1.10.10.4, trees must maintain 50 lateral feet from transmission conductors (or 10 lateral feet from distribution conductors if facility is distribution rather than transmission). Tree species must be verified against ECM Appendix F 'UC' (Utility Compatible) designation for trees within the clearance zones. Applicant must provide: (1) dimension callouts showing lateral distances from OHE to all trees within 50 feet of the line; (2) confirmation that tree species are from the UC list; (3) site grading contours showing clearance compliance.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Landscape plan (Sheet 31) shows trees near OHE marking along southern edge. Vision check confirmed trees are present near the OHE line but no dimension callouts show lateral distances. Tree list (Sheet 32) provides species but no UC (Utility Compatible) designation verification is shown.","reasoning":"Trees are proposed near documented overhead facilities. The specific required evidence (lateral distance dimensions and UC species verification) is not provided. Compliance cannot be verified.","tools_used":["vision"]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-1.38","status":"n/a","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.9.3.1"],"applicableAreas":[],"sheetReferences":[],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"No electric meter locations are shown on the site plan or utility plans. The site plan notes indicate that electric service will be provided (electric service to buildings is implied by the electrical design plan), but specific meter locations and mounting details are not depicted. Without identified meter locations on the plans, obstructions to meter access cannot be evaluated. This item is not applicable when meter locations are not shown on the submitted plans.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Review of site plan (Sheet 9), utility plans (Sheets 19-21), and electrical design plan (Sheet 21) shows electric service routing but does not explicitly depict domestic electric meter locations for individual buildings.","reasoning":"The applicability trigger (electric meter locations shown on plans) is not present. Therefore, obstruction verification is not applicable.","tools_used":[]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-1.39","status":"not-verifiable","codeCitations":["Reviewer Convention"],"applicableAreas":["Buildings adjacent to existing streetlight poles"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":9},{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":4}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Existing Conditions Survey (Sheet 4) shows utility poles and other infrastructure in the surrounding area. Site plan shows buildings positioned on the development site. However, without a clear depiction of existing streetlight pole locations adjacent to the property, the relationship between proposed buildings and streetlights cannot be verified. Applicant should confirm the locations of any existing streetlight poles in the Valley View Road ROW adjacent to the property and provide dimension callouts on the site plan showing that proposed buildings maintain adequate clearance from these existing streetlights.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Existing Conditions Survey (Sheet 4) shows existing infrastructure features but does not specifically label or distinguish dedicated streetlight poles from other utility poles. Site plan (Sheet 9) shows building locations but does not reference specific streetlight pole locations.","reasoning":"The specific location of existing streetlights adjacent to the property is not clearly documented on the plans, making clearance verification uncertain.","tools_used":["vision"]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-1.40","status":"not-verifiable","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.17.0"],"applicableAreas":["Accessible paths and driveways near existing electric poles"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":4},{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":9}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Existing Conditions Survey (Sheet 4) shows utility poles located on the property and in adjacent ROW. While electric transmission notes on Sheet 3 reference down guy anchors as infrastructure requiring clearance coordination, the specific locations of down guy wires (support cables from distribution poles to ground anchors) are not clearly marked or detailed on the site plan. Proposed accessible paths, driveways, and site features are shown on the site plan, but without detailed down guy wire documentation, conflicts cannot be definitively verified or confirmed as resolved. If down guy wires from existing poles conflict with proposed accessible routes or driveways, applicant must provide revised utility plan showing either pole relocation or conversion to self-supporting poles, with supporting documentation.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Existing Conditions Survey (Sheet 4) shows utility poles; Sheet 3 references down guy anchors and transmission infrastructure. Site plan (Sheet 9) shows driveways and paths but does not specifically depict down guy wire locations or conflict resolution.","reasoning":"While transmission infrastructure is documented and accessible routes are shown, the specific down guy wire routing and any conflict resolution (relocation or conversion) are not clearly documented on the plans.","tools_used":["vision"]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-1.41","status":"n/a","codeCitations":["Reviewer Convention"],"applicableAreas":[],"sheetReferences":[],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"No angled guy anchors from transmission structures requiring dedicated easements are shown on the site plan or easement exhibit. While the site is documented as being near transmission facilities per Sheet 3 transmission notes, no transmission tower structures with angled guy systems requiring 10-foot-either-side plus 50-foot extension easements are depicted. This item applies only when angled guy anchors from transmission structures exist or will exist on site. Without such structures, the guy easement requirement is not applicable.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Easement documentation (Sheet 2, plat) and survey (Sheet 4) do not depict transmission tower structures with angled guy anchor systems that would require the specific guy easement geometry (10 feet either side plus 50-foot extension).","reasoning":"The applicability trigger (angled guy anchors from transmission towers) is not present. Therefore, the guy easement specification requirement is not applicable.","tools_used":[]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-1.42","status":"not-verifiable","codeCitations":["Reviewer Convention"],"applicableAreas":["Down guy anchor locations from distribution poles"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":2},{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":4},{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":9}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Existing Conditions Survey (Sheet 4) shows utility poles on site and in adjacent ROW. If down guy anchors exist associated with these poles, they are not explicitly labeled or located on the survey. Easement plat (Sheet 2) does not clearly delineate dedicated down guy anchor easements showing the required 10-foot width and 5-foot extension past anchor ground entry. Applicant must provide detailed survey and easement exhibit showing down guy anchor locations (if any exist) with dedicated easements meeting the 10-foot width by 5-foot-extension specification per Austin Energy Transmission Engineering Standards.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Existing Conditions Survey (Sheet 4) shows poles but does not specifically identify and dimension down guy anchor locations. Easement exhibit (Sheet 2) does not clearly show dedicated down guy anchor easements.","reasoning":"While poles are present, specific down guy anchor locations and associated easement documentation are not clearly provided on the plans.","tools_used":["vision"]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-1.43","status":"n/a","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.3"],"applicableAreas":[],"sheetReferences":[],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"No transformers (pole-mounted or pad-mounted) are shown on the site plan or utility plan. The site is served by Austin Energy with underground electric service distribution to individual buildings. No on-site transformers are depicted. This item applies only when transformers are located on site and overhead electric lines exist above or adjacent to transformer locations. Without transformer installations on site, this requirement is not applicable.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Review of electrical design plan (Sheet 21) and utility plans (Sheets 19-21) shows underground electric service routing to buildings. No pole-mounted or pad-mounted transformer locations are depicted.","reasoning":"The applicability trigger (on-site transformer) is not present. Service is provided via underground distribution without on-site transformer equipment shown.","tools_used":[]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-1.44","status":"n/a","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.4"],"applicableAreas":[],"sheetReferences":[],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"No transformers or switchgears in niche service configurations (covered or recessed installations under structures or canopies) are proposed on the site plan. This item applies only to specialized niche configurations where equipment is installed within covered/recessed areas requiring 35-foot vertical clearance inside the niche. Standard on-site electrical service distribution does not include such configurations. This requirement is not applicable.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Review of electrical design plan (Sheet 21) shows standard underground electric service distribution. No specialized transformer or switchgear niche installations with canopies or covered areas above equipment are depicted.","reasoning":"The applicability trigger (niche-configured transformer/switchgear) is not present. Standard service distribution is shown without niche installations.","tools_used":[]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-1.45","status":"not-verifiable","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.2"],"applicableAreas":["Construction staging areas, equipment zones, and work platforms"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":3},{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":9}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Sheet 3 documents extensive construction coordination requirements for work near transmission facilities, referencing OSHA clearance requirements. However, no construction staging area plan, equipment laydown zone diagram, or work platform logistics plan is provided with the site plan submittal. During construction, equipment and materials must maintain 10-foot radial clearance from energized overhead lines per OSHA 1910.333 and UCM § 1.10.2 (this is distinct from permanent clearance requirements). Applicant must provide a detailed construction logistics plan showing staging areas, equipment operation zones, crane swing radius, and scaffold/platform locations with dimension callouts verifying 10-foot radial clearance from all overhead electric facilities during construction phases.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Sheet 3 references construction clearance requirements and OSHA standards. Site plan (Sheet 9) and general notes address construction but do not include a dedicated construction logistics plan with staging area boundaries, equipment zones, and clearance dimensions.","reasoning":"Construction clearance verification requires a construction logistics or phasing plan that is not provided in the current submittal. The requirement cannot be verified without this documentation.","tools_used":["vision"]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-1.46","status":"pass","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.2"],"applicableAreas":["General notes and construction requirements"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":3}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Sheet 3, Electric Transmission Notes section, Note #3 explicitly requires: 'A pre-construction safety meeting is required with Austin Energy 48 hours before commencement of construction. Call Andrew Perez at 512-505-7133 to schedule a tailgate safety meeting.' This requirement references the mandatory 48-hour notification to Austin Energy before work begins near high-voltage overhead lines, satisfying the requirement of UCM § 1.10.2 and Texas Health & Safety Code Chapter 752, Section 752.003.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Sheet 3, Electric Transmission Notes #3 contains explicit text requiring '48 hours before commencement of construction' notification to Austin Energy with specific contact information (Andrew Perez, 512-505-7133).","reasoning":"The required note explicitly documents the 48-hour pre-construction notification requirement to Austin Energy. This directly satisfies the code requirement. The note is present and visible on the general notes sheet.","tools_used":["vision"]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-1.47","status":"n/a","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.6.2"],"applicableAreas":[],"sheetReferences":[],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"No service-mast through-roof installations are shown on the building elevations. The site plan indicates Austin Energy will provide electric service, and the electrical design plan shows underground service distribution to buildings. No overhead service drops with rooftop mast penetrations are depicted. This item applies only when service-mast through-roof installations are proposed. Without such installations, the roof clearance requirement (3 feet minimum above roof, or 18 inches if within 4 feet of edge) is not applicable.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Review of electrical design plan (Sheet 21) and site plan (Sheet 9) shows underground service distribution. No building elevation views with rooftop service mast installations are depicted.","reasoning":"The applicability trigger (service-mast through-roof installations) is not present. Service is underground per standard practice.","tools_used":[]}}]},"fast_mode_state":"off","uuid":"9c3025be-268f-4091-8aa2-f818935b7594"}
