{"level":30,"time":1778188744117,"pid":122,"hostname":"e70bc6df-98e","step":"review-runs","item":"2.md","index":1,"runIndex":"run-1","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01MFdT7FpGUg9hZBv3Sdqk8n","type":"tool_result","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Based on a visual analysis of Sheet 21 (\"Preliminary Electrical Design Plan\"), here is the information regarding the utility poles on the OHE lines and their proximity to tree symbols:\n\n**1. Location of Utility Poles on the OHE Line**\nOverhead Electric lines are indicated on the plan by dashed lines labeled precisely as \"**OHE**\". They run generally along the outer perimeters of the site. Utility poles are typically represented by small circular symbols situated along these lines.\n*   **Western Perimeter:** An OHE line runs north-south near the western boundary. Identifiable pole symbols are located near the northwest corner (near the \"Existing #13466 Wastewater MH\"), midway down the line (near the \"Sidewalk Easement\"), and at the southwest property corner.\n*   **Southern Perimeter:** An OHE line runs east-west along the southern boundary. Pole symbols are located at the southwest corner, roughly south of Building 8 (near Unit 804/805), roughly south of Building 7 (near Unit 702), and at the southeast property corner.\n*   **Eastern Perimeter:** An OHE line runs north-south near the eastern boundary. Pole symbols are visible near the northeast corner, roughly east of Building 5, and at the southeast corner.\n\n**2. Proximity of Tree Symbols to Poles (within 10 feet)**\nUsing the graphic scale provided on the sheet (\"**Scale 1\" = 20'**\"), there do **not** appear to be any tree trunk symbols (the central crosshair or small circle within the scalloped canopy symbols) located definitively within 10 feet of a utility pole.\n\nWhile several large tree *canopies* overlap the OHE lines, the actual trunk locations are set further back from the specific pole locations.\n\n**3. Distance from Tree Trunk Symbols to the Nearest Poles**\nBased on visual estimation using the 20-foot scale bar, the distances to the closest tree trunks are as follows:\n\n*   **Closest Off-site Trees (Southern Boundary):** The tree trunk symbols located south of the property line are the closest to the poles on the southern OHE line.\n    *   The tree trunk south of the pole near Unit 702 is estimated to be approximately **10 to 15 feet** away.\n    *   The tree trunk south of the pole near Unit 804/805 is estimated to be approximately **15 to 20 feet** away.\n*   **Western Boundary Trees:** The tree trunk symbol closest to the northwest corner pole is estimated to be **15 to 20 feet** to the east.\n*   **Eastern Boundary Trees:** Tree trunks visible near the eastern OHE line poles are located further inside the property, at estimated distances exceeding **20 feet**."}]}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"9d122776-20ac-46ff-b558-35791e0f03e5","uuid":"437b51c2-a063-45c8-9dfe-1073957b3fd3","tool_use_result":[{"type":"text","text":"Based on a visual analysis of Sheet 21 (\"Preliminary Electrical Design Plan\"), here is the information regarding the utility poles on the OHE lines and their proximity to tree symbols:\n\n**1. Location of Utility Poles on the OHE Line**\nOverhead Electric lines are indicated on the plan by dashed lines labeled precisely as \"**OHE**\". They run generally along the outer perimeters of the site. Utility poles are typically represented by small circular symbols situated along these lines.\n*   **Western Perimeter:** An OHE line runs north-south near the western boundary. Identifiable pole symbols are located near the northwest corner (near the \"Existing #13466 Wastewater MH\"), midway down the line (near the \"Sidewalk Easement\"), and at the southwest property corner.\n*   **Southern Perimeter:** An OHE line runs east-west along the southern boundary. Pole symbols are located at the southwest corner, roughly south of Building 8 (near Unit 804/805), roughly south of Building 7 (near Unit 702), and at the southeast property corner.\n*   **Eastern Perimeter:** An OHE line runs north-south near the eastern boundary. Pole symbols are visible near the northeast corner, roughly east of Building 5, and at the southeast corner.\n\n**2. Proximity of Tree Symbols to Poles (within 10 feet)**\nUsing the graphic scale provided on the sheet (\"**Scale 1\" = 20'**\"), there do **not** appear to be any tree trunk symbols (the central crosshair or small circle within the scalloped canopy symbols) located definitively within 10 feet of a utility pole.\n\nWhile several large tree *canopies* overlap the OHE lines, the actual trunk locations are set further back from the specific pole locations.\n\n**3. Distance from Tree Trunk Symbols to the Nearest Poles**\nBased on visual estimation using the 20-foot scale bar, the distances to the closest tree trunks are as follows:\n\n*   **Closest Off-site Trees (Southern Boundary):** The tree trunk symbols located south of the property line are the closest to the poles on the southern OHE line.\n    *   The tree trunk south of the pole near Unit 702 is estimated to be approximately **10 to 15 feet** away.\n    *   The tree trunk south of the pole near Unit 804/805 is estimated to be approximately **15 to 20 feet** away.\n*   **Western Boundary Trees:** The tree trunk symbol closest to the northwest corner pole is estimated to be **15 to 20 feet** to the east.\n*   **Eastern Boundary Trees:** Tree trunks visible near the eastern OHE line poles are located further inside the property, at estimated distances exceeding **20 feet**."}]}
{"level":30,"time":1778188777851,"pid":122,"hostname":"e70bc6df-98e","step":"review-runs","item":"2.md","index":1,"runIndex":"run-1","type":"assistant","message":{"id":"gen_01KR24XXG0PMJB6P68D44Q03CH","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Let me now gather the final pieces of information I need and then conduct a thorough evaluation of all checklist items.\n\nBased on my research so far, here's what I've learned:\n\n**APPLICABILITY ANALYSIS:**\n1. **Overhead Electric Distribution Lines**: YES - visible on site plan along southern boundary, labeled as \"OHE\" (Overhead Electric)\n2. **Overhead Electric Transmission Lines**: The notes on Sheet 3 reference transmission easements and transmission structures, but I haven't confirmed if there's actually a transmission line on THIS project or just requirements for if there were\n3. **Trees proposed on the site**: YES - visible on landscape plan, including mitigation trees\n\n**KEY FINDINGS FROM RESEARCH:**\n\nFrom Sheet 31 (Landscape Plan):\n- OHE line runs along the southern boundary\n- Trees shown in southeast corner area near OHE line - labeled as \"M\" (Mitigation Trees)\n- No specific species names shown for trees on the landscape plan\n- The legend shows abbreviations: SY (Street Yard Tree), PL (Parking Lot Tree), P (Parking Buffer Point Tree), M (Mitigation Tree)\n\nFrom Sheet 21 (Electrical Plan):\n- OHE lines visible on electrical plan\n- Tree symbols shown with canopy overlapping OHE lines\n- No clearance dimensions or specifications marked\n- Tree trunks appear to be roughly 10-20+ feet from utility poles\n\nFrom Sheet 35 (Landscape Calculations):\n- Plant list provided showing species and quantities\n- Shows proposed trees: 10 Cedar Elm (100 gal.), 2 Live Oak (100 gal.), 6 Mexican Redbud (45 gal.), 2 Texas Mountain Laurel (45 gal.)\n- Shows shrubs and groundcovers\n- Plant legend identifies species names\n\nFrom Sheet 32 (Tree List):\n- Existing trees surveyed\n- Lists trees to remain vs. removed\n\n\n- Lists mitigation requirements\n\nFrom Sheet 3 (General Notes):\n- Block 13 references Electric Transmission Notes (25 feet clearance from transmission structures)\n- Block 17 and Block 19 reference electric notes and Austin Energy requirements for clearances\n- No specific mention that there IS a transmission easement on THIS project, these are just requirements if there were\n\nFrom facts.md:\n- No mention of transmission facilities or transmission easements on the property\n- Only mentions \"5' Electric Easements\" in the plat-dedicated easements section\n- References to distribution facilities, not transmission\n\n**KEY REGULATORY THRESHOLDS (from grouping file 2.md):**\n- Utility-compatible trees: ≤ 20 feet mature\n\nThe transmission line references appear to be standard boilerplate requirements rather than applicable to this specific project. The property has distribution easements documented, not transmission facilities. The proposed tree species—Cedar Elm, Live Oak, Mexican Redbud, and Texas Mountain Laurel—need to be evaluated against the 20-foot mature height threshold for utility compatibility. Looking at EL-2.1, the site has distribution lines with mitigation trees shown in the SE corner on the landscape plan. The plant list identifies Cedar Elm, Live Oak, Mexican Redbud, and Texas Mountain Laurel, but these species aren't cross-referenced with their locations relative to the distribution conductor on the landscape drawings. Without dimensional verification confirming these trees are positioned beyond the 15-foot clearance zone, I can't verify compliance.\n\nFor EL-2.2, no transmission lines appear to be present on the site.\n\nEL-2.3 presents a concern—Cedar Elm and Live Oak both mature to heights exceeding 40 feet, and they're positioned near the distribution line without documented clearances showing adequate separation from the 25-foot threshold.\n\nEL-2.4 and EL-2.5 don't apply since there's no transmission infrastructure or easement on the property.\n\nFor EL-2.6, trees near utility poles create ambiguity. The landscape plan shows tree symbols in close proximity to pole locations in the southeast corner, though Sheet 21 indicates estimated distances ranging from 10 to 20+ feet. Without dimensional clarification, it's unclear whether these symbols represent the same trees or are shown for reference only.\n\nEL-2.7 regarding pad-mounted equipment remains unclear—the landscape plan doesn't identify any pad-mount locations, requiring cross-reference with the electrical plan to determine if transformers or other equipment exist and whether trees are within the required 10-foot buffer.\n\nFor EL-2.8 and EL-2.9, the electrical plan shows underground lines and pull boxes, but their positions relative to trees on the landscape plan cannot be verified. Root barrier requirements for trees within 20 feet of underground equipment similarly cannot be assessed without first establishing proximity relationships.\n\nEL-2.10 applies since trees are positioned near overhead lines, yet the plant legend doesn't specify species in these critical areas.\n\nFor EL-2.11, both Cedar Elm and Live Oak exceed typical 40-foot heights and appear near electric facilities, but the plans don't differentiate large trees from smaller specimens.\n\nFor EL-2.12 and EL-2.13, no clearance dimensions appear anywhere in the submitted plans, so I cannot verify whether measurements are taken from pole centerlines or tree canopies rather than the correct reference points.\n\nFor EL-2.14, I need to see the next thinking to complete this item. The general notes acknowledge clearance requirements within ten feet of the overhead electrical line centerline, but no letter from Austin Energy approving the specific tree placements is provided in the submitted documents. Without documented approval for trees potentially within restricted zones, this cannot be verified as compliant.\n\nLooking at the landscape plan more closely, trees are shown near the southern boundary OHE line, but the species aren't identified directly on Sheet 31. Clearance dimensions are absent, and while the trees appear to be mitigation plantings, their exact species must be cross-referenced with Sheet 35's plant list. The connection between the plant schedule and the actual tree symbols on the landscape plan remains unclear. Since regulatory clearances require specific measurements and species verification, I need to determine whether the documentation adequately demonstrates compliance with clearance standards. The electrical plan shows tree canopies overlapping the overhead lines, with estimated distances ranging from 10-20+ feet from poles. There's some inconsistency between what the landscape and electrical sheets suggest about tree positioning relative to the facilities. For EL-2.6, the vision feedback from Sheet 31 indicates trees are \"extremely close\" to poles and potentially within the 10-foot radius, which would indicate non-compliance, though without explicit dimensioning I can't be entirely certain. The southeast corner of Sheet 31 appears to be the critical area to evaluate.","signature":""}],"model":"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001","stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":0},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"9d122776-20ac-46ff-b558-35791e0f03e5","uuid":"1982bf79-fc71-43f1-9133-4acf1dda0b2a"}
{"level":30,"time":1778188781504,"pid":122,"hostname":"e70bc6df-98e","step":"review-runs","item":"2.md","index":1,"runIndex":"run-1","type":"assistant","message":{"id":"gen_01KR24XXG0PMJB6P68D44Q03CH","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Based on my comprehensive review of the site plan documents, I have completed the research phase for all checklist items in this grouping. Let me now evaluate each item systematically.\n\n## RESEARCH SUMMARY\n\n**Overhead Electric Infrastructure Present:**\n- Distribution lines (OHE - Overhead Electric) shown along southern and western property boundaries on Site Plan (Sheet 9) and Landscape Plan (Sheet 31)\n- Utility poles visible at property corners along OHE lines\n- No transmission lines or transmission easements identified on this project (facts.md indicates only 5' electric easements)\n\n**Tree Planting Shown:**\n- Mitigation trees shown on Landscape Plan (Sheet 31) in southeast corner area near OHE line\n- Plant list on Sheet 35 identifies species: Cedar Elm (10 @ 100 gal.), Live Oak (2 @ 100 gal.), Mexican Redbud (6 @ 45 gal.), Texas Mountain Laurel (2 @ 45 gal.), plus shrubs and groundcovers\n- Sheet 32 provides tree survey data but focuses on existing trees\n\n**Critical Gaps Identified:**\n- Landscape Plan (Sheet 31) does not contain a plant legend identifying species for the specific trees shown near utilities\n- No clearance dimensions or measurements provided on any sheet relating trees to utility conductors or poles\n- Tree symbols on landscape plan appear close to utility pole symbols at SE corner, but no dimensional verification provided\n- No cross-reference between specific trees on Sheet 35 plant list and their locations on Sheet 31 landscape plan\n- No documented Austin Energy approval for any trees in utility clearance zones\n- Underground and pad-mounted electrical equipment locations not cross-referenced with landscape plan\n\n**Transmission Facilities:**\n- General notes on Sheet 3 include transmission requirements, but no transmission easement or transmission facility shown on this project per facts.md and electrical plan\n\n---\n\nNow I'll evaluate each checklist item:"}],"model":"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001","stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":0},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"9d122776-20ac-46ff-b558-35791e0f03e5","uuid":"ed57860a-6763-4dd8-ac2c-cbfe8b8b9a75"}
{"level":30,"time":1778188819160,"pid":122,"hostname":"e70bc6df-98e","step":"review-runs","item":"2.md","index":1,"runIndex":"run-1","type":"assistant","message":{"id":"gen_01KR24XXG0PMJB6P68D44Q03CH","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01HmRqEbeX8EiNay8xr8EEdw","name":"StructuredOutput","input":{"grouping":"2","findings":[{"deficiencyId":"EL-2.1","status":"not-verifiable","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.10.4"],"applicableAreas":["Southeast corner of site, near southern OHE line"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":31},{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":35}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Mitigation trees are shown on the landscape plan near the southern OHE distribution line, but species identification only appears on Sheet 35 plant list, not on the landscape plan where trees are shown. Utility-compatible status cannot be verified from the landscape plan without explicit species labels at planting locations. No clearance dimensions provided to verify compliance with 15-foot minimum clearance for non-utility-compatible trees.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Landscape plan (Sheet 31) shows tree symbols labeled 'M' (mitigation trees) in southeast corner near OHE line. Species names appear only on Sheet 35 plant schedule. No species identification legend on Sheet 31.","reasoning":"The requirement demands verification that species proposed near distribution conductors meet utility compatibility criteria. Sheet 31 landscape plan does not identify species names for the specific trees shown near utilities, making it impossible to verify UC status from the drawing where trees are located. This violates the documentation requirement regardless of actual species planted.","tools_used":["vision_check"]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-2.3","status":"not-verifiable","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.10.4"],"applicableAreas":["Southeast corner and other areas where large trees proposed near southern OHE distribution line"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":31},{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":35}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Plant list (Sheet 35) shows Cedar Elm and Live Oak trees (mature heights 50+ feet, exceeding 40-foot threshold) proposed as part of mitigation. These large trees are shown on landscape plan near the OHE distribution line, but no clearance dimensions verify they are more than 25 feet from the conductor. Large trees are not differentiated on the landscape plan from other tree types, preventing visual verification of their proximity to utilities.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Sheet 35 lists 10 Cedar Elm (100 gal.) and 2 Live Oak (100 gal.). Standard references show these species mature at 50+ feet, exceeding 40-foot ECM Appendix F threshold. Trees shown on Sheet 31 near OHE line but no dimensional callouts verifying distances.","reasoning":"UCM § 1.10.10.4 requires large trees (40+ feet) to be 25+ feet from distribution conductors. Landscape plan shows tree symbols near utilities but without clearance dimensions or differentiation of large tree types, compliance cannot be verified. The planting locations and mature heights must be cross-verifiable from the landscape plan itself.","tools_used":["vision_check"]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-2.6","status":"not-verifiable","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.10.4"],"applicableAreas":["Southeast corner at southern property boundary where OHE pole is located"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":31}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Tree symbols are shown on landscape plan in very close proximity to utility pole symbol at the southeast corner. Visual inspection of scaled drawing suggests trees are less than 10 feet from pole position. No dimensional verification or clarification provided to establish whether trees are measured at 10+ feet clearance from the pole center line.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Vision analysis of Sheet 31 revealed tree trunk symbols at southeast corner appearing 'extremely close' to the utility pole symbol and 'well under 10 feet' when scaled against the 1\" = 20' scale bar.","reasoning":"The landscape plan visually depicts trees within what appears to be the restricted 10-foot pole clearance zone based on the graphic scale. Without dimensional verification or clarification that these are off-site trees shown for context (not part of the proposed development), the apparent proximity to the pole represents a potential code violation that must be resolved with explicit dimensions.","tools_used":["vision_check"]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-2.10","status":"not-verifiable","codeCitations":["Reviewer Convention"],"applicableAreas":["Landscape plan area near overhead electric facilities (southern boundary OHE line)"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":31}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Landscape plan (Sheet 31) shows trees near overhead electric distribution line with symbols labeled only as 'M' (mitigation tree) and other abbreviations (SY, PL, P), but does not include a legend identifying the specific species names for trees shown in areas with utility facilities. Plant species identification requires reference to separate Sheet 35, which is not cross-referenced on the landscape plan.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Sheet 31 key notes legend identifies tree symbols only by category (M = mitigation tree, SY = street yard tree, etc.) without listing species names. Specific species are listed on Sheet 35 plant schedule.","reasoning":"The landscape plan, where tree clearances from utilities must be verified, does not provide species identification. A reviewer cannot determine from the landscape plan alone whether trees shown near utilities are utility-compatible without accessing a separate plant list sheet. This violates the requirement that species be identified on plans showing trees near electric facilities.","tools_used":["vision_check"]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-2.11","status":"not-verifiable","codeCitations":["Reviewer Convention"],"applicableAreas":["Areas on landscape plan where large trees (40+ feet) are proposed near overhead electric facilities"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":31}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Landscape plan shows all tree symbols using the same graphic representation without differentiation of large trees (40+ feet) from smaller trees. Cedar Elm and Live Oak trees (both exceeding 40-foot mature height) cannot be visually distinguished on the landscape plan from smaller species, preventing verification of their clearances from utilities.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Sheet 31 shows all trees as simple circle symbols with letters (M, SY, PL, P). No distinction made between trees of different mature heights. Sheet 35 lists mature heights in plant schedule but is not cross-referenced on landscape plan.","reasoning":"To verify large tree clearances from utilities, a reviewer must first identify which trees are large (40+ feet) on the landscape plan itself. The landscape plan does not differentiate large trees by symbol, size notation, or any visual means. This makes clearance verification impossible from the landscape plan.","tools_used":["vision_check"]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-2.12","status":"not-verifiable","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.10.4"],"applicableAreas":["All areas where tree clearances to overhead electric facilities might be dimensioned"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":31},{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":21}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"No clearance dimensions are provided on landscape plan or electrical plan showing distances from trees to overhead electric conductors or poles. Measurement methodology cannot be verified because no measurements are shown on the plans.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Review of Sheets 21 and 31 found no dimension lines or numeric callouts indicating distances between trees and OHE lines or poles.","reasoning":"This item requires verification that if clearances are dimensioned, they measure from the correct reference point (outside conductor, not pole centerline). Since no clearances are dimensioned at all, this requirement cannot be evaluated. However, this is a documentation gap that should be addressed.","tools_used":["vision_check"]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-2.13","status":"not-verifiable","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.10.4"],"applicableAreas":["All areas where tree clearances to overhead electric facilities might be dimensioned"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":31}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"No clearance dimensions provided on landscape plan showing distances from tree trunks to electric facilities. Measurement methodology cannot be verified because no measurements are shown.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Sheet 31 landscape plan contains no dimension lines or notes specifying clearances from tree trunks to utilities.","reasoning":"This item requires verification of measurement methodology IF clearances are dimensioned. Since no dimensions are present, this requirement cannot be directly evaluated. The absence of clearance documentation is itself a deficiency that should be addressed in the response phase.","tools_used":["vision_check"]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-2.14","status":"pass","codeCitations":["Reviewer Convention"],"applicableAreas":["Landscape plan showing areas near overhead electric facilities"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":31},{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":21},{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":9}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Trees are shown on landscape plan (Sheet 31) in relation to overhead electric distribution lines that are depicted on the plan. The OHE lines are clearly marked on the landscape plan, enabling relationship verification between trees and utilities.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Sheet 31 landscape plan clearly marks the OHE (Overhead Electric) line along the southern property boundary and shows tree symbols in this area. Sheet 9 and Sheet 21 also depict OHE lines, confirming utility locations are documented.","reasoning":"The requirement is satisfied when trees are shown on the landscape plan with sufficient clarity to verify their relationship to electric facilities. Trees and OHE lines are both depicted on Sheet 31, allowing visual comparison of their positions.","tools_used":["vision_check"]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-2.15","status":"not-verifiable","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.10.4"],"applicableAreas":["Areas near overhead electric distribution line where trees are proposed within potential restricted zones"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":3},{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":31}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Trees are shown on landscape plan near the overhead electric distribution line, but no documented written approval from Austin Energy is included in the site plan package or supplementary documents authorizing tree placement within restricted clearance zones. General notes on Sheet 3 reference Austin Energy requirements for tree work within 10 feet of utility lines but do not indicate explicit approval for proposed tree locations.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Sheet 3 General Notes (Block 17 and Block 19) state owner responsibility for tree removal/pruning within 10 feet of utility centerlines, but no approval letter or correspondence from Austin Energy authorizing specific tree placement within restricted zones was found in submittal documents.","reasoning":"The requirement specifies that trees within prohibited clearance zones must have documented Austin Energy written approval. Without such approval letter, and given the uncertainty about whether proposed trees comply with clearance distances (due to missing dimensions), compliance cannot be verified.","tools_used":[]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-2.2","status":"n/a","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.10.4"],"applicableAreas":[],"sheetReferences":[],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"No transmission lines or transmission easement are indicated on this project. Facts.md and utility plan documents confirm only distribution facilities (5' electric easement) are present. Transmission clearance requirements do not apply.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Review of facts.md, electrical plan (Sheet 21), and site plan (Sheet 9) revealed no transmission lines, transmission structures, or transmission easements on the property.","reasoning":"This item applies only when transmission facilities (60kV or higher) are present. The property has distribution facilities only. The general notes reference transmission requirements as standard design standards but do not indicate a transmission facility exists on this project.","tools_used":[]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-2.4","status":"n/a","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.10.4"],"applicableAreas":[],"sheetReferences":[],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"No transmission lines present on this project. This requirement applies only to transmission facilities (60kV or higher), which are not shown on the site plan.","agentTrace":{"observation":"No transmission facilities identified on project plans or in facts.md.","reasoning":"Large tree restrictions within 50 feet of transmission conductors apply only if transmission lines exist. This project has distribution facilities only.","tools_used":[]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-2.5","status":"n/a","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.10.4","UCM § 1.14.6"],"applicableAreas":[],"sheetReferences":[],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"No transmission easement is present on this property. Facts.md and the plat indicate only 5' electric easements (distribution). Categorical prohibition on trees within transmission easement does not apply.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Facts.md Section on Easements lists only 5' electric easements associated with the Mecey Subdivision plat, with no transmission easement indicated.","reasoning":"This requirement applies only when a transmission easement boundary is shown on the plans. No transmission easement is present on this property.","tools_used":[]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-2.7","status":"not-verifiable","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.10.4"],"applicableAreas":["Areas where pad-mounted electrical equipment may be located"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":31},{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":21}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Pad-mounted electrical equipment locations are not clearly identified or cross-referenced on the landscape plan (Sheet 31). While the electrical plan (Sheet 21) shows transformers and pull boxes, their precise locations relative to proposed trees on the landscape plan cannot be verified. Clearances between trees and pad-mounted equipment cannot be determined from available documentation.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Vision analysis of landscape plan (Sheet 31) found no explicitly labeled pad-mounted transformers or equipment. Electrical plan (Sheet 21) shows electrical infrastructure but locations not cross-referenced to landscape plan.","reasoning":"To verify compliance, landscape plan must show both trees and pad-mounted equipment locations. Without this cross-referencing or explicit equipment identification on the landscape plan, the 10-foot clearance requirement cannot be evaluated.","tools_used":["vision_check"]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-2.8","status":"not-verifiable","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.10.4"],"applicableAreas":["Areas where underground electrical equipment is located"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":31},{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":21}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Underground electrical equipment (pull boxes, vaults, other than duct banks/conduits) locations are shown on electrical plan (Sheet 21) but are not cross-referenced with tree planting locations on landscape plan (Sheet 31). The 5-foot clearance requirement cannot be verified without integration of tree and underground equipment locations on a single reference drawing.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Electrical plan shows underground utility lines and pull boxes, but landscape plan does not identify these features. Cross-reference between sheets is not provided.","reasoning":"The requirement mandates 5-foot clearances from trees to underground equipment. Without tree locations plotted against underground equipment locations on a common reference, compliance cannot be verified. The plans must show adequate spatial separation or clearances must be dimensioned.","tools_used":[]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-2.9","status":"not-verifiable","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.10.4"],"applicableAreas":["Areas where trees are proposed within 20 feet of underground electrical equipment"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":31},{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":37}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Root barrier specifications are not visible on landscape plan or landscape details (Sheet 37). The root barrier requirement applies only when trees are within 20 feet of underground equipment, which cannot be determined from available documentation due to lack of cross-reference between tree and equipment locations. No root barrier details or specifications are noted on the landscape plan for any trees near utilities.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Review of landscape plan (Sheet 31), landscape details (Sheet 37), and electrical plan found no specifications or notes indicating root barriers are required or proposed for any trees near underground equipment.","reasoning":"This item is inapplicable if no trees are shown within 20 feet of underground equipment. However, this proximity cannot be verified due to lack of integration of tree locations with underground equipment locations. Therefore, status is not-verifiable pending confirmation that no trees are within 20 feet of underground equipment.","tools_used":[]}}]}}],"model":"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001","stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":0},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"9d122776-20ac-46ff-b558-35791e0f03e5","uuid":"64e0a3fb-8743-4ef3-9de7-ac01d86a41ad"}
