gs have been documented in the structured output with agent trace information explaining the observation, reasoning, and verification methodology for each item.","stop_reason":"end_turn","session_id":"9d122776-20ac-46ff-b558-35791e0f03e5","total_cost_usd":0.37328255000000005,"usage":{"input_tokens":2319,"cache_creation_input_tokens":131627,"cache_read_input_tokens":1116598,"output_tokens":18954,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":131627},"inference_geo":"","iterations":[],"speed":"standard"},"modelUsage":{"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001":{"inputTokens":2319,"outputTokens":18954,"cacheReadInputTokens":1116598,"cacheCreationInputTokens":131627,"webSearchRequests":0,"costUSD":0.37328255000000005,"contextWindow":200000,"maxOutputTokens":32000}},"permission_denials":[],"structured_output":{"grouping":"2","findings":[{"deficiencyId":"EL-2.1","status":"not-verifiable","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.10.4"],"applicableAreas":["Southeast corner of site, near southern OHE line"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":31},{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":35}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Mitigation trees are shown on the landscape plan near the southern OHE distribution line, but species identification only appears on Sheet 35 plant list, not on the landscape plan where trees are shown. Utility-compatible status cannot be verified from the landscape plan without explicit species labels at planting locations. No clearance dimensions provided to verify compliance with 15-foot minimum clearance for non-utility-compatible trees.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Landscape plan (Sheet 31) shows tree symbols labeled 'M' (mitigation trees) in southeast corner near OHE line. Species names appear only on Sheet 35 plant schedule. No species identification legend on Sheet 31.","reasoning":"The requirement demands verification that species proposed near distribution conductors meet utility compatibility criteria. Sheet 31 landscape plan does not identify species names for the specific trees shown near utilities, making it impossible to verify UC status from the drawing where trees are located. This violates the documentation requirement regardless of actual species planted.","tools_used":["vision_check"]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-2.3","status":"not-verifiable","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.10.4"],"applicableAreas":["Southeast corner and other areas where large trees proposed near southern OHE distribution line"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":31},{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":35}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Plant list (Sheet 35) shows Cedar Elm and Live Oak trees (mature heights 50+ feet, exceeding 40-foot threshold) proposed as part of mitigation. These large trees are shown on landscape plan near the OHE distribution line, but no clearance dimensions verify they are more than 25 feet from the conductor. Large trees are not differentiated on the landscape plan from other tree types, preventing visual verification of their proximity to utilities.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Sheet 35 lists 10 Cedar Elm (100 gal.) and 2 Live Oak (100 gal.). Standard references show these species mature at 50+ feet, exceeding 40-foot ECM Appendix F threshold. Trees shown on Sheet 31 near OHE line but no dimensional callouts verifying distances.","reasoning":"UCM § 1.10.10.4 requires large trees (40+ feet) to be 25+ feet from distribution conductors. Landscape plan shows tree symbols near utilities but without clearance dimensions or differentiation of large tree types, compliance cannot be verified. The planting locations and mature heights must be cross-verifiable from the landscape plan itself.","tools_used":["vision_check"]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-2.6","status":"not-verifiable","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.10.4"],"applicableAreas":["Southeast corner at southern property boundary where OHE pole is located"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":31}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Tree symbols are shown on landscape plan in very close proximity to utility pole symbol at the southeast corner. Visual inspection of scaled drawing suggests trees are less than 10 feet from pole position. No dimensional verification or clarification provided to establish whether trees are measured at 10+ feet clearance from the pole center line.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Vision analysis of Sheet 31 revealed tree trunk symbols at southeast corner appearing 'extremely close' to the utility pole symbol and 'well under 10 feet' when scaled against the 1\" = 20' scale bar.","reasoning":"The landscape plan visually depicts trees within what appears to be the restricted 10-foot pole clearance zone based on the graphic scale. Without dimensional verification or clarification that these are off-site trees shown for context (not part of the proposed development), the apparent proximity to the pole represents a potential code violation that must be resolved with explicit dimensions.","tools_used":["vision_check"]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-2.10","status":"not-verifiable","codeCitations":["Reviewer Convention"],"applicableAreas":["Landscape plan area near overhead electric facilities (southern boundary OHE line)"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":31}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Landscape plan (Sheet 31) shows trees near overhead electric distribution line with symbols labeled only as 'M' (mitigation tree) and other abbreviations (SY, PL, P), but does not include a legend identifying the specific species names for trees shown in areas with utility facilities. Plant species identification requires reference to separate Sheet 35, which is not cross-referenced on the landscape plan.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Sheet 31 key notes legend identifies tree symbols only by category (M = mitigation tree, SY = street yard tree, etc.) without listing species names. Specific species are listed on Sheet 35 plant schedule.","reasoning":"The landscape plan, where tree clearances from utilities must be verified, does not provide species identification. A reviewer cannot determine from the landscape plan alone whether trees shown near utilities are utility-compatible without accessing a separate plant list sheet. This violates the requirement that species be identified on plans showing trees near electric facilities.","tools_used":["vision_check"]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-2.11","status":"not-verifiable","codeCitations":["Reviewer Convention"],"applicableAreas":["Areas on landscape plan where large trees (40+ feet) are proposed near overhead electric facilities"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":31}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Landscape plan shows all tree symbols using the same graphic representation without differentiation of large trees (40+ feet) from smaller trees. Cedar Elm and Live Oak trees (both exceeding 40-foot mature height) cannot be visually distinguished on the landscape plan from smaller species, preventing verification of their clearances from utilities.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Sheet 31 shows all trees as simple circle symbols with letters (M, SY, PL, P). No distinction made between trees of different mature heights. Sheet 35 lists mature heights in plant schedule but is not cross-referenced on landscape plan.","reasoning":"To verify large tree clearances from utilities, a reviewer must first identify which trees are large (40+ feet) on the landscape plan itself. The landscape plan does not differentiate large trees by symbol, size notation, or any visual means. This makes clearance verification impossible from the landscape plan.","tools_used":["vision_check"]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-2.12","status":"not-verifiable","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.10.4"],"applicableAreas":["All areas where tree clearances to overhead electric facilities might be dimensioned"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":31},{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":21}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"No clearance dimensions are provided on landscape plan or electrical plan showing distances from trees to overhead electric conductors or poles. Measurement methodology cannot be verified because no measurements are shown on the plans.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Review of Sheets 21 and 31 found no dimension lines or numeric callouts indicating distances between trees and OHE lines or poles.","reasoning":"This item requires verification that if clearances are dimensioned, they measure from the correct reference point (outside conductor, not pole centerline). Since no clearances are dimensioned at all, this requirement cannot be evaluated. However, this is a documentation gap that should be addressed.","tools_used":["vision_check"]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-2.13","status":"not-verifiable","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.10.4"],"applicableAreas":["All areas where tree clearances to overhead electric facilities might be dimensioned"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":31}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"No clearance dimensions provided on landscape plan showing distances from tree trunks to electric facilities. Measurement methodology cannot be verified because no measurements are shown.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Sheet 31 landscape plan contains no dimension lines or notes specifying clearances from tree trunks to utilities.","reasoning":"This item requires verification of measurement methodology IF clearances are dimensioned. Since no dimensions are present, this requirement cannot be directly evaluated. The absence of clearance documentation is itself a deficiency that should be addressed in the response phase.","tools_used":["vision_check"]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-2.14","status":"pass","codeCitations":["Reviewer Convention"],"applicableAreas":["Landscape plan showing areas near overhead electric facilities"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":31},{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":21},{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":9}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Trees are shown on landscape plan (Sheet 31) in relation to overhead electric distribution lines that are depicted on the plan. The OHE lines are clearly marked on the landscape plan, enabling relationship verification between trees and utilities.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Sheet 31 landscape plan clearly marks the OHE (Overhead Electric) line along the southern property boundary and shows tree symbols in this area. Sheet 9 and Sheet 21 also depict OHE lines, confirming utility locations are documented.","reasoning":"The requirement is satisfied when trees are shown on the landscape plan with sufficient clarity to verify their relationship to electric facilities. Trees and OHE lines are both depicted on Sheet 31, allowing visual comparison of their positions.","tools_used":["vision_check"]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-2.15","status":"not-verifiable","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.10.4"],"applicableAreas":["Areas near overhead electric distribution line where trees are proposed within potential restricted zones"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":3},{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":31}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Trees are shown on landscape plan near the overhead electric distribution line, but no documented written approval from Austin Energy is included in the site plan package or supplementary documents authorizing tree placement within restricted clearance zones. General notes on Sheet 3 reference Austin Energy requirements for tree work within 10 feet of utility lines but do not indicate explicit approval for proposed tree locations.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Sheet 3 General Notes (Block 17 and Block 19) state owner responsibility for tree removal/pruning within 10 feet of utility centerlines, but no approval letter or correspondence from Austin Energy authorizing specific tree placement within restricted zones was found in submittal documents.","reasoning":"The requirement specifies that trees within prohibited clearance zones must have documented Austin Energy written approval. Without such approval letter, and given the uncertainty about whether proposed trees comply with clearance distances (due to missing dimensions), compliance cannot be verified.","tools_used":[]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-2.2","status":"n/a","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.10.4"],"applicableAreas":[],"sheetReferences":[],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"No transmission lines or transmission easement are indicated on this project. Facts.md and utility plan documents confirm only distribution facilities (5' electric easement) are present. Transmission clearance requirements do not apply.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Review of facts.md, electrical plan (Sheet 21), and site plan (Sheet 9) revealed no transmission lines, transmission structures, or transmission easements on the property.","reasoning":"This item applies only when transmission facilities (60kV or higher) are present. The property has distribution facilities only. The general notes reference transmission requirements as standard design standards but do not indicate a transmission facility exists on this project.","tools_used":[]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-2.4","status":"n/a","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.10.4"],"applicableAreas":[],"sheetReferences":[],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"No transmission lines present on this project. This requirement applies only to transmission facilities (60kV or higher), which are not shown on the site plan.","agentTrace":{"observation":"No transmission facilities identified on project plans or in facts.md.","reasoning":"Large tree restrictions within 50 feet of transmission conductors apply only if transmission lines exist. This project has distribution facilities only.","tools_used":[]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-2.5","status":"n/a","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.10.4","UCM § 1.14.6"],"applicableAreas":[],"sheetReferences":[],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"No transmission easement is present on this property. Facts.md and the plat indicate only 5' electric easements (distribution). Categorical prohibition on trees within transmission easement does not apply.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Facts.md Section on Easements lists only 5' electric easements associated with the Mecey Subdivision plat, with no transmission easement indicated.","reasoning":"This requirement applies only when a transmission easement boundary is shown on the plans. No transmission easement is present on this property.","tools_used":[]}},{"deficiencyId":"EL-2.7","status":"not-verifiable","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.10.4"],"applicableAreas":["Areas where pad-mounted electrical equipment may be located"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":31},{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":21}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Pad-mounted electrical equipment locations are not clearly identified or cross-referenced on the landscape plan (Sheet 31). While the electrical plan (Sheet 21) shows transformers and pull boxes, their precise locations relative to proposed trees on the landscape plan cannot be verified. Clearances between trees and pad-mounted equipment cannot be determined from available documentation.","agentTrace":{"observation":"Vision analysis of landscape plan (Sheet 31) found no explicitly labeled pad-mounted transformers or equipment