his affects multiple sheets and requires coordination with Austin Energy for utility data. must provide registered surveyor field survey data showing existing overhead conductor elevations and clearance dimensions to all building features, with at least mid-span clearance measurements if vertical clearance appears marginal. Without this documented survey information, vertical clearances from overhead facilities to driveways, parking areas, and other site features cannot be verified. The plan set lacks any registered surveyor mid-span clearance measurements or pole location data needed to calculate clearances to site improvements. surveyed data confirming that vertical clearances meet the 16-foot (parking), 18-foot (roads), or 7.5-foot (horizontal) minimums, mid-span clearance verification cannot be performed. The applicant needs to submit a registered surveyor's field documentation that establishes pole locations, conductor elevations, and verified mid-span clearance distances beneath and adjacent to all proposed driveways and parking areas.\n\nOverhead electric lines are positioned near the site, with proposed building finished floor elevations ranging from 683.0' to 687.50', but actual conductor elevation data from a surveyor hasn't been provided. When clearances from overhead facilities to proposed improvements appear questionable or potentially inadequate based on available information, registered surveyor mid-span clearance documentation becomes necessary to confirm compliance.\n\nNow I'll structure the complete JSON with all 13 review comments and execute the tool.","signature":""}],"model":"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001","stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":0},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"5fec1e61-babc-4f6a-a405-298c428553e2","uuid":"1a440d38-3d99-489d-9acc-70b2813fc4bb"}
