y mark or call out which trees are large trees for verification purposes."},{"runNum":3,"status":"nv","comment":"Large trees (Live Oak and Cedar Elm, both 40+ feet mature height) are identified in plant schedule with species names and mature heights (implied by designation). However, landscape plan does not explicitly differentiate large trees with special notation, callouts, or 'LT' designation to allow field verification of clearances. Trees are listed in plant schedule but not flagged as 'large tree' on the main landscape drawing or in key notes, requiring cross-reference to determine which are large versus standard."}]}]},{"headline":"Clearances from overhead electric facilities and poles not documented","summary":"Proposed trees are positioned within required clearance zones from overhead electric distribution lines and utility poles but lack dimensional verification. Large trees (Live Oak, Cedar Elm, 40+ feet mature height) are placed 3-5 feet from the southern OHE line. No clearance dimensions shown on landscape or electrical plans.","sheets":[9,31,35],"applicableArea":"Utilities & Infrastructure","severity":3,"confidence":2,"crossDep":"Austin Energy approval required for trees within utility clearance zones per UCM § 1.10.10.4.","attn":"Run 3 of EL-2.3 confirms definitive non-compliance: large trees within 25-foot zone. Verify with Austin Energy whether tree relocation or written approval required.","details":[{"text":"Live Oak and Cedar Elm trees (both 40+ feet mature height) positioned 3-5 feet from southern boundary OHE distribution line. Minimum required clearance is 25 feet for large trees. No Austin Energy written approval provided for this deviation.","citation":"UCM § 1.10.10.4; ECM Appendix F","sourceId":"2:EL-2.3","confidence":3,"runComments":[{"runNum":1,"status":"nv","comment":"Plant list (Sheet 35) shows Cedar Elm and Live Oak trees (mature heights 50+ feet, exceeding 40-foot threshold) proposed as part of mitigation. These large trees are shown on landscape plan near the OHE distribution line, but no clearance dimensions verify they are more than 25 feet from the conductor. Large trees are not differentiated on the landscape plan from other tree types, preventing visual verification of their proximity to utilities."},{"runNum":2,"status":"nv","comment":"Trees are proposed at 5-25 feet from OHE distribution line, which overlaps the 25-foot zone where large trees (40+ feet mature height per ECM Appendix F) are restricted. Plant schedule lists Cedar Elm and Live Oak as shade trees in large containers (100 gal.), which could indicate mature size potential. However, no explicit mature height documentation is provided for these species per ECM Appendix F. Cannot verify whether proposed trees will exceed the 40-foot mature height threshold that triggers this requirement."},{"runNum":3,"status":"fail","comment":"Large trees with mature height ≥40 feet (Live Oak and Cedar Elm) are proposed within 25 lateral feet of OHE distribution conductor line. Live Oak trees are positioned approximately 3-5 feet from the southern boundary OHE line, and Cedar Elm trees are similarly positioned near the OHE boundary. Both species exceed the 40-foot mature height threshold (Live Oak 40-60+ ft; Cedar Elm 40-50 ft). No Austin Energy written approval provided for this violation."}]},{"text":"Trees at southeast corner positioned very close to utility pole position (less than 10 feet visually). Specific pole locations not dimensioned on site or landscape plans, preventing verification of required 10-foot clearance from pole centerline.","citation":"UCM § 1.10.10.4","sourceId":"2:EL-2.6","confidence":3,"runComments":[{"runNum":1,"status":"nv","comment":"Tree symbols are shown on landscape plan in very close proximity to utility pole symbol at the southeast corner. Visual inspection of scaled drawing suggests trees are less than 10 feet from pole position. No dimensional verification or clarification provided to establish whether trees are measured at 10+ feet clearance from the pole center line."},{"runNum":2,"status":"nv","comment":"Overhead electric poles are clearly present (indicated by '-OHE-' line on site and landscape plans, and by utility easement boundaries). However, specific pole locations are not dimensioned on either the site plan or landscape plan. Trees are shown near the OHE line but without dimensioned distances to specific pole locations. The 10-foot pole clearance requirement cannot be verified because pole positions are not precisely located relative to tree planting locations on the submitted plans."},{"runNum":3,"status":"nv","comment":"Utility pole locations are shown on site plan (Sheet 9) and landscape plan (Sheet 31) along the western and southern OHE boundaries. Proposed trees (especially mitigation trees near the southern boundary) appear to be positioned very close to the property line where poles are located. No dimension lines showing clearance distance from pole centers to tree trunks provided. Cannot definitively measure the 10-foot lateral distance (from pole to tree trunk center) from available plan scales without explicit dimensions."}]},{"text":"No clearance dimensions provided on landscape or electrical plans showing distances from trees to overhead electric conductors or poles.","citation":"UCM § 1.10.10.4","sourceId":"2:EL-2.12","confidence":1,"runComments":[{"runNum":1,"status":"nv","comment":"No clearance dimensions are provided on landscape plan or electrical plan showing distances from trees to overhead electric conductors or poles. Measurement methodology cannot be verified because no measurements are shown on the plans."}]},{"text":"Landscape plan lacks dimension lines from tree trunk centers to overhead electric facilities.","citation":"UCM § 1.10.10.4","sourceId":"2:EL-2.13","confidence":1,"runComments":[{"runNum":1,"status":"nv","comment":"No clearance dimensions provided on landscape plan showing distances from tree trunks to electric facilities. Measurement methodology cannot be verified because no measurements are shown."}]}]},{"headline":"Clearance from underground electrical equipment not documented","summary":"Landscape plan does not dimensionally relate trees to underground electrical equipment shown on electrical plan. Clearance from pad-mounted transformers (10-foot requirement), underground vaults and pull boxes (5-foot requirement), and applicability of root barrier requirements cannot be verified.","sheets":[9,21,31,37],"applicableArea":"Utilities & Infrastructure","severity":2,"confidence":2,"crossDep":"Electrical engineer must coordinate with landscape architect to verify clearances between trees and underground equipment shown on respective plans.","attn":"Root barrier requirements apply only if trees are within 20 feet of underground equipment. Applicability cannot be determined without dimensional cross-reference of plans.","details":[{"text":"Pad-mounted transformer locations shown on Sheet 21 electrical design plan. Locations not dimensionally cross-referenced with proposed trees on Sheet 31 landscape plan. Required 10-foot clearance from pad-mount equipment centerline cannot be verified.","citation":"UCM § 1.10.10.4","sourceId":"2:EL-2.7","confidence":2,"runComments":[{"runNum":1,"status":"nv","comment":"Pad-mounted electrical equipment locations are not clearly identified or cross-referenced on the landscape plan (Sheet 31). While the electrical plan (Sheet 21) shows transformers and pull boxes, their precise locations relative to proposed trees on the landscape plan cannot be verified. Clearances between trees and pad-mounted equipment cannot be determined from available documentation."},{"runNum":2,"status":"nv","comment":"Sheet 21 (Preliminary Electrical Design Plan) shows pad-mounted transformer locations. Sheet 31 (Landscape Plan) shows tree locations. However, these sheets are not dimensionally cross-referenced, and no analysis is provided showing the distance from each pad-mount transformer to nearby trees. The 10-foot clearance from pad-mount equipment centerline cannot be verified without dimensional analysis relating the two sheets."}]},{"text":"Underground electrical equipment (pull boxes, vaults) shown on electrical design plan but not cross-referenced with tree planting locations on landscape plan. Required 5-foot clearance from underground equipment cannot be verified without dimensional documentation linking the two sheets.","citation":"UCM § 1.10.10.4","sourceId":"2:EL-2.8","confidence":2,"runComments":[{"runNum":1,"status":"nv","comment":"Underground electrical equipment (pull boxes, vaults, other than duct banks/conduits) locations are shown on electrical plan (Sheet 21) but are not cross-referenced with tree planting locations on landscape plan (Sheet 31). The 5-foot clearance requirement cannot be verified without integration of tree and underground equipment locations on a single reference drawing."},{"runNum":2,"status":"nv","comment":"Underground electric equipment (pull boxes, utility lines) are indicated on the site plan and electrical design plan. Tree locations are shown on the landscape plan. However, no dimensional analysis or cross-reference is provided relating underground equipment locations to specific tree planting locations. The 5-foot clearance from underground equipment cannot be verified without dimensional documentation showing the relationship between proposed trees and underground utility vault/equipment locations."}]},{"text":"Root barrier requirements (4 feet deep, positioned 5 feet from underground equipment, applicable within 20-foot radius) cannot be determined or verified. No root barrier details or specifications provided on landscape plan or detail sheets. Applicability depends on tree/equipment proximity analysis not completed.","citation":"UCM § 1.10.10.4","sourceId":"2:EL-2.9","confidence":2,"runComments":[{"runNum":1,"status":"nv","comment":"Root barrier specifications are not visible on landscape plan or landscape details (Sheet 37). The root barrier requirement applies only when trees are within 20 feet of underground equipment, which cannot be determined from available documentation due to lack of cross-reference between tree and equipment locations. No root barrier details or specifications are noted on the landscape plan for any trees near utilities."},{"runNum":2,"status":"nv","comment":"Root barrier requirements apply only if trees are proposed within 20 feet of underground equipment (minimum 4 feet deep, positioned 5 feet from equipment). The landscape plan does not provide dimensional analysis of tree locations relative to underground equipment, so applicability cannot be determined. Additionally, no root barrier details or specifications are provided on the landscape plan or landscape details sheets. Cannot verify whether this requirement applies or, if it does, whether it is satisfied."}]}]},{"headline":"No Austin Energy written approval for trees in utility zones","summary":"Proposed trees are positioned within the 5-foot electric utility easement and within restricted clearance zones (15-foot for non-utility-compatible trees, 25-foot for large trees) without documented written approval from Austin Energy authorizing these reduced clearances.","sheets":[9,31,35],"applicableArea":"Utilities & Infrastructure","severity":3,"confidence":3,"crossDep":"Compliance requires either: (1) tree relocation to compliant distances, or (2) written approval from Austin Energy. Landscape architect and utility coordination required.","attn":"Runs 2 and 3 confirm non-compliance (status: fail). Approval letter from Austin Energy or documented variance required before site plan approval. Alternative: relocate trees to compliant clearance distances.","details":[{"text":"Trees proposed within 5-foot electric utility easement (recorded easements Volume 69 Page 14; Volume 5468 Page 885) and within 3-5 feet of southern boundary OHE distribution line. No written approval letter from Austin Energy provided in site plan package or supplementary documents. Required per UCM § 1.10.10.4 for trees within utility easement or reduced clearance zones.","citation":"UCM § 1.10.10.4","sourceId":"2:EL-2.15","confidence":3,"runComments":[{"runNum":1,"status":"nv","comment":"Trees are shown on landscape plan near the overhead electric distribution line, but no documented written approval from Austin Energy is included in the site plan package or supplementary documents authorizing tree placement within restricted clearance zones. General notes on Sheet 3 reference Austin Energy requirements for tree work within 10 feet of utility lines but do not indicate explicit approval for proposed tree locations."},{"runNum":2,"status":"fail","comment":"The landscape plan proposes trees (mitigation trees and other categories) at approximately 5-15 feet from the overhead electric distribution line along the southern property boundary, which falls within the utility easement area (5-foot electric easement per site plan) and within the 15-foot restricted clearance zone per UCM § 1.10.10.4. Site plan notes reference a '5' Electric Easement Vol. 69, Pg. 14' and '5' Elec. & Tele. Easement Vol. 5468, Pg. 885'. Proposed trees are located within or immediately adjacent to this utility easement without documented written approval from Austin Energy. No approval letter, permit exception, or authorization from Austin Energy is provided in the submitted plan set for any trees in utility easement areas. Variations to planting distances within utility easements require explicit written approval per UCM § 1.10.10.4."},{"runNum":3,"status":"fail","comment":"Trees are proposed within prohibited clearance zones: Large trees (Live Oak and Cedar Elm with mature heights 40+ feet) are positioned approximately 3-5 feet from the southern boundary OHE distribution line, which is less than the 25-foot minimum for large trees and the 15-foot minimum for other trees. No plan notes, correspondences, or Austin Energy written approval letters are present in the site plan package or supplementary documents to authorize this variation. Compliance requires either: (1) relocation of trees to compliant distances, or (2) documented written approval from Austin Energy explicitly authorizing the reduced clearance."}]}]}]},"fast_mode_state":"off","uuid":"3b9c2dc0-de1a-4df1-b967-831565298954"}
