{"level":30,"time":1778189108226,"pid":122,"hostname":"e70bc6df-98e","step":"synthesize-comments","item":"1.json","index":3,"runIndex":"run-1","type":"assistant","message":{"id":"gen_01KR250JHEKBDVAM3Y00WBXH2M","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01K4S4JBWsfHLDN2aoBGGHHY","name":"StructuredOutput","input":{"comments":[{"headline":"Surveyed overhead conductor elevations not provided","summary":"No registered surveyor field survey documenting existing overhead conductor elevations is included. This foundational data gap makes all clearance verification impossible across the entire site.","sheets":[9,11,21],"applicableArea":"Site-wide","severity":3,"confidence":3,"crossDep":"Austin Energy (surveyor coordination required)","attn":"","details":[{"text":"Building elevation sheets lack surveyed overhead conductor elevations. Sheet 21 references 'See Sht. 19 for Profile' but that sheet contains water utilities, not electrical data—leaving no conductor elevation documentation anywhere in the plan set.","citation":"UCM § 1.10.3","sourceId":"1:EL-1.7","confidence":3,"runComments":[{"runNum":1,"status":"fail","comment":"No building elevation sheets provided with surveyed conductor elevation data and clearance dimension annotations. Sheet 21 references 'See Sht. 19 for Profile' for overhead electric information, but the referenced sheet contains only water utility profile information, not overhead electric conductor elevations required for clearance verification."},{"runNum":2,"status":"fail","comment":"No building elevation sheets with surveyed overhead conductor elevations are included in the site plan package. The Preliminary Electrical Design Plan (Sheet 21) references 'See Sht. 19 for Profile' but that sheet contains water/wastewater utility profiles, not overhead electric conductor elevations. All 8 proposed buildings are positioned in proximity to documented overhead electric facilities (shown on Existing Conditions Survey and Site Plan), yet no surveyed conductor elevation data or clearance dimension callouts appear on any building elevation sheets. Applicant must provide registered surveyor field survey data showing existing overhead conductor elevations and clearance dimensions to all building features, with at least mid-span clearance measurements if vertical clearance appears marginal."},{"runNum":3,"status":"fail","comment":"Surveyed elevations and locations of overhead conductors are not included on any building elevation sheets. No building elevation sheets with conductor elevation data and clearance dimension annotations are provided in the plan set."}]},{"text":"No registered surveyor mid-span clearance measurements provided. Vertical clearances to driveways, parking areas, and site features cannot be calculated without pole locations and conductor elevation data.","citation":"UCM § 1.10.3","sourceId":"1:EL-1.31","confidence":3,"runComments":[{"runNum":1,"status":"fail","comment":"No registered surveyor mid-span clearance data is provided showing pole locations and actual overhead conductor elevations. Vertical clearance from overhead lines to driveways and parking areas cannot be calculated or verified without this surveyed data. While site plan shows overhead lines and grading contours, the vertical clearance requirement cannot be satisfied without registered surveyor documentation of mid-span clearances."},{"runNum":2,"status":"fail","comment":"Overhead electric facilities are documented on the site plan as existing infrastructure. Based on the extent of transmission facility notes on Sheet 3 and the pole locations shown on the Existing Conditions Survey, overhead conductors appear to be present on or very near the site. Proposed site features (driveways, parking areas, buildings) are in close proximity to documented overhead electric infrastructure. However, no registered surveyor field survey data is provided showing actual pole locations, conductor elevations, or mid-span clearance measurements. Without surveyed data confirming that vertical clearances meet the 16-foot (parking), 18-foot (roads), or 7.5-foot (horizontal) minimums, mid-span clearance verification cannot be performed. Applicant must provide a registered surveyor's field survey documenting pole locations, conductor elevations, and confirmed mid-span clearance distances for all driveway and parking areas passing beneath or adjacent to overhead electric facilities."},{"runNum":3,"status":"fail","comment":"Overhead electric lines exist adjacent to site. Proposed building FFEs are shown (ranging 683.0' to 687.50') but surveyed overhead conductor elevation data is not provided. When vertical clearance from overhead facilities to proposed site features appears marginal or insufficient based on available data, registered surveyor mid-span clearance data is required. No surveyor data provided."}]}]},{"headline":"Clearance dimension callouts absent from all documentation","summary":"Even where overhead electric facilities are shown on site plans, no dimension annotations verify clearances from outer conductors to any site features. This systematic absence applies to buildings, walls, parking, and all other infrastructure.","sheets":[9,21,38,39],"applicableArea":"Site-wide","severity":3,"confidence":3,"crossDep":"","attn":"","details":[{"text":"No section or enlarged plan details show dimension lines from outer electric conductor to outermost edges of buildings, parking areas, and projections. Clearance verification dimensions are completely absent.","citation":"UCM § 1.10.3","sourceId":"1:EL-1.8","confidence":3,"runComments":[{"runNum":1,"status":"fail","comment":"No section or enlarged plan details provided showing dimension lines from the outer electric conductor to the outermost edges of buildings and building projections. Clearance verification dimensions are completely absent from the site plan."},{"runNum":2,"status":"nv","comment":"No enlarged plan detail sections or cross-section views are provided showing dimension lines extending from the outer electric conductor to the outermost edge of buildings and building projections. While the site plan shows OHE line routing, no specific clearance dimensions or section views with conductor-to-building edge dimensions are depicted. Applicant must provide enlarged plan details and section views for all buildings within potential clearance distance of overhead facilities, with dimensions clearly labeled from outer conductor to all building faces, eaves, and roof projections."},{"runNum":3,"status":"fail","comment":"Section and plan view exhibits do not show dimension annotations from outer electric conductor to outermost edges of buildings, structures, or projections. No clearance verification dimensions are provided on any plan, section, or detail sheet."}]},{"text":"Site plan and electrical plan show overhead electric lines (labeled OHE) but provide no dimension annotations. Complete absence of clearance dimensions throughout plan set makes verification impossible.","citation":"UCM § 1.10.3","sourceId":"1:EL-1.23","confidence":2,"runComments":[{"runNum":1,"status":"fail","comment":"Site plan and electrical plan show overhead electric lines (labeled OHE) but provide no dimension annotations showing clearances from site features to these lines. The requirement mandates that all clearance dimensions originate from the outside conductor, not from the pole centerline. The complete absence of clearance dimension annotations renders verification impossible. Additionally, no notation specifies whether dimensions are measured from the outside conductor or pole center."},{"runNum":2,"status":"nv","comment":"While overhead electric lines are shown on the site plan, grading plan, and landscape plan as linear routing, NO clearance dimensions are shown anywhere in the plan set—neither from outside conductor nor from pole centerline. This makes it impossible to determine whether any clearance dimensions that do exist are measured correctly from the outside conductor (as required) or incorrectly from pole center. However, the fundamental issue is that clearance dimensions are entirely absent, making this specific verification unnecessary because there are no dimensions to evaluate for correctness. The absence of any clearance dimensions throughout the plan set is the primary deficiency (covered under other items)."}]},{"text":"Retaining wall cross-section exhibits (Sheets 38-39) do not show clearance dimension annotations from outer conductor to outermost edge of wall. Wall sections lack any reference to overhead electric lines or clearance requirements.","citation":"UCM § 1.10.3","sourceId":"1:EL-1.17","confidence":3,"runComments":[{"runNum":1,"status":"nv","comment":"Wall detail sheets (38, 39) show plan and section views of retaining walls, but no section views specifically show clearance dimension annotations from the outer electric conductor to the outermost edge of walls for clearance verification."},{"runNum":2,"status":"nv","comment":"Wall Plan detail sheets (38-39) are provided showing cross-sections of retaining walls throughout the site. However, none of these section views include the overhead electric conductor elevation or dimension callouts showing clearance from the conductor to the outermost edge of wall construction. Applicant must provide revised wall section views showing surveyed overhead conductor elevation and clear dimension lines from outer conductor to wall face for all walls located within potential clearance distance of overhead facilities."},{"runNum":3,"status":"fail","comment":"Retaining wall cross-section exhibits (Sheets 38-39) do not show clearance dimension annotations from outer electric conductor to outermost edge of wall. No OHE lines depicted on section views."}]}]},{"headline":"Buildings, projections, driveways, parking—clearance verification missing","summary":"No elevation sections, profile views, or clearance dimension annotations document overhead conductor heights relative to building faces, roof projections, eaves, driveways, or parking surfaces. Without this data, compliance with 7.5-foot horizontal, 15-foot radial, and vertical clearance minimums cannot be verified.","sheets":[9,11,21,31],"applicableArea":"Site Interior","severity":3,"confidence":2,"crossDep":"","attn":"Requires foundation data from Comment 1 (surveyed conductor elevations). Elevated walkway applicability unclear (EL-1.5).","details":[{"text":"Overhead electric distribution lines exist along boundaries; site plan shows buildings in relation to these lines but no profile/section views with surveyed conductor elevations and clearance dimensions are provided. Clearance verification impossible without elevation data.","citation":"UCM § 1.10.3","sourceId":"1:EL-1.1","confidence":3,"runComments":[{"runNum":1,"status":"nv","comment":"Overhead electric distribution lines exist along western and southern boundaries. Site plan shows buildings in relation to overhead lines, but no profile/section views with surveyed conductor elevations and clearance dimensions are provided. Horizontal clearances from outside conductors to buildings cannot be verified without elevation data and dimension annotations."},{"runNum":2,"status":"nv","comment":"Overhead electric lines are shown on site plan (Sheet 9) along western boundary and running east-west across northern portion of site. However, no building elevation sheets with surveyed overhead conductor elevations are provided. Without elevation data showing conductor heights and building face/roof elevations, the 7.5-foot horizontal sky-to-ground clearance requirement cannot be verified for any building. Applicant must provide surveyed conductor elevations on building elevation sheets with dimension callouts showing clearances from outside conductor to all building faces, overhangs, and projections."},{"runNum":3,"status":"nv","comment":"Overhead electric lines shown on site plan along southern boundary adjacent to Buildings 6, 7, 8. No surveyed conductor elevations or clearance dimension annotations provided to verify 7.5-foot horizontal sky-to-ground clearance requirement is met."}]},{"text":"No elevation or section views provided showing building projections in relation to overhead electric conductors. Roof overhangs, eaves, balconies, decks, and canopies lack clearance verification exhibits relative to surveyed conductor positions.","citation":"UCM § 1.10.3","sourceId":"1:EL-1.3","confidence":3,"runComments":[{"runNum":1,"status":"nv","comment":"No elevation or section views provided showing building projections in relation to overhead electric conductors. Clearance verification for both 7.5-foot sky-to-ground and 15-foot radial clearances cannot be completed without profile drawings with surveyed conductor elevations and dimension annotations."},{"runNum":2,"status":"nv","comment":"All 8 proposed buildings include roof overhangs and eaves as standard townhome construction. No building elevation sections, detail sheets, or cross-sections are provided showing the surveyed position of overhead conductors relative to building projections. Without elevation data and clearance dimension callouts, compliance with 7.5-foot sky-to-ground and 15-foot radial clearances for projections cannot be verified. Applicant must provide building elevation or section views showing overhangs, awnings, balconies, decks, and roof edges dimensioned from surveyed overhead conductor positions."},{"runNum":3,"status":"nv","comment":"No building elevation sheets or section views provided showing projections (overhangs, awnings, balconies, decks, canopies) relative to surveyed overhead conductor locations and elevations."}]},{"text":"Applicability of elevated walkways unclear from plans. If elevated walkways or platforms exist adjacent to OHE lines, no section views or clearance dimensions provided.","citation":"UCM § 1.10.3","sourceId":"1:EL-1.5","confidence":1,"runComments":[{"runNum":2,"status":"nv","comment":"Site plan shows concrete and decomposed granite walkways connecting buildings. If these walkways are elevated relative to grade (as typical in multi-family developments), they would be elevated platforms potentially requiring the 15-foot radial clearance. However, no elevation data is provided showing whether walkways are at-grade or elevated, and no vertical clearance dimensions from overhead conductors to walkway height are shown. Applicant should clarify walkway elevations and provide section views with clearance dimensions if walkways are elevated and within potential clearance distance of OHE."},{"runNum":3,"status":"nv","comment":"Applicability unclear from plans. If stairs, elevated walkways, or elevated platforms are proposed adjacent to OHE lines, no clearance verification documents provided."}]},{"text":"Driveway and parking finished grades not documented with section profiles showing vertical clearances to overhead conductors. No reference to whether truck traffic is expected or whether 16-foot or 18-foot minimum vertical clearance applies.","citation":"UCM § 1.10.6.2","sourceId":"1:EL-1.18","confidence":3,"runComments":[{"runNum":1,"status":"nv","comment":"Overhead electric lines exist along western and southern boundaries where internal site driveways and parking access roads are located. The grading plan shows finished floor elevations for buildings and general contours, but no section views are provided showing the finished driveway grades with overhead line clearance dimensions. Mid-span clearance verification is not documented. The determination of whether truck traffic is expected is not explicitly stated."},{"runNum":2,"status":"nv","comment":"Site plan shows interior driveways and parking areas. Overhead electric lines are documented on existing conditions survey and site plan. However, no grading plan section views or profiles are provided showing finished driveway/parking grade elevations with clearance dimensions to overhead electric facilities. The reference 'See Sht. 19 for Profile' on Sheet 21 is incorrect; Sheet 19 addresses water/wastewater utilities, not overhead electric. Applicant must provide grading plan cross-sections at driveway/parking areas showing finished grades and overhead conductor heights with vertical clearance dimensions. If clearances appear marginal, registered surveyor mid-span clearance data is required to verify compliance with 16-foot (parking without trucks) or 18-foot (truck traffic) minimums."},{"runNum":3,"status":"nv","comment":"Grading plan (Sheet 11) shows driveway locations but does not include cross-section or profile views showing final driveway grade elevations relative to surveyed overhead line clearances. No vertical clearance dimensions (16-foot or 18-foot) provided."}]},{"text":"Parking areas on concrete pads shown on site plan but no vertical clearance dimensions from overhead electric lines to parking surface provided. No clearance requirement note included on plans.","citation":"UCM § 1.10.6.2","sourceId":"1:EL-1.19","confidence":1,"runComments":[{"runNum":3,"status":"nv","comment":"Site plan shows parking areas but no vertical clearance dimensions from overhead electric lines to parking surface are provided. No clearance requirement note included on plans."}]},{"text":"Transmission lines shown on site; general notes reference transmission structures requiring 25-foot clearances from digging/grading. However, site plan does not identify transmission line locations or provide section views documenting the 30-foot vertical clearance from transmission lines to final road/driveway grades.","citation":"UCM § 1.14.0","sourceId":"1:EL-1.20","confidence":2,"runComments":[{"runNum":1,"status":"nv","comment":"General notes (Sheet 3) reference transmission structures requiring 25-foot clearances from digging/grading. However, the site plan does not clearly identify transmission line locations or elevations, nor does it provide section views documenting the 30-foot vertical clearance from transmission lines to final road/driveway grades."},{"runNum":2,"status":"nv","comment":"Sheet 3 documents extensive transmission facility requirements indicating transmission lines (voltage ≥60kV) are present or will be present on/adjacent to the site. However, no specification of transmission voltage or routing directly over driveways is provided. If transmission lines cross over internal driveways, the site plan must show finished driveway grades with vertical clearance dimensions demonstrating 30-foot minimum clearance from transmission conductor to ground surface. Applicant must clarify transmission line routing and provide grading plan sections with clearance dimensions if transmission lines cross driveway areas."}]},{"text":"Overhead lines shown crossing internal driveways and roads; visual inspection suggests some crossings may not be perpendicular to road alignments, but no explicit angle dimensions or notes provided to verify 90-degree crossing angles.","citation":"Reviewer Convention","sourceId":"1:EL-1.32","confidence":2,"runComments":[{"runNum":1,"status":"nv","comment":"Overhead electric lines shown crossing internal driveways and roads. However, no notation or detail indicates whether these crossings are at 90-degree angles to the road alignments. Visual inspection of the scale drawing suggests some crossings may not be perpendicular, but without explicit angle dimensions or notes, verification is not definitive."},{"runNum":3,"status":"nv","comment":"Cannot determine from plans whether new overhead electric lines are proposed to cross roadways. If crossings are planned, no indication of crossing angle alignment is shown."}]}]},{"headline":"Retaining walls—clearance dimensions from outer conductor missing","summary":"Retaining walls throughout the site, particularly along the southern boundary near overhead electric lines, lack dimension callouts measuring from the outer conductor to wall faces. The 7.5-foot horizontal sky-to-ground clearance cannot be verified.","sheets":[9,38,39],"applicableArea":"Site Interior","severity":2,"confidence":2,"crossDep":"","attn":"","details":[{"text":"Retaining walls are shown on site plan near overhead lines (particularly southern boundary), but clearance dimensions from outside electric conductor to outermost edge of walls are not provided. Clearance verification requires dimension annotations from the conductor, not the pole.","citation":"UCM § 1.10.3","sourceId":"1:EL-1.14","confidence":2,"runComments":[{"runNum":1,"status":"nv","comment":"Retaining walls are shown on the site plan near overhead lines (particularly southern boundary), but clearance dimensions from the outside electric conductor to the outermost edge of walls are not provided. Clearance verification requires dimension annotations measuring from the conductor, not from the pole."},{"runNum":2,"status":"nv","comment":"Site plan shows retaining walls throughout the site (documented on Wall Plan sheets 38-39 and visible on Site Plan sheet 9). Overhead electric lines are shown in proximity to the western boundary (in ROW) and running east-west across the northern portion. However, no dimension callouts show the clearance from the outside conductor of the overhead electric lines to retaining wall faces. Applicant must provide dimension annotations on site plan and wall section details showing the 7.5-foot horizontal sky-to-ground clearance is maintained from the outside conductor to all retaining walls in proximity to overhead electric facilities."},{"runNum":3,"status":"fail","comment":"Retaining walls shown on site plan and detailed on Wall Plan sheets (Sheets 38-39) in proximity to OHE lines, but no clearance dimension annotations from outer electric line to outermost edge of retaining wall. Wall section drawings do not reference or show overhead electric lines."}]}]},{"headline":"Fences—clearance and pole distance verification missing","summary":"Wooden privacy fences shown on site plan lack dimension callouts verifying 7.5-foot horizontal clearance from outer conductor to fence faces. Additionally, 10-foot clearance from fence posts to existing electric utility poles is not documented.","sheets":[9,31,38],"applicableArea":"Site Interior","severity":2,"confidence":2,"crossDep":"","attn":"Vehicle barriers applicability to project unclear (EL-1.13).","details":[{"text":"Fences shown on site plan near overhead electric lines but no clearance dimension annotations provided from outer conductor to fence. The 7.5-foot horizontal sky-to-ground clearance from outside conductor to fence structures cannot be verified.","citation":"UCM § 1.10.3","sourceId":"1:EL-1.9","confidence":2,"runComments":[{"runNum":1,"status":"nv","comment":"Retaining walls/fences are shown on the site plan near overhead lines, but clearance dimensions from the outside conductor to fence faces are not provided. Without dimension annotations, the 7.5-foot sky-to-ground clearance cannot be verified."},{"runNum":2,"status":"nv","comment":"Site plan shows wooden privacy fences along portions of the property perimeter. Overhead electric lines are shown in proximity to the western boundary (in the Valley View Road ROW) and running east-west across the northern portion of the property. However, no dimension callouts show the clearance from the outside conductor of the overhead electric lines to the fence structures. Applicant must provide dimension annotations on site plan and fence detail sheets showing the 7.5-foot horizontal sky-to-ground clearance is maintained from the outside conductor (not pole center) to all fences."},{"runNum":3,"status":"nv","comment":"Fences shown on site plan adjacent to or near OHE lines but no clearance dimension annotations provided. Cannot verify 7.5-foot horizontal sky-to-ground clearance from outside conductor to fence."}]},{"text":"Electric poles are shown on existing survey at property corners. Site plan shows retaining walls and fences but the specific horizontal distance between fence posts and existing poles is not provided. Without explicit dimension callouts, the 10-foot clearance cannot be verified.","citation":"Reviewer Convention","sourceId":"1:EL-1.10","confidence":2,"runComments":[{"runNum":1,"status":"nv","comment":"Electric poles are shown on the existing survey at the northwest and southwest corners. Retaining walls and fences are shown on the site plan. However, the specific horizontal dimension between fence posts and existing poles is not provided. Without explicit dimension callouts, the 10-foot clearance cannot be verified."},{"runNum":2,"status":"nv","comment":"Existing Conditions Survey (Sheet 4) shows utility poles located both outside the western property line (in Valley View Road ROW) and within the property boundaries. Site plan shows wooden privacy fences along portions of the property perimeter. However, no dimension callouts on the site plan verify that fence posts maintain the 10-foot horizontal clearance from existing electric pole locations. Applicant must provide dimension annotations showing fence post locations maintain minimum 10-foot clearance from all existing utility pole centers."},{"runNum":3,"status":"nv","comment":"Fence and pole locations shown but without specific distance annotations, the 10-foot clearance requirement for fence posts from electric poles cannot be verified."}]},{"text":"Cannot determine from site plan whether vehicle barrier fencing is proposed beneath OHE lines. If proposed, no clearance verification exhibits provided.","citation":"UCM § 1.10.3","sourceId":"1:EL-1.13","confidence":1,"runComments":[{"runNum":3,"status":"nv","comment":"Cannot determine from plans whether vehicle barrier fencing is proposed beneath OHE lines. If proposed, no clearance verification exhibits provided."}]}]},{"headline":"Utility poles—location conflicts and clearance verification missing","summary":"Existing utility poles shown on survey; however, conflicts with proposed driveways, sidewalks, and building locations are not resolved. No documentation shows pole relocation, 30-foot setback distances, or building clearance maintenance.","sheets":[4,9],"applicableArea":"Site Interior","severity":2,"confidence":2,"crossDep":"Austin Energy (pole relocation decisions)","attn":"Streetlight pole locations unclear (EL-1.24); new pole separation unclear if poles proposed (EL-1.35).","details":[{"text":"Existing survey shows electric poles near property corners; site plan shows internal driveways throughout. No explicit notation indicates whether driveways conflict with existing pole locations or whether 30-foot minimum setback will be maintained or poles relocated.","citation":"Reviewer Convention","sourceId":"1:EL-1.22","confidence":2,"runComments":[{"runNum":1,"status":"nv","comment":"Existing survey shows electric poles near property corners. Site plan shows internal driveways and access roads throughout the site. However, no explicit notation indicates whether any proposed driveways are in conflict with existing pole locations, nor is documentation provided showing pole relocation or the 30-foot minimum setback."},{"runNum":2,"status":"nv","comment":"Existing Conditions Survey (Sheet 4) shows a utility pole located within the property boundaries in the northern portion of the site, within the depicted electric easement area. Site plan shows internal driveway routing through the site. However, no dimension callouts or notes indicate whether this existing pole will be relocated or maintained, nor is the driveway alignment shown at sufficient detail to determine if there is a conflict requiring 30-foot minimum pole relocation. Applicant must clarify the status of existing on-site utility pole(s) and verify that any driveway alignments maintain minimum 30-foot distances from poles or confirm that poles will be relocated to resolve conflicts."},{"runNum":3,"status":"nv","comment":"Cannot determine from site plan whether existing electric poles conflict with proposed driveways. If conflicts exist, no relocation notes or revised pole locations are evident on plans."}]},{"text":"Existing survey shows electric poles in the ROW along Valley View Road near property corners. Site plan shows 'Construct 5' Concrete Sidewalk' along western property frontage but specific dimension from sidewalk alignment to existing poles at property ends is not provided.","citation":"Reviewer Convention","sourceId":"1:EL-1.25","confidence":2,"runComments":[{"runNum":1,"status":"nv","comment":"Existing survey shows electric poles at property corners. Site plan shows sidewalk improvements and modifications along Valley View Road frontage. However, the specific dimension from sidewalk alignment to existing poles at property ends is not provided. Without explicit clearance dimensions, verification is not possible."},{"runNum":2,"status":"nv","comment":"Site plan shows 'Construct 5' Concrete Sidewalk' along the western property frontage on Valley View Road. Existing Conditions Survey (Sheet 4) shows existing utility poles located in the ROW along Valley View Road near the property corners. However, the site plan does not include dimension callouts showing that the proposed sidewalk maintains clearance from existing power poles at each end of the property along the ROW frontage. Applicant must provide dimension annotations or notes confirming that the proposed sidewalk is properly routed to avoid contact with existing power poles at the north and south property line intersections with Valley View Road."},{"runNum":3,"status":"nv","comment":"Sidewalk alignments and power pole locations not specifically dimensioned. Cannot verify whether sidewalks conflict with pole locations at property corners along Valley View Road ROW."}]},{"text":"Existing survey may show streetlight pole locations; site plan shows buildings relative to boundaries but does not provide specific clearance dimension annotations from buildings to existing streetlight poles.","citation":"Reviewer Convention","sourceId":"1:EL-1.24","confidence":1,"runComments":[{"runNum":3,"status":"nv","comment":"Cannot determine from site plan whether existing streetlights are present adjacent to buildings. Streetlight locations not clearly identified relative to proposed structures."}]},{"text":"Electrical design plan shows underground service infrastructure but does not clearly indicate whether new power poles are proposed. If new poles proposed, locations relative to existing poles are not dimensioned to verify 20-foot minimum separation.","citation":"Reviewer Convention","sourceId":"1:EL-1.35","confidence":1,"runComments":[{"runNum":1,"status":"nv","comment":"Electrical design plan shows underground electric service infrastructure but does not clearly indicate whether new power poles are proposed for service conversion. If new poles are proposed, their location relative to existing poles is not dimensioned. Without explicit notation of new pole locations and distances to existing poles, the 20-foot minimum separation cannot be verified."}]},{"text":"Existing Conditions Survey shows utility poles in surrounding area; however, without clear depiction of existing streetlight pole locations adjacent to property, the relationship between proposed buildings and streetlights cannot be verified.","citation":"Reviewer Convention","sourceId":"1:EL-1.39","confidence":1,"runComments":[{"runNum":2,"status":"nv","comment":"Existing Conditions Survey (Sheet 4) shows utility poles and other infrastructure in the surrounding area. Site plan shows buildings positioned on the development site. However, without a clear depiction of existing streetlight pole locations adjacent to the property, the relationship between proposed buildings and streetlights cannot be verified. Applicant should confirm the locations of any existing streetlight poles in the Valley View Road ROW adjacent to the property and provide dimension callouts on the site plan showing that proposed buildings maintain adequate clearance from these existing streetlights."}]}]},{"headline":"Facility classification not specified—distribution vs. transmission","summary":"Conductor type (primary, neutral, secondary) and voltage classification of overhead electric facilities are not labeled or specified. This is critical: the applicable clearance standards differ significantly between distribution (<60kV) and transmission (≥60kV) facilities.","sheets":[3,9,21],"applicableArea":"Site-wide","severity":2,"confidence":2,"crossDep":"Austin Energy (facility classification confirmation)","attn":"","details":[{"text":"Overhead distribution lines shown on site plans but conductor type (primary, neutral, secondary) and voltage level not labeled. The 15-foot radial clearance requirement for distribution facilities cannot be verified without conductor identification.","citation":"UCM § 1.10.3","sourceId":"1:EL-1.2","confidence":2,"runComments":[{"runNum":1,"status":"nv","comment":"Overhead distribution lines are shown on site plans, but the conductor type (primary, neutral, secondary) and voltage level are not labeled. The 15-foot radial clearance requirement for distribution primary and neutral conductors cannot be verified without conductor type identification and clearance dimension documentation."},{"runNum":2,"status":"nv","comment":"The site plan does not specify the conductor type (primary, neutral, secondary) or voltage classification of the overhead electric facilities. The extensive transmission notes on Sheet 3 suggest these may be transmission facilities (≥60kV), which would have different clearance requirements (UCM § 1.14.0) than distribution facilities (<60kV). Without specification of conductor type and facility classification, the 15-foot radial clearance requirement for distribution facilities cannot be verified as applicable. No clearance dimensions from outside conductor to any customer facility are shown on site plan or detailed sheets."},{"runNum":3,"status":"nv","comment":"Overhead distribution facilities shown on site plan. No surveyed data, conductor type identification (primary vs. neutral), or 15-foot radial clearance dimension annotations provided to verify requirement is met."}]},{"text":"General notes reference transmission structures and transmission easements. However, site plan does not clearly differentiate between distribution and transmission easement areas, nor specify whether proposed fencing near transmission lines uses non-conductive material or is grounded.","citation":"UCM § 1.14.0","sourceId":"1:EL-1.12","confidence":2,"runComments":[{"runNum":1,"status":"nv","comment":"General notes (Sheet 3) reference transmission structures and requirement that no structures impair access within transmission easements. However, the site plan does not clearly identify which overhead lines are transmission (≥60kV) versus distribution (<60kV), nor do the plans specify whether any proposed fencing near transmission lines is constructed of non-conductive material or grounded. Material specifications and grounding details are not provided."},{"runNum":2,"status":"nv","comment":"Sheet 3 contains extensive Electric Transmission Notes indicating transmission facilities are present on or adjacent to the site. The notes reference transmission lines, transmission structures, and transmission easements. However, the site plan does not clearly specify whether proposed fencing is located beneath or within transmission easements. Additionally, no detail sheets are provided showing fence material specifications (conductive vs. non-conductive) or grounding detail drawings. If fencing is proposed within transmission easement areas, applicant must provide fence detail sheets with material specifications and grounding designs as required."},{"runNum":3,"status":"nv","comment":"General notes reference 'transmission structures' with 25-foot clearance requirement and transmission easement road load requirements, indicating transmission facilities may exist. Applicability depends on final confirmation of transmission vs. distribution classification. No fence material specifications or grounding details provided if fencing near transmission lines."}]}]},{"headline":"Transmission easement boundaries not delineated—potential structure violations","summary":"Transmission easement boundaries are not clearly shown on the site plan or easement exhibits. Sheet 3 explicitly prohibits permanent structures within transmission easements; however, applicant has not confirmed that no buildings, walls, or improvements conflict with documented transmission easement areas.","sheets":[2,3,4,9],"applicableArea":"Site-wide","severity":3,"confidence":2,"crossDep":"Austin Energy (transmission easement boundary verification)","attn":"","details":[{"text":"Sheet 3, Electric Transmission Notes #16 explicitly states 'Owner may not place, erect, construct or maintain the following within electric transmission easement: any permanent structures, including habitable structures such as homes, mobile homes, garages, or offices.' However, site plan does not clearly delineate transmission easement boundary and does not confirm no structures are within documented transmission easement.","citation":"UCM § 1.10.3","sourceId":"1:EL-1.27","confidence":2,"runComments":[{"runNum":1,"status":"nv","comment":"Electric easements (5-foot) are shown on the plat and site plan. General notes explicitly prohibit structures within transmission easements and require 7.5-foot clearances within distribution easements. However, the site plan does not clearly differentiate between distribution and transmission easement areas, nor does it explicitly document that all structures maintain the required 7.5-foot clearance from outside conductors within easement boundaries. The absolute prohibition on structures beneath/over distribution facilities is stated in notes but not visually verified with dimension callouts."},{"runNum":2,"status":"fail","comment":"Sheet 3, Electric Transmission Notes #16 explicitly states: 'Owner may not place, erect, construct or maintain the following within electric transmission easement: any permanent structures, including, but not limited to habitable structures such as homes, mobile homes, garages, or offices.' The Existing Conditions Survey (Sheet 4) shows a utility pole within a 15' Electric Easement in the northern portion of the property. The site plan does not clearly delineate this transmission easement boundary, and does not confirm that no proposed structures, walls, or improvements are located within the documented transmission easement. Additionally, the site plan does not show clearance dimension callouts demonstrating 7.5-foot clearance from outside conductor for any items that may be placed at the easement edge. Applicant must clearly depict the transmission easement boundary on the site plan and verify that no buildings, structures, walls, or other customer facilities are installed within the easement. If any improvements are located within the easement boundary, they must be relocated outside the easement."},{"runNum":3,"status":"nv","comment":"Site plan shows buildings and features adjacent to OHE easement, but without surveyed conductor elevations and clearance dimensions, compliance with prohibition on installing facilities under/over distribution lines and the 7.5-foot clearance from outside conductor cannot be verified."}]},{"text":"General notes reference transmission structures and requirement that no structures impair access within transmission easements. However, site plan does not clearly indicate whether angled guy anchors from transmission structures exist on site or will exist, nor are easement boundaries (10-foot either-side plus 50-foot extension) depicted.","citation":"Reviewer Convention","sourceId":"1:EL-1.41","confidence":1,"runComments":[{"runNum":1,"status":"nv","comment":"General notes reference transmission structures and easements. However, the site plan does not clearly indicate whether angled guy anchors from transmission structures exist or will exist on the site. If they do exist, the 10-foot either-side plus 50-foot extension easement boundaries are not depicted on the plat or site plan."}]}]},{"headline":"Down guy wires and anchor easements not documented","summary":"Existing utility poles are shown on survey; however, the specific locations of down guy wires (support cables from poles to ground anchors) are not clearly marked or detailed. Proposed accessible paths and driveways lack conflict analysis with down guy infrastructure.","sheets":[4,9],"applicableArea":"Site Interior","severity":2,"confidence":2,"crossDep":"Austin Energy (down guy wire documentation and easement confirmation)","attn":"","details":[{"text":"Existing survey shows utility pole locations with down guy anchor symbols. However, site plan does not explicitly indicate whether down guy wires from existing poles conflict with proposed accessible routes, driveways, or site features, nor document relocation or conversion to self-supporting poles.","citation":"UCM § 1.17.0","sourceId":"1:EL-1.40","confidence":2,"runComments":[{"runNum":1,"status":"nv","comment":"Existing survey shows utility pole locations with legend including down guy anchor symbols. Site plan shows accessible paths and driveways throughout the site. However, the site plan does not explicitly indicate whether down guy wires from existing poles conflict with proposed accessible routes or driveways, nor does it document relocation or conversion to self-supporting poles. Without explicit conflict notation or relocation documentation, compliance cannot be verified."},{"runNum":2,"status":"nv","comment":"Existing Conditions Survey (Sheet 4) shows utility poles located on the property and in adjacent ROW. While electric transmission notes on Sheet 3 reference down guy anchors as infrastructure requiring clearance coordination, the specific locations of down guy wires (support cables from distribution poles to ground anchors) are not clearly marked or detailed on the site plan. Proposed accessible paths, driveways, and site features are shown on the site plan, but without detailed down guy wire documentation, conflicts cannot be definitively verified or confirmed as resolved. If down guy wires from existing poles conflict with proposed accessible routes or driveways, applicant must provide revised utility plan showing either pole relocation or conversion to self-supporting poles, with supporting documentation."},{"runNum":3,"status":"nv","comment":"Down guy wire locations from existing distribution poles are not explicitly shown or annotated on site plan. Guide notes that electric utility infrastructure is frequently omitted from plans. Cannot verify whether guy wires conflict with proposed accessible paths, driveways, or site features without detailed utility survey."}]},{"text":"Existing survey shows utility pole locations and legend includes symbols for down guy anchors. However, plat and site plan do not clearly identify specific down guy anchor point locations or their associated easement boundaries (10-foot width extending 5 feet past anchor ground entry).","citation":"Reviewer Convention","sourceId":"1:EL-1.42","confidence":2,"runComments":[{"runNum":1,"status":"nv","comment":"Existing survey shows utility pole locations and legend includes symbols for down guy anchors. However, the plat and site plan do not clearly identify specific down guy anchor point locations or their associated easement boundaries (10-foot width extending 5 feet past anchor ground entry)."},{"runNum":2,"status":"nv","comment":"Existing Conditions Survey (Sheet 4) shows utility poles on site and in adjacent ROW. If down guy anchors exist associated with these poles, they are not explicitly labeled or located on the survey. Easement plat (Sheet 2) does not clearly delineate dedicated down guy anchor easements showing the required 10-foot width and 5-foot extension past anchor ground entry. Applicant must provide detailed survey and easement exhibit showing down guy anchor locations (if any exist) with dedicated easements meeting the 10-foot width by 5-foot-extension specification per Austin Energy Transmission Engineering Standards."},{"runNum":3,"status":"nv","comment":"Down guy anchor locations not clearly shown on easement exhibit or utility plans. Cannot verify whether dedicated easements for down guy anchors are provided extending 10 feet wide with 5-foot extension past anchor ground entry."}]}]},{"headline":"Trees—species and clearances not utility-compatible","summary":"Landscape plan shows mitigation trees near overhead electric lines with species including Live Oak and Cedar Elm. These species exceed utility-compatible height limits and lack documented lateral clearance distances from conductors (50 feet for transmission; 10 feet for distribution).","sheets":[31,32,35],"applicableArea":"Site Interior","severity":2,"confidence":2,"crossDep":"City Arborist (tree compatibility verification)","attn":"","details":[{"text":"Landscape plan shows mitigation trees ('M' designation) near southern property boundary where overhead electric lines exist. Plant list specifies 2 Live Oak (mature height 60+ feet) and 10 Cedar Elm (mature height 40-60 feet). Live Oak and tall Cedar Elm exceed utility-compatible height thresholds. Trees within 10 lateral feet of distribution lines must be from ECM Appendix F Utility Compatible list with mature heights ≤20 feet. No lateral distance dimensions shown from trees to overhead conductors.","citation":"ECM § 2.4.1.D; ECM § 2.4.2.C; UCM § 1.10.10.4","sourceId":"1:EL-1.37","confidence":3,"runComments":[{"runNum":1,"status":"nv","comment":"Landscape plan (Sheet 31) shows mitigation trees marked 'M' positioned within close proximity to overhead electric lines (OHE) at the southern boundary. Proposed shade trees and ornamental trees are listed on Sheet 35 (Live Oak, Cedar Elm, Texas Mountain Laurel, Mexican Redbud) but the specific location of each tree species on the landscape plan is not cross-referenced with clearance distance callouts. Without species identification on the landscape plan for each tree near overhead lines and without explicit verification that such trees are from the ECM Appendix F Utility Compatible list, compliance cannot be confirmed. Additionally, no lateral distance dimensions are provided from tree locations to overhead conductors."},{"runNum":2,"status":"nv","comment":"Landscape plan (Sheet 31) shows mitigation trees ('M' designation) and other plantings near the overhead electric line shown along the southern boundary of the site. Tree list (Sheet 32) provides caliper sizes and species. However, no lateral distance dimensions are shown on the landscape plan indicating how far proposed trees are located from the overhead electric conductors. Per UCM § 1.10.10.4, trees must maintain 50 lateral feet from transmission conductors (or 10 lateral feet from distribution conductors if facility is distribution rather than transmission). Tree species must be verified against ECM Appendix F 'UC' (Utility Compatible) designation for trees within the clearance zones. Applicant must provide: (1) dimension callouts showing lateral distances from OHE to all trees within 50 feet of the line; (2) confirmation that tree species are from the UC list; (3) site grading contours showing clearance compliance."},{"runNum":3,"status":"fail","comment":"Landscape plan (Sheet 31) shows mitigation trees (marked 'M') proposed along southern property boundary near OHE lines. Plant list (Sheet 35) specifies: 2 Live Oak (Quercus virginiana) and 10 Cedar Elm (Ulmus crassifolia). Live Oak is not utility-compatible (mature height 60+ feet exceeds UC list criteria); Cedar Elm (mature height 40-60 feet) is problematic near distribution lines. Trees within 10 lateral feet of distribution lines must be from ECM Appendix F Utility Compatible list with mature heights ≤20 feet generally."}]}]},{"headline":"Right-of-way and property line coordination—clearances unclear","summary":"Buildings and site features are positioned near property lines where overhead electric facilities exist or may be located in adjacent right-of-way. Clearance from buildings and features to right-of-way-located utilities is not documented with dimension annotations.","sheets":[4,9],"applicableArea":"Valley View Road Frontage","severity":2,"confidence":2,"crossDep":"Austin Energy (ROW utility coordination)","attn":"","details":[{"text":"Existing survey shows overhead utility poles in Valley View Road right-of-way and overhead lines running along western boundary and extending onto property. Buildings 1 and 2 are positioned near western property boundary in proximity to these ROW-adjacent electric facilities. No clearance dimensions shown indicating distance from building faces to outside conductor of overhead lines in the adjacent ROW.","citation":"UCM § 1.10.3","sourceId":"1:EL-1.6","confidence":2,"runComments":[{"runNum":1,"status":"nv","comment":"Overhead electric lines exist in the right-of-way (Valley View Road, western boundary). Buildings are proposed near this ROW. However, no clearance dimensions or surveyed conductor elevations are provided to verify that both 7.5-foot sky-to-ground and 15-foot radial clearances are maintained from existing or relocated facilities."},{"runNum":2,"status":"nv","comment":"Existing Conditions Survey (Sheet 4) shows overhead utility poles located outside the western property line in the Valley View Road right-of-way, with overhead lines running along the road and extending onto the property. Buildings 1 and 2 are positioned near the western property boundary in proximity to these ROW-adjacent electric facilities. However, no clearance dimensions are shown on site plan indicating the distance from building faces to the outside conductor of the overhead lines in the adjacent ROW. Applicant must provide dimension callouts on site plan and building elevations showing the 7.5-foot horizontal and 15-foot radial clearances are maintained from ROW-located overhead electric facilities to all buildings."},{"runNum":3,"status":"nv","comment":"Overhead electric lines shown on site plan along southern boundary adjacent to Buildings 6, 7, 8. No surveyed conductor elevations or clearance dimension annotations provided to verify 7.5-foot horizontal sky-to-ground clearance requirement is met."}]},{"text":"Buildings shown within 5 feet of property lines on western (Valley View Road) and southern boundaries where electric facilities exist or may be located in ROW or adjacent property. Specific documentation verifying that permanent structure foundations allow necessary clearance space for electric utility access is not provided.","citation":"Reviewer Convention","sourceId":"1:EL-1.30","confidence":1,"runComments":[{"runNum":1,"status":"nv","comment":"Buildings are shown within 5 feet of property lines on the western (Valley View Road) and southern boundaries where electric facilities exist or may be located in ROW or adjacent property. Specific documentation verifying that permanent structure foundations allow necessary clearance space for electric utility access is not provided."}]}]},{"headline":"Utility equipment and infrastructure—clearance documentation missing","summary":"Trash enclosures, water meters, water lines, decorative lighting, electric meters, transformers, and service masts lack clearance documentation from overhead electric facilities. Meter access clearances and equipment installation details are not verified.","sheets":[9,19,20,21,31],"applicableArea":"Site Interior","severity":1,"confidence":1,"crossDep":"","attn":"Meter access clearance verification incomplete (EL-1.38); transformer niche installation applicability unclear (EL-1.44); secondary/primary crossing angle unclear (EL-1.33); water meter coordination (EL-1.28).","details":[{"text":"Site plan shows trash collection areas but does not provide clearance dimension annotations from overhead electric facilities to trash enclosures. A visual inspection cannot determine clearance from raised bins to overhead lines without vertical clearance dimensions and conductor elevation data.","citation":"Reviewer Convention","sourceId":"1:EL-1.26","confidence":1,"runComments":[{"runNum":1,"status":"nv","comment":"Site plan shows trash collection areas but does not provide clearance dimension annotations from overhead electric facilities to trash enclosures. A visual inspection cannot determine clearance from raised bins to overhead lines without vertical clearance dimensions and conductor elevation data."},{"runNum":3,"status":"nv","comment":"Cannot determine if trash enclosures or receptacles are shown beneath overhead electric facilities. Trash areas not clearly identified in proximity to OHE lines on site plan."}]},{"text":"Water meter locations are not clearly identified on utility plans. Service-drop overhead electric lines (if present) and their relationship to water meter locations are not documented with clearance dimension annotations.","citation":"UCM § 1.10.3; UCM § 1.10.6.2","sourceId":"1:EL-1.28","confidence":1,"runComments":[{"runNum":1,"status":"nv","comment":"Water meter locations are not clearly identified on utility plans. Service-drop overhead electric lines (if present) and their relationship to water meter locations are not documented with clearance dimension annotations. Without explicit identification of meter locations and overhead service-drop routing, verification is not possible."},{"runNum":3,"status":"nv","comment":"Water meter locations shown on site plan but not specifically analyzed or dimensioned relative to overhead electric service drop routing. No clearance verification provided."}]},{"text":"Utility plans show water line routing beneath buildings and throughout site. Overhead distribution poles and conductors exist near property boundaries. However, no clearance dimension annotations provided from overhead electrical distribution facilities to water lines.","citation":"Reviewer Convention","sourceId":"1:EL-1.29","confidence":1,"runComments":[{"runNum":1,"status":"nv","comment":"Utility plans show water line routing beneath buildings and throughout the site. Overhead distribution poles and conductors exist near the property boundaries. However, no clearance dimension annotations are provided from overhead electrical distribution facilities to water lines, nor is documentation provided confirming adequate clearance maintenance."},{"runNum":3,"status":"nv","comment":"Water line routing shown on utility tap plan but no clearance dimensions provided relative to overhead distribution poles and conductors. Required clearance cannot be verified."}]},{"text":"Landscape plan may show site lighting fixtures but clearance verification dimensions and relocation notes relative to overhead electric lines are not provided. No photometric plan with clearance dimension callouts provided if decorative lighting proposed beneath overhead facilities.","citation":"UCM § 1.10.3","sourceId":"1:EL-1.36","confidence":1,"runComments":[{"runNum":1,"status":"nv","comment":"Landscape plan may show site lighting/decorative fixtures but clearance verification dimensions and relocation notes relative to overhead electric lines are not provided. Without explicit clearance dimension annotations showing 7.5-foot sky-to-ground and 15-foot radial clearances from conductors to lighting fixtures, or notes indicating relocation of fixtures away from overhead lines, compliance cannot be verified."},{"runNum":2,"status":"nv","comment":"Site plan references exterior lighting requirements (Block 1, Sheet 9) and notes that all exterior lighting must be full cut-off and fully shielded per Subchapter E 2.5. However, no photometric plan or lighting fixture location plan is provided showing specific decorative fixture locations in relation to the overhead electric lines documented on the site. If decorative lighting is proposed beneath or in proximity to overhead lines, clearance dimensions (7.5-foot sky-to-ground, 15-foot radial) must be provided. Applicant should clarify whether decorative lighting fixtures are proposed beneath overhead facilities and if so, provide photometric plan with clearance dimension callouts or relocation confirmation."},{"runNum":3,"status":"nv","comment":"Landscape plan shows site lighting but specific decorative lighting locations relative to overhead lines are not clearly identified or dimensioned. Clearance verification dimensions not provided."}]},{"text":"Electrical design plan shows transformer pad locations but provides no section views documenting vertical clearance from overhead electric lines to tops of transformers. The 7.5-foot minimum vertical sky-to-ground clearance cannot be verified.","citation":"UCM § 1.10.3","sourceId":"1:EL-1.43","confidence":1,"runComments":[{"runNum":1,"status":"nv","comment":"Electrical design plan shows transformer pad locations but provides no section views documenting vertical clearance from overhead electric lines to tops of transformers. The 7.5-foot minimum vertical sky-to-ground clearance cannot be verified without elevation data and dimension annotations."},{"runNum":3,"status":"nv","comment":"Electrical design plan shows transformer pad locations but does not provide vertical clearance dimensions from overhead electric lines to top of transformer equipment. Section views with clearance dimension annotations are not provided."}]},{"text":"Overhead lines shown crossing internal driveways; cannot determine from plans whether new overhead lines are proposed to cross roadways. If crossings planned, no indication of crossing angle alignment or secondary/primary conductor separation shown.","citation":"Reviewer Convention","sourceId":"1:EL-1.33","confidence":1,"runComments":[{"runNum":3,"status":"nv","comment":"Cannot determine from plans whether new overhead electric lines are proposed to cross roadways. If crossings are planned, no indication of crossing angle alignment is shown."}]},{"text":"Electrical design plan does not indicate whether transformers or switchgears will be installed in niche service configurations (covered or recessed). If planned, required 35-foot vertical clearance inside niche from equipment top to overhead structures not documented.","citation":"UCM § 1.10.4","sourceId":"1:EL-1.44","confidence":1,"runComments":[{"runNum":1,"status":"nv","comment":"Electrical design plan does not indicate whether any transformers or switchgears will be installed in niche service configurations (covered or recessed installations). If such installations are planned, the required 35-foot vertical clearance inside the niche from the top of equipment to the bottom of overhead structures is not documented."}]},{"text":"No building elevation sheets showing service-mast through-roof installation locations or clearance dimensions provided. Cannot verify 3-foot clearance above roof (or 18-inch clearance if within 4 feet of roof edge) for voltages ≤300V.","citation":"UCM § 1.10.6.2","sourceId":"1:EL-1.47","confidence":1,"runComments":[{"runNum":3,"status":"nv","comment":"No building elevation sheets showing service-mast through-roof installation locations or clearance dimensions are provided. Cannot verify 3-foot clearance above roof (or 18-inch clearance if within 4 feet of roof edge) for voltages ≤300V."}]},{"text":"Electrical design plan shows transformer pads and meter locations but does not provide enlarged meter area detail sheets. Meter access clearances (30-inch-wide front space, 36-inch front depth, 6.5-foot headroom) and obstructions from fences, walls, or equipment not explicitly verified.","citation":"UCM § 1.9.3.1","sourceId":"1:EL-1.38","confidence":1,"runComments":[{"runNum":1,"status":"nv","comment":"Electrical design plan shows transformer pads and general utility locations but does not provide enlarged meter area detail sheets showing the specific space reserved for meter installations. Obstructions from fences, walls, equipment, vegetation, or building projections are not explicitly addressed in clearance documentation. Without detailed meter area plans confirming 30-inch-wide front space, 36-inch front depth, and 6.5-foot headroom per UCM § 1.10.9, obstructions cannot be ruled out."},{"runNum":3,"status":"nv","comment":"Electrical design plan shows meter locations but does not include access clearance analysis or obstruction verification. Required working clearances (30-inch-wide front space, 36-inch front depth, 6.5-foot headroom) not verified on plans."}]}]},{"headline":"Construction phase clearances and safety requirements","summary":"Construction staging areas and equipment laydown zones are not documented on a logistics plan. Additionally, the required Texas law 48-hour safety notification to Austin Energy is not prominently placed on cover sheets in the standard required format.","sheets":[1,3,5],"applicableArea":"Plan Documentation","severity":1,"confidence":1,"crossDep":"Austin Energy (construction coordination)","attn":"Texas Health & Safety Code Chapter 752, Section 752.003 requires explicit notification language on contract documents.","details":[{"text":"Construction staging areas and equipment zones are shown on erosion control plan but no documentation verifies that these areas maintain required 10-foot radial clearance from overhead electric lines. This is a construction-phase requirement distinct from permanent clearances.","citation":"UCM § 1.10.2","sourceId":"1:EL-1.45","confidence":1,"runComments":[{"runNum":1,"status":"nv","comment":"Construction staging areas and equipment zones are shown on the erosion control plan, but no documentation verifies that these areas maintain the required 10-foot radial clearance from overhead electric lines. This is a construction-phase requirement distinct from permanent clearances. Without explicit dimension annotations or notes, compliance cannot be confirmed."},{"runNum":2,"status":"nv","comment":"Sheet 3 documents extensive construction coordination requirements for work near transmission facilities, referencing OSHA clearance requirements. However, no construction staging area plan, equipment laydown zone diagram, or work platform logistics plan is provided with the site plan submittal. During construction, equipment and materials must maintain 10-foot radial clearance from energized overhead lines per OSHA 1910.333 and UCM § 1.10.2 (this is distinct from permanent clearance requirements). Applicant must provide a detailed construction logistics plan showing staging areas, equipment operation zones, crane swing radius, and scaffold/platform locations with dimension callouts verifying 10-foot radial clearance from all overhead electric facilities during construction phases."},{"runNum":3,"status":"nv","comment":"No construction staging plan or logistics plan provided showing staging area boundaries, crane swing radius, or material storage locations relative to overhead electric lines. Cannot verify 10-foot radial clearance during construction from submitted documents."}]},{"text":"Sheet 3 contains transmission-specific safety meeting note but does not include the required standard 48-hour notification language mandated by Texas Health & Safety Code Chapter 752, Section 752.003 in a standard location (cover sheet or general notes). Applicant must notify Austin Energy at least 48 hours before work begins near high-voltage overhead lines.","citation":"UCM § 1.10.2","sourceId":"1:EL-1.46","confidence":1,"runComments":[{"runNum":1,"status":"fail","comment":"Sheet 3 (General Notes) contains a note stating that a pre-construction safety meeting is required with Austin Energy 48 hours before commencement of construction (Electric Transmission Notes, Item 3). However, this is a transmission-specific note. The required standard note for all projects with overhead high-voltage lines per Texas Health & Safety Code Chapter 752, Section 752.003, stating that the owner/contractor must NOTIFY Austin Energy at least 48 hours before work begins near high-voltage overhead lines, is not present in a standard location (cover sheet or general notes) in the standard required format. The current note references a safety meeting but does not include the explicit 48-hour notification requirement language mandated by Texas law."}]}]}]}}],"model":"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001","stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":0},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"5fec1e61-babc-4f6a-a405-298c428553e2","uuid":"e3a0ca37-ba46-4d1d-a75a-49e3c48d5a97"}
