{"level":30,"time":1778189164362,"pid":122,"hostname":"e70bc6df-98e","step":"synthesize-comments","item":"13.json","index":2,"runIndex":"run-1","type":"assistant","message":{"id":"gen_01KR25AFRYQGCQHBMRSR0SZEXD","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"## Synthesis Complete\n\nI've successfully synthesized 37 electrical infrastructure findings into **11 consolidated review comments** (3.7:1 consolidation ratio).\n\n### Comment Organization\n\n**Comments 1-11** cover these core themes:\n\n1. **Horizontal clearances to adjacent site features** (9 findings merged) — dimension callouts missing for clearances to buildings, sidewalks, site fixtures, and inter-pad spacing\n2. **Access door orientation** (2 findings) — not documented; blocks verification of vegetation and access clearances\n3. **Building feature clearances** (3 findings) — equipment type and building elevations not provided; windows/doors/balconies clearances undimensioned\n4. **Fire safety clearances** (3 findings) — fire exits, fire escapes, and fire lanes lack dimensional documentation\n5. **Vegetation management** (2 findings) — tree compatibility and root barriers not verified on landscape plan\n6. **Underground utility coordination** (5 findings) — water, wastewater, storm drain, gas, and general underground utilities lack clearance dimensions and coordination drawings\n7. **Vertical clearance documentation** (2 findings) — cross-sections and profiles missing for transformer-to-utility vertical relationships\n8. **Overhead conductor clearances** (3 findings) — sky-to-ground and radius clearances to distribution lines not dimensioned\n9. **Transformer equipment specs** (2 findings) — equipment type and AE Design-approved pad details not provided\n10. **Transformer easements & property compliance** (4 findings) — easements not exhibited; PUE placement lacks approval; electrical routing verification missing\n11. **Bollard and access protection** (2 findings) — vehicle protection bollards and confined space documentation not shown\n\n### Key Findings Summary\n\n- **All 37 input findings accounted for** via `sourceId` tracing\n- **Cross-department notes** flag fire protection, landscape, architecture, utilities, and public works coordination needs\n- **High-severity items** (3): fire safety clearances, utility coordination, easement compliance, and AE Design-approved pad specifications\n- **Confidence levels** reflect per-run consensus (most findings caught by all 3 runs = high confidence)\n- **Attention flags** note unconfirmed conditions, low-confidence findings, and prerequisite documentation\n\nAll reviewer observations from the 3 audit runs are preserved verbatim in `runComments` for full traceability."}],"model":"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001","stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":0},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"c74ff556-b845-41ec-b2c9-9037e48bc40f","uuid":"fd9b1098-ca84-47e8-bbc8-12b43b305d82"}
{"level":30,"time":1778189164423,"pid":122,"hostname":"e70bc6df-98e","step":"synthesize-comments","item":"13.json","index":2,"runIndex":"run-1","type":"result","subtype":"success","is_error":false,"duration_ms":333300,"duration_api_ms":333136,"num_turns":3,"result":"## Synthesis Complete\n\nI've successfully synthesized 37 electrical infrastructure findings into **11 consolidated review comments** (3.7:1 consolidation ratio).\n\n### Comment Organization\n\n**Comments 1-11** cover these core themes:\n\n1. **Horizontal clearances to adjacent site features** (9 findings merged) — dimension callouts missing for clearances to buildings, sidewalks, site fixtures, and inter-pad spacing\n2. **Access door orientation** (2 findings) — not documented; blocks verification of vegetation and access clearances\n3. **Building feature clearances** (3 findings) — equipment type and building elevations not provided; windows/doors/balconies clearances undimensioned\n4. **Fire safety clearances** (3 findings) — fire exits, fire escapes, and fire lanes lack dimensional documentation\n5. **Vegetation management** (2 findings) — tree compatibility and root barriers not verified on landscape plan\n6. **Underground utility coordination** (5 findings) — water, wastewater, storm drain, gas, and general underground utilities lack clearance dimensions and coordination drawings\n7. **Vertical clearance documentation** (2 findings) — cross-sections and profiles missing for transformer-to-utility vertical relationships\n8. **Overhead conductor clearances** (3 findings) — sky-to-ground and radius clearances to distribution lines not dimensioned\n9. **Transformer equipment specs** (2 findings) — equipment type and AE Design-approved pad details not provided\n10. **Transformer easements & property compliance** (4 findings) — easements not exhibited; PUE placement lacks approval; electrical routing verification missing\n11. **Bollard and access protection** (2 findings) — vehicle protection bollards and confined space documentation not shown\n\n### Key Findings Summary\n\n- **All 37 input findings accounted for** via `sourceId` tracing\n- **Cross-department notes** flag fire protection, landscape, architecture, utilities, and public works coordination needs\n- **High-severity items** (3): fire safety clearances, utility coordination, easement compliance, and AE Design-approved pad specifications\n- **Confidence levels** reflect per-run consensus (most findings caught by all 3 runs = high confidence)\n- **Attention flags** note unconfirmed conditions, low-confidence findings, and prerequisite documentation\n\nAll reviewer observations from the 3 audit runs are preserved verbatim in `runComments` for full traceability.","stop_reason":"end_turn","session_id":"c74ff556-b845-41ec-b2c9-9037e48bc40f","total_cost_usd":0.32535805,"usage":{"input_tokens":34,"cache_creation_input_tokens":81385,"cache_read_input_tokens":107428,"output_tokens":42570,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":81385},"inference_geo":"","iterations":[],"speed":"standard"},"modelUsage":{"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001":{"inputTokens":34,"outputTokens":42570,"cacheReadInputTokens":107428,"cacheCreationInputTokens":81385,"webSearchRequests":0,"costUSD":0.32535805,"contextWindow":200000,"maxOutputTokens":32000}},"permission_denials":[],"structured_output":{"comments":[{"headline":"Transformer clearances to adjacent features undimensioned","summary":"Five transformer pads lack required dimension callouts documenting clearances to buildings, sidewalks, utilities, and site features. Minimum distances range from 2 feet (sidewalks) to 5 feet (most features). No clearance annotations appear on the electrical plan.","sheets":[21,9],"applicableArea":"Utilities & Infrastructure","severity":2,"confidence":3,"crossDep":"Landscape design (vegetation near pads); Fire protection (hydrant coordination); Site civil design (sidewalk, parking, light pole placement)","attn":"Verify access door orientation required for fence clearance calculations (5-foot operator side, 3-foot non-operator side).","details":[{"text":"Five transformer pad locations require 5-foot minimum clearance to adjacent buildings. No dimension annotations showing compliance appear on electrical plan.","citation":"UCM § 1.10.4 Table 1.10.4; UCM § 1.10.5.B","sourceId":"13:EL-13.1","confidence":3,"runComments":[{"runNum":1,"status":"fail","comment":"Transformer pads lack documented minimum 5-foot clearance from adjacent buildings and structures. No clearance dimensions provided on electrical plan."},{"runNum":2,"status":"fail","comment":"Transformer pads appear to be located 3-5 feet from adjacent building footprints, which is less than the minimum 5-foot clearance required. No dimension annotations on the electrical plan document compliance with this clearance standard."},{"runNum":3,"status":"nv","comment":"Five transformer pads are shown on the electrical plan (Sheet 21) and site plan (Sheet 9), but no clearance distances are dimensioned or labeled on any sheet. The dashed boundary lines around transformer pads do not include numeric clearance measurements to adjacent buildings or structures. Cannot verify compliance with minimum 5-foot clearance requirement due to absence of labeled dimensions."}]},{"text":"Retaining walls present on site; 5-foot minimum clearance from transformer pads to retaining walls not dimensioned on plans (Sheets 21, 11).","citation":"Reviewer Convention","sourceId":"13:EL-13.2","confidence":3,"runComments":[{"runNum":1,"status":"nv","comment":"Retaining walls are present on site, but clearances from transformer pads to retaining walls are not documented on plans."},{"runNum":2,"status":"nv","comment":"Retaining walls are present on the site. However, no clearance dimensions are labeled showing the distance from transformer pads to retaining walls. Applicant must add dimension annotations confirming minimum 5-foot clearance from transformer pad edges to all retaining walls."},{"runNum":3,"status":"nv","comment":"Retaining walls are shown on the grading plan (Sheet 11), and transformer pads are shown on the electrical plan (Sheet 21), but no clearance dimensions are provided between transformer pads and retaining walls. Cannot determine if the minimum 5-foot clearance from retaining walls is maintained."}]},{"text":"Fence locations relative to transformer pads not documented; required clearances (5 feet operator side, 3 feet non-operator side) and access door orientation not shown.","citation":"UCM § 1.10.4 Table 1.10.4","sourceId":"13:EL-13.3","confidence":3,"runComments":[{"runNum":1,"status":"nv","comment":"Fence locations relative to transformer pads and access door orientations are not documented, preventing clearance verification."},{"runNum":2,"status":"nv","comment":"Fencing is present on the site. No access door orientation is identified for transformer pads, and no clearance dimensions are shown from transformer pads to fence lines. Applicant must add dimension annotations identifying access door orientation and confirming appropriate clearances (5 feet for operator sides, 3 feet for non-operator sides) from removable ventilated fences."},{"runNum":3,"status":"nv","comment":"While transformer pads are shown on the electrical and site plans, the access door orientation and locations are not clearly labeled. Additionally, no clearance distances (5 feet for sides with operators/controls, 3 feet for sides without) are provided. Cannot verify compliance with fence clearance requirements."}]},{"text":"Sidewalk locations adjacent to transformer pads; 2-foot minimum clearance from pad edges to sidewalk back edges not dimensioned (Sheets 21, 9, 22).","citation":"UCM § 1.10.4 Table 1.10.4","sourceId":"13:EL-13.7","confidence":3,"runComments":[{"runNum":1,"status":"nv","comment":"Sidewalks are adjacent to transformer locations, but clearances are not dimensioned on plans."},{"runNum":2,"status":"nv","comment":"Sidewalks are present on the site. No dimension annotations confirm minimum 2-foot clearance from transformer pad edges to back of sidewalks. Applicant must add dimension callouts showing 2-foot minimum distance maintained from all transformer pads to adjacent sidewalk back edges."},{"runNum":3,"status":"nv","comment":"While sidewalks are shown on the site plan (Sheet 9), the precise clearance distance from transformer pad edges to the back of sidewalks is not dimensioned. The minimum 2-foot clearance cannot be verified from the available plans."}]},{"text":"Fire hydrant location on site not related to transformer pad locations on electrical plan; 5-foot minimum clearance not dimensioned.","citation":"Reviewer Convention","sourceId":"13:EL-13.12","confidence":3,"runComments":[{"runNum":1,"status":"nv","comment":"Fire hydrant location on site is not shown in relation to transformer pad locations on electrical plan."},{"runNum":2,"status":"nv","comment":"A fire hydrant is shown on the site plan. No dimension annotations confirm minimum 5-foot clearance from transformer pads to the fire hydrant. Applicant must add clearance dimension callout(s) verifying 5-foot minimum distance maintained from all transformer pads to the fire hydrant."},{"runNum":3,"status":"nv","comment":"Fire protection plan (Sheet 10) shows one private fire hydrant on the site, but the precise distance from this hydrant to the transformer pad locations is not dimensioned. The required 5-foot clearance cannot be verified."}]},{"text":"Trash collection area shown on site plan; 5-foot minimum clearance from transformer pads to dumpsters not dimensioned (Sheets 21, 9).","citation":"Reviewer Convention","sourceId":"13:EL-13.16","confidence":3,"runComments":[{"runNum":1,"status":"nv","comment":"Dumpster enclosure locations relative to transformer pads are not documented on electrical plan."},{"runNum":2,"status":"nv","comment":"Trash collection area is shown on site plan. No dimension annotations confirm minimum 5-foot clearance from transformer pads to dumpster(s). Applicant must add clearance dimension callouts verifying 5-foot minimum distance from all transformer pads to waste containers/dumpsters."},{"runNum":3,"status":"nv","comment":"Site plan (Sheet 9) does not clearly show dumpster locations or label them with proximity to transformer pads. The required 5-foot clearance from dumpsters cannot be verified."}]},{"text":"Bicycle parking provided on site (39 long-term spaces); 5-foot minimum clearance from transformer pads to bike racks not dimensioned (Sheets 21, 9, 22).","citation":"Reviewer Convention","sourceId":"13:EL-13.17","confidence":3,"runComments":[{"runNum":1,"status":"nv","comment":"Bicycle parking locations relative to transformer pads are not documented on electrical or site plans."},{"runNum":2,"status":"nv","comment":"Bicycle parking is provided on site. No dimension annotations confirm minimum 5-foot clearance from transformer pads to bicycle racks. Applicant must add clearance dimension callouts verifying 5-foot minimum distance from all transformer pads to bike racks."},{"runNum":3,"status":"nv","comment":"Site plan (Sheet 9) shows bicycle parking spaces (39 long-term spaces provided), but the precise locations relative to transformer pad locations are not dimensioned. Required 5-foot clearances cannot be verified."}]},{"text":"Light poles present on site plan; 5-foot minimum clearance from transformer pads to lighting poles not dimensioned (Sheets 21, 9).","citation":"Reviewer Convention","sourceId":"13:EL-13.18","confidence":3,"runComments":[{"runNum":1,"status":"nv","comment":"Light pole locations relative to transformer pads are not verified on electrical plan."},{"runNum":2,"status":"nv","comment":"Light poles are present on the site plan. No dimension annotations confirm minimum 5-foot clearance from transformer pads to light poles. Applicant must add clearance dimension callouts verifying 5-foot minimum distance from all transformer pads to lighting poles."},{"runNum":3,"status":"nv","comment":"Site plan (Sheet 9) indicates exterior lighting will comply with full cut-off and fully-shielded requirements, but light pole locations relative to transformer pads are not dimensioned. Required 5-foot clearances cannot be verified."}]},{"text":"Five transformer pads must maintain 5-foot minimum spacing from each other; no dimension callouts verify compliance (Sheet 21).","citation":"Reviewer Convention","sourceId":"13:EL-13.20","confidence":3,"runComments":[{"runNum":1,"status":"fail","comment":"No minimum 5-foot clearance dimensions are shown between the five transformer pads on electrical plan."},{"runNum":2,"status":"nv","comment":"Five transformer pads are proposed on the site. No dimension callouts confirm minimum 5-foot clearance between individual transformer pads. Applicant must add clearance dimension annotations between all transformer pads verifying compliance with 5-foot minimum spacing requirement."},{"runNum":3,"status":"nv","comment":"Five transformer pads are shown on the electrical plan (Sheet 21). No clearance distances are provided between the transformer pads themselves. The required 5-foot separation between pads cannot be verified."}]}]},{"headline":"Transformer access door orientation not identified","summary":"Transformer pad access door sides are not clearly marked on electrical or landscape plans. Required clearances from access door sides (10 feet) and other sides (5 feet) to vegetation cannot be verified without door orientation documentation.","sheets":[21,31,9],"applicableArea":"Site Interior","severity":2,"confidence":3,"crossDep":"Landscape design (vegetation placement relative to transformer pads); Site access and circulation","attn":"Access door orientation marking is prerequisite for verifying vegetation clearances (10-foot from access side, 5-foot from others) and fire lane spacing.","details":[{"text":"Access door orientation not identified for any transformer pad; 10-foot hot-stick access clearance to adjacent building structures and open areas cannot be verified (Sheets 21, 9).","citation":"UCM § 1.10.4 Table 1.10.4","sourceId":"13:EL-13.10","confidence":3,"runComments":[{"runNum":1,"status":"fail","comment":"Transformer pad access door orientations and required 10-foot clearances are not documented on electrical plan."},{"runNum":2,"status":"fail","comment":"Transformer pad hot-stick access areas appear to lack minimum 10-foot clearance to adjacent building structures. No access door orientation is identified, and no clearance dimensions are provided to verify compliance."},{"runNum":3,"status":"nv","comment":"Transformer pads are shown on the plans but access door orientation is not clearly labeled, and no clearance distances are dimensioned. The 10-foot minimum clearance from the access door side to open areas or adjacent structures cannot be verified without these specifications."}]},{"text":"Landscape plan (Sheet 31) shows shrubs throughout site but does not label transformer pad locations; required 10-foot clearance from access side and 5-foot from other sides to shrubs/vegetation not dimensioned.","citation":"UCM § 1.10.10.4","sourceId":"13:EL-13.14","confidence":3,"runComments":[{"runNum":1,"status":"nv","comment":"Shrub and vegetation clearance distances from transformer locations are not documented on landscape or electrical plans."},{"runNum":2,"status":"nv","comment":"Landscape plan shows shrubs and groundcover throughout the site. No access door orientation is marked on transformer pads, and no clearance dimensions are provided. Applicant must identify access door orientation for each transformer pad and provide dimension callouts confirming 10-foot minimum lateral clearance from access door side and 5-foot minimum from other sides to all adjacent shrubs/vegetation."},{"runNum":3,"status":"nv","comment":"Landscape plan (Sheet 31) and electrical plan (Sheet 21) do not clearly cross-reference shrub/vegetation locations with transformer pad access door orientation. Required clearances (10 feet from access door side, 5 feet from other sides) cannot be verified due to missing orientation information."}]}]},{"headline":"Transformer equipment type and building feature clearances undocumented","summary":"Transformer equipment type is not specified, and clearances to building windows, doors, balconies, and overhangs are not dimensioned. If oil-filled equipment is proposed, a 12-foot minimum clearance to low windows and ventilation ducts is required.","sheets":[21,22,23,24,25,26,27,9],"applicableArea":"Building Envelope","severity":2,"confidence":2,"crossDep":"Architecture (building elevations, window/door locations, fire rating specifications); Fire protection (confined space assessment)","attn":"Confirm transformer equipment type (oil-filled vs. dry-type) as this drives multiple clearance requirements. Building elevations required for verification of all window, door, and duct locations.","details":[{"text":"Building elevations not provided; 5-foot lateral clearance from transformer pads to building balconies and overhangs cannot be dimensioned or verified (Sheets 21, 9).","citation":"UCM § 1.10.4 Table 1.10.4","sourceId":"13:EL-13.5","confidence":3,"runComments":[{"runNum":1,"status":"nv","comment":"Building elevations and sections showing potential balconies or overhangs above transformer locations are not provided, preventing verification."},{"runNum":2,"status":"nv","comment":"Building elevation drawings are not provided. Without elevations showing balcony and overhang locations, clearances from transformer pads to these features cannot be verified. Applicant must provide building elevation drawings with dimension callouts confirming minimum 5-foot lateral clearance from transformer pads to all balconies and overhangs, or confirm that overhead structures are not directly above pads."},{"runNum":3,"status":"nv","comment":"No clearance distances are provided between transformer pads and balconies, building overhangs, or structures directly above transformer locations. Building elevation and cross-section information would be needed to assess lateral clearance and overhead obstruction compliance."}]},{"text":"Transformer equipment type (oil-filled vs. dry-type) not specified; building elevations not provided; 12-foot minimum horizontal clearance from oil-filled equipment edges to low windows/doors/ducts cannot be verified (Sheets 21, 9).","citation":"UCM § 1.10.4 Table 1.10.4","sourceId":"13:EL-13.6","confidence":3,"runComments":[{"runNum":1,"status":"nv","comment":"Transformer equipment types and building window/door/duct locations relative to pads are not documented."},{"runNum":2,"status":"nv","comment":"Building elevation drawings and window/door/vent locations are not provided. Transformer type (oil-filled vs. dry-type) is not specified. Applicant must provide: (1) specification of transformer equipment type, (2) building elevations identifying all windows, doors, and ventilating ducts, and (3) dimension callouts confirming 12-foot minimum horizontal clearance from oil-filled equipment edges to any low windows/doors/ducts."},{"runNum":3,"status":"nv","comment":"No clearance dimensions are provided showing distances from transformer pads to windows, doors, or ventilating ducts. Transformer equipment type (oil-filled vs. dry-type) is not specified. Without these dimensions and specifications, 12-foot clearance compliance cannot be verified."}]},{"text":"If transformer pads proposed with clearances less than 5 feet to buildings, required documentation missing: written Austin Energy Design approval, 3-hour fire rating in clearance area, confined space confirmation, and vertical clearance verification (10+ feet to windows/doors, 15+ feet vertical).","citation":"UCM § 1.10.4 Table 1.10.4 footnote 2","sourceId":"13:EL-13.4","confidence":2,"runComments":[{"runNum":2,"status":"nv","comment":"If transformer pads are proposed with clearances less than 5 feet to buildings, applicant must provide: (1) written Austin Energy Design approval, (2) architectural specifications confirming 3-hour fire rating in clearance areas, (3) verification that location does not face confined space, (4) confirmation of 10+ feet clearance to windows/doors/ducts, and (5) verification of 15+ feet vertical clearance to windows/doors/ducts."},{"runNum":3,"status":"nv","comment":"No clearance dimensions are labeled on plans, so it cannot be determined whether reduced 3-foot clearances are shown. If reduced clearances exist, the required documentation (AE Design written approval, fire rating verification, confined space confirmation, vertical clearance to windows/doors) is not provided on the plans."}]}]},{"headline":"Fire safety clearances not documented or verified","summary":"Required clearances from transformer pads to fire exit stairs, fire escapes, and designated fire lanes are not dimensioned. If oil-filled equipment is used, a 20-foot clearance to fire escapes is required; all pads require 15-foot clearance to fire lanes.","sheets":[10,21,9],"applicableArea":"Site-wide","severity":3,"confidence":2,"crossDep":"Fire protection (emergency vehicle access, fire lane compliance, fire egress); Architecture (fire exit and fire escape locations, egress stair identification)","attn":"Requires coordination with fire protection plan. Verify fire lane boundaries and emergency access routes relative to all five transformer pad locations. Confirm whether fire escapes or exterior stairs serving as fire escapes are present.","details":[{"text":"Building floor plans identifying fire exit stairwell locations not provided; clearance dimensions from transformer pads to fire exit stairs not documented (Sheet 21).","citation":"Reviewer Convention","sourceId":"13:EL-13.8","confidence":2,"runComments":[{"runNum":2,"status":"nv","comment":"Building floor plans showing fire exit stairwell locations are not provided in the site plan submittal. Applicant must provide building floor plans identifying exit stair locations and dimension callouts confirming adequate clearance from transformer pads to all fire exit stairs."},{"runNum":3,"status":"nv","comment":"Fire egress elements are not clearly marked on the electrical or site plans relative to transformer pad locations. Without documentation of stairwell locations serving as fire exits and their relationship to transformer pads, required clearances cannot be verified."}]},{"text":"Building elevations not provided; if oil-filled equipment proposed, 20-foot minimum horizontal/radial clearance from pad edges to fire escapes or exterior stairs serving as fire escapes cannot be verified (Sheets 10, 21).","citation":"UCM § 1.10.4 Table 1.10.4","sourceId":"13:EL-13.9","confidence":2,"runComments":[{"runNum":2,"status":"nv","comment":"Building elevation drawings are not provided. Transformer type (oil-filled vs. dry-type) is not specified. Applicant must provide building elevations identifying fire escape locations (if any) and confirm 20-foot minimum horizontal/radial clearance from oil-filled transformer pad edges to fire escapes or exterior stairs serving as fire escapes."},{"runNum":3,"status":"nv","comment":"Fire protection plan (Sheet 10) and electrical plan (Sheet 21) do not clearly show the relationship between transformer pads and fire escapes/fire stairs. No clearance dimensions are provided. Equipment type (oil-filled vs. dry-type) is not specified. The required 20-foot clearance cannot be verified."}]},{"text":"Fire protection plan designates fire lanes on site; no dimension annotations confirm 15-foot minimum clearance from all transformer pads to fire lane boundaries (Sheets 10, 21).","citation":"Reviewer Convention","sourceId":"13:EL-13.19","confidence":3,"runComments":[{"runNum":1,"status":"nv","comment":"Clearance distances from transformer pads to fire lanes are not documented on electrical plan."},{"runNum":2,"status":"nv","comment":"Fire lanes are designated on the fire protection plan. No dimension annotations confirm minimum 15-foot clearance from transformer pads to fire lane boundaries. Applicant must add clearance dimension callouts verifying 15-foot minimum distance from all transformer pads to fire lanes."},{"runNum":3,"status":"nv","comment":"Fire protection plan (Sheet 10) designates fire lanes on the site, and electrical plan (Sheet 21) shows transformer pad locations, but no clearance dimensions are provided between fire lanes and transformer pads. The required 15-foot clearance cannot be verified."}]}]},{"headline":"Tree compatibility and root barrier details not verified","summary":"Landscape plan does not show transformer pad locations, preventing verification that tree species are utility-compatible and that root barriers are specified for trees within 20 feet of pads.","sheets":[31,32,21,37],"applicableArea":"Site Interior","severity":2,"confidence":3,"crossDep":"Landscape design (tree species selection, root barrier specification); Electrical coordination (transformer pad proximity to vegetation)","attn":"Landscape plan must clearly show transformer pad locations to allow cross-reference with tree list. ECM Appendix F utility-compatibility column ('UC') applies to trees within 10 lateral feet of transformer pads and 15 feet of overhead conductors.","details":[{"text":"Transformer pads not labeled on landscape plan (Sheet 31); tree species compatibility with ECM Appendix F utility-compatibility column cannot be verified for trees within 10 lateral feet of pads and 15 feet of overhead conductors (Sheets 31, 32).","citation":"UCM § 1.10.10.4; ECM Appendix F","sourceId":"13:EL-13.13","confidence":3,"runComments":[{"runNum":1,"status":"nv","comment":"Utility-compatible tree species verification requires detailed comparison of landscape plan tree locations with ECM Appendix F designations."},{"runNum":2,"status":"nv","comment":"Landscape plan shows trees and shrubs throughout the site. No documentation confirms that tree species are identified as utility-compatible per ECM Appendix F. Applicant must cross-reference the tree list (Sheet 32) against ECM Appendix F 'UC' column and confirm all trees within 10 feet of transformer pads and 15 feet of overhead conductors are utility-compatible species, or revise landscape plan."},{"runNum":3,"status":"nv","comment":"Landscape plan (Sheet 31) does not explicitly show transformer pads labeled, making it impossible to visually cross-reference tree species relative to transformer locations. Tree list (Sheet 32) is present, but cannot be correlated with transformer pad proximity without transformer pads identified on the landscape plan."}]},{"text":"Root barrier specifications and locations for trees within 20 lateral feet of transformer pads not documented in detail sheets; required minimum depth (4 feet) and distance from equipment (5 feet) not shown (Sheets 31, 37).","citation":"UCM § 1.10.10.4","sourceId":"13:EL-13.15","confidence":3,"runComments":[{"runNum":1,"status":"nv","comment":"Root barrier specifications and locations for trees near transformers are not verified against required standards."},{"runNum":2,"status":"nv","comment":"Landscape plan shows trees within 20 feet of transformer pad locations. No root barrier details or specifications are provided. Applicant must add root barrier detail sheets showing 4-foot minimum depth and 5-foot distance from transformer equipment for all trees within 20 lateral feet of pads, and add root barrier callouts to landscape plan."},{"runNum":3,"status":"nv","comment":"Landscape plan (Sheet 31) and detail sheets do not show root barrier specifications for trees within 20 feet of transformer pads. Transformer pad locations are not clearly marked on the landscape plan, preventing assessment of whether root barriers are required or provided."}]}]},{"headline":"Underground utility clearances not coordinated or documented","summary":"Water, wastewater, storm drain, gas, and other underground utilities are shown on separate plans but no coordination drawings or dimension callouts verify required clearances (5 feet for major utilities, 12-36 inches for others, measured OD to OD).","sheets":[21,19,12,11],"applicableArea":"Utilities & Infrastructure","severity":3,"confidence":3,"crossDep":"Water utility (water line coordination and sizing); Wastewater utility (sewer line coordination); Public works / stormwater (storm drain coordination); Gas utility (pressure specification and clearance requirements)","attn":"Utility coordination drawings with dimension callouts required. Confirm gas meter location and pressure specification (drives clearance: 24 inches for <60 psi, 36 inches for 60+ psi). Provide OD-to-OD measurements for all clearances.","details":[{"text":"Water lines shown on utility tap plan (Sheet 19); 5-foot minimum horizontal clearance from transformer pads not dimensioned; no utility coordination drawings provided.","citation":"UCM § 2.9.1.B.2","sourceId":"13:EL-13.21","confidence":3,"runComments":[{"runNum":1,"status":"fail","comment":"Required minimum 5-foot clearances from transformer pads to water lines are not documented on electrical plan."},{"runNum":2,"status":"nv","comment":"Water lines are shown on utility plan. No dimension annotations confirm minimum 5-foot horizontal clearance from transformer pads to water lines. Applicant must add clearance dimension callouts or provide utility coordination drawings verifying 5-foot minimum distance from all transformer pads to water service lines."},{"runNum":3,"status":"nv","comment":"Utility tap plan (Sheet 19) shows water line routing, and electrical plan (Sheet 21) shows transformer pad locations, but no clearance distances are dimensioned between these utilities. The required 5-foot minimum horizontal clearance from water lines cannot be verified."}]},{"text":"Wastewater lines shown on utility tap plan (Sheet 19); 5-foot minimum horizontal clearance from transformer pads not dimensioned; no utility coordination drawings provided.","citation":"UCM § 2.9.1.B.2","sourceId":"13:EL-13.22","confidence":3,"runComments":[{"runNum":1,"status":"fail","comment":"Required minimum 5-foot clearances from transformer pads to wastewater lines are not documented on electrical plan."},{"runNum":2,"status":"nv","comment":"Wastewater lines are shown on utility plan. No dimension annotations confirm minimum 5-foot horizontal clearance from transformer pads to wastewater lines. Applicant must add clearance dimension callouts or provide utility coordination drawings verifying 5-foot minimum distance from all transformer pads to wastewater service lines."},{"runNum":3,"status":"nv","comment":"Utility tap plan (Sheet 19) shows wastewater line routing, and electrical plan (Sheet 21) shows transformer pad locations, but no clearance distances are dimensioned between these utilities. The required 5-foot minimum horizontal clearance from wastewater lines cannot be verified."}]},{"text":"Storm drain lines shown on storm sewer plan (Sheet 12); 5-foot minimum horizontal clearance from transformer pads not dimensioned; no coordination drawings provided.","citation":"UCM § 2.9.1.B.2","sourceId":"13:EL-13.23","confidence":3,"runComments":[{"runNum":1,"status":"fail","comment":"Required minimum 5-foot clearances from transformer pads to storm drain lines are not documented on electrical plan."},{"runNum":2,"status":"nv","comment":"Storm drain lines are shown on site plans. No dimension annotations confirm minimum 5-foot horizontal clearance from transformer pads to storm drain lines. Applicant must add clearance dimension callouts or provide utility coordination drawings verifying 5-foot minimum distance from all transformer pads to storm drain infrastructure."},{"runNum":3,"status":"nv","comment":"Storm sewer plan (Sheet 12) shows drainage infrastructure, and electrical plan (Sheet 21) shows transformer pad locations, but no clearance distances are dimensioned between storm drain lines and transformer pads. The required 5-foot minimum horizontal clearance cannot be verified."}]},{"text":"Existing gas meters present on site (Sheet 11); precise location relative to transformer pads not dimensioned; gas line pressure specifications not documented (drives clearance: 24 inches for <60 psi, 36 inches for 60+ psi).","citation":"UCM § 1.10.5.A","sourceId":"13:EL-13.24","confidence":1,"runComments":[{"runNum":3,"status":"nv","comment":"Grading plan (Sheet 11) indicates existing gas meters are present on the site, but their precise locations relative to transformer pads are not dimensioned. Gas line pressure specifications are not documented. Required clearances (24 inches for less than 60 psi, 36 inches for 60 psi and higher) cannot be verified."}]},{"text":"Underground utilities at various locations; no clearance dimensions, profiles, or cross-sections show 12-inch minimum horizontal and vertical (OD to OD) separation from transformer pads to other underground utilities.","citation":"UCM § 1.10.5.A","sourceId":"13:EL-13.25","confidence":3,"runComments":[{"runNum":1,"status":"fail","comment":"Required minimum 12-inch horizontal and vertical clearances from transformer pads to other underground utilities are not documented."},{"runNum":2,"status":"nv","comment":"Underground utility lines are shown at various locations. No utility coordination drawings, profiles, or cross-sections show vertical and horizontal clearances from transformer pads to other underground utilities. Applicant must provide utility coordination drawings with dimension callouts confirming 12-inch minimum horizontal and vertical clearance (OD to OD) from transformer pads to all other underground utilities."},{"runNum":3,"status":"nv","comment":"While utility lines are shown on various sheets, no clearance dimensions are provided between transformer pads and underground utilities. The required 12-inch minimum horizontal and vertical separation (outside diameter to outside diameter) from other underground utilities cannot be verified."}]}]},{"headline":"Cross-section drawings for vertical clearance verification missing","summary":"No utility coordination profiles or cross-sections are provided showing vertical relationships between transformer pads, underground utilities, and building foundations. Compliance with clearance and encroachment prohibitions cannot be verified.","sheets":[21,11,9],"applicableArea":"Utilities & Infrastructure","severity":2,"confidence":3,"crossDep":"Civil / grading design (foundation and garage structure elevations); Other utilities (vertical coordination with water, sewer, storm, electrical lines)","attn":"Cross-sections must show transformer pad elevation relative to other utility lines and building foundations to confirm 12-inch minimum clearance and prevent encroachment. Particularly critical for integrated garage parking structure.","details":[{"text":"Vertical spatial relationships between transformer facilities and other utility lines not documented; no profile or cross-section drawings confirm transformer pads and AE facilities are not located directly over or under other utilities or customer building foundations (Sheets 21, 19).","citation":"UCM § 1.10.5.B","sourceId":"13:EL-13.26","confidence":3,"runComments":[{"runNum":1,"status":"nv","comment":"Vertical spatial relationships between transformer pads and utility lines are not documented; cross-sections required for verification."},{"runNum":2,"status":"nv","comment":"Electrical plan shows transformer pads and underground utilities at the same location. No profile or cross-section drawings show vertical relationships between transformer facilities and other utilities. Applicant must provide utility coordination profile drawings confirming transformer pads and underground electrical facilities are not located directly over or under other utility lines."},{"runNum":3,"status":"nv","comment":"Utility and grading plans do not provide documentation showing whether transformer pads are placed over or under other utility lines, or whether customer buildings, foundations, or structures are installed over AE underground facilities. Compliance with this prohibition cannot be verified."}]},{"text":"Cross-section drawings showing vertical clearances at transformer pad locations, especially in proximity to integrated garage parking and enclosed areas, not provided; vertical clearance compliance cannot be demonstrated (Sheets 21, 9).","citation":"UCM § 1.10.3","sourceId":"13:EL-13.31","confidence":3,"runComments":[{"runNum":1,"status":"fail","comment":"Cross-section drawings showing vertical clearances from transformer pads to overhead structures are not provided."},{"runNum":2,"status":"nv","comment":"Site plan shows integrated garage parking. No cross-section drawings are provided showing vertical clearances at transformer pad locations to verify adequate headroom and overhead clearance for equipment access and operation."},{"runNum":3,"status":"fail","comment":"Cross-section drawings showing vertical clearances in access paths with overhead structures, parking garages, enclosed areas, or niche configurations are not provided. Without these drawings, compliance with vertical clearance requirements cannot be demonstrated."}]}]},{"headline":"Overhead conductor clearances not documented or verified","summary":"Overhead distribution lines on the western boundary lack dimension callouts or profile drawings documenting required clearances from transformer pads (7.5 feet sky-to-ground, 15-foot radius). Customer facilities' vertical relationship to overhead lines cannot be verified.","sheets":[21,31,9],"applicableArea":"Utilities & Infrastructure","severity":2,"confidence":3,"crossDep":"Landscape design (light pole, antenna, sign placement); Architecture (building and structure placement relative to overhead lines); Utility coordination","attn":"Overhead electric line locations noted on landscape plan as 'Overhead Electric' but specific clearance dimensions not provided. Verify conductor height and horizontal routing. Customer facilities (buildings, structures, light poles, antennas) must not be placed vertically under or over conductors.","details":[{"text":"Overhead distribution conductors on western boundary; 7.5-foot minimum horizontal sky-to-ground clearance from transformer pads to conductors not dimensioned or profiled (Sheets 21, 31).","citation":"UCM § 1.10.3","sourceId":"13:EL-13.27","confidence":3,"runComments":[{"runNum":1,"status":"fail","comment":"Required minimum 7.5-foot horizontal sky-to-ground clearances from overhead distribution conductors are not documented for transformer pads near OHE line."},{"runNum":2,"status":"nv","comment":"Overhead distribution lines are shown on utility plan. No dimension annotations or profile drawings confirm 7.5-foot minimum horizontal sky-to-ground clearance from transformer pad locations to overhead distribution conductors. Applicant must add profile cross-sections or dimension callouts verifying 7.5-foot clearance from ground level vertically through conductor height."},{"runNum":3,"status":"nv","comment":"Overhead electric line locations are shown on landscape plan (Sheet 31) as 'Overhead Electric', but specific clearance dimensions (7.5-foot horizontal sky-to-ground clearance) from transformer pads to overhead distribution line conductors are not provided. Compliance cannot be verified."}]},{"text":"15-foot radius clearance from overhead distribution primary and neutral conductors (measured from conductors, not pole centerline) not dimensioned; no overlay or dimension callouts on electrical plan (Sheets 21, 31).","citation":"UCM § 1.10.3","sourceId":"13:EL-13.28","confidence":3,"runComments":[{"runNum":1,"status":"fail","comment":"Required minimum 15-foot radius clearance from overhead distribution conductors is not documented on electrical plan."},{"runNum":2,"status":"nv","comment":"Overhead distribution lines are shown on utility plan. No dimension annotations confirm 15-foot radius clearance from transformer pads to overhead distribution primary and neutral conductors (measured from conductors, not pole centerline). Applicant must add clearance dimension callouts or overlay 15-foot radius circles around overhead conductors demonstrating compliance."},{"runNum":3,"status":"nv","comment":"Overhead electric lines are noted on landscape plan but the specific 15-foot radius clearance from overhead distribution primary and neutral conductors (measured from conductors, not pole centerline) is not dimensioned on any sheet. Compliance cannot be verified."}]},{"text":"Site plan shows various customer facilities (buildings, parking structures, light poles, antenna); relationship to overhead distribution lines not documented; vertical encroachment compliance not verifiable (Sheets 21, 31, 9).","citation":"UCM § 1.10.3","sourceId":"13:EL-13.39","confidence":3,"runComments":[{"runNum":1,"status":"nv","comment":"Vertical clearances between customer facilities (buildings, structures) and overhead distribution lines are not documented on electrical plan."},{"runNum":2,"status":"nv","comment":"Overhead distribution facilities are shown on utility plan. No profile or cross-section drawings verify that customer buildings, parking structures, and other facilities do not extend vertically into overhead conductor space. Applicant must provide utility coordination profile drawings confirming no customer facilities are located directly under overhead distribution lines."},{"runNum":3,"status":"nv","comment":"Overhead electric lines are noted on landscape plan (Sheet 31) as 'Overhead Electric'. Site plan (Sheet 9) shows various site features including light poles, structures, and antenna mounts. However, no specific documentation confirms whether customer facilities (buildings, parking garages, light poles, signs, antennas, tanks) are installed under or over Austin Energy overhead distribution facilities. Compliance cannot be verified."}]}]},{"headline":"Transformer equipment type and AE-approved pad details not provided","summary":"Transformer equipment type (oil-filled vs. dry-type) and service configuration are not specified. AE Design-approved transformer pad specification sheets matching the proposed service type are not included in construction details.","sheets":[21,11,22,23,24,25,26,27],"applicableArea":"Plan Documentation","severity":3,"confidence":3,"crossDep":"Austin Energy Design (pad specification approval, standard details, service configuration); Grading / Civil design (drainage if oil-filled equipment)","attn":"Obtain transformer pad detail sheets from Austin Energy Design matching proposed service type (single-phase or three-phase). Clarify equipment type early to confirm all clearance requirements — oil-filled equipment has stricter clearances than dry-type.","details":[{"text":"Transformer equipment type not specified on electrical plan (Sheet 21); if oil-filled equipment proposed, grading plan (Sheet 11) does not show drainage direction annotations confirming surface water flow away from buildings.","citation":"UCM § 1.10.4 Table 1.10.4 footnote 1","sourceId":"13:EL-13.32","confidence":3,"runComments":[{"runNum":1,"status":"nv","comment":"Transformer equipment types are not specified, and drainage direction around pads is not documented."},{"runNum":2,"status":"nv","comment":"Transformer equipment type (oil-filled vs. dry-type) is not specified. If oil-filled equipment is proposed, applicant must provide grading plan with drainage arrows showing surface water slope direction around transformer pads, confirming liquid/drainage flow is directed away from buildings."},{"runNum":3,"status":"nv","comment":"Transformer equipment type (oil-filled vs. dry-type) is not specified on the electrical plan (Sheet 21). Grading plan (Sheet 11) does not show specific drainage direction around transformer pad locations. If oil-filled equipment is specified, drainage must flow away from building; this cannot be verified due to missing equipment type specification and drainage documentation."}]},{"text":"AE Design-approved transformer pad specification sheets (dimensions and construction details) not provided; pad locations shown but no details matching proposed service type (single-phase or three-phase) included in Sheets 22-27; service type not documented.","citation":"UCM § 1.5.2.6; UCM § 1.18.0","sourceId":"13:EL-13.37","confidence":3,"runComments":[{"runNum":1,"status":"fail","comment":"Austin Energy Design-approved transformer pad specification sheets are not provided, and pad dimensions are not documented on electrical plan."},{"runNum":2,"status":"fail","comment":"Transformer pad construction details and specifications matching Austin Energy Design-approved standards are not provided. Applicant must obtain transformer pad detail sheets from AE Design and add them to construction details, showing dimensions and specifications for the proposed single-phase or three-phase service type."},{"runNum":3,"status":"fail","comment":"Transformer pad locations are shown on electrical plan (Sheet 21) and site plan (Sheet 9), but no detail sheets are provided showing transformer pad dimensions or specifications. No AE Design-approved transformer pad detail sheets matching the specified service type (single-phase or three-phase) are included in the plan set. Service type is not documented."}]}]},{"headline":"Transformer easement exhibits and property boundary compliance undocumented","summary":"Transformer easement boundaries required for Austin Energy accessibility are not depicted. Electrical equipment placement within utility easement corridors lacks written AE Design approval. Electrical routing from transformers to meters is not verified to remain 100% on private property.","sheets":[21,11,2,9],"applicableArea":"Plan Documentation","severity":3,"confidence":2,"crossDep":"Austin Energy Design (easement approval, easement requirements, routing verification); Public Works / ROW (property line verification, easement coordination)","attn":"Verify transformer pad locations relative to easements described in facts.md. Two critical easements noted as not depicted on submitted plans — must be verified and shown. Obtain AE Design written approval if placement within easements is unavoidable. Confirm property lines and electrical routing on revised plans.","details":[{"text":"Transformer pads appear located within Public Utility Easement (PUE) corridors shown on plat; written Austin Energy Design approval for placement within easements not provided (Sheets 21, 2).","citation":"UCM § 1.10.4 Table 1.10.4 footnote 4","sourceId":"13:EL-13.33","confidence":2,"runComments":[{"runNum":2,"status":"fail","comment":"Transformer pads are located within Public Utility Easement (PUE) and other utility easement corridors without documented Austin Energy Design written approval for such placement. Applicant must provide AE Design approval letter or revise pad locations to avoid easement conflicts."},{"runNum":3,"status":"nv","comment":"Site plan and plat do not include specific notes confirming that transformer pads are located 100% on private property (not straddling property lines or in public right-of-way). Property boundaries are shown, but no specific callouts verify transformer pad location relative to property lines."}]},{"text":"Easement boundaries shown on plat (Sheet 2) and grading plan (Sheet 11) including drainage, wastewater, electrical, public utility, and greenbelt easements, but no specific notes confirm transformer pads located 100% outside prohibited easements; facts.md indicates two critical easements not depicted (Sheets 21, 11, 2).","citation":"UCM § 1.10.4 Table 1.10.4 footnote 4","sourceId":"13:EL-13.34","confidence":3,"runComments":[{"runNum":1,"status":"nv","comment":"Easement boundaries (drainage, water, wastewater, sewer, electrical) are not clearly depicted on electrical plan, making verification of prohibited easement violations unclear. One pad may be in drainage easement area."},{"runNum":2,"status":"fail","comment":"Transformer pads are located within Public Utility Easement (PUE) and other utility easement corridors without documented Austin Energy Design written approval for such placement. Applicant must provide AE Design approval letter or revise pad locations to avoid easement conflicts."},{"runNum":3,"status":"nv","comment":"Grading plan (Sheet 11) and plat (Sheet 2) show multiple easements (drainage, wastewater, electric, public utility, greenbelt), but no specific notes or documentation confirm whether transformer pads are located outside these prohibited easements. Facts.md indicates two critical easements not depicted on submitted plans. Cannot verify compliance without explicit confirmation."}]},{"text":"Transformer easements (width to be confirmed by AE Design) required for accessibility and equipment maintenance not shown or dimensioned on site plan (Sheet 9), plat (Sheet 2), or electrical plan (Sheet 21) for any of the five transformer pad locations.","citation":"UCM § 1.10.3","sourceId":"13:EL-13.35","confidence":3,"runComments":[{"runNum":1,"status":"fail","comment":"Transformer easements required for Austin Energy accessibility are not shown around any transformer pad locations on electrical plan."},{"runNum":2,"status":"fail","comment":"Transformer easements are not shown on any sheet of the site plan. Austin Energy requires transformer easements to be depicted and dimensioned around all pads for accessibility and maintenance. Applicant must add transformer easement exhibits showing required width (to be confirmed by AE Design)."},{"runNum":3,"status":"fail","comment":"No transformer easements are shown or labeled on the site plan, plat, or electrical plan. The required easement dimensions for Austin Energy accessibility and equipment maintenance are not documented. Transformer easements must be shown around all pads."}]},{"text":"Electrical routing from transformer pads to meters shown on electrical plan; no dimension callouts or notes confirm all conduit remains 100% on private property and does not cross public right-of-way (Sheets 21, 9).","citation":"UCM § 1.10.4 Table 1.10.4 footnote 4","sourceId":"13:EL-13.36","confidence":3,"runComments":[{"runNum":1,"status":"nv","comment":"Complete electrical routing paths from transformers to meters are not explicitly documented as 100% on private property."},{"runNum":2,"status":"nv","comment":"Electrical routing from transformer pads to meters is shown but not dimensioned relative to property lines. Applicant must provide annotated routing with dimension callouts confirming all electrical conduit from transformer pads to meters remains 100% on private property and does not cross into public right-of-way or restricted easements."},{"runNum":3,"status":"nv","comment":"Electrical plan (Sheet 21) shows underground electrical line routing and transformer pad locations, but no specific notes or documentation confirm that electrical routing from transformer to meters is 100% on private property, not crossing public right-of-way. Compliance cannot be verified."}]}]},{"headline":"Bollard protection and equipment access documentation incomplete","summary":"All five transformer pads are positioned within 4 feet of vehicle circulation routes and require protective bollards, which are not detailed. Confined space access clearances and bollard specifications are not documented.","sheets":[21,9,22],"applicableArea":"Site Interior","severity":2,"confidence":2,"crossDep":"Landscape / Site design (parking layout, vehicle route proximity); Transportation / traffic design (bollard placement and spacing)","attn":"Verify confined space configuration at transformer pad locations. Bollard specifications must match AE Design-approved pad details. Spacing must allow equipment access door opening per manufacturer and AE Design specifications.","details":[{"text":"No cross-section drawings provided showing whether transformer pads face confined spaces (niches, vaults, or enclosed areas with 3+ sides); 15-foot clearance requirement for confined space access cannot be verified (Sheets 21, 9, 11).","citation":"UCM § 1.10.4 Table 1.10.4","sourceId":"13:EL-13.11","confidence":1,"runComments":[{"runNum":3,"status":"nv","comment":"No cross-section drawings are provided showing whether transformer pads face confined spaces (niches, vaults, or enclosed areas with 3+ sides). No niche-specific details or configurations are documented. The 15-foot clearance requirement for confined space access cannot be verified."}]},{"text":"All five transformer pads within 4 feet of vehicle circulation routes require 4-inch minimum diameter galvanized rigid metal bollard protection; no bollard specifications shown in construction details (Sheets 22-27) or locations indicated on electrical plan (Sheet 21); spacing must allow equipment door opening per AE Design details.","citation":"UCM § 1.10.4 Table 1.10.4","sourceId":"13:EL-13.38","confidence":3,"runComments":[{"runNum":1,"status":"nv","comment":"Clearances from transformer pads to parking areas are not dimensioned, and bollard protection details are not shown on electrical plan."},{"runNum":2,"status":"fail","comment":"All transformer pads are positioned within 4 feet of vehicle circulation routes and therefore require protective bollards. No bollards are shown on the electrical plan or detailed in construction details. Applicant must add 4-inch diameter galvanized rigid metal bollard details to the construction detail sheets and indicate bollard locations on Sheet 21, spaced to allow equipment door opening per AE Design equipment pad specifications."},{"runNum":3,"status":"nv","comment":"Site plan (Sheet 9) shows parking layout and transformer pad locations, but no clearance dimensions are provided showing whether transformer pads are within 4 feet of parking areas. If within this distance, 4-inch minimum diameter galvanized rigid metal bollards with proper spacing per AE Design details are not shown. Bollard specifications cannot be verified."}]}]}]},"fast_mode_state":"off","uuid":"ccae62ea-a657-4220-b917-aa85c0c443c3"}
