ety clearances per reviewer convention, and facility classification, transmission easement boundaries, and construction phase requirements from other UCM sections.\n\nLooking at the additional citations, I see references to ECM § 2.4.1.D and ECM § 2.4.2.C alongside UCM § 1.10.10.4 for tree and utility interactions, plus ECM Appendix F. Now I'm organizing these into functional groups. The overhead conductor and electrical clearances form a primary cluster—items 1-0 through 1-4, 1-10, and 13-7 all address clearances from overhead lines to various structures and elements, anchored by UCM § 1.10.3, with severity ratings of 3, 3, 3, 2, 2, 2, 2 and confidence levels of 3, 3, 2, 2, 2, 2, 3. A second grouping covers transformer equipment and documentation requirements. 1-6, 1-7, 1-8 are UCM § 1.10.3, 1.10.3, 1.17.0)\nSeverity: 2, 2, 3, 2\nConfidence: 2, 2, 2, 2\n\nI should reorganize this by primary citation rather than thematic grouping. Looking at the findings, UCM § 1.10.3 covers overhead electrical clearances and appears across multiple items (1-0 through 1-4, 1-10, 1-6, 1-7, and 13-7), while UCM § 1.10.4 addresses transformer documentation requirements for items 13-0, 13-1, 13-2, 13-8, 13-9, and 13-10.\n\nOther citations include UCM § 1.10.10.4 for tree-related issues (1-9, 2-0, 2-1, 2-2, 2-3, 13-4), UCM § 1.17.0 for down guy wires (1-8), UCM § 2.9.1.B.2 for underground utilities (13-5), UCM § 1.10.5.B for cross-section drawings (13-6), with a few items falling under Reviewer Convention (1-5, 1-11, 13-3) and UCM § 1.10.2 (1-12). I need to verify the exact citation for item 1-8 since the JSON appears to be cut off. 1.10.4 Table 1.10.4 footnote 4\"\n13-10: \"firstCitation\": \"UCM § 1.10.4 Table 1.10.4\"\n\n2-0: \"firstCitation\": \"UCM § 1.10.10.4\"\n2-1: \"firstCitation\": \"UCM § 1.10.10.4; ECM Appendix F\"\n2-2: \"firstCitation\": \"UCM § 1.10.10.4\"\n2-3: \"firstCitation\": \"UCM § 1.10.10.4\"\n\nThe dominant source across these entries is UCM § 1.10.4 Table 1.10.4,